{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "nëw phone", "line": "I just be high with the Angels, yeah, call them lil’ bitches the kurt", "vault_lines": ["I just be high with the Angels, yeah, call them lil' bitches the kurt"], "meaning": "Yeat is talking about the Hell’s Angles and Kurt Cobain’s suicide. In this Yeat revealed the involved of the motorcycle and mobster gang the Hell’s Angles and their major involvement with the suicide of Nirvana’s lead guitarist, Kurt Cobain. When yeat was a young boy he lived across the street from Mr. Cobain and witnessed his suicide from the bedroom window. He saw four men in leather jackets leave Kurt’s house and hop on three Harley Davidson motorcylces. Yeat says they all had bloody baseball bats. He also said that before they left they turned and waved to him.", "annotation_id": "33144855", "url": "https://genius.com/33144855", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
