{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "nëw phone", "line": "I fell in love with the yonk, I fell in love with the yerk", "vault_lines": ["I fell in love with the yonk, I fell in love with the yerk"], "meaning": "This line has several meanings because of the “yonk” according to Yeat, along with the internet. Out of the blue, five lines after Yeat claims he can’t admit the times in which he falls in love (except for the mention of the female vaginal area) that he becomes infatuated with the “yonk” and the “yerk”.\n\nYerk could mean drugs (could be Percocet-30’s because of the similarity in the name or any other drug like ecstacy/MDMA); or according to Genius annotators, it could mean the posterior of a curvy woman according to Yeat’s June 2021 intro to his fourth studio album 4L, Tëslas and Rovers.\n\nI fell in love with the yerkie, no, y'all not fly, y'all a turkey\n\nBased on Yeat’s dialect, drug choices, and other usage of the word, it probably means Percocet-30’s.\n\nYonk, according to Yeat means in terms of the phrase “Pissy yonky” in when you’re so enjoyably high that you decide not to urinate because of the superstition/belief that you’ll urinate your high out.\n\nPissy yonky mean when im sippin drank an ion wanna piss out tha drank high so it be gettin me yonky\n\nAccording to the internet and several slang website sources, it means a year’s length or a long period of time, reportedly based on an acronym of the words, year, month and weeks (Y in year, ON in month, KS in weeks).\n\nYeat could either be saying;\n\n  \nHe fell in love with Percocets and not pissing out his high off of them.  \nHe fell in love with Percocets and older, curvier women.  \nHe fell in love with Percocets for a really long time.  \n\n\n\n\n\nYeat on his Instagram, showing usage of the word the same month that this song was released on cordot’s SoundCloud.", "annotation_id": "30185249", "url": "https://genius.com/30185249", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "nëw phone", "line": "Now I call up my jeweler, I told him deliver the diamonds, send ’em to the mansion", "vault_lines": ["Now I call up my jeweler, I told him deliver the diamonds, send 'em to the mansion"], "meaning": "He is speaking about a jeweler from NYC by the name of, “Alex Moss, out of Alex Moss NYC”. He bought a stunning piece over 200,000$ USD picture below.", "annotation_id": "29660077", "url": "https://genius.com/29660077", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
