{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Countup", "line": "I just be shippin’ that Za’, shippin’ that somebody farted, huh", "vault_lines": ["I just be shippin' that Za', shippin' that somebody farted (Huh)"], "meaning": "The Za that he is shipping is ‘gas’, a term that can be used to describe high-grade, good quality weed. ‘Gas’ also can also be used to describe farts, and he is incorporating the double meaning of gas into his line.", "annotation_id": "25170655", "url": "https://genius.com/25170655", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Countup", "line": "Bitch, I done got rich, yeah, with no advance", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I done got rich, yeah, with no advance"], "meaning": "Yeat is telling his audience that he became significantly wealthy without receiving an upfront payment from his label.\n\nDefinition of Advance: payment up front on account of sums that become due to an artist, producer or royalty participant. -Thomson Reuters Practical Law", "annotation_id": "25096707", "url": "https://genius.com/25096707", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Countup", "line": "I got that shit on me, don’t try it unless you wanted to float (Float) No, I ain’t talkin’ ’bout no boat (No)", "vault_lines": ["I got that shit on me, don't try it unless you wanted to float (Float)"], "meaning": "In this line Summrs is explaining that he is armed (“I got that shit on me,”) and that he is not afraid to use said firearm (“don’t try it unless you wanted to float”). Summrs is likening a a dead body to a fish in this line, because fish float after they pass away. He is stating that if you try him, you will end up floating (in water, dead), and no, he’s not talking ‘bout no boat.", "annotation_id": "25064998", "url": "https://genius.com/25064998", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Countup", "line": "Oh, she told you she don’t? Then you’re probably not him (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Oh, she told you she don't? Then you're probably not him (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Here Summrs is saying the line ‘’ Oh, she told you she don’t? Then you are probably not him'‘ stating that the female he was messing around with told a guy that she does not eat ’‘dick’‘ meaning that she most likely has no interest in the guy", "annotation_id": "25036690", "url": "https://genius.com/25036690", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Countup", "line": "I take at least a twenty piece on me when I’m hitting the road", "vault_lines": ["I take at least a twenty piece on me when I'm hitting the road"], "meaning": "The artist with the rapper name “Summrs” states in this specific bar of the song that when he goes on the road (the highway) he carries at least 20 condoms with him since he works as a stripper/sex worker on the highway.", "annotation_id": "24771641", "url": "https://genius.com/24771641", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Countup", "line": "My brother been still on the run, this shit on our back, it’s a target (Oh, word) No, I ain’t talkin’ ’bout a store (Damn, Trgc made that? Huh)", "vault_lines": ["No, I ain't talkin' 'bout no boat (No)"], "meaning": "Target is a chain superstore featuring various items ranging from food supplies to clothing articles to home amenities.\n\nIn referencing the chain with the line,\n\nNo, I ain’t talkin' ‘bout a store\n\nThe artist ties together the previous line signifying the comparison between the international superstore to the target that government officers and federal detectives have against the subject in an attempt to put him behind bars.", "annotation_id": "24593201", "url": "https://genius.com/24593201", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Countup", "line": "Yeah, some of my niggas be Crips, they tryna take off the brim (Brim) That mean they take off your hat", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, some of my niggas be Crips, they tryna take off the brim (Brim)"], "meaning": "Crips are members and of Crip gang, an affiliation of gangsters in different hoods across America, though they are most prevalent in areas like Los Angeles, California, Compton, California and Brooklyn, New York. Brims are the bloods, the rival gang in most areas who usually feud with Crip members over territorial parts of cities and loss of loved ones by gang violence. The Brims were one of the first subgroup under the Blood gang category. A brim is also an anatomical part of a hat, usually a snapback or fitted.\n\nSummrs compares his Crip affiliates “taking off the Brim” to someone taking off one’s hat.", "annotation_id": "24556650", "url": "https://genius.com/24556650", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Countup", "line": "How you got crossed up in real life? Both your ankles broke, yeah", "vault_lines": ["How you got crossed up in real life? Both your ankles broke, yeah"], "meaning": "To “cross” someone up is to use your agility, footwork and/or handling skills to shift or embarrass a defender in sports such as basketball, football and soccer. In the case of this lyric, crossing someone up is often referred to as “breaking someone’s ankles” being that the ankle is often the breaking point of getting a defender to bite the move.\n\nBeing that basketball is just a game, Yeat compares artists not having money to buy ankle jewelry, or money to spend to take care of themselves and “cover their ankles” as the popular idiom goes, to basketball players being crossed up.", "annotation_id": "24556625", "url": "https://genius.com/24556625", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
