{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "zaza", "line": "Fuckin’ this ho, she a goat (Yeah) Met that lil’ ho in LA (Nah) Then we flew back to the O", "vault_lines": ["Fuckin' this ho, she a goat (Yeah)"], "meaning": "KanKan allegedly had sexual intercourse with a goat in Los Angeles, CA, and then proceeded to head to the O block in Chicago, Illinois. He most likely did this to get away from California’s strict beastiality laws\n\nhttps://images.app.goo.gl/Pu4a73yEkas5mAem8", "annotation_id": "26348306", "url": "https://genius.com/26348306", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "zaza", "line": "I’m smokin’ za out the bowl (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm smokin' za out the bowl"], "meaning": "Yeat like many others have misheard Goonie’s lyric from where he says:\n\nI’m smokin' za out the bowl\n\nHe appears to be interpolating the line from the chorus but ends up mistakenly saying “I’m smoking za on the boat” for this verse.", "annotation_id": "26225907", "url": "https://genius.com/26225907", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "zaza", "line": "Bowl", "vault_lines": ["I'm smokin' za out the bowl"], "meaning": "The correct line is: “I’m smokin' za out the ‘bow” Which means Goonie is smoking weed by the pound. (Bow -> Elbow -> LB -> pound)", "annotation_id": "26041747", "url": "https://genius.com/26041747", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "zaza", "line": "Rich with no fuckin’ degree", "vault_lines": ["Rich with no fuckin' degree"], "meaning": "Before the modern era, it was slim to impossible to imagine the success teenagers and early 20s aged men and women could have without the need for collegiate learning. Our grandparents nearly drill into our heads the importance of college for the purpose of access to better paying jobs, when it is becoming less and less of a necessity.\n\nGoonie is making it clear that he has reached financial comfortability without the need of a college degree. Likely his musical outputs have brought him the success he speaks of here.", "annotation_id": "24684633", "url": "https://genius.com/24684633", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "zaza", "line": "She jump when she put on her jeans", "vault_lines": ["She jump when she put on her jeans"], "meaning": "“Jumping in jeans” is an accomplishment a large percentage of women look to attain, as it is a sign of gains in the glutes and thighs areas as a result of working towards become thicker. As thick women are preferred by men generally, some women are naturally thick, some work to become thick, and some obtain this beauty standard artificially. Nonetheless, needing to jump to put in jeans is an honor code for attractive women.\n\nGoonie uses this symbolism to point out the kind of women he has access to. He is in the accompaniment of females with this body type because of the status he is on as a result of his financial comfortability & musical fanbase.", "annotation_id": "24684608", "url": "https://genius.com/24684608", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
