{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "z06", "line": "Treat this music shit like school (Swerve), I can’t even turn it in, yeah (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Treat this music shit like school (Swerve), I can't even turn it in, yeah (Yeah)"], "meaning": "In this Yeat lyric, Yeat compares the music industry to schoolwork or homework provided by the school system. The given analogy explains that Yeat cannot turn, or upload to streaming services and platforms the accumulation of his music because the label does its best to prevent Yeat from releasing extraneous amounts of music at one time, as he is proven to be a hardcore studio session enjoyer and creator of music.\n\nDespite how fire this song may be whilst being unreleased, unoriginally sourced, and coming from a rap-based SoundCloud page, it can be deemed reasonable to withhold an artist like Yeat from releasing too much music at one time.\nAt one time, Yeat was revealed to have made approximately two hundred songs in a singular month through an affiliate’s Instagram story.\n\nAlong with that, around the time that Yeat did his Complex cover story in November of 2022, he stated that he had created over two hundred songs solely with Lil Uzi Vert, their first collab dating two-thirds of a year back averaging at least one song per day.", "annotation_id": "30529229", "url": "https://genius.com/30529229", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
