{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "wit da gods", "line": "A lot of these rappers got they swag from me, but ain’t say nothin’ (Shh, uh-uh, ooh) And some of ‘em used to buy features off me when they was nothin’ (Ooh) [Bridge] And really, I don’t give a fuck about it, but we gon’ see who run it (Yeah, show ’em) We gon’ see who just make songs, and who make money (Show sum) Easily, we gon’ see who made the sauce, and who took from me (Yeah, on me) ‘Cause every song I make ain’t been the same, I’m new on some’ (Yeah, turn it up)", "vault_lines": ["A lot of these rappers got they swag from me, but ain't say nothin' (Shh, uh-uh, ooh)"], "meaning": "Yeat refers to rappers buying features and stealing his sound, while not blowing up or acknowledging him. Yeat also says he’ll evolve so much that they won’t be able to keep up copying him.", "annotation_id": "27612423", "url": "https://genius.com/27612423", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "wit da gods", "line": "How would I change, but I ain’t left the earth? (Earth) [Verse] Palm Angels sweatsuit (Woo), and I still talk to my demons (Yeah) How you stay the same, get no bread? I couldn’t believe it (Ah)", "vault_lines": ["How would I change, but I ain't left the earth? (Earth)"], "meaning": "Yeat is referring to changing with help from his demon and alien friends, and criticizes people from staying the same and broke.", "annotation_id": "27612420", "url": "https://genius.com/27612420", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
