{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "neon green", "line": "They told me Teslas save the climate, so I took me fifty-three (Fifty-three)", "vault_lines": ["They told me Teslas save the climate, so I took me fifty-three (Fifty-three)"], "meaning": "Yeat uses a clever double entendre playing on environmentalism and drug culture. On the surface Yeat is saying he bought 53 electric cars to help save the environment. “Teslas” is street slang for Ecstasy (MDMA) pills stamped with the car company’s logo. In party culture, altering the “climate” means changing the vibe or mood of a room. In reality he doesnt give a fuck about the environment and just wants to take molly. Yeat used a similar line on “Sorry ‘Bout That”", "annotation_id": "41176042", "url": "https://genius.com/41176042", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
