{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "bigger thën everything", "line": "Huh, I been blockin’ shade, I sit under umbrellas (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Huh, I been blockin' shade, I sit under umbrellas (Ooh)"], "meaning": "“Blockin' shade”:\n“Shade” can mean negativity, criticism, or unwanted attention. So, “blockin' shade” could mean the person is deflecting or avoiding those negative things.\nIt could also mean they are preventing others from “throwing shade” at someone else. They are protecting others.\n“I sit under umbrellas”:\nLiterally, an umbrella provides protection from the elements. Figuratively, it could represent:\nProtection from problems or stress.\nA comfortable or sheltered existence.\nHaving a way to stay out of the negative things that are happening around them.\nOverall meaning:\nThe sentence suggests the person is adept at avoiding negativity and staying in a safe or comfortable space. They’ve learned how to protect themselves from the “shade” that others might throw.\nIt could also be a statement of how they have created a safe space for themselves and others.\nIt also has a very “street” or “slang” type of delivery, so it is meant to come across as very casual, and confident.\nIn essence, it’s a statement of self-protection and resilience in the face of negativity.", "annotation_id": "34747264", "url": "https://genius.com/34747264", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "bigger thën everything", "line": "I could make the money come, I can make it go", "vault_lines": ["I could make the money come, I can make it go"], "meaning": "This is a referrence to Kanye West line on 2008 track Paranoid\n\n“I could make you come, I could make you go”", "annotation_id": "31914817", "url": "https://genius.com/31914817", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
