{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "bigger thën everything", "line": "I just hopped the jet, this shit go straight to heaven", "vault_lines": ["I just hopped the jet, this shit go straight to Ella"], "meaning": "“Ella” refers to LA or Los Angeles. Yeat commonly stylizes it as Ella, such as in his song “Goin back 2 Ella.\"", "annotation_id": "31110237", "url": "https://genius.com/31110237", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "bigger thën everything", "line": "I-I-I-I— I-I-I-I— I-I-I-I-I’m working on dying BNYX", "vault_lines": ["I-I-I-I-I'm working on dying"], "meaning": "This is the producer tag of Philadelphia producer collective Working on Dying, known for their work with artists like Lil Uzi Vert, Playboi Carti, Ken Carson, and more. BNYX, the producer of “Talk”, has been a member of the group since 2021 as well as the main producer for Lyfe, producing songs on the project like “Talk” and “Wat it feel lykë” and has been a frequent collaborator of Yeat for his past few projects. Yeat has also worked with other Working on Dying members such as Brandon Finnesin (on “Big Tonka” with Lil Uzi Vert) and F1lthy (on “Smooktober”)", "annotation_id": "30929364", "url": "https://genius.com/30929364", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
