{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "bigger thën everything", "line": "Why? Every time I look back, they surprised", "vault_lines": ["Why? Every time I look back, they surprised"], "meaning": "Yeat refers to the three gigantic grim-reaper-looking figures on the cover art as “They”, “Devils” that also refer to Yeat as “Him”, “God”. Yeat is saying that he gets so euphoric (high) that he becomes so confident and self assured  which amazes “They” the “Devils” and that they “can cut out one of his eyes” as an induction into a cult like a masonic brotherhood or even the illuminati", "annotation_id": "29331717", "url": "https://genius.com/29331717", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
