{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "[ADL IS COMING]", "line": "BNYX", "vault_lines": ["You couldn't live it, couldn't be it, couldn't want it"], "meaning": "Benjamin Saint Fort (born April 23, 1995), professionally known as BNYX®, (pronounced Benny X), is a record producer from Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. He is known for his production for Drake, Yeat, Lil Uzi Vert, Travis Scott, and Lancey Foux, among others.\n\nBNYX® acquired his pseudonym as a result of taking his nickname, Benny, and attaching it to the letter X, which he describes stands for “extreme,” a quality that he strives to achieve when creating music.\n\nIn 2021, BNYX® signed to record label and production group, Working on Dying.\n\nI-I-I’m working on dying, BNYX", "annotation_id": "41572276", "url": "https://genius.com/41572276", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "[ADL IS COMING]", "line": "Got the factory PJ on us, that’s that private jane", "vault_lines": ["Got the factory PJ on us, that's that private jane"], "meaning": "“PJ” stands for private jet. “Factory” suggests brand-new. “Private Jane” is wordplay on “Mary Jane” (weed).", "annotation_id": "38797979", "url": "https://genius.com/38797979", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "[ADL IS COMING]", "line": "Bitch, you back again, you already know the drill", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, you back again, you already know the drill"], "meaning": "Yeat implies the woman has returned and already understands how their dynamic works. “You already know the drill” highlights the repetitive, routine nature of his lifestyle and relationships.", "annotation_id": "38797966", "url": "https://genius.com/38797966", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
