{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "[ADL IS COMING]", "line": "I live the dream (Reach out your hand for me) Yeah, I live the dream (Reach out your hand) Yeah, baby, I live the dream (Reach out your hand)", "vault_lines": ["I live the dream (Reach out your hand for me)"], "meaning": "Yeat lives the “dream”, which could be related to the “American dream”, meaning he is a successful artist, but also this “dream” does not reflect his life. He later supports this argument by suggesting that his act of walking around casually in the Hamptons does not directly relate to his status. Once again, this means he lives the dream without reflecting on his achievements.", "annotation_id": "37110232", "url": "https://genius.com/37110232", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
