{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Yea Yea", "line": "Chanel", "vault_lines": ["I just pulled up in Chanel"], "meaning": "According to wikipedia:\n\n“Chanel is a French luxury fashion house founded in 1910 by Coco Chanel in Paris. Chanel specializes in women’s ready-to-wear, luxury goods, and accessories and licenses its name and branding to Luxottica for eyewear. Chanel is well known for its No. 5 perfume and \"Chanel Suit”\"\n\nYeat has infromed us that he has entered a Chanel store presumable to make a sizeable purpose.\n\nYeat has expressed adoration for the Chanel brand prior, going as far as naming and releasing a track after the brand entitled “Chanëlly” as track 7 on his june 2021 mixtape “4L”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4QTt1XERn24", "annotation_id": "27794921", "url": "https://genius.com/27794921", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Yea Yea", "line": "Margiela", "vault_lines": ["Put her in Margiela"], "meaning": "according to wikipedia:\n\n“Maison Margiela, formerly Maison Martin Margiela, is a French luxury fashion house founded by Belgian designer Martin Margiela and Jenny Meirens in 1988 and headquartered in Paris”\n\nIn this bar Mr. Bans implies that he has put a female companion in clothing manufactured by Maison Margiela, “formerly Maison Martin Margiela” which would be considered luxury clothing as their products tend to be considered expensive because of the price being un affordable to the average consumer.", "annotation_id": "27794869", "url": "https://genius.com/27794869", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Yea Yea", "line": "Cartiers, need diamond eye (Yeah)”", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, told 'em, \"I need them Cartiers, need diamond eye (Yeah)\""], "meaning": "according to wikipedia:\n\n“Cartier International SNC, or simply Cartier, is a French luxury goods conglomerate that designs, manufactures, distributes, and sells jewellery, leather goods, and watches. Founded by Louis-François Cartier in Paris in 1847”\n\nIn this bar, Yeat refers to the glasses sold by Cartier\n\n\n\nThe diamond eye portion of the bar refers to certain types of glasses sold by Cartier glasses that feature diamonds in the frame, as pictured above.", "annotation_id": "27794838", "url": "https://genius.com/27794838", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Yea Yea", "line": "Heard that fuck nigga been talking that shit, that stick on me like glue", "vault_lines": ["Heard that fuck nigga been talking that shit, that stick on me like glue"], "meaning": "In this line Mr. Bans refers to both glue sticks and firearms. The analogyhe is providing here is that the “fuck nigga” in question will have an encounter with bans or his affiliates and said “fuck nigga” will then be assaulted with a firearm. the glue stick termanology comes in when the term “stick” is used as slang for a firearm and the popular item, the “Glue Stick” which is defined by wikipedia as:\n\n“solid and hard adhesives in twist or push-up tubes. Users can apply glue by holding the open tube to keep their fingers clean and rubbing the exposed stick against a surface.”", "annotation_id": "27794813", "url": "https://genius.com/27794813", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Yea Yea", "line": "In a brand new ’Cat, nigga, fuck Scat Pack, the inside seats all blue", "vault_lines": ["In a brand new 'Cat, nigga, fuck Scat Pack, the inside seats all blue"], "meaning": "A “Scat Pack” is defined by\n\n“A trim level for both the Dodge Charger and the Dodge Challenger. The term Scat Pack was first coined dates back to advertising in the late 1960s. ‘Scat’ refers to the term scat, as in “Get out of here!”. The ‘Pack’ part comes from Frank Sinatra’s Rat Pack”\n\nIn this line, Mr. Bans implies that he has had his Scat Pack customized by getting the interior seats either replaced or reskinned to change the color to blue.", "annotation_id": "27794782", "url": "https://genius.com/27794782", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Yea Yea", "line": "They asked if that’s a cranky", "vault_lines": ["They asked if that's a cranky"], "meaning": "A “Cranky\"refers to a Percocet pill also reffered to as a \"Perc”, “Perky” and “Yerky” as a couple examples. According to Wikipedia:\n\n “Oxycodone/paracetamol, sold under the brand name Percocet among others, is a fixed-dose combination of the opioid oxycodone with paracetamol, used to treat moderate to severe pain”\n\nIn the refrence used in this bar it is assumed that a companion has inquired about what type of pill Yeat was taking, which is imlied to be for recreational manner rather than the proper and intended medical use. It may be possible that the companion is inquiring about either the type of pill or the authenticity of the pill and recently pills, in particular “Percocets”, “Xans” [also known by “Xanax” and “Alprazolam”] and “Molly” [also commonly reffered to as “MDMA”, “X” or “Ecstasy”] have recently been counterfieted with “Fentanyl” being added to the ingredients as it is cheaper and easier to aquire compared to the ingredients typically included in the drug. It can get to the point where the entire drug apart from one or two outside layers are made of Fentanyl. asking if “That is a Cranky” could be inquiring on if the ingredients in the drug are not Fentanyl and are the proper ingredients for the drug to be considered authentic.", "annotation_id": "27794674", "url": "https://genius.com/27794674", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
