{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Yam", "line": "(Keep it up, sharkboy)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I'm a trooper, yeah, with a lot of bands"], "meaning": "This is the producer tag for Sharkboy, a producer and samplemaker from Russia. He is best known for his work with American rapper Yeat, notably co-producing his breakout single, “Sorry Bout That”.\n\nHe has also notably worked with DC The Don, Kankan, and UnoTheActivist, among others.", "annotation_id": "28315092", "url": "https://genius.com/28315092", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Yam", "line": "Yeah, it’s a hit every time I speak, bitch, I’m out the park (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, it's a hit every time I speak, bitch, I'm out the park (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat is actually saying “out the park” as it rhymes with “in the dark”.\n\nYeat is casually seen wearing an MLB fitted almost all the time.\n\nSaying it’s a hit every time he speaks and that he is out the park. He’s trying to say all his songs are home runs.", "annotation_id": "25554610", "url": "https://genius.com/25554610", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Yam", "line": "All my diamonds Michael Jackson, watch they dance they heads off", "vault_lines": ["All my diamonds Michael Jackson, watch they dance they heads off"], "meaning": "Michael Jackson had cemented himself as one of the greatest live performers of the modern era. Yeat’s acknowledgement of this comes in the form of comparing Michael’s supreme dance moves to his own set of diamonds. Diamonds, when authentic, should shine ( or “dance”) in any setting/lighting.\n\nhttps://giphy.com/gifs/michael-jackson-moonwalk-sJs1Ag97x0MV2", "annotation_id": "24749298", "url": "https://genius.com/24749298", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
