{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Ya Ya", "line": "Yeah, I just left the Earth, they askin’, “What that mean?”", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I just left the Earth, they askin', \"What that mean?\""], "meaning": "New Amiri jeans, when I ask what you want, bitch say a million things\n\nYeat says he has just “left the earth”, referring to spinning off a perc (getting high off a perc) and he explains that people do not know what he means", "annotation_id": "30117628", "url": "https://genius.com/30117628", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Ya Ya", "line": "New Amiri jeans, when I ask what you want, bitch say a million things", "vault_lines": ["New Amiri jeans, when I ask what you want, bitch say a million things"], "meaning": "New Amiri jeans, when I ask what you want, bitch say a million things\n\nYeat (in his new designer Amiri jeans) says when he asks his presumably partner what she wants she should say a “million things”. This line flaunts his wealth and shows his amazing generosity", "annotation_id": "30117584", "url": "https://genius.com/30117584", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Ya Ya", "line": "Yeah, bitch, I’m on the drugs, that’s what we on", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, bitch, I'm on the drugs, that's what we on"], "meaning": "yeat once again is on drugs another word used for drugs are percs and X. the common slangs he uses for drugs are percs and X", "annotation_id": "29999897", "url": "https://genius.com/29999897", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Ya Ya", "line": "But I had to walk ’round before I had a car If I don’t slow down, I won’t make it far", "vault_lines": ["But I had to walk 'round before I had a car"], "meaning": "Yeat employs the literary device of “paradox” in these back-to-back lines.\n\nYeat writes that he was not able to afford a car at one point in his life, so he was forced to walk around, which is slower than driving. However, now that he has a car, he is able to go as fast as he wants. That means Yeat is prone to fatal car accidents, though, which means he needs to “slow down” in his car (which was supposed to allow him to travel faster) or else he “won’t make it far” in life.", "annotation_id": "29400538", "url": "https://genius.com/29400538", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Ya Ya", "line": "I can’t rock with them broke boys, you ain’t on the team, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I can't rock with them broke boys, you ain't on the team, yeah"], "meaning": "This attitude is frequently expressed by Yeat. He won’t mess with people who are not of any wealth.", "annotation_id": "29036901", "url": "https://genius.com/29036901", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
