{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "YEET", "line": "John Cena, why you waving your finger, man?", "vault_lines": ["John Cena, why you waving your finger, man?"], "meaning": "Yung Kayo makes a reference to John Cena’s popular celebration, “you can’t see me”, where he is seen waving his hand over his face, signifying to his opponent that he is not seen.", "annotation_id": "36360286", "url": "https://genius.com/36360286", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "YEET", "line": "In the garden, bitch, I feel like I’m Peter Pan", "vault_lines": ["In the garden, bitch, I feel like I'm Peter Pan"], "meaning": "Yung Kayo makes a reference to the novel, Peter Pan in Kingston Gardens.\n\n\n\nIn this novel, Peter Pan is just a seven-day-old infant who used to be a part bird like all other infants, but finds out that he is more human rather than bird by Solomon Caw.", "annotation_id": "36360241", "url": "https://genius.com/36360241", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "YEET", "line": "Pay away like I’m Gaga, got poker face", "vault_lines": ["Pay away like I'm Gaga, got poker face"], "meaning": "Yung Kayo makes a reference to “Poker Face”, a viral track by Lady Gaga which released on September 23rd, 2008.\n\nCan’t read my, can’t read my\nNo, he can’t read my poker face\n\nAdditionally, having a poker face, refers to a person expressing a face with no emotions, which Kayo seems to allude to.", "annotation_id": "36360002", "url": "https://genius.com/36360002", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "YEET", "line": "We in Chanel with a honeybun", "vault_lines": ["We in Chanel with a honeybun"], "meaning": "Honeybun is a term for $100k, which is also referred to as 100 Bandz / Bands; i.e. A Hundred Bandz. That phrase is then abbreviated to “Honeybun.”", "annotation_id": "30391390", "url": "https://genius.com/30391390", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "YEET", "line": "All of my diamonds, they flooded, from Elliante, bitch I turn up for sure", "vault_lines": ["All of my diamonds, they flooded, from Elliante, bitch I turn up for sure"], "meaning": "Yeat explains how his Elliante diamonds are ‘flooded’. This refers to the common slang in calling chains/jewelry ‘ice’ and that their flooded from the excessive amount of show.\n\nElliante is a luxury brand that specialises in Jewelry and accessories. Yeat often mentions Elliante, seen in his 5 song of his album ‘4L’, ‘Goin back 2 Ella’", "annotation_id": "29833929", "url": "https://genius.com/29833929", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "YEET", "line": "I be as high as the God, as the fiends, bitch, and I put that on every mom", "vault_lines": ["I be as high as the God, as the fiends, bitch, and I put that on every mom"], "meaning": "Yeat makes the claim that he is “as high as the god, as the fiends”, high referring to the state of mind one is induced into after smoking (typically) marijuana. He makes the allusion to God because, in all monotheistic religions, God is considered to reside in heaven, which is a location where those who repented during life go when they pass away. Although not confirmed, many believe heaven to be far beyond the skies and unattainable by human beings on Earth. So Yeat is essentially exclaiming that he is so high that he is on the same level as God, who would be on an astronomically high plane. Rather than simply putting that statement upon his own mother, which is a common phraseology used when someone is emphasizing the seriousness of their words, he puts that on everyone’s mother to make sure none mistake how high he truly is.\nYeat also mentions being as high as the Gods in another song, Talk 2 God, off of his widely popular album 4L, in which he states:\n\n“Yeah, bitch told me she love God, I’m high with the gods…”\n\nA visual interpretation of heaven:", "annotation_id": "25102852", "url": "https://genius.com/25102852", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "YEET", "line": "Me, Yeat, I’m he", "vault_lines": ["Me, Yeat, I'm he"], "meaning": "He is Yeat", "annotation_id": "25042295", "url": "https://genius.com/25042295", "state": "pending", "votes": 67, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "YEET", "line": "Yeat, me, diamonds, flooded on me Bad thotties, pull up, uh, on me", "vault_lines": ["Yeat, me, diamonds, flooded on me"], "meaning": "In Yeat’s unreleased track for his next upcoming album, “Outsidë” he uses the same flow tecnique used in the track.\n\nRollie flooded, diamonds flawless\nBad thotties, big bodies", "annotation_id": "25001750", "url": "https://genius.com/25001750", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "YEET", "line": "I went and just flooded my rings, I blew up, they call me Osama son", "vault_lines": ["I went and just flooded my rings, I blew up, they call me Osama son"], "meaning": "Osama Bin Laden is a terrorist that is most well known for the attacks that occurred on September 11, 2001, where the New York twin towers were destroyed after airplanes crashed into them. “Blowing up” is also a slang term used to describe a quick rise in popularity.\n\nYeat compares the September 11th attacks, credited to being done by Osama Bin Laden, to his quick, sudden rise throughout the music industry.\n\nYeat has also referenced Osama Bin Laden various times in his songs before, an example being on his October 2021 song “All of It,” featuring Yung Kayo:\n\nI was serving bags then blew up like I’m Osama (Boom)", "annotation_id": "25000715", "url": "https://genius.com/25000715", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "YEET", "line": "I got the knit, it’s on top of the Yves Laurent", "vault_lines": ["I got the knit, it's on top of the Yves Laurent"], "meaning": "Kayo is most likely referring to wearing a high quality knit sweater on top of a classic Yves Saint Laurent button up.", "annotation_id": "24997474", "url": "https://genius.com/24997474", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
