{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Xtra Krazy", "line": "I mix that Number (N)ine up with that Louis (Woo, I mix that Number (N)ine up with that Louis, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I mix that Number (N)ine up with that Louis (Woo, I mix that Number (N)ine up with that Louis, yeah)"], "meaning": "Number (N)ine is a clothing brand simillarly to Louis Vuitton. Yeat is saying he styled both brands into his outfit.", "annotation_id": "28772499", "url": "https://genius.com/28772499", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Xtra Krazy", "line": "We the hottest rappers out, so they call us Jacuzzi", "vault_lines": ["We the hottest rappers out, so they call us Jacuzzi"], "meaning": "The term “hot” used in this context means good or the best or poppin'. People call him and Yeat the hottest pretty much saying they’re the greatest rappers out here.\n\nA Jacuzzi is a term is used to describe a hot tub which is why “they” would call Yeat and SeptembersRich a Jacuzzi.", "annotation_id": "28772461", "url": "https://genius.com/28772461", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Xtra Krazy", "line": "We ’bout to Eternal Atake everything that you got with the Uzi", "vault_lines": ["We 'bout to Eternal Atake everything that you got with the Uzi"], "meaning": "Eternal Atake is an album made by Lil Uzi Vert, Eternal Atake is a play on words of “Take everything” if you hear correctly.\n\nBoth Yeat and SeptembersRich have clearly been inspired by Uzi, as demonstrated by the various mentions of Lil Uzi in both their solo and collaborated tracks. For example, Yeat mentions Uzi on his track, “X ta C”\n\nI feel like Lil Uzi, you heard what I said, lil' bitch\n\nAnd interpolates him again on his breakout hit “Money Twërk”.\n\nMy twizzy gon' lose it, pull out the lil' Uzi\n\nLil Uzi spoke on a call with influencer and streamer Adin Ross about his opinions on Yeat’s album, “2 Alivë”.\nUzi and Yeat have three collaborations together which were teased to drop on the deluxe version of the album, however they did not end up on it.", "annotation_id": "25339390", "url": "https://genius.com/25339390", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
