{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "WΤw?? [Duplicate]", "line": "Floats", "vault_lines": ["Like I told you I be high with the floats"], "meaning": "Floats — more than likely one of Yeat’s made-up words that he hasn’t revealed yet.\n\nOther phrases made up by Yeat:\nTwizzy — a friend or accomplice\nLuh — shortened version of little by only keeping “li”\nTonka — a larger vehicle\nGeeky — an intoxicated individual\nHoneybun — a large amount of money\nFloats — probably another word for friend", "annotation_id": "29074677", "url": "https://genius.com/29074677", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "WΤw?? [Duplicate]", "line": "Worried ’bout that shit, worried ’bout the pint", "vault_lines": ["I got long money, yeah"], "meaning": "His drug addiction is so bad that the only thing that concerns him is his drug addiction;\nPint referring to Lean, usually sold in pint bottles from pharmacies, hence the name.", "annotation_id": "29063961", "url": "https://genius.com/29063961", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "WΤw?? [Duplicate]", "line": "I had a plain jane, before I buss it up", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I had a plain jane, before I buss it up"], "meaning": "Plain jane is slang for a standard watch with no diamonds, hes explaining the journey and how his watches reflect that, and now he has more money he can afford to waste money on aftermarket diamonds", "annotation_id": "29063937", "url": "https://genius.com/29063937", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
