{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Wtw", "line": "Yeah, my pockets swollen, yeah, money tall as God", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, my pockets swollen, yeah, money tall as God"], "meaning": "When yeat says that his pockets are “swollen” he is essentially saying that there are large amounts of money in his pockets.\n\nWhen he says that his money is “tall as god” he is saying that when his money is stacked up it goes all the way up to heaven and above god or, in other words, his money is “tall as god.”", "annotation_id": "28265613", "url": "https://genius.com/28265613", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
