{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Wonky", "line": "I ain’t talkin’ ’bout no Newport, know Twizz keep a SIG", "vault_lines": ["I ain't talkin' 'bout no Newport, know Twizz keep a SIG"], "meaning": "SIG is short for “Sig Sauer” a manufacturer that produces handguns. In this line, “SIG” is a play on words with “cig,” short for cigarette. Newport is a brand of cigarette.", "annotation_id": "29555046", "url": "https://genius.com/29555046", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Wonky", "line": "No, we not a band but play the drums like it’s the eighties", "vault_lines": ["No, we not a band but play the drums like it's the eighties"], "meaning": "A drum magazine is a type of magazine for guns which hold rounds in a cylindrical shape, similar to a drum. Therefore, Yeat uses “play the drums” to mean firing off rounds. So the phrase both means to shoot a gun, and literally play the drums instrument.\n\nNote the end of the bar, which says “like it’s the eighties,” when rock bands with heavy and fast drums were very mainstream. Yeat consciously took this into consideration while writing this bar, using it to emphasize the amount of shooting taking place.", "annotation_id": "29535093", "url": "https://genius.com/29535093", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Wonky", "line": "Nowadays I cut ’em off (Cut ’em off), my only friend I got is Benjamin", "vault_lines": ["Nowadays I cut 'em off (Cut 'em off), my only friend I got is Benjamin"], "meaning": "Benjamin Franklin is on the $100 bill, so Yeat is saying now he has a lot of money rather than friends, whom he cut off so that he could focus on making money.", "annotation_id": "29534922", "url": "https://genius.com/29534922", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Wonky", "line": "No bullshit, I think I’m getting addicted, 30's start to feel like 10's", "vault_lines": ["No bullshit, I think I'm getting addicted, 30's start to feel like 10's"], "meaning": "Noah Olivier Smith is saying that he is so addicted to percs, he has built up a tolerance to them. This results in 30 mg percs feeling like 10 mg  to him.", "annotation_id": "29534916", "url": "https://genius.com/29534916", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Wonky", "line": "I feel like I’m ISIS with the beats and with the coupes, I cut the head off (Head off)", "vault_lines": ["I feel like I'm ISIS with the beats and with the coupes, I cut the head off (Head off)"], "meaning": "ISIS is a terrorist organization who gained notoriety from posting videos of them cutting peoples heads off. They have also been known to use this as a form of execution.\n\nYeat is saying that with these beats, he kills them (by cutting their head off)\n\nAs well as implying that he takes the top off of his cars, aka a convertible. Often being seen as a sign of importance.", "annotation_id": "29478602", "url": "https://genius.com/29478602", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
