{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Woa...!", "line": "Woah, fuck the law, fuck your money I got all them honey bunnies (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Woah, fuck the law, fuck your money, I got all them honey bunnies (Yeah)"], "meaning": "A “honey bun” is a term that Yeat evolved in the music rap scene and clarified it meant $100,000. It came to notice through an Instagram DM, where a fan asked him about the price for a feature, to which Yeat responded:\n\n85 höneybunzzz\n\n\n\nPictured: DMs with Yeat saying “honey buns.”\n\nThis hasn’t been the first time Yeat exploited the use of the word, to which he did in his October 2021 track “Sick”:\n\nBitch, I’m sick and I’m still countin' hundreds, honeybuns\nBitch, I’m sick and I’m still countin' hundreds, still ain’t done", "annotation_id": "27895527", "url": "https://genius.com/27895527", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Woa...!", "line": "Whole lotta fuckin’ money, just to swim in it, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Whole lotta fuckin' money, just to swim in it, yeah"], "meaning": "He says that since he has a lot of money, he can convert it into bills (presumably) and swim in it. The “Money pool” is usually used in TV shows to indicate a large amount of money.\n\n)", "annotation_id": "27894670", "url": "https://genius.com/27894670", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
