{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "What I Want", "line": "Yeah, put it in a bowl and then I fucking mix", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, put it in a bowl and then I fucking mix"], "meaning": "Yeat could be talking about a bowl of cereal as in an interview with Channel 5 with Andrew Callagan during the 2022 Chicago Rap Festival Yeat mentioned that his favourite food was frosted flakes and that he eats “like 13, 14” bowls per day.\n\nKellogg’s Frosted Flakes are a popular breakfast cereal consisting of toasted corn flakes coated in sugar.", "annotation_id": "39170969", "url": "https://genius.com/39170969", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "What I Want", "line": "I can shoot it blindfolded, still come out on top, uh", "vault_lines": ["I can shoot it blindfolded, still come out on top, uh"], "meaning": "Regardless of what Yeat does, or how he does something he still suceeds.", "annotation_id": "39170961", "url": "https://genius.com/39170961", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "What I Want", "line": "I could drop an album, sell it all and call it burglary", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I could drop an album, sell it all and call it burglary"], "meaning": "Yeat exaggerates his dominance by implying his success feels like “stealing” from the industry. This line reinforces his confidence while also framing his impact as disruptive, positioning himself above competition.", "annotation_id": "39149217", "url": "https://genius.com/39149217", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "What I Want", "line": "Every time my demons call my phone, you know it’s lurin’ me", "vault_lines": ["Every time my demons call my phone, you know it's lurin' me"], "meaning": "Yeat personifies his inner struggles as “demons,” suggesting they are persistent and intrusive. The idea of them “calling” him implies temptation is constant, reinforcing that his lifestyle isn’t fully under his control despite what he claims.", "annotation_id": "39149198", "url": "https://genius.com/39149198", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "What I Want", "line": "I just do the fuck I want when the fuck I want", "vault_lines": ["I just do the fuck I want when the fuck I want"], "meaning": "Yeat presents absolute freedom as the ultimate goal, suggesting he operates without limits or restrictions. However, within the context of ADL, this freedom feels less like control and more like impulsivity, where his actions are driven by desire rather than intention.", "annotation_id": "39149190", "url": "https://genius.com/39149190", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
