{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "What I Want", "line": "Went from thirteen to thirty-two to seventy, uh This gon’ hit one hundred forty ’cause it’s heavenly, yeah And the next one’ll go two-eighty ’cause it’s meant for me, mm", "vault_lines": ["Wеnt from thirteen to thirty-two to seventy, uh"], "meaning": "While the song was originally teased in late February 2023 (after the release of AftërLyfe), Yeat seemingly revisited this song after the release of 2093. In these set of lines, he brags about his continuous increase in sales, as 2 Alivë sold around 32k units and 2093 had sold close to 70k units. He uses this common trend of increase in sales to predict his next albums doing around 150k and 300k units respectively.", "annotation_id": "39143330", "url": "https://genius.com/39143330", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "What I Want", "line": "Heard your album flopped, uh, yeah, uh (BNYX)", "vault_lines": ["Heard your album flopped, uh, yeah, uh (BNYX)"], "meaning": "working on dying tag. WOD is a music production collective with many major producers such as f1lthy, bnyx, and more, many of which have worked with yeat in the past", "annotation_id": "30555901", "url": "https://genius.com/30555901", "state": "pending", "votes": -19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
