{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Went Wrong", "line": "Came inside and ripped up all your posters (All your posters, all your posters)", "vault_lines": ["Came inside and ripped up all your posters (All your posters, all your posters)"], "meaning": "Posters are usually something that is hanged on the wall and display something of value ,like an idol or someone you look up to.\nThe line might mean that in the destroyed house (a.k.a. the relationship), there is no point in keeping a reminder of the person youŗe no longer with.\nRipping posters -> Trying to forget the past.", "annotation_id": "39156326", "url": "https://genius.com/39156326", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Went Wrong", "line": "[Chorus: Yeat & 070 Shake] Oh, we was waitin’ (Oh, oh) To see where we went wrong Watch us fail Like we didn’t exist (Heartbeat all gone, my heartbeat burnin’ down) Like we didn’t exist (My heartbeat burnin’ down, my heartbeat burnin’ down) Like we didn’t ex— (My—)", "vault_lines": ["Like we didn't exist (Heartbeat all gone, my heartbeat burnin’ down)"], "meaning": "In 2021, Symone Ryley (Instagram influencer/model, @symonery, also known for her clothing brand Sync by Symone) and Yeat went public with their relationship in 2021.\n\nThey were together for several years until late 2024 (around December) when they broke up.\n\nSymone has stated they remained on good terms, stayed friends, and there was no bad blood.\n\nHis heartbreak is probably about Symone.", "annotation_id": "39151006", "url": "https://genius.com/39151006", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Went Wrong", "line": "[Chorus: Yeat & 070 Shake] Oh, we was waitin’ (Oh, oh) To see where we went wrong Watch us fail Like we didn’t exist (Heartbeat all gone, my heartbeat burnin’ down) Like we didn’t exist (My heartbeat burnin’ down, my heartbeat burnin’ down) Like we didn’t ex— (My—)", "vault_lines": ["Like we didn't exist (Heartbeat all gone, my heartbeat burnin’ down)"], "meaning": "In 2021, Symone Ryley (Instagram influencer/model, @symonery, also known for her clothing brand Sync by Symone) and Yeat went public with their relationship in 2021.\n\nThey were together for several years until late 2024 (around December) when they broke up.\n\nSymone has stated they remained on good terms, stayed friends, and there was no bad blood.\n\nHis heartbreak is probably about Symone.", "annotation_id": "39150993", "url": "https://genius.com/39150993", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Went Wrong", "line": "I need it, for God to show me where it is not needed", "vault_lines": ["I need it, for God to show me where it is not needed"], "meaning": "Yeat expresses internal conflict by wanting something while also questioning whether he actually needs it. By asking God to show him where it’s “not needed,” he reveals uncertainty and dependence, suggesting he can’t distinguish between what he wants and what’s harmful.", "annotation_id": "39149444", "url": "https://genius.com/39149444", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Went Wrong", "line": "I think I need a witness", "vault_lines": ["I think I need a witness"], "meaning": "Yeat expresses uncertainty about his own perception, suggesting he needs external confirmation to understand what went wrong. This reflects confusion and lack of clarity in the aftermath of the relationship.", "annotation_id": "39149432", "url": "https://genius.com/39149432", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Went Wrong", "line": "Who came to my house and just destroyed it? (Just destroyed it, just destroyed it)", "vault_lines": ["Who came to my house and just destroyed it? (Just destroyed it, just destroyed it)"], "meaning": "The “house” can symbolize a relationship or emotional space. Its destruction reflects the aftermath of instability and conflict, tying back to earlier imagery like “Dangerous House,” where the environment itself was already unsafe.", "annotation_id": "39149427", "url": "https://genius.com/39149427", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Went Wrong", "line": "Rainin’ down on our bodies, do you feel it?", "vault_lines": ["Rainin’ down on our bodies, do you feel it?"], "meaning": "The imagery creates a moment of intensity and emotion, contrasting with his usual detachment. It suggests a fleeting connection, where feeling exists but isn’t sustained.", "annotation_id": "39149421", "url": "https://genius.com/39149421", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Went Wrong", "line": "I got a new girl every time on the road, I’m in here", "vault_lines": ["I got a new girl every time on the road, I’m in here"], "meaning": "Yeat indirectly admits his role in the relationship’s failure. Constantly moving on to new partners shows a lack of commitment, highlighting how his lifestyle prevents stability.", "annotation_id": "39149415", "url": "https://genius.com/39149415", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Went Wrong", "line": "Miss me with all the bullshit, with all the bullshit Yeah, you could miss me I’ve been outside the city, with bad bitches toppin’ me", "vault_lines": ["Miss me with all the bullshit, with all the bullshit"], "meaning": "Yeat is referring to the “bullshit” of real love, as he feels at this point, it doesn’t even exist, and instead of trying to find it, he now just relies on going from woman to woman.", "annotation_id": "39144277", "url": "https://genius.com/39144277", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Went Wrong", "line": "Oh (Where), where did we go wrong? Where did we? (Where, where, where, where?) (What doin’? Yeah) Girl, I knew it all along, oh, ooh (Yeah, ooh) [Chorus: Yeat & 070 Shake] Oh, we was waitin’ (Oh, oh) To see where we went wrong Watch us fail Like we didn’t exist (Heartbeat all gone, my heartbeat burnin’ down) Like we didn’t exist (My heartbeat burnin’ down, my heartbeat burnin’ down) Like we didn’t ex— ah (My—)", "vault_lines": ["Like we didn't exist (Heartbeat all gone, my heartbeat burnin’ down)"], "meaning": "Idek what ts is genuinely about but i feel him", "annotation_id": "39143782", "url": "https://genius.com/39143782", "state": "pending", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
