{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Way back", "line": "My money been dancin’, my money been twerkin’, my money slut", "vault_lines": ["My money been dancin', my money been twerkin', my money slut"], "meaning": "Yeat is alluding to a bar in his hit song Monëy so big, off of his debut major-label studio album Up 2 Më..\nOn this track he used the lines:\n\nMy money be twerkin', my money do dances (Woah)\n\nYeat is known for flaunting his money in his music  in unusual ways. Examples of such can include when he claims that his money does flips, his money works-out the gym, his money being big, his money twerking, etc.\n\nThese expressions and unusual lines can be found in multiple songs by Yeat; most notably in Trëndy way, where he uses bars like:\n\nFirst my money twerk, now it’s lifting weights\nMoney in the gym, now it’s heavyweight\n\nHe even has a song dedicated to his frequent references of these terms off of 4L’s “Money Twërk.”\n\nYeat has always referenced money in his music with several unreleased and released records boasting his fortunes in musical formats such as the title, the lyrics, or even the art. For reference, money can be seen in the cover-art of multiple songs such as “Big Trunk” and “Flip.”", "annotation_id": "25485855", "url": "https://genius.com/25485855", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Way back", "line": "Heard you was switchin’ the sides, you criss-cross applesauce, switch on your guys, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Heard you was switchin' the sides, you criss-cross applesauce, switch on your guys, yeah"], "meaning": "A few days before the full song was previewed, Yeat posted the lyric on Instagram:\n\nYall crisscross applesauce switch on ya guys #nothere", "annotation_id": "25475759", "url": "https://genius.com/25475759", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
