{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Watch It", "line": "Know enough", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you'on know enough"], "meaning": "Know Enough. Know Enough. Know Enough. Know Enough. Know Enough. Know Enough. Know Enough.\n\nNoell Uff was a friend of Yeat who he met in the library. Unfortunately in 2013, Mr Uff was swallowed by a sinkhole while studying abroad in Rome. Yeat, over his many careers in astrophysics, pharmoseuticals, and most recently being an inflential audiologist, makes tributes to Noell in his works.\n\nDuring an interview on Fox News in 2015, Yeat announced that he was previously in a romantic relationship with Uff. This shocked the community, who tried to poison his crops afterwards.\n\nThis lyric, “Know enough” is showing that Yeat’s fans certainly know enough about him and his life.\n\nHowever, the lyric has a certain deeper, darker meaning. 6 consonants and 4 vowels. 6 x 4 is 10, widely known to be the largest number. Yeat is showing that he will become Larger Than Large, and join the Freemasons in 2025.", "annotation_id": "29503422", "url": "https://genius.com/29503422", "state": "pending", "votes": -4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Watch It", "line": "’", "vault_lines": ["m goin' up, I'm goin' up"], "meaning": "This apostrophe is a perfect representation of Yeats beautiful spelling and grammar, famously, in Yeat’s early life, he had a 400.0 GPA and was actually accepted into Harvard. This apostrophe connotes his expertise with words in a beautiful manner, whilst also belittling the skills of such Shakespeares and Dickens.", "annotation_id": "29503394", "url": "https://genius.com/29503394", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Watch It", "line": "…", "vault_lines": ["m goin' up, I'm goin' up"], "meaning": "the elispses at the end suggest a sad, apocalyptic Doom awaits Yeat in the afterlife (possibly a reference to his 2023 album Afterlyfe) The three dots symbolise the Father, The Son, and the Holy Ghost. These are the 3 forms of God in the Religion called Christianity. The elipses following the word “Down” imply that he is missing God, to go Down to Hell, ruled by the Devil in Christianity.", "annotation_id": "29503393", "url": "https://genius.com/29503393", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Watch It", "line": "Yeah, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you'on know enough"], "meaning": "using subliminal messaging such as repeating the word “yeah”, yeat is slowly inserting the idea that YES, he is watching Up, and YES, he will soon finish.", "annotation_id": "29503382", "url": "https://genius.com/29503382", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
