{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Watch", "line": "Baguettes on watch", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I got plenty of rock, bitch, I got baguettes on watch"], "meaning": "Baguettes refers to a cut of diamond that resembles a French baguette. The term “Baguettes” has been used by Young Thug, Cardi B, Lil Uzi Vert, 21 Savage, Post Malone, Gunna, Mustard, Smokepurrp, and many more rappers.\n\nIn this line, Yeat refers to his flawless clean-cut diamonds that he has on his watch.", "annotation_id": "32687806", "url": "https://genius.com/32687806", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Watch", "line": "Lil’ bitch, you best know that I’m havin’ racks", "vault_lines": ["Lil' bitch, you best know that I'm havin' racks"], "meaning": "As you can see the lyric is pretty self-explanatory but if you still need assistance, “Lil' bitch, you best know what I’m havin', racks” Yeat most definitely, is staying with them “racks” also known as money and a lot of it. He had to let his “bitch” know that.", "annotation_id": "29909400", "url": "https://genius.com/29909400", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Watch", "line": "I pull up, an arm and a hand, I pull up, an arm and a hand", "vault_lines": ["I pull up, an arm and a hand, I pull up, an arm and a hand"], "meaning": "A play on words for the saying “Costs an arm and a leg.” meaning it’s very expensive to the average person.", "annotation_id": "29635794", "url": "https://genius.com/29635794", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Watch", "line": "Don’t fuck with the gang, bitch, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Don't fuck with the gang, bitch, yeah"], "meaning": "Don’t fuck with the gang. He is saying if you mess around as in try to fight yeat’s gang, he will kill you, or have his gang and twizzies shoot you up.", "annotation_id": "29635765", "url": "https://genius.com/29635765", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Watch", "line": "I got the gun with the lock", "vault_lines": ["I got the gun with the lock"], "meaning": "Could be referring to a switch as it locks in place like a lego piece, also could be how glock’s font has the G being a lock which plays into the idea of it being a switch as glocks are converted into switches primarily due to their slide mechanism", "annotation_id": "29251757", "url": "https://genius.com/29251757", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Watch", "line": "Bitch, I’m as high as a crane", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm as high as a crane"], "meaning": "The use of the simile refers to Yeat getting high of drugs. He uses a simile to compare how high he is, to a crane used in construction.", "annotation_id": "27936313", "url": "https://genius.com/27936313", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
