{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Wat it feel lykë", "line": "I’m working on dying", "vault_lines": ["Uh, everything 'bout this shit come down to real life"], "meaning": "This is the producer tag for the Philadelphia-based collective Working On Dying. This track’s producer, BNYX, is one of the group’s best known members, The collective produced songs for the likes of Lil Uzi Vert, Matt Ox, Yeat, Drake, Bladee, and CHXPO.\n\nMembers of Working On Dying are, Brandon Finessin, BNYX, F1lthy, The Loosie Man, ilykimchi, Oogie Mane, Jarek, and FAXXONLY. Former member is Forza.", "annotation_id": "26779905", "url": "https://genius.com/26779905", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Wat it feel lykë", "line": "Yeah, I got a blick with a tooth and it bite down back (Ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I got a blick with a tooth and it bite down back (Ayy)"], "meaning": "The slang word “blick” or “blicky” alludes to a handgun, and originates from New York. Yeat has previously mentioned a “blick” on earlier tracks such as his February 2022 track “Rëal six,” on which he raps:\n\nI pull up, we turn up a notch, we turning it sick\nRide ‘round that bitch with a, yeah, blick\n\nA “blick with a teeth” refers to the trigger on a handgun. Furthermore, for it to “bite down back” means it has been fired–as well as asserting to the firearm’s “violent” impact on an individual.", "annotation_id": "26688152", "url": "https://genius.com/26688152", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Wat it feel lykë", "line": "I wanna flood my Red’ like I went and flooded the coupe, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I wanna flood my Red' like I went and flooded the coupe, yeah"], "meaning": "Redeye is a term the car manufacturer Dodge uses to describe their high-end vehicles with extra horsepower. The phrase is often used to reference their Challenger Hellcat Redeye Widebody, which costs upward of $82,430. In this case, Yeat uses the term “flooded” to describe how he maxed out and personally customized the luxury Redeye vehicle.\n\n\n\nPictured: The 2022 Dodge Challenger SRT Hellcat Redeye Widebody", "annotation_id": "26230573", "url": "https://genius.com/26230573", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Wat it feel lykë", "line": "Yeah, tell me what it feel like", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, tell me what it feel like"], "meaning": "This song was played during the 1017 ALYX 9SM SS23 runway show on 6.17.2022. The day before the show, @alyxstudio posted a screenshot of an audio file titled YEAT ALYX SS23 WAT IT…\n\n\n\nBecause of this lyric, we can assume the full song title will be something along the lines of “Wat it fëel like”", "annotation_id": "26089657", "url": "https://genius.com/26089657", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
