{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Wanna be më*", "line": "Yeah, I was in a basement, I was eatin’ noodles, now I’m on the yacht", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I was in a basement, I was eatin' noodles, now I'm on the yacht"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the song ‘'Twizzy Rich’‘ from Yeat’s third independently-released album, Up 2 Më.\n\nI used to be eating noodle-oodles sittin' in the basement with the roaches in it\n\nYeat also remarked about eating noodles in the basement in the song “All I See” from his fourth studio album, 4L\n\nUsed to eat them noodles in the basement, now it’s steak", "annotation_id": "28484175", "url": "https://genius.com/28484175", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
