{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "WAR 2", "line": "This perc just told me, I’m OD, but I ain’t dyin’ yet", "vault_lines": ["This perc just told me, I'm OD, but I ain't dyin' yet"], "meaning": "OD (also spelled Odee) refers to slang originated in New York which stands for over do, alluding that someone is being extra or doing the most. To OD also means to overdose. A perc is a common drug that can result in an overdose and Yeat is using personification to say the perc is telling him he’s being extra while having the double entendre of the phrase OD", "annotation_id": "30027326", "url": "https://genius.com/30027326", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
