{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "WAR 2", "line": "Yeah, this the last song, you gettin’ till Alivë hit, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, this the last song, you gettin' till Alivë hit, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat expresses to his fans and listeners that this will be the last piece of music that he will be officially releasing until his 2 bonus track 20 track album, Alivë, is released. Featuring many hit songs such as Back2Bed, DiedB4, and the 1st version of this song, ‘War 1’", "annotation_id": "28122031", "url": "https://genius.com/28122031", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "WAR 2", "line": "I lost my bitch, I cut ‘em off myself, I ain’t cryin’", "vault_lines": ["I lost my bitch, I cut 'em off myself, I ain't cryin'"], "meaning": "In this line Yeat is stating that he stopped talking to (aka cut off) his bitch, and he isn’t sad about it.", "annotation_id": "27835935", "url": "https://genius.com/27835935", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "WAR 2", "line": "Yeah, you playin’ like it’s April 1st, bitch It’s April 5th", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you playin' like it's April 1st, bitch It's April 5th"], "meaning": "If someone plays with Yeat or tests him, they would typically give Yeat an excuse to make sure Yeat doesn’t hold a grudge. By saying “ Bitch it’s April 5th he’s saying that your excuse isn’t valid and that he will get revenge.", "annotation_id": "27741794", "url": "https://genius.com/27741794", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "WAR 2", "line": "The X got rid of all my emotions, no more tears", "vault_lines": ["The X got rid of all my emotions, no more tears"], "meaning": "When Yeat takes X or (Ecstasy) he loses his emotions, stripping remorse he has for anyone who opposes him, also preventing him to care or acknowledge the existential dread that comes with being addicted to drugs, knowing that his premature death is inevitable.", "annotation_id": "27741772", "url": "https://genius.com/27741772", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "WAR 2", "status": "done", "targets": 21, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-war-2-lyrics", "genius_title": "WAR 2", "genius_id": 6604795, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "WAR 1", "line": "I understand why you’re hating when you’re a millionaire (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I understand why you're hating when you're a millionaire (Yeah)"], "meaning": "In this context, the line exposes the mental wretchedness of someone who has already won the material game: having reached the economic summit, money ought to confer absolute indifference and the freedom to stop competing with anyone; thus, seeing a millionaire expend energy hating, hindering, or envying those on the way up reveals only deep-seated insecurity, a paranoid fear of being replaced, and an ego so fragile that even limitless resources could not heal it.", "annotation_id": "41387998", "url": "https://genius.com/41387998", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
