{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Up off X", "line": "Up all night ’cause I’m up off X Up all night ’cause I’m up off X (Yeah, yeah) Up all night ’cause I’m up off ecstasy Up all night ’cause I’m up off ecstasy", "vault_lines": ["Up all night 'cause I'm up off ecstasy"], "meaning": "Yeat is referring to the drug ‘ecstasy’, and appears to stay awake all night due to him being influenced by the drug. Ecstasy is known to cause sleep disruption and hallucination.", "annotation_id": "28429512", "url": "https://genius.com/28429512", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Up off X", "line": "Yeah, she gon’ suck it up, she gon’ gulp them kids (What?)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, she gon' suck it up, she gon' gulp them kids (What?)"], "meaning": "Yeat is not conveying that his girlfriend has been consuming children, but sperm. Sperm transforms into a child in the womb during a pregnancy, hence why Yeat called them ‘kids’. Yeat implies that she has been swallowing his sperm after he ejaculates during a sexual practice commonly referred to as ‘head’ or a ‘blowjob’ (BJ)", "annotation_id": "27812772", "url": "https://genius.com/27812772", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
