{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Up From Here", "line": "I went and moved out to state of New York with 5K and a dream on my mind", "vault_lines": ["I went and moved out to state of New York with 5K and a dream on my mind"], "meaning": "Yeat opens up more about his moving to New York from Portland, right after graduating highschool. In his interview with Zach Lowe, he explains this dream as “doing the thing I love and having a roof on top of my head”, and compares it to what he has today.\n\nHe first revealed moving to New York to pursue music in his interview with Our Generation Music, back in 2021.", "annotation_id": "39151527", "url": "https://genius.com/39151527", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Up From Here", "line": "I’m the only one out of my generation changin’ music this time So I got a lot on the line", "vault_lines": ["I'm the only one out of my generation changin' music this time"], "meaning": "King Tonka thinks he has a lot of pressure because he is the only artist of out of his generation to break out and change musically, something he has talked about  in his sit-down interview with Zach Lowe. Yeat said:\n\n“I’m definitely trying to change it up, trying to give the youth some real music, some real art… I think I’m done with the slop, people are done with it too”\n\nFans were quick to point out how he called his work that they loved “slop”, but a lot of people seems to agree with Yeat moving on from that sound and trying to bring more things to the table artistically.", "annotation_id": "39151466", "url": "https://genius.com/39151466", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Up From Here", "line": "Bitch, I’m the purpose general, I provide you with purpose in life", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm the purpose general, I provide you with purpose in life"], "meaning": "Here, Yeat references the first track on ADL “Purpose General” from the first disc A DANGEROUS LYFE, which he confirms he really is the purpose general he had talked about", "annotation_id": "39143219", "url": "https://genius.com/39143219", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
