{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "US", "line": "I took a alien language [?], cause I know these kids gone, but this [?]", "vault_lines": ["I took a alien language [?], cause I know these kids gone, but this [?]"], "meaning": "Yeat stays on theme for the Different Creature 2 tape, by saying he feels like E.T. and speaking alien language.\n\nPhone home is also a reference to what many think E.T. says in the movie, but is a misconception for home phone.'\n\nThe alien language bar could be referring to his song with the same name off of his second mixtape I’m So Me.", "annotation_id": "27547949", "url": "https://genius.com/27547949", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "US", "line": "Shawty think she straight, it’s okay, hop in the G65 with us", "vault_lines": ["Shawty think she straight, it's okay, hop in the G65 with us"], "meaning": "Yeat refers to the inside of his coupe, the “guts”, being neon, or colorful. Lil Uzi Vert’s hit song Neon Guts is what he means by “No Uzi”.", "annotation_id": "27547930", "url": "https://genius.com/27547930", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
