{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "I’m just ridin’ in the Tonka, bitch, I know I’m the shit", "vault_lines": ["I'm just ridin' in the Tonka, bitch, I'm on this shit"], "meaning": "He’s driving his car and is proud of who he is.\n\nYou can hear him say “I know I’m the shit” instead of “I’m on this shit” more clearly in this clip from his live around 3:13:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PmHm-ixmRHY", "annotation_id": "28372604", "url": "https://genius.com/28372604", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "I’m turning up but I’m nodding off", "vault_lines": ["I'm turning up but I'm not alone"], "meaning": "The drugs gave him energy to rage (turning up) but also made him sleepy (nodding off).\n\nYou can hear him more clearly say “nodding off”, instead of “not alone”, on this clip from his live around 4:25:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PmHm-ixmRHY", "annotation_id": "28372474", "url": "https://genius.com/28372474", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "We some real rockstars, it’s a pill, pop all of ’em", "vault_lines": ["We some real rockstars, it's a pill, pop all of 'em"], "meaning": "Yeat commonly uses the word rockstar to refer to people or behaviors who take prescription drugs, usually in the context of pills.", "annotation_id": "28065548", "url": "https://genius.com/28065548", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "He must’ve thought that we was kidding, my twizzy pulled up and just popped him", "vault_lines": ["He must've thought that we was kidding, my twizzy pulled up and just popped him"], "meaning": "Yeat’s rivals thought that he was bluffing about his threats/warnings, and to prove he wasn’t, one of his accomplices, commonly referred to as a “twizzy” by Yeat, showed up and “popped him”. Slang for shooting someone.", "annotation_id": "28065509", "url": "https://genius.com/28065509", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "I could keep goin’ for days but I just gotta chill just so they think that they close to us", "vault_lines": ["I could keep goin' for days but I just gotta chill just so they think that they close to us"], "meaning": "Yeat claims he could continue to keep discrediting his opponents who he talks about frequently in his music, but decides to hold off so they think they’re on good terms with him, which makes sure they don’t plot or try anything against Yeat.", "annotation_id": "28065484", "url": "https://genius.com/28065484", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "Had to go and put some diamonds on my neck so they show me some respect, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Had to go and put some diamonds on my neck so they show me some respect"], "meaning": "Expensive jewelry and gems make their mark in the quite materialistic plane of Yeat’s music, allowing him to garner respect by simply just displaying his wealth and not something with more depth.", "annotation_id": "28065470", "url": "https://genius.com/28065470", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "When you get to the top with the dogs You get to flex all that shit in they face", "vault_lines": ["When you get to the top with the dawgs"], "meaning": "The “dawgs” in this line are either referring to those associated to Yeat and the successes that comes with that connection, or people already big in the rap game. When you “get to the top”, you can brag/“flex” down upon those lesser than you, such as those who haven’t made in yet.", "annotation_id": "28065405", "url": "https://genius.com/28065405", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "Huh, when you rich like this, it feel great, huh When you get a lot of shit on your plate, huh", "vault_lines": ["When you rich like this, it feel great"], "meaning": "Yeat’s level of wealth brings immense gratification, along with the ability to afford much more than presumably before, such as food on your plate.", "annotation_id": "28065399", "url": "https://genius.com/28065399", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
