{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "I got beef with my kidney, he said that we got a problem", "vault_lines": ["I got beef with my kidney, he said that we got a problem"], "meaning": "This is talking about how Yeat takes a lot of drugs and drinks a lot of alcohol, and how it is really affecting his kidneys.", "annotation_id": "26663062", "url": "https://genius.com/26663062", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "I don’t feel the same, no, not at all", "vault_lines": ["I don't feel the sun, no, not at all"], "meaning": "I believe Yeat is implying that because of him wearing a Turban, it blocks the suns rays to his head and he does not feel it. It is commonly worn in warmer areas to protect the wearer from sun rays.", "annotation_id": "25934501", "url": "https://genius.com/25934501", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "Might go hit my garage and pull out the GLE for fun", "vault_lines": ["Might go hit my garage and pull out the GLE for fun"], "meaning": "The Mercedes-Benz AMG GLE coupe is one of the most prestigious luxury and performance-focused SUVs in the market. Yeat currently owns one.\n\nYeat states that he would casually drive his GLE just for fun, referring to the idea that it is not meaningful to him possessing and using expensive vehicles.\n\n\n\nPicture of a Metallic Gray AMG GLE 63 S Coupe.", "annotation_id": "25844098", "url": "https://genius.com/25844098", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "Yeah, I just popped an X pill and half my body glitched", "vault_lines": ["I just popped a X pill and half my body glitched"], "meaning": "Yeat is alluding to Ecstasy, a psychoactive mind-altering drug that can be used to get high. Users of Ecstasy can experience extreme feelings of euphoria and hallucinations. His hallucinations from the pill make him feel like his body is out-of-touch with reality, hence the use of “glitch.”\n\n\n\nVisual representation of a “glitch;” colorful and twitchy sightings.\n\nThis colorful example of a glitch can be similar to what a user of Ecstasy may see.\n\nYeat has mentioned the drug previously in songs such as “X ta C,” which is a song dedicated to his relationship/connection to the drug as the title is the spelled pronunciation of the word “Ecstasy.” In the record he mentioned the drug with lines such as:\n\nShut up baby girl, I want them drugs, you really my Ecstasy", "annotation_id": "25537082", "url": "https://genius.com/25537082", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "Yeah, had to take a break from X, bitch, I could feel it in my chest", "vault_lines": ["Had to take a break from X, bitch, I could feel it in my chest"], "meaning": "Yeat has made his love of ecstasy abundantly clear in his music, making many lyrical references to the drug throughout his songs. He lists it among some of his favorite highs on Gët Busy:\n\nDrank and X, molly with Perc’, that’s my shit (Yeah, yeah)\n\nOn Nvr again, he admits to have “lost the magic” due to his daily use of molly:\n\nI used to go boot off the molly all day, now it don’t even work\n\nHowever, in this bar as well as the one that follows, he is grappling with the inevitable consequences of his excessive drug abuse. Given that MDMA is a potent stimulant that raises heart rate and blood pressure, Yeat may be feeling the strain that his cardiovascular system has been repeatedly subjected to. Additionally, frequent, heavy use of MDMA can potentially cause changes in the heart valves that resemble early cardiac fibrosis, among other kinds of long-term damage to parts of the brain and body. This is likely driven by overstimulation of the 5-HT2B receptor, a type of serotonin receptor that has an important role in regulating heart function and structure, as other 5-HT2B agonists have been associated with cardiac valvulopathy as well.", "annotation_id": "25491657", "url": "https://genius.com/25491657", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "I don’t be savin’ my money, I spend it all day, bitch, I made it all back, yeah, I doubled up", "vault_lines": ["I don't be savin' my money, I spend it all day, bitch, I made it all back, yeah, I doubled up"], "meaning": "In these lines, Yeat is stating that he doesn’t save his money like others do. He tends to spend it all in one setting but make more than what he had spent.", "annotation_id": "25482497", "url": "https://genius.com/25482497", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "I just got the Chrome Heart, mixed it up, then sauced it on", "vault_lines": ["I just got the Chrome Heart, mixed it up, then sauced it on"], "meaning": "Yeat states he acquired some drip from Chrome Hearts, a popular luxury fashion and streetwear brand  founded in 1988 by Richard Stark. Clothing and jewelry from this brand is known for being very expensive, proving that Yeat’s pockets are in fact Shmunkëd", "annotation_id": "25425361", "url": "https://genius.com/25425361", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "Thotty gon’ pull up on me, she gon’ gulp up my dick like a motherfuckin’ 7-Eleven cup", "vault_lines": ["Thotty gon' pull up on me, she gon' gulp up my dick like a motherfuckin' 7-Eleven cup"], "meaning": "Yeat claims that a thot (a hoe) is going to come to his location and give him fellatio and relates it to the action of gulping a Slurpee (a frozen carbonated drink) out of a cup from 7-Eleven (a gas station).\n\nHe could be talking about the Big Gulp cup from 7-Eleven as well.", "annotation_id": "24930963", "url": "https://genius.com/24930963", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "line": "They said that they went and touched the moon, I touched the sun", "vault_lines": ["They said that they went and touched the moon, I touched the sun"], "meaning": "When Yeat heard that somebody(s) went to the moon (Approx. 238,900 miles from the Earth) and touched it, he responded by going to touch the sun (Approx. 91.474 million miles from the Earth). One-upping said person(s) because he strives to be better than everyone at everything.", "annotation_id": "24930920", "url": "https://genius.com/24930920", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U could tëll", "status": "done", "targets": 30, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-u-could-tell-lyrics", "genius_title": "U could tëll", "genius_id": 7175367, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U Should Know", "line": "I know you say you know me, I know you know you think you different", "vault_lines": ["I know you say you know me, I know you know you think you different"], "meaning": "These lyrics are classic Yeat—they sound simple, but there’s a lot of subtext about identity, perception, and ego.\n\nPeople often project a version of him based on fame, image, or past interactions.\n\nThey perceive they know him\nThey perceive they’re different\n\nBut in reality he’s saying: both are illusions\n\nThis leaves his audience in an existential crisis—what is life even?", "annotation_id": "39332726", "url": "https://genius.com/39332726", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U Should Know", "line": "I could help you see, I could help you breathe, I could", "vault_lines": ["I could help you see, I could help you breathe, I could"], "meaning": "Yeat has the ability to change one’s life—through his\nacquisition of wealth, he is able to provide experiences that others simply cannot.", "annotation_id": "39332698", "url": "https://genius.com/39332698", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
