{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U Should Know", "line": "But I don’t give no fucks ’bout nobody but me ’cause I should", "vault_lines": ["But I don't give no fucks 'bout nobody but me 'cause I should"], "meaning": "Throughout this album (2093) yeat talks about how he is selfish and continuing this theme in his song “U Should Know” featured on his 4th studio album “2093” he states.”, “Am I wrong for bein' selfish?\nAm I wrong for puttin' me first?”\nProving that he claims to be selfish and questions himself on his choices. This line could also be a reference to his hit song with Drake named “IDGAF” (I don’t give a fuck) which was featured on Drakes album “For All The Dogs” and was released in October of 2023.", "annotation_id": "30928997", "url": "https://genius.com/30928997", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
