{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "U DONT KNOW LYFE", "line": "Yeah (Yeah), look how they trippin’, they slippin’ up, they only got one leg", "vault_lines": ["Yeah (Yeah), look how they trippin', they slippin' up, they only got one leg"], "meaning": "Yeat is pointing out the vulnerability and instability of his rivals. By saying they “only got one leg,” he implies that they are prone to making mistakes. This suggests that his opponents are at a disadvantage and are unable to keep up with him, highlighting their weakness and his own superiority.", "annotation_id": "33450361", "url": "https://genius.com/33450361", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
