{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tëslas & Rovers", "line": "Yeah, my brother he really been scammin’ a lot, Swiper, no swipin’ (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, my brother he really been scammin' a lot, Swiper, no swipin' (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat’s former affiliate, SeptembersRich, is notorious for scamming; in fact, SeptembersRich admits to scamming across many of his songs.\n\nWoke up, then I scammed some lames, bitch, we too up\n— “YEAH”\nI just made thirty thousand jugging kids on the ‘Gram\n— “Trëndy way (ft. SeptembersRich)”\n\nYeat has also been involved in scamming before he gained popularity, with him also mentioning the unethical act in his past songs:\n\nI scammed myself with diamond rings\nDropped fifteen-hunnid on my feet\nThat’s what got these diamonds dancing\n— “Can’t Think”\n\n\n\nAn exchange between Yeat and a fan allegedly swiping together. Although the validity of the exchange cannot be confirmed, it still provides an insight into both Yeat and SeptembersRich’s business scheme.\n\nYeat later allegedly cut off SeptembersRich from his independent label, TwizzyRich most likely due to him still pursuing scamming.\n\nSwiper, no swiping is a reference to Swiper from the children’s TV show, Dora The Explorer. A swiper is also slang for a person who does online credit card scams in order to gain information that could later be used to withdraw from a bank account that isn’t theirs.", "annotation_id": "25296816", "url": "https://genius.com/25296816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tëslas & Rovers", "line": "Yeah, I put paint on that lil’ bitch’s face, just like my Margiela feets", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I put paint on that lil' bitch's face, just like my Margiela feets"], "meaning": "Yeat makes a reference towards designer brand Maison Margiela and their popular shoe the “Paint Drop”. Stating that he’ll put paint on the women’s face, referring to ejaculation.", "annotation_id": "25263792", "url": "https://genius.com/25263792", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tëslas & Rovers", "line": "I’m still rich, but I been shippin’ kale", "vault_lines": ["I'm still rich, but I been shippin' kale"], "meaning": "“Shipping kale” (or to “ship kale”) means to sell/deal marijuana. Yeat is saying that regardless of his status (and fame) because of his success as a rapper, he still is selling drugs.", "annotation_id": "25064944", "url": "https://genius.com/25064944", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tëslas & Rovers", "line": "We turn them boys into soup, soup, mhm We’ll never tell you the truth, mhm", "vault_lines": ["We turn them boys into soup, soup, mhm"], "meaning": "Here, “turned into soup” is slang for murder. Yeat and his crew eliminated their opposition.\n\nNo one involved will tell anyone about the crime they committed.\n\nYeat is following up from the previous bar where he used food (ice cream) as an adjective for his jewelry. He’s created a pattern of this by using “soup” to describe the condition of his opposition after they pull up on them.", "annotation_id": "24640539", "url": "https://genius.com/24640539", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tëslas & Rovers", "line": "Yeah, chain made of ice cream I scoop, scoop, mhm", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, chain made of ice cream I scoop, scoop, mhm"], "meaning": "Yeat is using “ice cream” as an adjective for his chain, which is slang for diamonds, or another stone that glistens and shines similar to frozen ice cream.\n\nThis slang was popularized by Chief Keef, in his track “Ice Cream” produced by Young Chop in 2018.", "annotation_id": "24640537", "url": "https://genius.com/24640537", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tëslas & Rovers", "line": "Yeah, we going up to the top, so they wanna copy", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we going up to the top, so they wanna copy"], "meaning": "Yeat has a somewhat unique sound, especially in his vocals and choice of instrumentals that he pairs with them.\n\nHe’s been rapidly gaining popularity in the past year, and because of that, he’s noticed other artists mimicking his formula in an attempt to get their music recognized like his.", "annotation_id": "24640535", "url": "https://genius.com/24640535", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tëslas & Rovers", "line": "I’m on Mars, I’m on a rover (Come on, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm on Mars, I'm on a rover (Come on, yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat is creating a double-meaning of the term “high”, by using the metaphor of “being on Mars” to describe how high he is. While on “Mars” (his drug experience), he finds a Mars rover (referencing the rovers that the US placed on Mars to collect data).\n\nThis is a double-meaning stemming from the previous bar about Tesla Inc. The CEO of Tesla Inc., Elon Musk, also is the CEO of SpaceX, who is known for taking massive steps towards the expansion of human civilization onto Mars.", "annotation_id": "24640456", "url": "https://genius.com/24640456", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tëslas & Rovers", "line": "Yeah, chain made of ice cream I scoop, scoop, mhm", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, chain made of ice cream I scoop, scoop, mhm"], "meaning": "Yeat is using “ice cream” as an adjective for his chain, which is slang for diamonds, or another stone that glistens and shines similar to frozen ice cream.\n\nThis slang was popularized by Chief Keef, in his track “Ice Cream” produced by Young Chop in 2018.", "annotation_id": "24640362", "url": "https://genius.com/24640362", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tëslas & Rovers", "line": "Yeah, I see y’all smokin’ rocks, y’all smokin’ boulders (Crap, uh-huh)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I see y'all smokin' rocks, y'all smokin' boulders (Crap, uh-huh)"], "meaning": "True cannabis connoisseurs are aware of the controversy behind “moonrocks”, a product created by manufacturers in which a cannabis flower (historically Girl Scout Cookies) is dipped or sprayed with concentrates, and then rolled in kief.\n\nThe debate is that most moonrocks are low quality. Moonrocks may seem exciting to the new, unexperienced, and enthusiastic consumer, BUT, ESPECIALLY when buying black market moonrocks, more often than not, moonrocks are just a way for the manufacturer to get rid of some old stock. Since the consumer is (mostly) unable to see the original flower being used inside of the moonrock, they can get away with using a lower quality, less appealing flower, and covering it in a (usually) low quality THC oil concentrate, sourced from God knows what grow (trim is used to make most THC distillates, which is usually the oil you’ll find in black market moonrocks).\n\n“Boulders” are a synonym of “rocks”.", "annotation_id": "24640253", "url": "https://genius.com/24640253", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tëslas & Rovers", "line": "I watched y’all copy how I sound, bitch, y’all some parakeets (Ooh, ah)", "vault_lines": ["I watched y'all copy how I sound, bitch, y'all some parakeets (Ooh, ah)"], "meaning": "Yeat compares his competitors to parekkets; who are known for repeating speech; yeat is effectively saying that his competition is constantly copying him and unable to make their own content.", "annotation_id": "24623822", "url": "https://genius.com/24623822", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tëslas & Rovers", "line": "I fell in love with the yerky (Ooh, ah, ha) No, y’all not fly, y’all a turkey (Ha)", "vault_lines": ["I fell in love with the yerky (Ooh, ah, ha)"], "meaning": "“Yerkie” is slang term for the posterior of a curvy woman\nYeat fell in love with a curvy woman\n\nIn the second part, Yeat compares the listener to a turkey, which is a flightless bird, thereby calling the listener (or opp) NOT fly\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: Yerky means percs in Twizzy Language\n\nDue to the important Twizzy language lesson (thanks), this bar seems to have double meaning", "annotation_id": "24623811", "url": "https://genius.com/24623811", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tëslas & Rovers", "line": "Bitch, I’m in a 911 coupe (A coupe, mhm) Bitch, I’m in a 911 coupe (That coupe, mhm) Bitch, I’m in a 911 coupe (It’s true, mhm) (I blow up) Bitch, I’m in a 911 coupe (It’s true, mhm) (I show up) Bitch, I’m in a 911 coupe (It’s true, mhm)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm in a 911 coupe (A coupe, mhm)"], "meaning": "Yeat is talking about being in a 911 Carrera which is a fast luxurious and expensive sports car sold by German car manufacturer Porsche.", "annotation_id": "23696087", "url": "https://genius.com/23696087", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
