{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Type monëy", "line": "I was just swervin’ the motherfuckin’ Tonk’", "vault_lines": ["I was just swervin' the motherfuckin' Tonk'"], "meaning": "With Tonk' he means Tonka. Luxury SUV. Trackhawk, durango, X6, GLE63", "annotation_id": "28464251", "url": "https://genius.com/28464251", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Type monëy", "line": "Yeah, seven-seven-seven, send ‘em to heaven, I’m talkin’ to God, bitch (Phew)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, seven-seven-seven, send 'em to heaven, I'm talkin' to God, bitch (Phew)"], "meaning": "Thats just Yeat boasting about his power and potential to send his enemies to heaven while communicating with God. The use of the phrase “seven-seven-seven” is likely a reference to the biblical number 777, which is often associated with good luck and spiritual perfection.\n\nThis is a reference to John Ross’s clothing line (Seventh Heaven) and record label (sevensevenseven). Yeats 2022 single “Hollon” was released by Ross’s label.", "annotation_id": "28464250", "url": "https://genius.com/28464250", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Type monëy", "line": "Yeah, you blurred, bitch, yeah (Bang, bang)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I got snipers aimin' down at your head (Bang, bang), yeah, you blurred, bitch, yeah (Bang, bang)"], "meaning": "“You are blurred” means that you have been shot and filmed. This is probably referring to gore videos, since most of them are blurred in the news.", "annotation_id": "28464246", "url": "https://genius.com/28464246", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Type monëy", "line": "Yeah, I’m poppin’ the motherfuckin’ X", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I'm poppin' the motherfuckin' X"], "meaning": "This lyric contains drug references, specifically to the drug ecstasy (often abbreviated as “X”). The phrase “poppin' the muhfuckin' X” likely refers to ingesting the drug in pill form.", "annotation_id": "28464244", "url": "https://genius.com/28464244", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Type monëy", "line": "One, two, three, four shots leave him dead (He dead) 5.56, big bullets to the head", "vault_lines": [", big bullets to the head (Woo, woo)"], "meaning": "In these lines, Yeat is actually counting. He begins the number sequence by describing the amount of times he has shot someone before they died, ending at 4. However, the next line begins with “.556” which not only describes the bullets he used, but also cleverly continues the counting because 5 and 6 come after 4.", "annotation_id": "28363055", "url": "https://genius.com/28363055", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Type monëy", "line": "Yeah, I got snipers aimin’ down at your head", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I got snipers aimin' down at your head"], "meaning": "This might be a nod to the og song where the beat comes from, “Sniper” prod by Opium Jai, the beat interlopes wt this one so could be it, iunno tho this mf sometimes js say stuff too. shit’s still fire tho.", "annotation_id": "28225913", "url": "https://genius.com/28225913", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Type monëy", "line": "5.56", "vault_lines": ["5.56, big bullets to the head"], "meaning": "The 5.56×45mm NATO (official NATO nomenclature 5.56 NATO, but often pronounced “five-five-six”) is a rimless bottlenecked intermediate cartridge family developed in the late 1970s in Belgium by FN Herstal.\n\nThis cartridge is commonly used by firearms like M16 rifles, or semi-automatic AR-15 rifles.", "annotation_id": "28071826", "url": "https://genius.com/28071826", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Type monëy", "line": "Back in the trap with no sign of a hearse", "vault_lines": ["Back in the trap with no sign of a hearse"], "meaning": "A hearse is a vehicle used to carry coffins containing a dead person.\n\nIf there’s no sign of a hearse, then there’s no sign that someone is dead.\n\nThis line could have two meanings:\n\n1) He is respected in his “trap” and no one will attempt to kill him\n\n2) His career is flourishing and won’t die anytime soon", "annotation_id": "27940567", "url": "https://genius.com/27940567", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
