{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Type monëy", "line": "I’m a big star, call the astronomers", "vault_lines": ["I'm a big star, call the astronomers"], "meaning": "Yeat boasts about his cele status, suggesting they are a “big star” worthy of being studied by astronomers (who study “stars” scientifically). This line highlights the theme of self-aggrandizement present throughout the song, as the speaker flaunts their wealth and success.", "annotation_id": "27893743", "url": "https://genius.com/27893743", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Type monëy", "line": "I got dirty money buried in dirt, type of money, put that boy on a shirt (Shirt, shirt)", "vault_lines": ["I got dirty money buried in dirt, type of money, put that boy on a shirt (Shirt, shirt)"], "meaning": "Yeat is describing the illegal and “dirty” nature of his money, which he has buried in the ground to hide it from authorities. “put on a shirt” means to be murdered. It comes from the tradition of memorial shirts made in honor of the deceased.", "annotation_id": "27893728", "url": "https://genius.com/27893728", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
