{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "I could tell real from the fake, we just be having abundance", "vault_lines": ["I could tell real from the fake, we just be having abundance"], "meaning": "His climb to fame meant he met a lot of fake people ‘we just be having abundance’\n\nAnd then learnt the skill of discerning the real from the fake because of it", "annotation_id": "36966061", "url": "https://genius.com/36966061", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "Diamonds on big-boy water, got these bitches straight out the well, uh", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds on big-boy water, got these bitches straight out the well, uh"], "meaning": "in gemstones like diamonds, ‘first water’  means its the highest quality, as in it’s clear like water\n\nSaying its ‘out the well’ implies he got them directly from the source", "annotation_id": "36966009", "url": "https://genius.com/36966009", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "You don’t got no money but you judging, call you Judy", "vault_lines": ["You don't got no money but you judging, call you Judy"], "meaning": "Within this lyric, the artist Yeat articulates a pointed censure against the hypocrisy of his detractors, who, despite their own precarious and unsound financial circumstances, audaciously presume to level criticism against him. This indictment is then masterfully punctuated by an allusion to the esteemed television jurist Judge Judy, thereby couching his rebuke within the framework of a popular courtroom spectacle and lending a tone of authoritative, yet ironic, finality to his retort.", "annotation_id": "36897375", "url": "https://genius.com/36897375", "state": "pending", "votes": -4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "You know it’s not shit to go pull out the Wraith, bring it out in automatic", "vault_lines": ["You know it's not shit to go pull out the Wraith, bring it out in automatic"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that whatever he’s doing is not enough to pull out the “Wraith” Referring to a Rolls-Royce Wraith. In the second half of this bar Yeat could either be referring to a car with automatic transmission, or saying that he is going to commit a drive-by with an automatic weapon.", "annotation_id": "32615369", "url": "https://genius.com/32615369", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "How you gon’ turn to a snitch? Yeah, how you talk shit but you runnin’?", "vault_lines": ["How you gon' turn to a snitch? Yeah, how you talk shit but you runnin'?"], "meaning": "In the first part of this bar Yeat is referencing someone who turned on him and “Snitched” or revealed truths (or lies) about Yeat. In the second part of this bar Yeat is saying that someone spoke to Yeat probably in a negative way, however when pressed on the matter ran away.", "annotation_id": "32615339", "url": "https://genius.com/32615339", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "I just try keeping it real, but I’m always gon’ keep it a hundred", "vault_lines": ["I just try keeping it real, but I'm always gon' keep it a hundred"], "meaning": "“Keeping it real” and “Keeping it 100” Are both terms meaning he is going to tell the truth, and be down to earth. Essentially giving a pure answer.", "annotation_id": "32615327", "url": "https://genius.com/32615327", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "I OD on the pills so much, I hired a full-time medic", "vault_lines": ["I OD on the pills so much, I hired a full-time medic"], "meaning": "This line vividly captures a cycle of pill abuse, revealing the extreme measure of hiring a full-time medic to cope with the consequences.\n\nIt reflects the raw honesty and complexity of addiction, hinting at the speaker’s desperate struggle for redemption and healing.", "annotation_id": "30879036", "url": "https://genius.com/30879036", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "First time touchin’ a mil’, life never felt so real (Real)", "vault_lines": ["First time touchin' a mil', life never felt so real (Real)"], "meaning": "yeat is likely referencing the first million dollars he made, stating that in that moment life felt surreal. could be referring to a million of something else but thats js my interpretation", "annotation_id": "30798905", "url": "https://genius.com/30798905", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "You sippin’ on lil’ stretched Wock’, bitch, I’m just crackin’ the seal (Hey)", "vault_lines": ["You sippin' on lil' stretched Wock', bitch, I'm just crackin' the seal (Hey)"], "meaning": "cough syrup usually comes in tamper-evident bottles with a visible seal, so you know if its been opened before or not. yeat is stating that the bottle is fresh and hasnt been opened before.", "annotation_id": "30798872", "url": "https://genius.com/30798872", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "Pull up on my bitch and she eat me like lunch, said I got rid of her headache", "vault_lines": ["Pull up on my bitch and she eat me like lunch, said I got rid of her headache"], "meaning": "Yeat believes that his skills in intercourse are very profound, and even have the ability to cure headaches. This would be a breakthrough in science if researched further, making Tylenol and other pain relieves obsolete. If this line is true, it is likely that large pharmaceutical companies may attempt to assassinate yeat in order to keep the public from receiving this miracle cure.", "annotation_id": "29517216", "url": "https://genius.com/29517216", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "Signin’ a deal would just be a mistake, I got my money out of nothing", "vault_lines": ["Signin' a deal would just be a mistake, I got my money out of nothing"], "meaning": "im pretty sure he said “signing a deal would just be a mistake, I got my money out of nothing” meaning he wants to be his own boss and not have to risk his creative decision making for a labels money. He gets money without a label.", "annotation_id": "29332387", "url": "https://genius.com/29332387", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "Gotta pay for a good-ass lawyer, we ain’t sittin’ in no cell, hey", "vault_lines": ["Gotta pay for a good-ass lawyer, we ain't sittin' in no cell, hey"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that he doesn’t want to go to jail, hence, “we ain’t sittin' in no cell” so he would like to a pay for a good lawyer to fight his case if he ever gets charged.", "annotation_id": "28706036", "url": "https://genius.com/28706036", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "Said you can’t trust me, lil’ bitch, I’m a snake, go behind your back and stab it", "vault_lines": ["Said you can't trust me, lil' bitch, I'm a snake, go behind your back and stab it"], "meaning": "“You” here is probably Wick (Autumn!). This song was released around the time of Yeats beef with Wick.\nShort explanation: Fellow underground rapper KanKan briefly went to jail for domestic abuse. Wick obviously didn’t support KanKan, so the two fell out and started beefing.\nAutumn also gained Yeat all his recognition by putting him on MEh. A snippet of Yeat on MEh blew up. Wick then continually helped Yeat gain a small following, which grew very fast. Becoming friends with KanKan, though, Yeat began to beef the person who made him, Wick, because KanKan was beefing him and Yeat doesn’t know how to think for himself.\nTherefore, Wick thinks Yeat is a snake, because he went behind his back with KanKan and “stabbed it”", "annotation_id": "27846472", "url": "https://genius.com/27846472", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "I was just shipping some bales, yeah", "vault_lines": [", I was just shipping some bales, yeah"], "meaning": "While in maritime La Jolla, Yeat states that he was shipping bails, or bales, of drugs. Yeat may be referencing times when bales of marijuana washed ashore in La Jolla in 2010 or alluding to the narcotics industry at large.\n\nhttps://www.sandiegouniontribune.com/sdut-marijuana-bales-seized-la-jolla-beach-2010jun01-story.html", "annotation_id": "26571226", "url": "https://genius.com/26571226", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "Ayy, it’s all up to me It’s all up to me, ayy", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, it's all up to me"], "meaning": "Up to me or “Up 2 Më” is the album this song takes place in", "annotation_id": "25720796", "url": "https://genius.com/25720796", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "All of my twizzies is up, bitch, we been next in line", "vault_lines": ["All of my twizzies is up, bitch, we been next in line"], "meaning": "“twizzy” is a slang term that refers to the word “twin” and is used when mentioning someone is a “close friend”.\n\nHe is saying that him and his friends have put in the work and it’s their turn to reap the rewards", "annotation_id": "25631882", "url": "https://genius.com/25631882", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "VS1 flawless, all of ’em shine", "vault_lines": ["VS1 flawless, all of 'em shine"], "meaning": "A VS1 diamond is a high clarity grade with no visible inclusions and only small, hard-to-identify inclusions under 10x magnification. These diamonds represent the top 5 percent of all gem-quality stones. The most common VS1 inclusions are crystal (white or black), feather, indented natural, knot, or needle.", "annotation_id": "25631867", "url": "https://genius.com/25631867", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "I always gotta dodge all the hate, I gotta dodge the assumptions", "vault_lines": ["I always gotta dodge all the hate, I gotta dodge the assumptions"], "meaning": "I see a lot of people try to say Yeat is a Playboi Carti clone / rip off. I watched Fantano’s reaction to Still Countin and he called him Carti’s son. I never really got this opinion. They genuinely don’t sound alike at all. If anything I would say Yeat is more similar to Young Thug than Carti.", "annotation_id": "25631848", "url": "https://genius.com/25631848", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "I was just out in La Jolla", "vault_lines": ["I was just out in La Jolla"], "meaning": "La Jolla is a neighborhood in Western San Diego, California, that borders 7 miles of the Pacific Ocean.\n\nSo Yeat is saying that he was recently in a coastal region of San Diego. Perhaps Twizz has a fascination with saltwater-maritime locations.", "annotation_id": "24731176", "url": "https://genius.com/24731176", "state": "pending", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "You sippin’ on lil’ stretched Wock’, bitch, I’m just crackin’ the seal (Hey)", "vault_lines": ["You sippin' on lil' stretched Wock', bitch, I'm just crackin' the seal (Hey)"], "meaning": "Is this line, Yeat says that the listener drinks a diluted, “stretched” version of Wockhardt Promethazine w/ Codeine cough syrup. On the contrary, Yeat’s syrup is brand new and has not been tampered with, which is proved by the seal on his bottle.", "annotation_id": "24579545", "url": "https://genius.com/24579545", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "I tried replacing the X with the Percs, but, bitch, you don’t know how that feel (Boot up)", "vault_lines": ["I tried replacing the X with the Pеrcs, but, bitch, you don't know how that feel (Boot up)"], "meaning": "Yeat is stating that even taking strong pharmaceutical opioids such as oxycodone (Percs), doesn’t give him as intense of a high or euphoria as MDMA (X), and that replacing the latter with the former in his pill-popping routine is rather difficult.", "annotation_id": "24579447", "url": "https://genius.com/24579447", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Twizzy Rich", "line": "Yeah, told you stop calling my phone, told you stop wasting my time", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, told you stop calling my phone, told you stop wasting my time"], "meaning": "In this bar, yeat is describing his misogynistic qualities through his lyrics. He tells a female to stop wasting his time; only further portraying Yeat’s mentality. The beauty in this writing is truly portrayed when yeat explains to his female that she needs to stop hitting his phone.", "annotation_id": "24167518", "url": "https://genius.com/24167518", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
