{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Turban", "line": "I already did what I can (Her move, her move)", "vault_lines": ["I already did what I can (Her move, her move)"], "meaning": "This line is Yeat explaining that he has done what he can already do and his work is not good followed by “(I’m on, I’m on)”. The term “I’m on” means various things but based off of the previous statement this means he going to stop making music. Followed up by the line “it’s her move” which yeat is referring to the daughter of the devil and that she is either going to replace him or influence him strongly", "annotation_id": "30584258", "url": "https://genius.com/30584258", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
