{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Turban", "line": "I took the coupe out the lot, bitch, I’m thinkin’ ’bout swervin’, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I took the coupe out the lot, bitch, I'm thinkin' 'bout swervin', yeah"], "meaning": "A coupe is a two-door motor vehicle, typically spec’d with rear-wheel drive. Yeat states that he just purchased a new vehicle of this type, and he’s contemplating exiting the dealership in style by drifting into the road.", "annotation_id": "26679015", "url": "https://genius.com/26679015", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Turban", "line": "Perfect, rockin’ a turban (Oh yeah, oh yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Perfect, rockin' a turban (Oh yeah, oh yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat compares the designer scarf wrapped around his neck and face to a turban. A turban is a headdress, consisting of a long length of cotton or silk wound around the head, worn by people of various cultures, including Muslims and Sikhs.\n\nNotably, Yeat wears a Dior scarf, or “turban,” throughout the song’s music video.\n\n\n\nPictured: Yeat wearing a Dior “turban.”", "annotation_id": "25177681", "url": "https://genius.com/25177681", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Turban", "line": "I wrapped my money up, this shit look like a turban", "vault_lines": ["I wrapped my money up, this shit look like a turban"], "meaning": "Noah Olivier Smith, more professionally known as Yeat, is referring to the large sums of money he has acquired in his recent years. He is inquiring that he has so much money that he needs to wrap it up, much like a turban. A turban is a common piece of clothing from India. (see photo below)", "annotation_id": "25135583", "url": "https://genius.com/25135583", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Turban", "line": "I better sign for a lot ’cause this shit ain’t urgent (Okay)", "vault_lines": ["I better sign for a lot 'cause this shit ain't urgent (Okay)"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that he is waiting to get signed by a record label so he can get signed for much more money. By claiming “this shit ain’t urgent,” Yeat is explaining that he knows his value as a rapper and will continue to release music independently until he is being signed by a label that recognizes his worth.", "annotation_id": "25065017", "url": "https://genius.com/25065017", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Turban", "line": "Sippin’ on mud but this bitch like bourbon (Dirty, dirty)", "vault_lines": ["Sippin' on mud but this bitch like bourbon (Dirty, dirty)"], "meaning": "“Mud” is a slang term for lean, a mixture of codeine cough syrup and soda. In this line, Yeat compares his lean to bourbon, a type of American whiskey. He likely means that there is a high concentration of codeine in his lean, giving it a dark color that resembles bourbon.", "annotation_id": "24575819", "url": "https://genius.com/24575819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Turban", "line": "Got off the phone with my twizzy", "vault_lines": ["Got off the phone with my twizzy"], "meaning": "“Twizzy” is a term used like the word twin, as in he’s a “brother.” The term was made up by Yeat himself and is used by his associates. The term was incorporated into the name of Yeat’s record label, TwizzyRich.", "annotation_id": "24352095", "url": "https://genius.com/24352095", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
