{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Truely", "line": "Go in the stu’ when I tweak (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Go in the stu' when I tweak (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Whenever Yeat “tweaks”, experiencing hallucinations or just going kinda crazy he goes to the Stu in order to feel better. This could be a result of his psychosis which has influenced him from a young age as he describes Demons and Aliens talking to him. However this could be musical charm as part of the drugged out “ Yeat” persona, but he does claim to spill his soul in every song and I wouldn’t doubt that Yeat’s demons tell him the method on how to reach the top. what a real nigga", "annotation_id": "37104553", "url": "https://genius.com/37104553", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Truely", "line": "Even when I rock Palm Angels, still talk to my demons (Grr-grr)", "vault_lines": ["Even when I rock Palm Angels, still talk to my demons (Grr-grr)"], "meaning": "Even when wearing the clothing of Angles, Yeat still talks to hell’s creatures, the demons. Specifically his demons or hallucinations that he experiences.", "annotation_id": "37104552", "url": "https://genius.com/37104552", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
