{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tru to U", "line": "I went and took this bitch out on a date, and it was Oxy’", "vault_lines": ["I went and took this bitch out on a date, and it was Oxy'"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying his true love and the thing he spends the most time with is Oxycodone, an opioid.", "annotation_id": "36940888", "url": "https://genius.com/36940888", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tru to U", "line": "I got the racks at the bottom myself, then I bought that gat again (Again)", "vault_lines": ["I got the racks at the bottom myself, then I bought that gat again (Again)"], "meaning": "“Gat” is slang for a gun. He’s saying that after making money by himself when he was alone at the bottom (poor) , he bought another firearm. The repetition (“again”) stresses that this isn’t the first time, it’s part of his lifestyle and how he protects himself and his success.", "annotation_id": "36940869", "url": "https://genius.com/36940869", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
