{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tru to U", "line": "Why you on my phone every day, every night? This shit is too exhausting", "vault_lines": ["Why you on my phone every day, every night? This shit is too exhausting"], "meaning": "This is a prime example of a male expressing how too much clinginess will lead to the downfall of a relationship and how much it can tire out a man.", "annotation_id": "25786358", "url": "https://genius.com/25786358", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tru to U", "line": "She ask me what’s a damn Trackhawk, I told her the best Jeep", "vault_lines": ["She ask me what's a damn Trackhawk, I told her the best Jeep"], "meaning": "Reference to the Jeep Grand Cherokee Trackhawk which is the performance variant of a regular Cherokee coming in with 707 horsepower it is indeed the best Jeep", "annotation_id": "25777300", "url": "https://genius.com/25777300", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tru to U", "line": "Really just been too goated with this punchin’ in shit, I feel like Ali", "vault_lines": ["Really just been too goated with this punchin' in shit, I feel like Ali"], "meaning": "“Punching in” is a term rappers use to define a recording technique that has the rapper record a song line by line with breaks between takes instead of in a singular one, commonly used when freestyling to give the rapper time to think of what to say next.\n\nYeat likens his skills in the studio to those of Muhammed Ali, known to be one of the greatest boxers of all time who threw extremely powerful punches at his opponents.", "annotation_id": "25777288", "url": "https://genius.com/25777288", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
