{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "Bitch, I just caught the vibe, but I can’t slide if it ain’t no cash in it", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I just caught the vibe, but I can't slide if it ain't no cash in it"], "meaning": "can’t get high if the contract and check aren’t signed", "annotation_id": "30342902", "url": "https://genius.com/30342902", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "Cut off all my old friends, I left they ass in last place", "vault_lines": ["Cut off all my old friends, I left they ass in last place"], "meaning": "Reference to Slayworld in how Yeat rose above all of them and hasn’t looked back since.", "annotation_id": "30167260", "url": "https://genius.com/30167260", "state": "pending", "votes": -5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "Just tell me if you rock with it, tell me if you popping it Tell me if you ever want some cash, you know I’m dropping it Yeah, I pour a four inside a soda, it’s some drop in it Know I gotta change before I die but I can’t stop this shit", "vault_lines": ["Just tell me if you rock with it, tеll me if you popping it"], "meaning": "this part is recorded far away from the mic, and at the end yeats voice echos, showing his disassiotion from the rest of the world", "annotation_id": "30033347", "url": "https://genius.com/30033347", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "I was talking ’bout the Tonka so I bought it, fuck a rental", "vault_lines": ["I was talking 'bout the Tonka so I bought it, fuck a rental"], "meaning": "Yeat bought a Tonka (A big SUV) instead of just renting one since he usually mentions Tonkas in his songs.", "annotation_id": "29681800", "url": "https://genius.com/29681800", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "Yeah, I just called twizz, yeah, just called up the Martians", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I just called twizz, yeah, just called up the Martians"], "meaning": "In the first part of this line yeat is calling up his “Twïzzy” which means “Twin” usually referring to someone you hang out with a lot and is a good friend.\n\nIn the second part yeat states the fact that he just called up “The Martians” referring to the fact that martians are Aliens who usually live out of our planets orbit, meaning that yeat is out of our planets orbit, which is word play for being tremendously high(intoxicated, usually using substances like, paracetamol, MDMA or even weed) that he is physically out of orbit(again, wordplay on “high”), meaning that because he’s out of orbit he can call up “The Martians” who are also out of orbit.", "annotation_id": "29430462", "url": "https://genius.com/29430462", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "Twizzy pulled up on this kid, he shot him up, now he’s a lentil", "vault_lines": ["Twizzy pulled up on this kid, he shot him up, now he's a lentil"], "meaning": "Yeat’s “Twizzy”, (home slice or dawg) pulled up on this kid, shot him, and turned him to a bean", "annotation_id": "28388317", "url": "https://genius.com/28388317", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "I been sippin’ sideways", "vault_lines": ["I been sippin' sideways"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying he sips sideways, meaning when he drinks lean the cup is sideways so he can drink more", "annotation_id": "28353020", "url": "https://genius.com/28353020", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "I been off the opiates so long, I feel like crashing it", "vault_lines": ["I been off the opiates so long, I feel like crashing it"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying he’s been off the opiates (percocets) that he feels like crashing (sleeping)", "annotation_id": "28353009", "url": "https://genius.com/28353009", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "Cook it up like it’s some Bonchon, we still been servin’ chickens", "vault_lines": ["Cook it up like it's some Bonchon, we still been servin' chickens"], "meaning": "Bok choy is a plant typically used in chinese cooking, frequently in soups. Yeat is using it here to illustrate how he is cooking up some drugs. Serving chickens also refers to selling (serving) cocaine (chickens).", "annotation_id": "27800894", "url": "https://genius.com/27800894", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "Bitch, I rock these turbans like I’m crazy like an Arab", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I rock these turbans like I'm crazy like an Arab"], "meaning": "Arabs don’t wear turbans. Yeat is thinking of a Keffiyeh (كُوفِيَّة) a headdress commonly worn by arab men, and one that bares resemblance to his signature scarf.", "annotation_id": "25689398", "url": "https://genius.com/25689398", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "Know I gotta change before I die but I can’t stop this shit", "vault_lines": ["Know I gotta change before I die but I can't stop this shit"], "meaning": "Yeat’s heavy drug usage is a result of addiction. Lean specifically has numerous health effects that can eventually be fatal. Yeat is saying he knows he needs to get clean before the drugs kill him but he can’t because his addiction is too strong.", "annotation_id": "26599388", "url": "https://genius.com/26599388", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "I went into the Porsche, bitch, I went and bought a Cayenne", "vault_lines": ["I went into the Porsche, bitch, I went and bought a Cayenne"], "meaning": "The Cayenne is a luxury SUV, or “Tonka,” produced by German automobile manufacturer Porsche.", "annotation_id": "26113390", "url": "https://genius.com/26113390", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "Yeah, I just called Tose’ up, yeah, I just called up Barneys", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I just called Tose' up, yeah, I just called up Barneys"], "meaning": "In this line, Yeat calls up his plug for “Tose'” referring to the codeine “Toseína” brand. He rephrases this by saying he called up Barney’s, due to the purple color of the character.", "annotation_id": "26103673", "url": "https://genius.com/26103673", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "Yeah, I pour a four inside a soda, it’s some drop in it", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I pour a four inside a soda, it's some drop in it"], "meaning": "A “four” refers to 4 ounces of codeine. He made lean.", "annotation_id": "26029730", "url": "https://genius.com/26029730", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "Yeah, it feel like I was dying slowly but surely, yeah, Temple", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, it feel like I was dying slowly but surely, yeah, Temple"], "meaning": "Here, Yeat uses a play on words to make a reference to the late American actress, singer, and dancer, Shirley Temple, while relating his drug use to the temple, the weakest part of the human brain.\n\n“Slowly but surely” is a common phrase used to show definite progress that something is going to occur. Stated here, Yeat makes it clear that he is feeling the effects of the drugs previously talked about, which affects basic functions of the human brain, mostly affecting the temple.", "annotation_id": "25815848", "url": "https://genius.com/25815848", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "And when she pull up on me, she suck dick, she do so passionate Just tell me if you rock with it, tell me if you popping it Tell me if you ever want some cash, you know I’m dropping it", "vault_lines": ["And when she pull up on me, she suck dick, she do so passionate"], "meaning": "These three lines are about/toward Yeat’s bitches.\n\nFirst line: His bitch gives gobsmacking brain. Just rambunctious jaw. She’s just great at head towards Yeat.\n\nSecond line: “Tell me if you rock with it, Tell me if you’re poppin it” is a message to two things. 1) Tell me if you’re happy with me and our situation and 2) tell me if we’re having sex today.\n\nThird Line: Yeat loves his girl so much he has a ‘What’s mine is yours’ mentality.", "annotation_id": "25618816", "url": "https://genius.com/25618816", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Told ya", "line": "You gotta listen to what I’m saying, I ain’t screaming but I’m shoutin’", "vault_lines": ["You gotta listen to what I'm saying, I ain't screaming but I'm shoutin'"], "meaning": "Yeat tells the listener that he isn’t just screaming, he’s shouting.\n\nScreaming is a word used to describe nonverbal warning.\n\nShouting usually contains words.\n\nExample of Screaming: “AAAAAAAAAAAAAaaAA”\n\nExample of Shouting:\n“HOLY SMOKES THERE’S A BEE!”", "annotation_id": "25618786", "url": "https://genius.com/25618786", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
