{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "The Bell", "line": "Shawty say she feel like it’s made for herself", "vault_lines": ["Shawty say she feel like it's made for herself"], "meaning": "His partner feels like she belongs in his luxury world.\n\nAlso shows how Yeat’s lifestyle attracts people who think they fit in.", "annotation_id": "36849483", "url": "https://genius.com/36849483", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "The Bell", "line": "(Ruff, ruff) I can’t stand my— (I’m hungry), ha (Phew) (Ki-King Tonka) Yeah I can’t stand myself, ah-ah, I can’t stand my ass (Ki-King Tonka), yeah", "vault_lines": ["I can't stand myself, ah-ah, I can’t stand my ass (Ki-King Tonka), yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat throws in his signature ad-libs (“ruff ruff” dog bark, “phew”), building chaotic energy.\n\n“I can’t stand myself” reflects the inner conflict beneath the flex—drugs, fame, and excess leave him restless.", "annotation_id": "36849473", "url": "https://genius.com/36849473", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "The Bell", "line": "I uncovered the juice, I uncovered the twist (I-I-I-I-I-I—)", "vault_lines": ["I uncovered the juice, I uncovered the twist (I-I-I-I-I-I—)"], "meaning": "In slang terms, one has ‘juice’ if they have ‘respect, influence, power, authority, or sexual desirability (Dictionary.com)’, which Yeat’s lyrics flaunt to a large extent.\n\nUncovering the twist means the same, but possibly alludes to the fruit juice brand Twister.", "annotation_id": "36063906", "url": "https://genius.com/36063906", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
