{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "The Bell", "line": "Molly in my cup, it’s got me turnin’ sideways", "vault_lines": ["Molly in my cup, it's got me turnin' sideways"], "meaning": "MDMA is a drug known for its intoxicating effects. In standard drug fashion, Molly is taken in pill or capsule form, but can be dissolved in a drink, which is less common but not unheard of.", "annotation_id": "35245046", "url": "https://genius.com/35245046", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "The Bell", "line": "All my diamonds speak to me (Yeah) All my diamonds on Major League", "vault_lines": ["All my diamonds speak to me (Yеah)"], "meaning": "“Major League” implies that his diamonds consist of the highest quality. He connects the players in Major League to the quality of his jewelry — his diamonds don’t just consist of luxury; they are the best of the best on the market.\n\nIt’s also worth noting, the term “diamond” might serve as a double entendre here. A diamond is a small shiny little stone, but in baseball slang, “diamond” can refer to the inner field area on a baseball field, which happens to be diamond-shaped.", "annotation_id": "35244804", "url": "https://genius.com/35244804", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
