{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tell më", "line": "I just put it all together, send a note to a letter", "vault_lines": ["I just put it all together, send a note to a letter"], "meaning": "This could be saying that he gets a text from a girl sending a long paragraph and he replies with a short text or one word because he don’t care", "annotation_id": "41007363", "url": "https://genius.com/41007363", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tell më", "line": "Pay more just to feel", "vault_lines": ["Pay more just to feel"], "meaning": "Yeat is referencing how people “pay more” for drugs so that they can “feel more”/feel something.", "annotation_id": "36286971", "url": "https://genius.com/36286971", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tell më", "line": "Don’t you feel good? You say you feel good (Good)", "vault_lines": ["Don't you feel good? You say you feel good (Good)"], "meaning": "I have two interpretations:\n\nFirst interpretation; Yeat continue’s to throw shade at artist who have “sold their souls to the devil” for fame and fortune. He is rhetorically asking these celebrities the question of if they truly feel good or not, as many celebrities claim to have it all but are often left with nothing, as the record labels and studios take most of their earnings, with the money they flaunt just being a façade at the end of the day.\n\nSecond interpretation: This line can also be referring to Yeat’s previously mentioned drug addiction (if we being real). This line could be Yeat talking to himself and questioning if the drugs are actually what he wants of If they are just hurting him in the long run.", "annotation_id": "36286913", "url": "https://genius.com/36286913", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tell më", "line": "I guess two-zero-nine-three is not for you (You, you, you, you)", "vault_lines": ["I guess two-zero-nine-three is not for you (You, you, you, you)"], "meaning": "Here, Yeat is saying that if you dislike the themes of 2093, the album is “not for you”.\n\nIn hindsight, this line is pretty ironic considering the massive backlash that 2093 received upon its release, with many fans openly disliking the tonal shift in style, utilizing a more experimental sound. This is opposed to Yeat’s previous albums and tracks that, more or less, share a common consistency in their overall sound, mumble-lyrics and composition.\n\nAdditionally, Yeat, while criticizing those who dislike the album, simultaneously predicted the initial “failure” of the album not being as successful as his last.", "annotation_id": "36286807", "url": "https://genius.com/36286807", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tell më", "line": "I can’t go back on my words ’cause that’d be rude", "vault_lines": ["I can't go back on my words 'cause that'd be rude"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that he doesn’t consider himself a hypocrite or a person who opposes or contradicts themself because quote “that’d be rude”.\n\nIn his opinion, he’d rather stay true to his word and authentic.", "annotation_id": "36286780", "url": "https://genius.com/36286780", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tell më", "line": "I wish you would feel like me I wish you could see like me And there’s more to life than that And there’s more to life than this", "vault_lines": ["I wish you would feel like me"], "meaning": "Considering that the album takes place where he is the final mortal being on earth, it is suggested that he feels alone but at the same time gains an immense power from feeling that alone as he is the only one to be feeling like that.", "annotation_id": "35043651", "url": "https://genius.com/35043651", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tell më", "line": "Go be fake, bitch, yeah, being real’s not better", "vault_lines": ["Go be fake, bitch, yeah, being real's not better"], "meaning": "PROPOSED SUGGESTION:\n\nHe means that it doesnt matter if “she” is real or acting fake, both are awfull", "annotation_id": "33047237", "url": "https://genius.com/33047237", "state": "pending", "votes": -5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tell më", "line": "Lotta baggage to unpack, and it’s cool", "vault_lines": ["Lotta baggage to unpack, and it's cool"], "meaning": "Yeat, being a rich CEO in a dystopian society being clear headed and sober, now has a lot of mental baggage to unload", "annotation_id": "33638267", "url": "https://genius.com/33638267", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tell më", "line": "It’s a burnt smell (Yeah), as far as I could tell It get deeper than a well", "vault_lines": ["It's a burnt smell (Yeah), as far as I could tell"], "meaning": "“It’s a burnt smell, as far as I could tell” uses imagery to describe the environment of hell, suggesting that the situation is so extreme that it even smells like something is burning.\n“It get deeper than a well” implies that the issues or emotions run very deep, much deeper than they might initially appear.", "annotation_id": "33133135", "url": "https://genius.com/33133135", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Tell më", "line": "And it’s fine, that’s fair, yeah, I would never care", "vault_lines": ["And it's fine, that's fair, yeah, I would never care"], "meaning": "He doesn’t care about anyone, he left everyone to get up, just the way he left his old washed friends. KANKAN and Sep.", "annotation_id": "33047265", "url": "https://genius.com/33047265", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
