{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Team ceo", "line": "I could see the future with one eye", "vault_lines": ["I could see the future with one eye"], "meaning": "The Norse god, Odin, gained the ability to see into the future by gouging out one of his eyes.\n\nhttps://www.worldhistory.org/img/r/p/1500x1500/13835.jpg.webp?v=1699399809\n\nYeat/Psycho CEO, who boasted of the ability to make gods cry just prior, stakes his claim to a similar power. What did he have to sacrifice to acquire it, though?", "annotation_id": "31883716", "url": "https://genius.com/31883716", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Team ceo", "line": "It’s like fittin’ all that Porsche up inside a purse", "vault_lines": ["It's like fittin' all that Porsche up inside a purse"], "meaning": "how u gon fit a porsche in a purse", "annotation_id": "31369807", "url": "https://genius.com/31369807", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Team ceo", "line": "Do you know what happens when you die?", "vault_lines": ["Do you know what happens when you die?"], "meaning": "Yeat here prompts reflection on the mysteries surrounding death and the various beliefs, theories, and uncertainties that humans contemplate regarding the afterlife or the cessation of existence. It opens up a conversation about existential questions and the unknown aspects of the human experience.", "annotation_id": "31208176", "url": "https://genius.com/31208176", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Team ceo", "line": "I heard it from my fuckin’ space ship, huh You thinkin’ all that shit, but you don’t say shit, huh", "vault_lines": ["I heard it from my fuckin' space ship, huh"], "meaning": "Yeat claims to have heard what others say about him from his “space ship,” implying an elevated perspective due to his rise in fame and money. The second line implies that while others may have thoughts or opinions, they are not vocalizing them. They think that they are great, however, Yeat is superior.", "annotation_id": "31112730", "url": "https://genius.com/31112730", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Team ceo", "line": "Do you live a lot? Do you live a lie?", "vault_lines": ["Do you live a lot? Do you live a lie?"], "meaning": "Many of Yeat’s previous works are references to “Lyfe” and how he lives. Here, Yeat presents a question that juxtaposes his lifestyle with the opposition’s to preface several couplets that chronicle is grasp of life and death. If Yeat makes gods cry and he lives in the future, any claims that someone is living a more thrilling life must be false from his perspective.", "annotation_id": "30908182", "url": "https://genius.com/30908182", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Team ceo", "line": "That mean you can’t fit in with the GOATs of this motherfuckin’ shit", "vault_lines": ["That mean you can't fit in with the GOATs of this motherfuckin' shit"], "meaning": "Goats meaning “Greatest Of All Time” signifying many other rappers and music creators cannot fit in with the true Goats of his music", "annotation_id": "30907485", "url": "https://genius.com/30907485", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Team ceo", "line": "Do you live a lot? Do you live a lie?", "vault_lines": ["Do you live a lot? Do you live a lie?"], "meaning": "More than likely in relation to how rappers portray a fake life they live or once lived in their music.", "annotation_id": "30907478", "url": "https://genius.com/30907478", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Team ceo", "line": "I don’t try dyin’ Yeah, might’ve tried once Way too many X pills,", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I die tryin', I don't try dyin'"], "meaning": "This line is a double entendre. On one hand, Yeat is alluding to the previous line, “I know what happens when you die…” speaking of his previous overdose and supposed encounter with the devil. The line “Yeah, might’ve tried once…” is a direct reference to his temporary death and whatever may have ensued during it. It can also be interpreted as what the line means, with Yeats saying he will never give up on his career. It is worth noting he may also be referencing his suicidal thoughts previously mentioned in unreleased songs.", "annotation_id": "30906584", "url": "https://genius.com/30906584", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Team ceo", "line": "I know what happens when you die", "vault_lines": ["I know what happens when you die"], "meaning": "Some say that Yeat may have had a near death experience early in his career, possibly from an overdose. He credits the devil for saving him in another song", "annotation_id": "30905466", "url": "https://genius.com/30905466", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Team ceo", "line": "Is it a blessin’ or curse? I just did it first I could ruin ya’ life, make it a lot worse", "vault_lines": ["Is it a blessin' or curse? I just did it first"], "meaning": "Yeat speaks on his schizophrenia n those who also have it(fairly common genetic trait)", "annotation_id": "30904342", "url": "https://genius.com/30904342", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Team ceo", "line": "Yeah, might’ve tried once Way too many X pills, yeah, for one album", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, might've tried once"], "meaning": "Yeat is trying to go sober\n(This could also explain why is sound is changing, Give him time to settle down)\n\nThe line ‘might’ve tried once’ describes when Yeat overdosed off drugs and came back to life which inspired his 2021 album ‘Alive’. He also mentions this incident on a song from the same album ‘Died B4’\n\n‘Way too many X pills, yeah for one album’ Yeat is reflecting on his past ecstasy addiction where he’d use daily. More specifically in 2021 during the time of recording his albums 4L and Up 2 Me.", "annotation_id": "30904132", "url": "https://genius.com/30904132", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Team ceo", "line": "I got new shit, I invent a word", "vault_lines": ["I got new shit, I invent a word"], "meaning": "YEAT is talkin about how he invents words that dont exist for things that are present in his life.\nExample: Twizzy, shmunk, luh, Yonky, etc.", "annotation_id": "30902230", "url": "https://genius.com/30902230", "state": "pending", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
