{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk Money", "line": "Make you touch a bow for a bag", "vault_lines": ["Make you touch a bow for a bag"], "meaning": "To touch a bow for a bad means that Yeat would likely make a person shoot a gun (the metaphorical bow) for a bag, a large sum of money.", "annotation_id": "30693369", "url": "https://genius.com/30693369", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk Money", "line": "I’ve been in the kitchen, making hits, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I've been in the kitchen, making hits, yeah"], "meaning": "The “kitchen” is actually the studio as he is cooking up something (a song) really good. Songs that go viral or are very good are called “hits” so Noah Oliver Smith is making songs that are bound to go viral in the studio.", "annotation_id": "27522992", "url": "https://genius.com/27522992", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk Money", "line": "Yeah, twizzy serving chickens, serving bricks", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, twizzy serving chickens, serving bricks"], "meaning": "Yeat nods to his twizzy (slang for twin) who is serving chickens (slang for a kilo of cocaine). Long live the trap", "annotation_id": "24979958", "url": "https://genius.com/24979958", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
