{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "Potty trained my diamonds, yeah, they smackin’ head to toe", "vault_lines": ["Potty trained my diamonds, yeah, they smackin' head to toe (Boom, boom, boom, boom, boom, yeah)"], "meaning": "Canary diamonds, or “yellow” diamonds are a rarer type of diamond than the more common white counterpart.\n\nIn this line, Yeat’s joking about having to potty train his diamonds because they’re urine colored.", "annotation_id": "29626742", "url": "https://genius.com/29626742", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "I-I-I’m working on dying", "vault_lines": ["Jump out at the show, uh (I-I-I'm working on dying), jump out at the show"], "meaning": "This is the producer tag of Philadelphia producer collective Working on Dying, known for their work with artists like Lil Uzi Vert, Playboi Carti, Ken Carson, and more. BNYX, the producer of “Talk”, has been a member of the group  since 2021 as well as the main producer for Lyfe, producing songs on the project like “Talk” and “What it feel lykë” and has been a frequent collaborator of Yeat for his past few projects. Yeat has also worked with other Working on Dying members such as Brandon Finessin (on “Big Tonka” with Lil Uzi Vert) and F1lthy (on “Smooktober”).", "annotation_id": "27482668", "url": "https://genius.com/27482668", "state": "accepted", "votes": 91, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "I don’t give a fuck what you sayin’, I don’t listen to it, I don’t wanna hear ’bout none", "vault_lines": ["I don't give a fuck what you sayin', I don't listen to it, I don't wanna hear 'bout none"], "meaning": "In this line Yeat is affirming that he doesn’t listen to (most likely) Haters and that he doesn’t want to hear their opinions, because he will always make what he wants to.", "annotation_id": "27209016", "url": "https://genius.com/27209016", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "Riding ‘round, I’m in the Cayenne, lil’ bitch, I’ma tear up the city, I’m afraid of the sun (Hey, hey, hey)", "vault_lines": ["Yeat concert, Yeat, Yeat (Come on, man)"], "meaning": "Yeat references German car manufacturer Porsche and their Cayenne luxury SUV model. The 2022 Cayenne has a base price of $69,000 for the standard body.\n\n\n\nPicture of a 2022 Porsche Cayenne.\n\nFollowing his sentiment, Yeat alludes to driving around at night in a Cayenne under the influence of drugs. He asserts himself as an “night owl,” favoring being awake during the late hours of the night, which may be a follow-up reference to his next bar.", "annotation_id": "26644820", "url": "https://genius.com/26644820", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "I went and painted the Benz, I switched shit up, I wanted it done by the dawn", "vault_lines": ["I went and painted the Benz, I switched shit up, I wanted it done by the dawn"], "meaning": "Yeat alludes to his Mercedes-AMG GLE 63 Coupe. On January 14, 2022, the rapper uploaded a picture of his SUV—displaying a new satin black wrap along with green hints. Yeat previously mentioned his car in his February 2022 track “Dnt lië,” rapping:\n\nYeah, I’m tellin' you I’m parked outside, it’s harder to get (Brr)\nGot a G63 on the coupe (Brr)\n\n\n\nPictured: Yeat revealing the wrap in January 2022.\n\nA “Don” refers to a crime boss or a kingpin. This further affirms Yeat’s covert lifestyle, as well as implies his desired concept to re-wrap his entire SUV black, due to most crime bosses transporting themselves in a traditional blacked-out vehicle in order to remain privatized.\n\n\n\nPicture of a blacked out 1993 Cadillac V12 Town Sedan.", "annotation_id": "26643991", "url": "https://genius.com/26643991", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "And the whip got two R, yeah, Rolls Royce truck, yeah, what the Cullinan bought (Hey, hey, hey)", "vault_lines": ["And the whip got two R, yeah, Rolls Royce truck, yeah, what the Cullinan bought (Hey, hey, hey)"], "meaning": "Yeat references the British luxury automobile maker Rolls-Royce, known for its luxurious and expensive cars. A “Rolls Royce truck” refers to a Cullinan, the brand’s SUV model, with a starting price of $351,250.\n\n\n\nPictured: A Rolls-Royce Cullinan.\n\nIn a possible double entendre, he could be saying that he literally has two Rolls Royce cars, affirming his wealth.", "annotation_id": "26637543", "url": "https://genius.com/26637543", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "Yeat concert, Yeat, Yeat (Come on, man) Man, one of the biggest artists in the world right now We seen it all, niggas was gettin’ tazed Bitches was poppin’ pussy by the front door Niggas was throwin’ chairs, everything was goin’ down Fifty-thousand people, Yeat concert, twizz shit right here Real twizz shit right here (Real twizzy shit right here) You guys don’t know ’bout it", "vault_lines": ["Yeat concert, Yeat, Yeat (Come on, man)"], "meaning": "This is a sample from a fan interview outside Yeat’s February 2022 2 Alivë listening party at the Roxy Theater in Los Angeles, California. They describe the manic experience they went through, as the free show exceeded the maximum capacity. Over 1,000 people gathered outside waiting, resulting in Yeat’s ban from the venue alongside the venue being shut down by police.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/W8w2ssbG_Z0?t=120", "annotation_id": "26630543", "url": "https://genius.com/26630543", "state": "accepted", "votes": 94, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "And I just brought in some M’s, lil’ bitch, it’s the first of the month", "vault_lines": ["And I just brought in some M's, lil' bitch, it's the first of the month"], "meaning": "The first of the month implies that Yeat is copping some drugs since dealers re-up then.\n\nIt could also imply that he brought in an “M” or another million dollars, because pay day happens on the 1st of the month and every “Month” starts with an “M”.\n\nYeat interpolates Bone Thugs-n-Harmony’s 1995 track “1st Of Tha Month,” which was similarly referenced by Playboi Carti on his song “Sky”:\n\nWake up (Wake up, wake up, woah)\nIt’s the first of the month (Slatt, slatt, slatt, slatt)", "annotation_id": "26628169", "url": "https://genius.com/26628169", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "And I don’t give a fuck ’bout the coupe, yeah, I pop the bitch on Tes’, huh (Woo, woo, woo)", "vault_lines": ["And I don't give a fuck 'bout the coupe, yeah, I pop the bitch on Tes', huh (Woo, woo, woo)"], "meaning": "Yeat will have sex with a woman while under the influence of MDMA in tablet form, known as ecstasy. “Tes” refers to a Tesla logo-shaped ecstasy tablet. He says he doesn’t care about a coupe to dispel ambiguity with a Tesla car.", "annotation_id": "26626692", "url": "https://genius.com/26626692", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "Had to change my flow, yeah, had to change the joke (Hey, hey, hey, BNYX)", "vault_lines": ["Had to change my flow, yeah, had to change the joke (Hey, hey, hey, BNYX)"], "meaning": "Yeat acknowledges that he has had several different “flows” and cadences. Throughout his albums, EPs, and singles, you can hear a linear evolution of different rapping styles and beats to get him to the point that he is at now.", "annotation_id": "26626322", "url": "https://genius.com/26626322", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "All of my fans is my family, my cult, my brother, my slime, my twizzy, my money (Hey, hey, hey)", "vault_lines": ["Yeat concert, Yeat, Yeat (Come on, man)"], "meaning": "Yeat appreciates his strong-bonded fanbase that was instrumental in his come-up the same way he does his family and friends. He uses the slang term “twizzy”— another word for twin—and the renowned hip-hop term “slime”—a synonym of a close friend—to further strengthen his claim.\n\nMore morbidly, he likens himself to a cult leader in the way they both have a tight-knit, overly obsessed following. Yeat has previously used this dark analogy in his February 2022 track “Rollin,” rapping:\n\nMy fans just like a cult, they read my Bible (Bible)", "annotation_id": "26623379", "url": "https://genius.com/26623379", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "Riding ’round with these bust-down watches on me, I got my blicky tucked (Hey, hey, hey)", "vault_lines": ["Riding 'round with these bust-down watches on me, I got my blicky tucked (Hey, hey, hey)"], "meaning": "The term “bust-down” describes an expensive piece of jewelry that is set with diamonds. In this case, it is a watch set with diamonds.\n\n\n\nPictured: Yeat with a diamond set Audemars Piguet watch.\n\n“Blicky” is a slang term for a handgun, originating in New York. Yeat has used the term a few times in his music, including tracks like “Dub,” or “3G”.", "annotation_id": "26564632", "url": "https://genius.com/26564632", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "Huh, riding in that, big ass lil’ Tonka truck", "vault_lines": ["Huh, riding in that, big ass lil' Tonka truck"], "meaning": "“Tonka” is a term Yeat uses to describe the size of a luxury SUV vehicle, which is usually powered by a V8 or V10 engine. He often uses this term in his music:\n\nBig Tonka, big Tonka, big Tonka, big Tonka, big Tonka\n\n\nYeat on “Big tonka”\n\n\n\n\nI just pulled up in a Tonka with all of the minions, we takin' a picture (Ooh, ah-ooh)\n\n\nYeat on “Rich Minion”\n\n\n\n\nHe also already used the term for many titles, such as “Big tonka”, “Tonka”, “Tonka 2” or “King Tonka”.", "annotation_id": "26558318", "url": "https://genius.com/26558318", "state": "accepted", "votes": 83, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "line": "Hittin’ number one up on these charts, bitch, yeah, it’s stuck as fuck A-A-All we do is just go number one, huh (Hey, hey, hey)", "vault_lines": ["Hittin' number one up on these charts, bitch, yeah, it's stuck as fuck"], "meaning": "Yeat reflects on his success. Even as a newcomer to the rap game, he proclaims to be dominating the music charts. These wouldn’t be farfetched claims, as, throughout late 2021 and 2022 alone, Yeat has:\n\n\nMade his first ever Billboard 200 entry with September 2021’s Up 2 Më, placing at #183.\nDebuted at #6 on the Billboard 200, as well as #3 on Billboard’s US Top R&B/Hip-Hop Albums with his February 2022 album 2 Alivë.\nScored a song apart of Illumination Entertainment’s Minions: The Rise of Gru film, titled “Rich Minion.” It was accompanied by a trailer directed by Cole Bennett.\nMade his first festival appearance for Lyrical Lemonade’s 2022 Summer Smash Festival.\nMany of his songs went viral on TikTok, including the aforementioned “Rich Minion” and more, building anticipation for his next releases.", "annotation_id": "26249239", "url": "https://genius.com/26249239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Talk", "status": "done", "targets": 16, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-talk-lyrics", "genius_title": "Talk", "genius_id": 8106473, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Taliban", "line": "Ayy, I just walked in with the Taliban", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, I just walked in with the Taliban (Woo)"], "meaning": "Contrary to popular belief, the origin of the name “Taliban” doesn’t come from the organization. It comes from this song and the terrorist organization in Afghanistan was a big fan of Yeat so they decided to name their group after their favourite Yeat track on 2alive.", "annotation_id": "40209951", "url": "https://genius.com/40209951", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Taliban", "line": "I just walk in with the Taliban", "vault_lines": ["I just walk in with the Taliban"], "meaning": "According to many credible resources, the Taliban are a highly dangerous terrorist organization. So him walking with them could mean that he be dangerous too fr.", "annotation_id": "40209932", "url": "https://genius.com/40209932", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Taliban", "line": "I don’t know what the fuck you thought this was (Ugh) I don’t know what the fuck you thought this was ’cause you not nobody (Ugh) I don’t know what the fuck you thought this was, ho, not yo’ buddy (Ugh) I don’t know what the fuck you thought this was, ho, you don’t got no money", "vault_lines": ["I don't know what the fuck you thought this was (Ugh)"], "meaning": "he doesnt know what u thought that was bru", "annotation_id": "33568730", "url": "https://genius.com/33568730", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Taliban", "line": "Poured a three in that bitch, that bitch bleedin’ (Ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Poured a three in that bitch, that bitch bleedin' (Ayy)"], "meaning": "“Poured a three” This refers to pouring a three of lean which in slang is a term for a mixture of prescription cough syrup containing codeine and promethazine with soda. The three is the amount of syrup (in ounces) being consumed.\n“that bitch bleedin’” This expression is indicating that the drink is potent or having strong effects as it is an opioid a class of drug known for potent highs.", "annotation_id": "33203418", "url": "https://genius.com/33203418", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Taliban", "line": "Is you doing what I told you? Is you doing what I said? (Ayy) It ain’t shit for me to hold you, all I do is count the bread (Go)", "vault_lines": ["Is you doing what I told you? Is you doing what I said? (Ayy)"], "meaning": "“Is you doing what I told you? Is you doing what I said?”\n- This line suggests a demand for compliance and highlights the speaker’s expectation that the other person should adhere to their guidance.\n\n“It ain’t shit for me to hold you, all I do is count the bread.”\n- “hold you” implies emotional support, while “count the bread” refers to getting money or wealth. Yeat implies that his focus is primarily on financial gain rather than emotional connections.\n\nThese lyrics revolve around authority, expectations in relationships, and prioritizing material success over personal connections.", "annotation_id": "33203367", "url": "https://genius.com/33203367", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Taliban", "line": "We just been sending out packs And we just be high all day", "vault_lines": ["We just been sending out packs"], "meaning": "“We just been sending out packs”\n– This likely refers to distributing packages dealing with illegal substances.\n“And we just be high all day”\n– This line suggests that Yeat is under the influence of drugs for most of the day.\n\nThese lyrics reflect on drug dealing and substance use.", "annotation_id": "33203273", "url": "https://genius.com/33203273", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Taliban", "line": "I’m on the phone with my demon", "vault_lines": ["I'm on the phone with my demon"], "meaning": "His demon(s) are taunting him once again as he tells us in multiple other songs.", "annotation_id": "30488954", "url": "https://genius.com/30488954", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
