{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Taliban", "line": "Ayy, I just walked in with the Taliban", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, I just walked in with the Taliban (Woo)"], "meaning": "Yeat may be referring to the way he has affected the fashion sense of his many supporters and listeners. Yeat commonly wears a head scarf that covers his face which he calls a “Turban”. Since Yeat became popular, wearing Turbans has also become a common dressing style among his fans and even among fellow “underground” artists. When Yeat says he walked in with the Taliban he is saying he is walking in to whichever establishment with a bunch of Turban rocking, Tris’ sippin, Twizzy demons.", "annotation_id": "25909218", "url": "https://genius.com/25909218", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
