{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "TURNMEUP", "line": "I don’t tell ‘em nothin’ ’cause they tell me that I’m crazy (Crazy)", "vault_lines": ["I don't tell 'em nothin' 'cause they tell me that I'm crazy (Crazy)"], "meaning": "In this lyric, Yeat may be expressing a reluctance to share his thoughts or emotions because he feels misunderstood or judged by others. Being labeled “crazy” could reflect his frustration with societal expectations and how people perceive his lyfestyle (heh) and mindset. This suggests a disconnect between his true self and how others interpret his actions, leading him to keep things to himself to avoid other people bullshit.", "annotation_id": "33390532", "url": "https://genius.com/33390532", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
