{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "THE MARTIAN", "line": "You don’t gotta, be honest Bitch, I’m right where I wanna be", "vault_lines": ["You don't gotta lie, just be honest"], "meaning": "Here, Yeat shuts down any outside noise or criticism by making it clear that he’s exactly where he wants to be. Whether it’s his place in the rap game, his financial freedom, or his overall life, he’s totally comfortable running things on his own terms without caring about anyone else’s approval.", "annotation_id": "41563006", "url": "https://genius.com/41563006", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "THE MARTIAN", "line": "Bounce up and down like hydraulics", "vault_lines": ["Bounce up and down like hydraulics"], "meaning": "Yeat compares the repetitive up-and-down motion of oral sex to the movement of hydraulic systems, which are commonly used to raise and lower vehicles or heavy machinery.", "annotation_id": "40650855", "url": "https://genius.com/40650855", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "THE MARTIAN", "line": "Bitch, I’m the general I’m the Tonka General, huh", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm the general"], "meaning": "“Tonka” is one of Yeat’s recurring names for himself and his lifestyle, originally inspired by Tonka trucks and later connected to large, powerful vehicles.\n\nBy calling himself the Tonka General, Yeat presents himself as the leader of the people and culture surrounding his Tonka persona.", "annotation_id": "40650177", "url": "https://genius.com/40650177", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "THE MARTIAN", "line": "Yeah, I’m fly like a comet be", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I'm fly like a comet be"], "meaning": "Yeat compares himself to a comet, continuing the song’s space theme established by the title “MARTIAN” and the repeated references to Martians in the intro.\n\n“Fly” can also mean stylish or impressive, giving the line a second meaning.", "annotation_id": "40650167", "url": "https://genius.com/40650167", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "THE MARTIAN", "line": "I was just shoppin’ at Barneys I was just shoppin’ at Barneys", "vault_lines": ["I was just shoppin' at Barneys"], "meaning": "Barneys is a luxury department store known for designer clothing. The brand is a cultural staple for high end fashion streetwear spending. While the New York location was shut down due to bankruptcy the Japan location remains open today.", "annotation_id": "40598062", "url": "https://genius.com/40598062", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
