{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "THE COSTËS", "line": "I just hit the Chilt’, we in London", "vault_lines": ["I just hit the Chilt', we in London"], "meaning": "The Chilt' refers to The Chiltern Firehouse, a luxurious 5-star hotel located in the heart of London, UK. Staying at this hotel costs nearly $1,000 USD per night.", "annotation_id": "34020867", "url": "https://genius.com/34020867", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "THE COSTËS", "line": "If my neck could talk to me, all he would say is, “Brr”", "vault_lines": ["If my neck could talk to me, all he would say is, \"Brr\" (Woo)"], "meaning": "Yeat is referring to that his neck would be saying “Brr” because it is “icy” because of his jewelry.", "annotation_id": "33511683", "url": "https://genius.com/33511683", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "THE COSTËS", "line": "I just pulled up out to Paris, Costes what it cost her (Yeah, her)", "vault_lines": ["I just pulled up out to Paris, Costes what it cost her (Yeah, her)"], "meaning": "Costes is a 5-star hotel in Paris where Yeat stayed in early 2024. The visit gained significant attention because Playboi Carti was also staying at the hotel at the same time.", "annotation_id": "33337773", "url": "https://genius.com/33337773", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "THE COSTËS", "line": "Big boy Tonka, yeah, bring that tractor in", "vault_lines": ["Big boy Tonka, yeah, bring that tractor in"], "meaning": "Yeat is using “Tonka” to refer to big body luxury SUVs, which he often mentions in his lyrics. By saying “bring that tractor in” he’s making another reference to the actual Tonka brand, known for its tough and durable toy trucks & tractors. This emphasizes the heavy-duty power of these luxury vehicles.", "annotation_id": "33324560", "url": "https://genius.com/33324560", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "THE COSTËS", "line": "If my neck could talk to me, all he would say is, “Brr” (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["If my neck could talk to me, all he would say is, \"Brr\" (Woo)"], "meaning": "In rap culture jewelry is often referred to as “ice” because of its shiny, glistening appearance, similar to ice. The “brr” sound is similar to what someone would say if they are cold like ice and this emphasizes the coolness and high value of his expensive jewelry.", "annotation_id": "33324463", "url": "https://genius.com/33324463", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "THE COSTËS", "line": "Yeah, shut your mouth, “Shh” what the cops heard", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, shut your mouth, \"Shh\" what the cops heard"], "meaning": "Yeat is warning people to stay silent and not inform the police about his activities. He’s emphasizing the importance of not snitching to avoid getting into trouble with the authorities.", "annotation_id": "33324435", "url": "https://genius.com/33324435", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
