{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "TELL U AGAIN", "line": "Hublot, Richard Mil’, yeah, I’m still pourin’ dirt", "vault_lines": ["Hublot, Richard Mil', yeah, I'm still pourin' dirt"], "meaning": "In this bar Yeat claims he has a “Hublot Richard Millie” Which is a luxury watch but he still indulges in “Pourin' dirt” Which is another way of saying he is drinking illegal substances like codeine/promethazine which is a reoccurring theme in Yeats music. For example his 2nd song on his debut studio album “Up 2 Me” is called “Mornin Mudd' Which is all about how he is addicted to these substances.", "annotation_id": "28566152", "url": "https://genius.com/28566152", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
