{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sïck", "line": "I signed a deal for a lil’ seven mil’ and I told ‘em I’m still gon’ evolve", "vault_lines": ["I signed a deal for a lil' seven mil' and I told 'em I'm still gon' evolve"], "meaning": "Yeat’s evolution and the foreshadowing before it is an odd yet distinguishable theme in his discography, with his manager Zack Bia mentioning Yeat predicting and achieving his accomplishments as an artist in an interview. In these lines, Yeat foreshadows his evolution as an artist, and is possibly related to his switch of genre with the release of his 2024 album, 2093.", "annotation_id": "30848990", "url": "https://genius.com/30848990", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sïck", "line": "I made a company, I started rentin’ some cars and I made me a whole lot of racks", "vault_lines": ["I made a company, I started rentin' some cars and I made me a whole lot of racks"], "meaning": "In this lyric, Yeat is showing off his entrepreneurial talent, by telling the story of how he started his business renting cars, and how that accelerated his wealth to pursue music, which in turn made him extraordinarily more wealthy.\n\n(I assume he’s talking about running cars on TURO, I don’t think he just said I made a company, then I started renting cars to drive, I think he’s talking about a business he pursued)", "annotation_id": "30372632", "url": "https://genius.com/30372632", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
