{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Systëm", "line": "Ain’t even fuck with nobody at all, lil’ bitch, I just rock with the gang (Gang) Ain’t ever switch on my bro or my twizzy, lil’ bitch, I am stayin’ the same (Go, same, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["They can't even fuck with the gang (Gang)"], "meaning": "Noah has said many times that he keeps his circle very small and doesn’t like communicating with people, and doesn’t really like social media too much either", "annotation_id": "28179649", "url": "https://genius.com/28179649", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Systëm", "line": "The kid said that he ’bout to pull up and shoot some shit, yeah, he got some nerve", "vault_lines": ["The kid said that he 'bout to pull up and shoot some shit, yeah, he got some nerve"], "meaning": "Yeat’s opps are bluffing and claiming that they’re gonna come shoot him. He thinks they’re full of shit.\n\nThis might refer to the “lil kid” mentioned later in the song.", "annotation_id": "27918971", "url": "https://genius.com/27918971", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Systëm", "line": "They can’t be fuckin’ with my slang (Swoop)", "vault_lines": ["They can't be fuckin' with my slang (Swoop)"], "meaning": "Yeat is referring to all the slang he has created such as: “Luh crank”, “Luh twizz”, “Twizzy”, “Yonky”, “Smöoktober” and much more.", "annotation_id": "26694989", "url": "https://genius.com/26694989", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Systëm", "line": "Just poured up a deuce of the Wock’ with a one-eighth of red for the foot of my Sprite (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Just poured up a deuce of the Wock' with a one-eighth of red for the foot of my Sprite (Yeah)"], "meaning": "“Wock'” is slang for the global pharmaceutical company Wockhardt. To “pour up a deuce” alludes to a cough syrup based drink which contains a combination of codeine and promethazine and notably, both used to create lean.\n\n\n\nPictured: Lean.\n\nLean is a liquid that consolidates a series of drugs to produce a purple-colored drink, serving the effect of instability and more. “One-eight of red for the foot” denotes the syrup sinking to the bottom of drink, which in his case, is the “foot” of the drink.", "annotation_id": "26694667", "url": "https://genius.com/26694667", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Systëm", "line": "I got a big ol’ Glock with a switch (Yeah) You gon’ get you a mop (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I got a big ol' Glock with a switch (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat alludes to a “Glock switch” or simply known as a “switch.” Adding the small attachment to handguns—converts the firearm into a fully automatic, which is largely utilized by gang members.\n\n\n\nPictured: A Glock with a switch attachment.\n\nArguably, Yeat sends potential threats—possibly toward an enemy—thus addressing the aftermath as he proclaims that he’d create a mess when the gun is fired.", "annotation_id": "26694539", "url": "https://genius.com/26694539", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Systëm", "line": "Lil’ kid talkin’ that shit (Yeah), now he can’t say no words", "vault_lines": ["Lil' kid talkin' that shit (Yeah), now he can't say no words"], "meaning": "Opp talked shit and was killed or had his tongue cut out.", "annotation_id": "26667923", "url": "https://genius.com/26667923", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Systëm", "line": "Been in the coupe, Bruce Wayne", "vault_lines": ["Been in the coupe, Bruce Wayne"], "meaning": "Bruce Wayne—Batman’s alter-ego—is known for driving luxurious cars such as his famous Batmobile, adapted throughout many films. Yeat compares himself to Bruce Wayne, as the two can be spotted in high-end vehicles.", "annotation_id": "25203176", "url": "https://genius.com/25203176", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
