{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Still did it", "line": "I told ’em wipe it off your feet and dip the pool with ’em (Yeah, ha-ha)", "vault_lines": ["I told 'em wipe it off your feet and dip the pool with 'em (Yeah, ha-ha)"], "meaning": "Yeat continues the theme of being overwhelmed by annoying energy around him. Telling someone to “wipe it off your feet” suggests they should leave behind the negativity they’re bringing into his space. But instead of a normal, respectful action like removing shoes, he exaggerates the flex by saying they can “dip the pool with ’em” — walking straight into a luxury pool with their shoes on.", "annotation_id": "37440209", "url": "https://genius.com/37440209", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
