{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Stay Up", "line": "The money keep callin’, I know it’ll come", "vault_lines": ["The money keep callin', I know it'll come"], "meaning": "Yeat has manifested his success since his inception as a rapper in early 2017. In an interview with his manager, Zack Bia, he admits that Yeat has essentially foreshadowed his popularity as an underground artist, and fans didn’t let this go unnoticed, with one Reddit user noticing that Yeat had mentioned that 2020 was going to be his era as an underground artist on “Intro 2022”, which proved to be true following the release of Wake Up Call in January of 2019:\n\nI know that in twenty plus twenty, in my era, it’s a whole new decade and shit", "annotation_id": "30760886", "url": "https://genius.com/30760886", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Stay Up", "line": "But I’m still countin’ these pesos", "vault_lines": ["But I'm still countin' these pesos"], "meaning": "This could be a reference to Yeat’s Mexican heritage. The Peso is Mexico’s currency, and is also used widely throughout Latin America.", "annotation_id": "25224766", "url": "https://genius.com/25224766", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
