{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Split", "line": "I want Bentley, I want money I want Bentley, I want money", "vault_lines": ["Bentley, I want Bentley, I want— (Yeah-ah-ah, yeah)"], "meaning": "These lyrics show to us that Yeat is consumed with wants. A bentley and an excessive amount of money is a want and is not necessary in life. The repetition of the line emphasises how desperate he is for these wants and is engulfed by his inate greed and selfishness. This can also be linked to his concerning substance abuse problems. The ‘percs’ and ‘lean’ have corrupted his mind", "annotation_id": "28898921", "url": "https://genius.com/28898921", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Split", "line": "I want Bentley, I want money I walk in, they want my money", "vault_lines": ["Bentley, I want Bentley, I want— (Yeah-ah-ah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat is mocking those who look at him solely for his amounts of monëy and furthermore try to take him for granite.", "annotation_id": "28898920", "url": "https://genius.com/28898920", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
