{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Split", "line": "I’m in this motherfuckin’ drop-top, bitch, that drop-top, bitch, stay swervin’ the ’Cat (Ah)", "vault_lines": ["I’m in this motherfuckin' drop-top, bitch, that drop-top, bitch, stay swervin' the ’Cat (Ah)"], "meaning": "Possibly in relation to Hell Cat, a famous brand of car, which he is swerving with.\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: YEAT has been known to reference service vehicles like Caterpillar (CAT) and Bobcats, and the fictional Tonka brand.", "annotation_id": "27976129", "url": "https://genius.com/27976129", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Split", "line": "I’m in this motherfuckin’ drop-top, bitch, that drop-top, bitch, I’m swervin’ the ’Cat (Ah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm in this motherfuckin' drop-top, bitch, that drop-top, bitch, I'm swervin' the 'Cat (Ah)"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying he’s swerving in a “big cat” this is a reference to the British auto company Jaguar. He’s saying he has so much money that he can “swerve” a luxury car such as a jaguar", "annotation_id": "27947651", "url": "https://genius.com/27947651", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
