{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Split", "line": "(CHASETHEMONEY, CHASETHEMONEY)", "vault_lines": ["Bentley, I want Bentley, I want— (Yeah-ah-ah, yeah)"], "meaning": "CHASETHEMONEY is a St. Louis producer, who has a specific “808” drum sound under his name, respectively called the “CHASETHEMONEY 808” or “ctm 808”. The significance of this sound is that many Yeat songs, especially those who have blown up, have the ctm 808 in them. Making the ctm 808 a staple for Yeat type beats and even other artists.\n\nSome songs that have the ctm 808 in them are:\n\nDoublë – https://youtu.be/qx3qTrTTZwg\n\nTalk: https://youtu.be/7Qe6qcNuyYY\n\nWay back: https://youtu.be/Y5fSW5Y8MHE\n\nRich Minion: https://youtu.be/7fX2kMaiMGI", "annotation_id": "27879679", "url": "https://genius.com/27879679", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
