{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sorry Bout That", "line": "She said, “I wanna watch a movie if you get the picture” (Ha)", "vault_lines": ["She said, \"I wanna watch a movie if you get the picture\" (Ha)"], "meaning": "This relates to the phrase “Netflix and chill,” which means to have sex. So basically, she subtly wants to have sex with him without having to ask him outright.", "annotation_id": "28458662", "url": "https://genius.com/28458662", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sorry Bout That", "line": "(Damn, Trgc made that?)", "vault_lines": ["She eat me up like it's Beni-bachi"], "meaning": "This is the producer tag of music producer and songwriter Trgc. He is a frequent collaborator of Yeat’s, producing notable Yeat songs such as “Rackz Got Me”, “Money Twerk”, and “Money So Big” and is even signed to Yeat’s record label Twizzy Rich Entertainment.\n\nIn addition to his work with Yeat, Trgc has worked with artists like Lil Uzi Vert, Summrs, and SoFaygo.", "annotation_id": "27805055", "url": "https://genius.com/27805055", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sorry Bout That", "line": "She said she feel it now, I don’t even feel it though Bitch, I be high on these drugs every day of my life I don’t know at all if I should quit or not (Woo, woo) How the fuck could I choose if this is bad for me When everything goin’ out sad on my life?", "vault_lines": ["I don't know at all if I should quit or not (Woo, woo)"], "meaning": "Although Yeat has risen to fame, his life isn’t much better than it was before. He is enjoying himself, but at the end of the day, his mental health is still poor. He copes with his problems by using drugs, resulting in a high tolerance in comparison to an average person.", "annotation_id": "25585589", "url": "https://genius.com/25585589", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sorry Bout That", "line": "I’m sorry for you, kid, that’s just your life (Ha, life)", "vault_lines": ["I'm sorry for you, kid, that's just your life (Ha, life)"], "meaning": "This reminds me of the old meme where the kid had a bad cut and the guy was roasting him.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bVyBJqsH9BE", "annotation_id": "24585246", "url": "https://genius.com/24585246", "state": "pending", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sorry Bout That", "line": "She said she need a big ol’ booty, called up Bob the Builder (Ha)", "vault_lines": ["She said she need a big ol' booty, called up Bob the Builder (Ha)"], "meaning": "“Can We Fix It?” is the theme song of the childrens' television program Bob the Builder. The plot of every Bob the Builder episode has Bob fix something. Yeat dismisses her issue, satirically implying that he called up Bob the Builder to fix his girl’s problem (i.e., he did nothing about the issue).", "annotation_id": "23998188", "url": "https://genius.com/23998188", "state": "accepted", "votes": 95, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sorry Bout That", "line": "Yeah, and they just told me, if I bought that Tesla I’m helpin’ the climate so I’m finna pop a hundred (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, and they just told me, if I bought that Tesla"], "meaning": "Yeat uses a double entendre, mentioning the Tesla car manufacturers and the Tesla ecstasy pills. Tesla cars are known for their economic benefits due to their electric vehicles, which reduce gas emissions. Rather than purchasing a Tesla car, Yeat would take a hundred Tesla pills to save the climate instead.\n\nHe uses the same wordplay on his March 2021 track “Tesla” with SeptembersRich, rapping:\n\nI can tell when I’m just high up off this Tesla, way I’m driving", "annotation_id": "23707036", "url": "https://genius.com/23707036", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sorry Bout That", "line": "I’m not a kid, I’m a man like Pacqui (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm not a kid, I'm a man like Pacqui (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat is referring to the Filipino boxer and politician Manny Pacquiao", "annotation_id": "23696063", "url": "https://genius.com/23696063", "state": "pending", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sorry Bout That", "line": "They told me that I murder every beat like Columbine (Bop-bop-bop-bop) Sorry ’bout that", "vault_lines": ["Sorry 'bout that (Phew, phew)"], "meaning": "On April 20, 1999, Eric Harris and Dylan Klebold committed a school shooting and attempted bombing, murdering 12 students and a teacher at their school Columbine High School. Yeat violently plays off this massacre by saying he “murders\"—or performs exceedingly on—every beat, the same way the Columbine shooters murdered their victims.\n\nWhether intentional or not, Yeat then raps “Sorry ‘bout that” to apologize for the controversial bar.", "annotation_id": "23528475", "url": "https://genius.com/23528475", "state": "accepted", "votes": 154, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sorry Bout That", "line": "Bitch, I’ma sip on the Wock’ or the Tris (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'ma sip on the Wock' or the Tris (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat explains that he will pour Wockhardt or Tris in his soda. Many lean connoisseurs prefer Wockhardt over Tris, but #RR and affiliates do not discriminate, some even prefer Tris over Wockhardt. Yeat is showing he does not care about the brand, he just wants to get high.\n\n“I literally don’t be carin bout Wock Tris hit harder”- KanKan via Twitter, 2021.", "annotation_id": "23508336", "url": "https://genius.com/23508336", "state": "pending", "votes": 64, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sorry Bout That", "line": "ATV what she ridin’ on (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["ATV what she ridin' on (Woo)"], "meaning": "An all-terrain vehicle, often referred to as an “ATV” is a light utility vehicle, with a seat that is straddled by the operator, along with handlebars for steering control.\n\n\n\nYeat likens the action of riding an ATV to his significant other riding on him during sex.", "annotation_id": "23382518", "url": "https://genius.com/23382518", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sorry Bout That", "line": "She eat me up like it’s Beni-bachi", "vault_lines": ["She eat me up like it's Beni-bachi"], "meaning": "Benihibachi is a food truck franchise located throughout the West Coast, particularly California. Yeat’s girl “eat’s him up,” or gives him fellatio in the same way she’d eat from Benihibachi.\n\n\n\nPictured: Benihibachi’s ‘New York Steak, Chicken & Shrimp Trio’", "annotation_id": "23382501", "url": "https://genius.com/23382501", "state": "accepted", "votes": 141, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
