{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Slimd Em Out", "line": "Yeah, yes I really been off this X, I’m crossing my X and O’s", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, yes I really been off this X, I'm crossing my X and O's"], "meaning": "This is a quadruple entendre with four distinct meanings:\n\n\nHe refers to ecstasy (the drug he’s on) as X.\nBy saying he’s crossing his letters, Yeat references the common idiom, “dot your I’s and cross your T’s,” which signifies extreme attention to detail and perfection in his actions.\nCrossing his X’s also means crossing his exes (his former romantic partners). In this use, “crossing” means betraying or cutting out his exes.\n“X’s and O’s” refers to the game Tic Tac Toe where you win by “crossing out” three X’s or O’s in a row. Yeat is saying he is playing the “game” of the industry and winning.", "annotation_id": "39596692", "url": "https://genius.com/39596692", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
