{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Slamm", "line": "I got ’em sick, Corona", "vault_lines": [", I got 'em sick, Corona"], "meaning": "Here Yeat references “Corona” also known as “Coronavirus” which is a type of virus that can cause respiratory illness in humans. The current strain, known as COVID-19, was first identified in 2019 and became a global pandemic. It spreads through respiratory droplets and close contact with infected individuals. Symptoms can range from mild to severe and can include fever, cough, and difficulty breathing. Prevention measures such as wearing masks, social distancing, and vaccination can help reduce the spread of the virus.", "annotation_id": "27879242", "url": "https://genius.com/27879242", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Slamm", "line": "Flamboyant", "vault_lines": ["You a bitch and you slow, heard you flamboyant"], "meaning": "Flamboyant, not reoffering to the dictionary definition (of a person or their behavior) tending to attract attention because of their exuberance, confidence, and stylishness. Though referring to when niggas be gay.", "annotation_id": "27879064", "url": "https://genius.com/27879064", "state": "pending", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
