{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sit bakk", "line": "I came in and I shitted on this beat, I took a turd (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["I came in and I shitted on this beat, I took a turd (Ooh)"], "meaning": "me", "annotation_id": "37877171", "url": "https://genius.com/37877171", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Sit bakk", "line": "All you rock is glass diamonds, call you Cinderella (Call you)", "vault_lines": ["All you rock is glass diamonds, call you Cinderella (Call you)"], "meaning": "In the story Cinderella, the main character of the same name’s glass slipper (created by her “dainty” grandparent) fell off of her foot at the stroke of midnight as she fled the King’s castle.\n\nThe listener (you), even after warned by fairytales that glass, in most situations is not a reliable or attractive, luring sign of wealth, proceeds to flaunt diamonds that aren’t even VVS or S.I quality, and Yeat takes it up to call them out on it.\n\nCalling diamonds that are of great quality “glass” can even be considered an insult, especially regarding engagement rings.", "annotation_id": "36851940", "url": "https://genius.com/36851940", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
