{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Simplë", "line": "You would crash out like a dummy if you was high as me (Mhm)", "vault_lines": ["You would crash out like a dummy if you was high as me (Mhm)"], "meaning": "This lyric shows exceptional wordplay from Yeat. He is referencing both crash test dummies and the popular term “crashout” used to denote people who have short tempers, which drugs tend to exacerbate.", "annotation_id": "39508234", "url": "https://genius.com/39508234", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
