{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Simon Says", "line": "Like Simon says, do what I said, to him (Told him ”Let’s go”)", "vault_lines": ["Like Simon says, do what I said, to him (Told him \"Let's go\")"], "meaning": "Simon says is a game where u have 2do what simon says 🐶", "annotation_id": "32313182", "url": "https://genius.com/32313182", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Simon Says", "line": "So much bread, it don’t make sense when you—", "vault_lines": ["So much bread, it don't make sense when you—"], "meaning": "“So much bread, it don’t make sense to him yet”, The phrase likely means that someone has acquired or encountered a large amount of money (or wealth), While someone else is having trouble understanding or processing it. They might be inexperienced with handling such wealth, leading to a sense of disbelief or confusion because he hasn’t seen so much money in his lifetime.", "annotation_id": "32250536", "url": "https://genius.com/32250536", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Simon Says", "line": "Guillotine his head and send his head to him", "vault_lines": ["Guillotine his head and send his head to him"], "meaning": "The guillotine is an apparatus designed for carrying out executions by beheading. It consists of a tall, upright frame from which a weighted and angled blade is suspended. The device became particularly famous during the French Revolution as a method of execution perceived to be humane and efficient.\n\nYeat is saying here, if he beheads someone he will send it to his friend", "annotation_id": "32250529", "url": "https://genius.com/32250529", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Simon Says", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-simon-says-lyrics", "genius_title": "Simon Says", "genius_id": 10599830, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Silk Facë", "line": "Run it back again, do that shit again Do that shit again, run it back, uh", "vault_lines": ["Run it back again, do that shit again"], "meaning": "In these lines, Yeat slurs his voice, deliberately avoiding his teeth to rely entirely on his soft palate. This continues his analogy in the previous line that those that “bite” his wave are “toothless”. This delivery is satirical mockery to caricature those clones.\n\nThe words “run it back again” and “do that shit again” continue to mock imitators that bite Yeat’s style, as they repeatedly beg for retries or more attempts to copy him. In this way, the “biters” are completely dependent and submissive to Yeat.", "annotation_id": "40115549", "url": "https://genius.com/40115549", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Silk Facë", "line": "I don’t really wanna brag I don’t even wanna brag no more (Yeah) I don’t wanna brag, I don’t wanna brag", "vault_lines": ["I don't really wanna brag"], "meaning": "Throughout Yeat’s rise in fame from 2021 to 2023, many of his songs feature bodacious bragging about his wealth, success, and women. Some of his older popular songs, like “Gët Busy” and “Got Rich,” show him bragging about his success.\n\nOn ADL, however, Yeat acknowledges his tendency to boast about these subjects and expresses a desire to move away from them. This is reflected in the following line, where he recognizes that he continues to boast about money despite wanting to change:\n\nAll this money that you never fuckin’ had\n\nThis idea is also explored in the album’s intro, “Purpose General,” where Yeat says he wants to make music according to his own preferences rather than focusing on chart performance:\n\nYeah, I’ma make the music that I want, give a fuck ’bout chartin’", "annotation_id": "39592232", "url": "https://genius.com/39592232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Silk Facë", "line": "Oh, I took a step away, yeah I play a different game, yeah Take a different game, yeah Save it for a different day, yeah (Huh) I seen it changin’, I seen what it take (Uh) I seen you changin’, I’m still the same (Uh) I seen what it take, uh Gotta help, it’s no more I can take, huh And I seen it take its shape (But)", "vault_lines": ["Oh, I took a step away, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat could be talking about drugs, he’s been taking them and he sees what they can do to you and he’s been going a different direction by not taking as much drugs as he did before or none at all.", "annotation_id": "39221273", "url": "https://genius.com/39221273", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Silk Facë", "line": "Can’t feel my face, icon", "vault_lines": ["Can't feel my face, icon"], "meaning": "The phrase “Can’t feel my face” is said a couple times in other Yeat records. For example the track “Tonka” from his album “Alive”. In that particular song he says “Eight AM, I took another one, can’t feel my face.” indicating the abuse of dr#gs. Although in this song (Silk Face) he does not mention dr#gs, his words before this phrase might indicate the use of them. Nevertheless phrase “Can’t feel my face” indicates use of dr#gs to a point of becoming numb.", "annotation_id": "39207376", "url": "https://genius.com/39207376", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Silk Facë", "line": "Seen you bite the wave, but you toothless", "vault_lines": ["Seen you bite the wave, but you toothless"], "meaning": "“Bite” can mean two different things.\nIn hip-hop, biting is the act of stealing or copying another artits rap style, flow, etc.\nOther rappers try to copy or steal yeat’s rap style or the wave he’s currently on, but they fail because they are toothless and can’t bite properly in a figurative sense.", "annotation_id": "39148575", "url": "https://genius.com/39148575", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
