{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Shhhh", "line": "I’m fuckin’ my money, I flew it to France", "vault_lines": ["I'm fuckin' my money, I flew it to France"], "meaning": "Yeat loves his money so much that he once again describes his connection to it in romantic and sexual terms.\n\nIn this line, Yeat declares that he has arrived in France with his money to spend or “fuck” it, likening the act to taking a girl out on a date during a trip abroad.", "annotation_id": "40830101", "url": "https://genius.com/40830101", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Shhhh", "line": "I pop a hundred Perkies, bitch, when I land", "vault_lines": ["I pop a hundred Perkies, bitch, when I land"], "meaning": "Yeat is on a plane while dosing on “Perkies” which refers to Percocet, which is a painkiller made by a combination of oxycodone and acetaminophen.", "annotation_id": "39268913", "url": "https://genius.com/39268913", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
