{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Shhhh", "line": "I mix the syrup with soda, yeah, and I had to mix it, lil’ bitch (Luh syrup)", "vault_lines": ["I mix the syrup with soda, yeah, and I had to mix it, lil' bitch (Luh syrup)"], "meaning": "“Syrup with Soda” refers to a drink commonly referrend in rap as “Lean” , “Purple Drank”, “Sizzurp” or “Dirty Sprite”. It is made by mixing prescription grade cough syrup  with an opoid drug and antihistamine drug with a soft drink(Sprite) or hard candy. Usually the syrup used is codeine or promethazine. Hazards include respiratory problems, slurred speech or even death.\n\nHere Yeat names lean as “Luh syrup” and talks about him preparing lean, something thats been mentioned plenty of times in his songs", "annotation_id": "39268880", "url": "https://genius.com/39268880", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Shhhh", "line": "Need no coupe, watch you sled (Uh)", "vault_lines": [", need no coupe, watch you sled (Uh)"], "meaning": "Yeat uses extreme imagery (“ISIS flag”) to emphasize a militant, intimidating presence when he arrives. He contrasts this with “need no coupe” suggesting he doesn’t rely on material flexes to assert dominance, and finishes by warning opponents that they’ll “sled,” implying they’ll be taken down or forced to retreat", "annotation_id": "39030484", "url": "https://genius.com/39030484", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
