{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Shhhh", "line": "Bullets make you spread, make you dead, cut yo’ head (Hol’ up)", "vault_lines": ["Bullets make you spread, make you dead, cut yo' head (Hol' up)"], "meaning": "The bullet to at yeat uses is probably 9mm: The most common caliber and widely-used ammo out there, the 9mm is often used as Glock™ ammo. . 380 ACP: Referred to as a “three-eighty,” this is usually seen in smaller handguns. How I know this is because back in September 9, 2021, yeat drops his album “Lÿfe” the second song on the list is “Up off X” now in this song yeat states “ Got two twin Glocks on my side like this” knowing that yeat uses Glocks, these are the bullets used in Glocks or smaller hand guns usually. Bullets are ejected out of the barrel of a gun and have enough power and pressure to go through your head. Your brain is located in your head in your skull. Which if a bullet travels through your brain you probably will parish on the spot. For a bullet to “cut yo head” it would have to go through your head pericing your skin. Which is another form of cutting.", "annotation_id": "31276892", "url": "https://genius.com/31276892", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
