{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "Uh, ’cause we fried all night (All night)", "vault_lines": ["Uh, 'cause we fried all night (All night)"], "meaning": "In this bar when yeat says he is “fried all night”, to clarify he is saying that he is feeling the effects of what we can assume the drug marijuana.", "annotation_id": "33498590", "url": "https://genius.com/33498590", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "“Shut your mouth, shut the fuck up,” I keep tellin’ ’em (Phew) “Shut the fuck up,” I keep tellin’ ’em (Shh) “Shut the fuck up,” I keep tellin’ ’em (Phew)", "vault_lines": ["Shh, \"Shut the fuck up,\" I keep tellin' 'em (Yeah)"], "meaning": "YEAT has faced a lot of adversity throughout his short career. In 2020-2021, YEAT exploded in popularity after   he was cosigned by Drizzy Drake. Back then, people were saying he would fall off soon, giving him about a year before it happened. There is also supposedly beef between YEAT and the 00pium label, mostly fueled by Lil88’s corny ass. We can assume that 00pium, or Ken Carson at the very least, perceive YEAT as a threat, since Ken Carson waited until the day YEAT dropped “LYFESTYLE” to release the music video for his hit single, “overseas”. Since his spike in popularity, YEAT has constantly been experimenting with new sounds, shown on the album “2093” and the EP “King Tonka”. This can also be seen here, as he integrated a sample of Memphis-style rapper 2 Low Key’s “Test My Nutz” into his instrumental, and with the new type of sound he used on BË QUIET.\n\nYEAT has prospered through all this adversity, with his message to his haters being “Shut the fuck up”, and as we can see, he keeps telling them this, as he repeats this message 3 times, and he does it again in the second chorus. resulting in a total of 6 times he says this. This message is often abbreviated to “STFU”, which happens to be the name of the song.", "annotation_id": "33396638", "url": "https://genius.com/33396638", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "Test", "vault_lines": ["Uh, we get fried, uh, yeah, all night, (Test sum')"], "meaning": "Touch? Thats what I hear", "annotation_id": "33379601", "url": "https://genius.com/33379601", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "Seen ’em turn on they own gang, own guys", "vault_lines": ["Seen 'em turn on they own gang, own guys"], "meaning": "Yeat expresses how he’s seen “fakes friends” betray their own friend group, implying he only interacts with close and true friends", "annotation_id": "33346846", "url": "https://genius.com/33346846", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "Seen ’em turn for a couple dollars, oh, surprise Seen ’em turn for a crack pipe and some fives", "vault_lines": ["Seen 'em turn for a couple dollars, oh, surprisе"], "meaning": "In these 2 lines Yeat disses someone who betrayed him and turn against him for couple dollars and for crack pipe – in a figurative sense, “crack pipe” represents device for using cocaine thru his steam.\n\nImage of crack pipe:", "annotation_id": "33336290", "url": "https://genius.com/33336290", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "I only need one person, bitch, myself", "vault_lines": ["I only need one person, bitch, myself"], "meaning": "Yeat could be saying here that he has no desire to impress any females other than Symone Ryley, showing his dedicated loyalty.", "annotation_id": "33323038", "url": "https://genius.com/33323038", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "It’s a geek party (Geek), so we geekin’ all night", "vault_lines": ["It's a geek party (Geek), so we geekin' all night"], "meaning": "The word ‘geek’ is used by Yeat many times and means high. By geekin all night, he means to be high all night.", "annotation_id": "33323012", "url": "https://genius.com/33323012", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "Test me, touch my things, and you die", "vault_lines": ["Test me, touch my things, and you die"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying here that he is highly possessive of his items, to the point where if you test and touch his items, he will kill you.", "annotation_id": "33322991", "url": "https://genius.com/33322991", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "Blind to your fuckin’ broke shit like braille (Like braille)", "vault_lines": ["Blind to your fuckin' broke shit like braille (Like braille)"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying he’s completely ignoring the person’s financial struggles, comparing his indifference to how braille allows blind people to read without seeing.", "annotation_id": "33322844", "url": "https://genius.com/33322844", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "Grindin’ your fuckin’ gears up like rail (Rail)", "vault_lines": ["Grindin' your fuckin' gears up like rail (Rail)"], "meaning": "This is a double entendre. “Grinding gears” refers to when gears are mismatched in speed or not engaged properly, often causing the teeth to be worn down. On the other hand, “grinding rail”, or railgrinding, is a skateboarding term for sliding along the edge of a rail.", "annotation_id": "33319285", "url": "https://genius.com/33319285", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "It’s a geek party, so we do what we like", "vault_lines": ["It's a geek party, so we do what we like"], "meaning": "The word “geek” used in this context means to get high. This line emphasizes the freedom and enjoyment of being intoxicated, where everyone is doing whatever they want without any restrictions.", "annotation_id": "33242875", "url": "https://genius.com/33242875", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "We was outside with the rag, like the Taliban (Shh)", "vault_lines": ["We was outside with the rag, like the Taliban (Shh)"], "meaning": "Yeat is likening himself and his crew to the Taliban by mentioning their headwear, specifically turbans. By “rag,” he refers to a turban, a piece of cloth wrapped around the head. This comparison suggests a militant and imposing presence, highlighting their readiness and dominance while out in public. The “Shh” implies that their actions were meant to be discreet or secretive.", "annotation_id": "32253658", "url": "https://genius.com/32253658", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "STFU", "line": "Fence full of-fence full of-fence full of pigs in the crowd Now who give a fuck? D-I-E, buster, I’m a OG, test my— (Test my—)", "vault_lines": ["Fence full of-fence full of-fence full of pigs in the crowd"], "meaning": "Vocal sample by 2 Low Key, taken from his first verse in his 1995 release, “Test My Nutz”—originally featured on his underground debut solo tape Test My Nutz:\n\nFence full of pigs in the crowd\nNow who give a fuck?\nD-I-E, buster, I’m a OG, test my nuts\n\nhttps://youtu.be/TCduxfGDs0k?si=ZAAIw8wYKjs9cwaM&t=74", "annotation_id": "31471724", "url": "https://genius.com/31471724", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
