{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SPEEDBALL", "line": "Stance, look at your motherfuckin’ stance, that’s why yo’ shit gon’ flop", "vault_lines": ["Stance, look at your motherfuckin' stance, that's why yo' shit gon' flop"], "meaning": "yeat disses rapper ian for his album valedictorian, where ian is standing funny", "annotation_id": "33380851", "url": "https://genius.com/33380851", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SPEEDBALL", "line": "I should put flags on the motherfuckin’ Maybach, yeah, watch it sail", "vault_lines": ["(Yeah) I should put flags on the motherfuckin' Maybach, yeah, watch it sail"], "meaning": "Putting flags on something means to claim it and has connotations of victory and triumph. The flags on the Maybach are compared to sails, likening the car to a yacht. Yachts are also luxurious assets, just like the Maybach.", "annotation_id": "33351442", "url": "https://genius.com/33351442", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SPEEDBALL", "line": "They can’t fuck with us, how ’bout you check the price on ’em? (Ah, ah, ah)", "vault_lines": ["They can't fuck with us, how 'bout you check the price on 'em? (Ah, ah, ah)"], "meaning": "Yeat is challenging others to compare their worth or status to his by looking at the high price of the items he owns, implying they can’t compare to him.", "annotation_id": "33323196", "url": "https://genius.com/33323196", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SPEEDBALL", "line": "I got the Bentley, I got this shit on my lights, I got all this shit on the drop (These lights, these lights)", "vault_lines": ["I got the Bentley, I got this shit on my lights, I got all this shit on thе drop (These lights, thesе lights)"], "meaning": "Bentley, a British luxury car company. Yeat is saying here that he has got a Bentley, and it is not the first time he has mentioned Bentleys, such as on Split.", "annotation_id": "33323186", "url": "https://genius.com/33323186", "state": "pending", "votes": -5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SPEEDBALL", "line": "Pull up in a Tonka, put them lights on ’em, lights on ’em (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Pull up in a Tonka, put them lights on 'em, lights on 'em (Yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Tonka is the term that Yeat refers to, usually being big body luxury SUV’s. These can be SUV’s such as Lamborghini Urus, Mercedes GLE, and Mercedes G-Wagon, all of which Yeat has owned/currently owns.", "annotation_id": "33323182", "url": "https://genius.com/33323182", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SPEEDBALL", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-speedball-lyrics", "genius_title": "SPEEDBALL", "genius_id": 10991873, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "Why am I paranoid? (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, woo) Uh, we got like fifteen in these pockets, ayy (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm)", "vault_lines": ["Why am I paranoid? (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, woo)"], "meaning": "Yeat often mentions symptoms and side effects of both his drug use (Lean & Percocets) and fame. Despite being so rich, he still carries a sense of unease, whether it be being plotted on, or simply being anxious (reasonably so)!\n\nAlso, the “fifteen in his pockets” has a double meaning: $15,000 in cash & 15 rounds in a clip.", "annotation_id": "41600522", "url": "https://genius.com/41600522", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "Not a La-Z-Boy, but your bitch reclinin", "vault_lines": ["Not a La-Z-Boy, but your bitch reclinin' (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, woo)"], "meaning": "La-Z-Boy is a renowned American furniture brand, best known for inventing the iconic, comfortable reclining chair in 1927", "annotation_id": "39240242", "url": "https://genius.com/39240242", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "I named my diamonds lil’ La Croix", "vault_lines": ["I named my diamonds lil' La Croix (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm)"], "meaning": "LaCroix is a popular brand of sparkling water known for its wide variety of fruit-flavored options, marketed as a healthy alternative to soda with zero calories, sweeteners, and sodium, flavored with natural essence oils", "annotation_id": "39240198", "url": "https://genius.com/39240198", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "I don’t wanna hear no, “Yeat, please, Yeat, this, Yeat, can you do this?” It’s been a silent Y-E-A-T since I had this cheese", "vault_lines": ["I don't wanna hear no, \"Yeat, please, Yeat, this, Yeat, can you do this?\""], "meaning": "This represents the pressure he receives from the industry and his fans; both want him to do certain things with his music, in addition to leaking it. The repetition of his name mimics how people always demand something from him.", "annotation_id": "37039933", "url": "https://genius.com/37039933", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "I’m livin’ comfortable, I paid the maid to make me breakfast It was one egg, two pieces of bacon, paid her eighty", "vault_lines": ["I'm livin' comfortable, I paid the maid to make me breakfast"], "meaning": "A ridiculous flex for overspending on something so trivial. Yeat is so wealthy that he can carelessly use it on things to be funny and memorable.", "annotation_id": "37039921", "url": "https://genius.com/37039921", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "Silly, told him that he’s broke, he can’t get in this rich party (Rich)", "vault_lines": ["Silly, told him that he's broke, he can't get in this rich party (Rich)"], "meaning": "Money over Status. Yeat frames wealth and financial status as the true ticket to “making it,” rather than simply having clout or being well-known.", "annotation_id": "37039917", "url": "https://genius.com/37039917", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "You a broke-ass oldhead, go hit retirement (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, go hit retirement, ayy)", "vault_lines": ["You a broke-ass oldhead, go hit retirement (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, go hit retirement, ayy)"], "meaning": "Yeat basically clowns the older generation of rappers and regular folk, telling them that their time is over, especially since they don’t like or understand the “new wave” of music that he’s helped create.", "annotation_id": "37039881", "url": "https://genius.com/37039881", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "They copy what I say, told ’em “Call me Simon” (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm), ayy", "vault_lines": ["They copy what I say, told 'em \"Call me Simon\" (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm), ayy"], "meaning": "A reference to the game “Simon Says”  and the fact that Yeat has influenced a wave of fans and underground and mainstream artists since 2021.\n\nPeople literally mimic his sound, production style, slang (“Twizzy,” “Tonka,” “Luh Geek,” etc.”) and style.", "annotation_id": "37039854", "url": "https://genius.com/37039854", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "Not a La-Z-Boy, but your bitch reclinin’ (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, woo)", "vault_lines": ["Not a La-Z-Boy, but your bitch reclinin' (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, woo)"], "meaning": "La-Z-Boy recliner chair + Sexual imagery", "annotation_id": "37039837", "url": "https://genius.com/37039837", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "I named my diamonds lil’ La Croix (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm) ‘Cause they sparklin’ in any climate (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm), ayy", "vault_lines": ["I named my diamonds lil' La Croix (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm)"], "meaning": "Here, Yeat compares his jewelry to the ‘La Croix’ Sparkling Water brand. It’s a metaphor that highlights the authenticity of his diamonds that shine under any light, something fake diamonds can’t do.", "annotation_id": "37039819", "url": "https://genius.com/37039819", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "Tinted windows, can’t see me while I’m drivin’ (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm), ayy", "vault_lines": ["Tinted windows, can't see me while I'm drivin' (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm), ayy"], "meaning": "Tinted windows represents his mysterious persona and need for privacy. He likes the idea of people “not seeing” him, both literally and figuratively.", "annotation_id": "37039811", "url": "https://genius.com/37039811", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "I got a brand new toy (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["I got a brand new toy (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, skrrt)"], "meaning": "The toy is a brand new tonka (car in Yeatnese).", "annotation_id": "37039782", "url": "https://genius.com/37039782", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "Why am I paranoid? (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, woo) Uh, we got like fifteen in these pockets, ayy (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm)", "vault_lines": ["Why am I paranoid? (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, woo)"], "meaning": "Yeat often mentions symptoms and side effects of both his drug use (Lean & Percocets) and fame. Despite being so rich, he still carries a sense of unease, whether it be being plotted on, or simply being anxious (reasonably so)!\n\nAlso, the “fifteen in his pockets” has a double meaning: $15,000 in cash & 15 rounds in a clip.", "annotation_id": "37039680", "url": "https://genius.com/37039680", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SOSAYEAT", "line": "Don’t play with him, my twin gon’ hit your ass with a bongo, shit got a drum on it (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, buh), ayy", "vault_lines": ["Why am I paranoid? (Mm-mm-mm-mm-mm, woo)"], "meaning": "Simple wordplay he uses to describe violence: “bongo” = drum = drum magazine (a part for guns/firearms)", "annotation_id": "37039626", "url": "https://genius.com/37039626", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
