{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SO WHAT", "line": "I got the Bentley goin’ overdrive", "vault_lines": ["I got the Bentley goin' overdrive"], "meaning": "Bentley Motors Limited is a British designer, manufacturer and marketer of luxury cars and SUVs. Headquartered in Crewe, England, the company was founded by W. O. Bentley in 1919 in Cricklewood, North London, and became widely known for winning the 24 Hours of Le Mans in 1924, 1927, 1928, 1929 and 1930.", "annotation_id": "33812117", "url": "https://genius.com/33812117", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SO WHAT", "line": "(So what?) And I’m fried, so what? (What?) And I’m high, so what? And I’m rich, so what? (Woo) And this bitch drink my nut (Yeah), and I’m lit, so what? (So what?) And I’m fried, so what? (What?) And I’m high, so what? (So what?)", "vault_lines": ["And I'm high, so what? And I'm rich, so what? (Woo)"], "meaning": "As opposed to 2093, Yeat makes it obvious in this track and thereby this album that he has started his use of substances again; albeit being relatively self-aware about it in later songs like FATË where there is clear acknowledgement of Yeat’s previous overdose and the damaging effects of drug abuse. SO WHAT is indicative of a return to the past from 2093’s future – a return to style, however with it comes Yeat’s drug issues. This chorus was also cited by Anthony Fantano as to be the evidence of being “indignant” of his struggles with substances.\n\nThose who praise 2093 for it’s movements in conceptual and experimental structure claim that Yeat’s sobriety played a big part in it’s creation, and LYFESTYLE as a whole shows a shift from a larger emphasis on experimentalism and moving backwards towards what made Yeat popular in the first place.", "annotation_id": "33509595", "url": "https://genius.com/33509595", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SO WHAT", "line": "Yeah, coming through in this big body Tonka, you ’posed to move", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, coming through in this big body Tonka, you 'posed to move"], "meaning": "Noah Smith (AKA Yeat) is saying in this bar that when he is passing by in his Tonka (A large SUV, e.g Bentley, Maybach, Range Rover), you better get out of the way because he WILL run you over. This could be interpreted in literal or figurative terms. In a figurative meaning, he could be saying he will pass you in terms of status or monetary reasons.", "annotation_id": "33354406", "url": "https://genius.com/33354406", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
