{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SMDP", "line": "Suck my dick, pussy Sex, money, drugs, power S.M.D.P S.M.D.P (S.M.D.P)", "vault_lines": ["Suck my dick, pussy"], "meaning": "Here Yeat showcases his ability to assign, while rapping, the multiple meanings of the acronym S.M.D.P as both “Suck My Dick, Pussy” and “Sex, Money, Drugs, Power”.", "annotation_id": "38694305", "url": "https://genius.com/38694305", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SMDP", "line": "Houston, I’m tryna leave Earth", "vault_lines": ["Houston, I'm tryna leave Earth"], "meaning": "This line references the Apollo 13 Mission. Specifically, it references a famous (albiet misquoted) line from the mission: “Houston, we have a problem.” By making this reference, Yeat metaphorically declares that he wants to transcend Earth, addressing Houston (the location of the famous Mission Control Center for the Apollo 13 Mission). This notion of leaving Earth also agrees with Yeat’s theme of being an extraterrestrial being, which he has consistently maintained throughout his career.", "annotation_id": "38050037", "url": "https://genius.com/38050037", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "SMDP", "line": "I’m a real species, I’m in danger", "vault_lines": ["I'm a real species, I'm in danger"], "meaning": "This is a reference to an endangered species, an animal species that is threatened with extinction. Yeat makes this comparison to convey his perceived peril or struggle to survive.", "annotation_id": "38049975", "url": "https://genius.com/38049975", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
