{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rëal six", "line": "Like a Trump man, could bleed your head", "vault_lines": ["Like a Trump man, could bleed your head"], "meaning": "Yeat violently intimidates his opponent, likely threatening to shoot them in the head — causing a rush of blood. He likens this to Donald Trump supporters, as Trump’s sloganed “Make America Great Again” hats are typically all red.", "annotation_id": "25214669", "url": "https://genius.com/25214669", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rëal six", "line": "I been on pills all day, MIA", "vault_lines": ["I been on pills all day, MIA"], "meaning": "After taking various prescription medications and losing his sense of awareness, Yeat goes MIA — an initialism for “missing in action.” The term is widely used as a designation given to those who go missing on the battlefield.", "annotation_id": "25171478", "url": "https://genius.com/25171478", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rëal six", "line": "All my pockets really filled up with some knots, yeah, bitch, they really breaded", "vault_lines": ["All my pockets really filled up with some knots, yeah, bitch, they really breaded"], "meaning": "Yeat continues to use wordplay as he refers to the “knots” of money in his pockets. He doubles down as he says they are “breaded”. This metaphor of bread refers to both money being called “bread” and ties in with garlic knots, a common form of bread served at many restaurants.", "annotation_id": "25168718", "url": "https://genius.com/25168718", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rëal six", "line": "My wrist livin’ underwater, might as well call this kelp", "vault_lines": ["My wrist livin' underwater, might as well call this kelp"], "meaning": "Yeat is implying that his wrist is “wet” and compares it to kelp, kelp is a type of flat brown seaweed that that forms underwater.", "annotation_id": "25163792", "url": "https://genius.com/25163792", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
