{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Run Thëy Mouth", "line": "If you talking to a god, keep it short and quick (Shh) I’m busy living all this life that you’ll never live", "vault_lines": ["If you talking to a god, keep it short and quick (Shh)"], "meaning": "Yeat implies that he is a god therefore he is too busy with his lavish lifestyle and personal endeavors to talk to anyone unless they get straight to the point with him.", "annotation_id": "30958102", "url": "https://genius.com/30958102", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Run Thëy Mouth", "line": "Told the coach to put me in ’cause I’m just tryna ball", "vault_lines": ["Told the coach to put me in 'cause I'm just tryna ball"], "meaning": "Yeat is tired of sitting on the bench and is ready to get in the game and ball out getting money, cars, clothes, and jewelry, but most importantly running the rap game.", "annotation_id": "30958062", "url": "https://genius.com/30958062", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Run Thëy Mouth", "line": "My body fiending for some dopamine", "vault_lines": ["My body fiending for some dopamine"], "meaning": "Dopamine is a neurotransmitter in the brain. It’s a chemical that our bodies make that give the brain and nervous system the ability to experience joy. It helps us focus, find things interesting, learn, etc. Yeat used to have an addiction to drugs, which can release a jolt of dopamine into the body, and his body got hooked to how it felt when he used drugs, so he’s experiencing withdrawal symptoms because he quit drugs.", "annotation_id": "30939196", "url": "https://genius.com/30939196", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
