{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Run Thëy Mouth", "line": "When you level up, you get the money like it’s Follywood", "vault_lines": ["When you level up, you get the money like it's Follywood"], "meaning": "“Follywood” a fake word made up by Yeat probably mean to imply that people and things in Hollywood are fake as he cleverly replaces the “H” in Hollywood with an “F”.", "annotation_id": "30898618", "url": "https://genius.com/30898618", "state": "pending", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Run Thëy Mouth", "line": "I was alive for 4L, but it’s up to me for after now", "vault_lines": ["I was alivе for 4L, but it's up to me for after now"], "meaning": "In this line Yeat uses his discography creatively to string together a bar, referencing four of his albums that really took him next level.\n\n\n\n Alivë album cover, Yeat 2021\n\nhttps://i.scdn.co/image/ab67616d0000b2732a2ca1ad79dd181c31e08c814L album cover, Yeat 2021\n\n\n\nUp 2 Më album cover, Yeat 2021\n\n\n\nAftërLyfe album cover, Yeat 2023\n\nYeat also maybe be possibly referencing the Now song at the end of the bar, featuring his alter-ego “Luh gëeky”\n\nAlso further disses Autumn! by using the same lyrical idea he had. “I was Alive for 4L, but it’s Up 2 Me for after now.” In Autumn!’s song “Two Chrome Necklaces!” he said “Feel 2 Alive, Imma be here 4L, mama told me they look Up 2 Me.”", "annotation_id": "30898392", "url": "https://genius.com/30898392", "state": "pending", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Run Thëy Mouth", "line": "I go up in every season, even in the fall I won’t talk about ’em, I just cut ’em off But they love to talk about me, love to run they mouth", "vault_lines": ["I go up in every season, even in the fall"], "meaning": "This appears to be a direct shot towards Autumn!, a rapper who influenced Yeat in early 2021 contributing to his style the same year of his rise to fame.\n\nYeat seems to be subliminally referring to Autumn! as “the fall”, insinuating that Autumn! is capped off at a peak while Yeat goes up every season.\n\nAutumn! repeatedly taking fake mugshots to get the perfect one.\nYeat started beefing with Autumn! In early 2021 after finding out he faked going to jail. The spark in conflict itself is unknown, however this led to Yeat dissing him on a song named 2x2 pt 2.\n\nMany of Yeat’s fans never noticed to point this out to Autumn!, likely because of the division between SLAYWORLD listeners and Yeat’s old fanbase.\n\nOn the other hand, Autumn! who thought they were still friends, dropped the infamous mEh remix, which resulted in being Yeat’s biggest song at the time, having 2 million plays that summer (now 8 million)\n\n\n\nLater that year when Kankan had beef with Autumn!, Yeat jumped back in on the action to call him out, which led to him becoming furious Yeat changed after giving him his then biggest song (bigger than Sorry Bout That and Gët Busy). Ever since the beef cooled down the following year and Autumn! supposedly moved on, he still has been referencing and sneak-dissing Yeat on various Instagram stories, and making diss songs such as Bentley Bentayga!, and We Ain’t Forget, even provoking Yeat with his signature bell on his song prompting Yeat to respond.", "annotation_id": "30884623", "url": "https://genius.com/30884623", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
