{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rollin", "line": "Where my Tes’? I just wanna ball", "vault_lines": ["Where my Tes'? I just wanna ball"], "meaning": "Tesla is a luxury motor-vehicle brand, known for their futuristic and high-quality vehicles. Since their prices are expensive to purchase a vehicle, Yeat is saying that he can still buy it despite the expensive price.\nFor reference, Tesla prices can range from $46,990 – $150,000.\n\n\n\nTesla Model X, most expensive Tesla model.\n\nYeat has also referenced the luxury motor-vehicle brand in other songs before; most notably, “Poppin” where he used the line:\n\nYou might catch me in the Tesla ‘cause it’s drivin’, I’m nodding off", "annotation_id": "25484239", "url": "https://genius.com/25484239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
