{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rokstar", "line": "All my brothers rich, still all we got is hundons", "vault_lines": ["All my brothers rich, still all we got is hundons"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that his brothers, slang for friends, are wealthy, having a large amount of money.\n\n\n\n“Hundons” is a slang term referring to a hundred thousand dollars.", "annotation_id": "28698470", "url": "https://genius.com/28698470", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rokstar", "line": "Bitch, this drank I got it’s real, I just cracked the seal", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, this drank I got it's real, I just cracked the seal"], "meaning": "“Drank” is a variation of the slang term “lean”.\n\n\n\nLean is a recreational drug beverage. It is a mixture of prescription cough or cold syrup, usually containing codeine and promethazine, mixed with a soft drink, such as Sprite. The drink is usually accompanied with hard candies, such as Jolly Ranchers, to make the drink taste sweeter.\n\nWhen Yeat says “I just cracked the seal”, he is referring to cracking open a pint bottle of cough medicine used to make the drink.", "annotation_id": "28698384", "url": "https://genius.com/28698384", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
