{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rokstar", "line": "Bitch, you ain’t touched a mil’, you don’t know how I feel", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, you ain't touched a mil', you don't know how I feel"], "meaning": "He’s saying to people with low cash, that they’ve never touched a million dollars physically, so they don’t correlate the same feelings as him.\n\nOR\n\nbruh yall aint touch a mil like me yet bruh, broke as niggas, touch a mil then talk to me.", "annotation_id": "25310285", "url": "https://genius.com/25310285", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rokstar", "line": "I’m a kickstand off this drank, bitch, I step in heels", "vault_lines": ["I'm a kickstand off this drank, bitch, I step in heels"], "meaning": "A kickstand is a metal rod attached to a two wheeled vehicle, usually a bicycle, and used to prop up the vehicle when it is not in use. When propped up, the vehicle is leaning.\n\nHeels is referring to high heels, a shoe with a raised heel that puts a tilt in wearer’s hips. This causes the hips to be leaning.\n\nYeat is drinking lean and then walks around, while leaning.", "annotation_id": "24992392", "url": "https://genius.com/24992392", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rokstar", "line": "Told that bitch to Bob the Build that booty if she really want one", "vault_lines": ["Told that bitch to Bob the Build that booty if she really want one"], "meaning": "It is implied that a woman asked Yeat to finance a plastic surgery procedure on her butt. In response, Yeat recommended that she work on getting a larger butt herself by referencing Bob the Builder. Bob is from an American children’s cartoon in which he is the main character who works as a construction expert who solves problems through building things.", "annotation_id": "23950857", "url": "https://genius.com/23950857", "state": "pending", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rokstar", "line": "I just hit LV with a twenty, I got zero now", "vault_lines": ["I just hit LV with a twenty, I got zero now"], "meaning": "Yeat ventured into famous luxury fashion brand Louis Vuitton with $20,000 and spent all of his money on clothing. Louis Vuitton is often shortened to ‘LV’ to match their famous monogram logo.", "annotation_id": "23950853", "url": "https://genius.com/23950853", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rokstar", "line": "Bitch, my bread hurt, I just bought a crib in the Hills", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, my bread hurt, I just bought a crib in the Hills"], "meaning": "Yeat just spent a lot of money on an abode in the world-famous Beverly Hills neighborhood in California. Bread is just American slang for cash, and it is only hurting because he had to spend so much of it in order to acquire the house", "annotation_id": "23950817", "url": "https://genius.com/23950817", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
