{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rockin It", "line": "Rockin it", "vault_lines": ["Rockin it, rockin it"], "meaning": "“Rockin it” is a contraction of the phrase “rocking it,” where “rocking” is a verb meaning “doing something with energy, style, or success.” Therefore, “rockin it” can be translated as “doing something with energy and style.” In this context, “it” refers to a specific task, activity, or situation that the person is engaged in or performing with energy and style.", "annotation_id": "31148893", "url": "https://genius.com/31148893", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rockin It", "line": "She sucking my blood, call her Count Dracula", "vault_lines": ["She sucking my blood, call her Count Dracula"], "meaning": "Count Dracula is a vampire, and vampires suck blood. Yeat could be referring to what he usually says he does with girls on his songs, or she could be sucking the money (blood) out of him.", "annotation_id": "29877134", "url": "https://genius.com/29877134", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
