{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Repent", "line": "I got plenty of fuckin’ morphine, yeah And I’m off a bean again, and again Sayin’ that you love me, it could be morphine", "vault_lines": ["I got plenty of fuckin' morphine, yeah"], "meaning": "It suggests numbness or escapism—using morphine or “beans” (ecstasy) to cope. “Sayin' that you love me, it could be morphine” hints at doubting the sincerity of emotions, wondering if they’re real or just dulled by substances", "annotation_id": "33510046", "url": "https://genius.com/33510046", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Repent", "line": "This that high in the club with the nosebleed", "vault_lines": ["This that high in the club with the nosebleed"], "meaning": "Yeat refers to the feeling of being under the influence of drugs at a club, “with the nosebleed” likely refers to the physical effect of snorting drugs, which can cause nosebleeds implying yeat has started snorting drugs to get higher.", "annotation_id": "33133037", "url": "https://genius.com/33133037", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Repent", "line": "(Woo) Told her ”Put it back in”, huh One (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["(Woo) Put your back in"], "meaning": "freak tonk", "annotation_id": "33129294", "url": "https://genius.com/33129294", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Repent", "line": "I was walkin’ round, I’m feindin’", "vault_lines": ["I was walkin' round, I'm feindin'"], "meaning": "Could be taken in many ways, especially with the lyrics above, though it is most likely it is Yeat further talking about his struggle with his addiction to drugs. Drugs could also be another thing he is “Repenting” for in the song.", "annotation_id": "33129289", "url": "https://genius.com/33129289", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Repent", "line": "Look up (Uh-uh-uh-uh-uh-uh-uh-uh) Repent my sins (Uh-uh-uh-uh-uh-uh-uh-uh)", "vault_lines": ["Repent my sins (Uh-uh-uh-uh-uh-uh-uh-uh)"], "meaning": "Yeat is talking about “Repenting his sins” meaning he is acknowledging what he did that was wrong and is remorseful for those actions. And the act of looking up is symbolizing him looking up to God as he repents.", "annotation_id": "33129271", "url": "https://genius.com/33129271", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Repent", "line": "I’ma sit back, reckon no one knows me", "vault_lines": ["I'ma sit back, reckon no one knows me"], "meaning": "“He mentioned a time when he was at the same club as Playboi Carti in Paris, but everyone acted like he was a ghost, completely ignoring him and only focusing on Carti.”", "annotation_id": "33094292", "url": "https://genius.com/33094292", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Repent", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-repent-lyrics", "genius_title": "Repent", "genius_id": 10484859, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rendezvous", "line": "Everything cool at the rendezvous", "vault_lines": ["Everything cool at the rendezvous"], "meaning": "“Rendezvous” is from the French word meaning an arranged meeting or a designated gathering spot. It literally translating to “you guys return”. Here, Don Toliver uses it to describe a private, exclusive meeting place, VIP section, or a late-night link-up.", "annotation_id": "41458971", "url": "https://genius.com/41458971", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rendezvous", "line": "I don’t play pretend, bitch, we really through (Yeah, yeah) Fuckin’ on this bitch and I got her screwed (Woah, woo, woo) Got this bitch sick like she got the flu, oh", "vault_lines": ["I'ma fuck this bitch, I fuck her off the shrooms (Yeah), woah"], "meaning": "Yeat tells the girl there’s no pretending or emotional facade, that whatever connection existed between them is already over.\n\nBoth “fucking on” and “screwed” derive from vulgar slang for having sex, so on the surface, Yeat is repeating the same idea using two different terms. In a broader social context, “to get somebody screwed” means to cheat, trick or leave somebody in a bad position. Yeat implies here that by the time he’s done with her, the girl is the one who loses.\n\nIn the third line, “sick” may carry layered meanings. Literally, it evokes illness which why he compares it to catching flu. Metaphorically, it can describe the feeling of anxiety or heartbreak. It can also be read as her being lovesick, overwhelmed and overtaken by Yeat’s lifestyle and wealth.", "annotation_id": "38623517", "url": "https://genius.com/38623517", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rendezvous", "line": "And she always wet, I call her wavy", "vault_lines": ["And she always wet, I call her wavy"], "meaning": "Yeat and Don use a double entendre in this bar. “Wet” is a common vulgar slang term for female sexual arousal. In the second half of the line, that idea flips into the word “wavy” which can literally relate to fluid but is more often used in hip-hop to describe someone who looks good, moves smoothly, or carries an appealing vibe.", "annotation_id": "38604308", "url": "https://genius.com/38604308", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
