{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Trendsettër", "line": "I don’t listen to nobody music but myself, that’s facts", "vault_lines": ["I don't listen to nobody music but myself, that's facts"], "meaning": "in a recent textbased interview with 032c magazine, yeat stated that he makes music primarily because he likes to listen to it, which makes him want to improve.\n\nhe also stated that he doesn’t really listen to other artists' music a lot unless they’re incredibly significant, for example, if drake were to drop an album, he’d listen to a couple songs.\n\nyeat also stated that the only music (other than his own ofc) that he really does listen to is “old-ass” music. in fact, one song he likes was made all the way back in the 1800s.", "annotation_id": "30555955", "url": "https://genius.com/30555955", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
