{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Trendsettër", "line": "Eah, you fail to get rich, yeah, you a government bum", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you fail to get rich, yeah, you a government bum"], "meaning": "In this lyric, Yeat is expressing his pure distaste for people who do not possess his entrepreneurial capabilities and musical talent, for acquiring large sums of wealth.\n\nHe resorts to calling them “government bums” for leeching off of government welfare cheques, EDDs or “stimmys”, and not working to obtain the wealth he has achieved.", "annotation_id": "30372567", "url": "https://genius.com/30372567", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
