{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Trendsettër", "line": "I see everybody make the same music, tryna sound like me (Yeah-uh-yeah) I see everybody make the same music, tryna sound like the—", "vault_lines": ["I see everybody make the same music, tryna sound like me (Yeah-uh-yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat explains that he sees everybody copying his flow and style to sound like him.\n\nTherefore, this explains why in the subsequent verse, he refers to himself as the “Real Trendsetter”", "annotation_id": "29621244", "url": "https://genius.com/29621244", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
