{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Life Shit", "line": "This my season to breathe Shit get too cold, it’s hard to sleep Like my Glock, I’m overloaded and I squeeze the trig’", "vault_lines": ["Like my Glock, I'm overloaded and I squeeze the trig'"], "meaning": "Lines that reinforce the overall theme of uneasiness and discomfort in Yeats life at the moment, referencing his struggles.\n\n(Maybe even those related to the relatively recent break up with Symone)", "annotation_id": "39204536", "url": "https://genius.com/39204536", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Life Shit", "line": "I’m lookin’ for a reason to tweak (Woo, woo, woo) I’m lookin’ for a reason to tweak (I tell, I tell, I tell)", "vault_lines": ["I'm lookin' for a reason to tweak (Woo, woo, woo)"], "meaning": "Yeat expresses built-up tension, suggesting he’s ready to snap or react at any moment. This line reflects instability beneath his confidence, showing that his aggression may be a response to internal pressure.", "annotation_id": "39149468", "url": "https://genius.com/39149468", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Life Shit", "line": "From this side lookin’ in, you just a square, your angles bendin’ right Ninety (Ninety), degrees, uh (Woo, woo, woo)", "vault_lines": ["From this side lookin' in, you just a square, your angles bendin' right"], "meaning": "Yeat uses geometric imagery to describe someone as rigid and predictable (“square”). The “90 degrees” line emphasizes conformity, contrasting with his own identity as someone who operates outside normal structure.", "annotation_id": "39149467", "url": "https://genius.com/39149467", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Life Shit", "line": "From this side lookin’ in, you just a square, your angles bendin’ right Ninety (Ninety), degrees, uh (Woo, woo, woo)", "vault_lines": ["From this side lookin' in, you just a square, your angles bendin' right"], "meaning": "Yeat uses geometric imagery to describe someone as rigid and predictable (“square”). The “90 degrees” line emphasizes conformity, contrasting with his own identity as someone who operates outside normal structure.", "annotation_id": "39149466", "url": "https://genius.com/39149466", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Life Shit", "line": "If I said that I was gon’ do it, then I’m gon’ do it, those words, I meant it", "vault_lines": ["If I said that I was gon' do it, then I'm gon' do it, those words, I meant it"], "meaning": "Yeat emphasizes authenticity and consistency, presenting himself as someone who follows through on his words. This contrasts with the emotional uncertainty shown earlier, suggesting he regains confidence by focusing on action over feeling.", "annotation_id": "39149457", "url": "https://genius.com/39149457", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
