{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Is rarë", "line": "I don’t know what I love more, the pink or blues?", "vault_lines": ["I don't know what I love more, the pink or blues?"], "meaning": "Yeat is most likely referring to 2 different pills of Oxycodone the pink being the 10mg K 56 pill made by KVK Tech while the blue being the 30mg M box pill made by Mallinckrodt or the 30mg K 9 pill also made by KVK Tech\n\nAlthough they all contain the same active compound many addicts have a preference on the specific pill itself thought to have better effects\n\nIt is possible Yeat is referring to Ecstasy/MDMA for the pink and Oxycodone for blue, this is uncertain", "annotation_id": "31968845", "url": "https://genius.com/31968845", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Is rarë", "line": "I don’t know what I love more, the pink or blues?", "vault_lines": ["I don't know what I love more, the pink or blues?"], "meaning": "Yeat is most likely referring to 2 different pills of Oxycodone the pink being the 10mg K 56 pill made by KVK Tech while the blue being the 30mg M box pill made by Mallinckrodt or the 30mg K 9 pill also made by KVK Tech\n\nAlthough they all contain the same active compound many addicts have a preference on the specific pill itself thought to have better effects\n\nIt is possible Yeat is referring to Ecstasy/MDMA for the pink and Oxycodone for blue, this is uncertain", "annotation_id": "31968734", "url": "https://genius.com/31968734", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Is rarë", "line": "They don’t got no drank, they sippin’ street juice", "vault_lines": ["They don't got no drank, they sippin' street juice"], "meaning": "In this line, Yeat is implying that the people he’s referring to don’t have access to legitimate or high-quality beverages, specifically mentioning that they don’t have any “drank” (slang for lean or cough syrup mixed with soda). Instead, they’re drinking what he calls “street juice,” which likely implies a lower quality or less desirable alternative.", "annotation_id": "31810138", "url": "https://genius.com/31810138", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Is rarë", "line": "I just be sitting back, I just be calculating Yeah, I just be counting up, I just be mathemating", "vault_lines": ["I just be sitting back, I just be calculating"], "meaning": "In these lines, Yeat is likely describing his mindset and approach to his finances and success. He’s portraying himself as someone who takes a strategic and analytical approach, always assessing his next move and calculating his gains. “Counting up” refers to tallying his earnings, while “mathemating” is a playful term he uses to convey his constant calculations and strategic thinking. Overall, he’s emphasizing his focus on wealth accumulation and success.", "annotation_id": "31810136", "url": "https://genius.com/31810136", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Is rarë", "line": "And when I sign my first deal, I need five mil’s, no budging (No)", "vault_lines": ["And when I sign my first deal, I need five mil's, no budging (No)"], "meaning": "Yeat is expressing his ambition and financial goals. He’s stating that when he signs his first record deal, he’s not willing to settle for anything less than five million dollars. This line underscores his confidence in his worth and the value he brings to the table as an artist.", "annotation_id": "31810133", "url": "https://genius.com/31810133", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Real Is rarë", "line": "Yeah, they stab you in your back, they right behind you", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, they stab you in your back, they right behind you"], "meaning": "Yeat could be referring to people who pretend to be supportive or friendly but ultimately betray you when you’re not looking. It suggests a sense of duplicity and deceitfulness in some relationships where individuals may act friendly to your face but harbor ill intentions behind your back.", "annotation_id": "31810128", "url": "https://genius.com/31810128", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
