{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rackz got më", "line": "Racks, racks (Yeah, okay) Racks, racks (Let’s get paid) Racks, racks Racks, racks, yeah, okay", "vault_lines": ["Racks, racks (Yeah, okay)"], "meaning": "Racks” is slang for large amounts of money, usually stacks of cash. Repeating the word emphasizes wealth, success, and financial obsession. The ad-libs like “let’s get paid” and “yeah, okay” reinforce a celebratory, confident mindset, framing money not just as income but as status and motivation.", "annotation_id": "38349289", "url": "https://genius.com/38349289", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rackz got më", "line": "Make a nigga bleed like a tampon, o-okay (Okay)", "vault_lines": ["Make a nigga bleed like a tampon, o-okay (Okay)"], "meaning": "The line uses a provocative simile to emphasize causing harm, comparing bleeding to a tampon for shock value. By pairing an image typically associated with femininity with violence, the rapper amplifies the sense of dominance and humiliation. The casual ad-lib afterward reinforces how effortless and unimportant the act feels to him.", "annotation_id": "38349279", "url": "https://genius.com/38349279", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
