{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rackz got më", "line": "Yeah, they been on rocks, on gravel Yeah, I’m on a whole ’nother level", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, they been on rocks, on gravel"], "meaning": "“Yeah, they been on rocks, on gravel”\n- This imagery shows a rough or difficult path.  As “Rocks” and “gravel” symbolize obstacles that others have faced.\n“Yeah, I’m on a whole ‘nother level”\n   - This indicates yeat feels superior compared to others.\n\nSo, the overall message is about Yeats’s success and overcoming obstacles, positioning himself above others who are struggling.", "annotation_id": "33203169", "url": "https://genius.com/33203169", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
