{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rackz got më", "line": "And if I give that lil’ pussy a chance I don’t know what they say behind my back And you know I ain’t goin’ for that", "vault_lines": ["Racks don't stab my back"], "meaning": "In this line yeat expresses how he cannot trust anyone. Stating “if I give that lil pussy a chance, I don’t know what they say behind my back” showing that he doesn’t like to give people chances. To continue this, in the next line he mentions “and you know I ain’t goin’ for that” inferring that he doesn’t like to trust people so he keeps his circle close only trusting people he has known for a long time.", "annotation_id": "30926009", "url": "https://genius.com/30926009", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Rackz got më", "line": "We rock chains, we stars", "vault_lines": ["We rock chains, we stars"], "meaning": "In this line yeat references how he has grown in popularity over the last few years. As well as how he has acquired large sums of money Allowing him to be able to afford expensive jewelry such as chains, watches, bracelets and more.", "annotation_id": "30925983", "url": "https://genius.com/30925983", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
