{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "Why you movin’ slow? This not a game, lil’ bitch, you lethargic", "vault_lines": ["Why you movin' slow? This not a game, lil' bitch, you lethargic"], "meaning": "“Lethargic” means being unusually slow, sluggish, or lacking energy.\n\nYeat uses the word literally after asking “Why you movin' slow?”, criticizing someone for not moving with enough urgency. By adding “this not a game,” he stresses that he views the situation seriously and expects the other person to keep up rather than act sluggish or unfocused.", "annotation_id": "41613127", "url": "https://genius.com/41613127", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "Yeah, I guess I paid the lease I guess I got this bitch hooked up, I got this bitch on leash Hmm, shh, we don’t do police Bitch, you look like easy target, we gon’ call you fleece", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I guess I paid the lease"], "meaning": "The passage conveys themes of financial success, personal control, discretion, and opportunism. It presents a persona who has the resources to maintain a comfortable lifestyle, exercises influence over those around him, avoids unnecessary attention from law enforcement, and recognizes individuals who may be vulnerable to being exploited. Overall, it emphasizes power, independence, and maintaining a guarded approach to one’s surroundings.", "annotation_id": "41352702", "url": "https://genius.com/41352702", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "Yeah, we can all see in, it’s me you breathin’ in", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we can all see in, it's me you breathin' in"], "meaning": "Yeat refers back to the previous line:\n\nYou in a glass box (Hey, yeah)\n\nHe’s saying that everyone can see into this metaphorical “glass box” of total visibility. The glass box representing this person wanting their lifestyle to be hidden away from judgement and public view so they put themselves inside this “box”, however this person hasn’t done a good job of this and this thought to be secure hide away from society is actually made of glass, meaning people can see into this persons life.\n\n…it’s me you breathin' in\n\nThis could be yeat’s way of saying this person is obsessed with him and that he and others can see that inside this “glass box” they can see she’s breathing him in(obsessing over him).", "annotation_id": "41004310", "url": "https://genius.com/41004310", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "I pull up, I don’t park it", "vault_lines": ["I pull up, I don't park it"], "meaning": "Yeat references valet parking, which is a service offered by many upscale restaurants and hotels in which a designated employee parks the customer’s car.", "annotation_id": "40839638", "url": "https://genius.com/40839638", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "We don’t gotta say nothin’ about it", "vault_lines": ["We don't gotta say nothin' about it"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying “We dont gotta say nothin about it” which is in regard to this song and more importantly ADL itself being so dogshit that it makes soul train sound good", "annotation_id": "40360700", "url": "https://genius.com/40360700", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "If you put your side to the pride, lil’ bitch, ain’t never gon’ say that", "vault_lines": ["If you put your side to the pride, lil' bitch, ain't never gon' say that"], "meaning": "Position yourself with your pride, you not gon hate on urself\n\nDifferent from putting pride to the side, which would be removing urself from ur pride", "annotation_id": "39288681", "url": "https://genius.com/39288681", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "Do it with purpose, do it with purpose", "vault_lines": ["Do it with purpose, do it with purpose"], "meaning": "To reach his fanbase, Yeat states “do it with purpose” references put your whole self into what you do like he does in this album.", "annotation_id": "39178206", "url": "https://genius.com/39178206", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "Yeah, all your money all paper thin, lil’ bitch, we call you parchment", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, all your money all paper thin, lil' bitch, we call you parchment"], "meaning": "In the previous bar, Yeat talks about his hard work and how it made him a lot of money, but then disses an unknown person(s) for having little to no money by calling it “thin” and relating it to parchment paper. Parchment paper is used for baking sheets, known for being very thin, even translucent.", "annotation_id": "39177876", "url": "https://genius.com/39177876", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "You like to talk online, but when you in person, you like, “You start it”", "vault_lines": ["You like to talk online, but when you in person, you like, \"You start it\""], "meaning": "Calling out people who hate on the internet saying stuff they would never say face to face. In person, these people lose their confidence and wait for him to make the first move because they’re intimidated.", "annotation_id": "39176824", "url": "https://genius.com/39176824", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "Yeah, we move like the mafia, dinner tables, conversations about it", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we move like the mafia, dinner tables, conversations about it"], "meaning": "In traditional mob structure, the most important decisions aren’t made on the street or in the club, they happen at the dinner table, where the family sits down to discuss business, settle disputes, and plan their next moves in private. By saying he “moves like the mafia,” Yeat is claiming that his career is now a highly organized operation built on high level strategy.", "annotation_id": "39176749", "url": "https://genius.com/39176749", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "You hate what you makin’", "vault_lines": ["You hate what you makin'"], "meaning": "A shot at artists who just chase trends and make music they aren’t proud of just to stay relevant.", "annotation_id": "39176713", "url": "https://genius.com/39176713", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "Yeah, I cut the roof off of the Maybach", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I cut the roof off of the Maybach"], "meaning": "Ye refrence, Yeat talked about how he has been recently getting inspired by Ye in his recent apple music interview he refrences the Otis music video", "annotation_id": "39168336", "url": "https://genius.com/39168336", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "Yeah, we can all see in, it’s me you breathin’ in", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we can all see in, it's me you breathin' in"], "meaning": "This line builds on the “glass box” imagery. “We can all see in” reinforces that sense of exposure, where people’s lives are constantly on display.\n\n“It’s me you breathin’ in” suggests Yeat’s influence and dominance is something unavoidable like air. He implies that his presence, sound, and lifestyle is omnipresent.\n\nFinally, this line also references his 2nd most played song on 2093, “Breathe”. This song was particularly popular on TikTok. This further reinforces the idea that Yeat is ubiquitous and that his influence isn’t just visible, but something people live in and consume daily.", "annotation_id": "39158150", "url": "https://genius.com/39158150", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "Yeah, we move like the mafia, dinner tables, conversations about it", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we move like the mafia, dinner tables, conversations about it"], "meaning": "Yeat compares his group to the mafia, which is culturally known for secrecy, loyalty, and big moves handled behind closed doors.\n\n“Dinner tables” references the classic movie image of mafia meetings happening over meals, where important decisions are made quietly. The line emphasizes that Yeat believes that real power doesn’t always need to be loud, and that he prefers “moves” that are planned and privately, without public discussion.", "annotation_id": "39158120", "url": "https://genius.com/39158120", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "Yeah, fuck that bundles, for that money, we go retarded (Bah, bah, bah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, fuck that bundles, for that money, we go retarded (Bah, bah, bah)"], "meaning": "Yeat doubles down on his statement on the bar before, and explains he doesn’t care about charting or album sales, and the bundles are for the extra money.\n\nSelling albums in bundles with clothing, posters, signed items and more has been a popular tactic among mainstream artists, used to inflate first-week sales number and climb up in the charts.\n\nYeat has used this strategy in his previous album LYFESTYLE, and sold a total of 89,000 units, debuting #1 on Billboard.", "annotation_id": "39150986", "url": "https://genius.com/39150986", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "This is where opportunity meets chance Where purpose meets a plan This is a new life A new possibility, a new day", "vault_lines": ["This is where opportunity meets chance"], "meaning": "The intro to Yeat’s “Purpose General” samples July 2025’s “This Dance” by Belgian producer KYRIL.\n\nYou can find where the song was sampled here:\nhttps://youtu.be/49Om_7K6-1o?si=iJlZcSCaxmpU-bnC&t=5", "annotation_id": "39150951", "url": "https://genius.com/39150951", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "You wanna know why I made this money? Lil’ bitch, ’cause I worked the hardest", "vault_lines": ["You wanna know why I made this money? Lil' bitch, 'cause I worked the hardest"], "meaning": "Yeat asserts a self-made narrative, attributing his success to effort rather than luck. This contrasts with the intro’s mention of “chance,” subtly highlighting the duality between control and randomness that defines the album.", "annotation_id": "39149108", "url": "https://genius.com/39149108", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "I make too much money to sleep, I’m drownin’, oh", "vault_lines": ["I make too much money to sleep, I'm drownin', oh"], "meaning": "Despite the success, Yeat frames wealth as overwhelming rather than fulfilling.\n“Drownin’” suggests that money and fame have become excessive to the point of suffocation, hinting early at the loss of control explored later in the album.", "annotation_id": "39149101", "url": "https://genius.com/39149101", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "I give you purpose, I give you purpose, I give you purpose", "vault_lines": ["I give you purpose, I give you purpose, I give you purpose"], "meaning": "Yeat positions himself as a figure who not only finds purpose, but provides it. This can be interpreted as a reflection of his influence over fans and culture, suggesting that his music defines direction for others.\nHowever, as the album progresses, this claim becomes ironic as he struggles with control and identity.", "annotation_id": "39149087", "url": "https://genius.com/39149087", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "You in a glass box (Hey, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["You in a glass box (Hey, yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat uses the “glass box” as a metaphor for total visibility, where someone’s life is constantly exposed and judged by others.\nIt highlights a lack of privacy, while also placing Yeat outside of that space — as the one observing rather than being observed.", "annotation_id": "39145985", "url": "https://genius.com/39145985", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "Market, at Dover Street, the Market", "vault_lines": ["Market, at Dover Street, the Market"], "meaning": "Dover Street Market is a multi-brand retail store in London. It was originally located on Dover Street in the Mayfair district, from which it takes its name.\n\nThe store was founded by Rei Kawakubo, a Japanese designer and the creator of the Comme des Garçons brand, together with her husband Adrian Joffe.\n\nDSM is known for its avant-garde approach to retail, where fashion intersects with art and culture. The store is frequently visited by celebrities, one of whom is Kanye West.", "annotation_id": "39145962", "url": "https://genius.com/39145962", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "You in a glass box (Hey, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["You in a glass box (Hey, yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat uses the “glass box” as a metaphor for total visibility, where someone’s life is constantly exposed and judged by others.\nIt highlights a lack of privacy, while also placing Yeat outside of that space — as the one observing rather than being observed.", "annotation_id": "39145707", "url": "https://genius.com/39145707", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Purpose General", "line": "Yeah, I’ma make the music that I want, give a fuck ‘bout chartin’", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I'ma make the music that I want, give a fuck 'bout chartin'"], "meaning": "Yeat is known for constantly experimenting with his sound, with each project bringing something new instead of sticking to a single style.\nThis reflects his overall artistic approach — he doesn’t care about public opinion or industry expectations, choosing to create music on his own terms.\nThat mindset ties directly into the idea of “ADL” as a whole, emphasizing creative freedom and individuality throughout the project.", "annotation_id": "39145654", "url": "https://genius.com/39145654", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
