{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Psychocainë", "line": "Tell me that you fuckin’ God, I tell ya’ “lies” I’m the only one of them, that’s no despise", "vault_lines": ["Tell me that you fuckin' God, I tell ya' \"lies\""], "meaning": "He’s mocking God and saying that he’s the only god but that is ultimately not true.", "annotation_id": "37181729", "url": "https://genius.com/37181729", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Psychocainë", "line": "I try to take you seriously, but I laugh a lot (Yeah, yeah) I could sell ya hope, yeah, or I could sell you lies (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I could take a loss, I could take a loss"], "meaning": "This lyric states that Yeat doesn’t take this individual seriously by saying he laughs at then a lot. He also states he can tell this person the truth of why he doesn’t take them seriously, or tell lies and comfort them.", "annotation_id": "32635997", "url": "https://genius.com/32635997", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Psychocainë", "line": "I forgot, yeah, I forgot", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I could sell you peace, but I could kill it too"], "meaning": "In this Lyric it seems Yeat has forgotten the last time he took a loss. This indicates that Yeat either has very poor memory or has not taken a loss in so long he forgot.", "annotation_id": "32635974", "url": "https://genius.com/32635974", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
