{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Psychocainë", "line": "Don’t you love that I got condos out up on the moon?", "vault_lines": ["Don't you love that I got condos out up on the moon?"], "meaning": "A condo (short for condominium) is a building or building complex containing a number of individually owned apartments or houses.", "annotation_id": "30988448", "url": "https://genius.com/30988448", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Psychocainë", "line": "Yeah, I could sell you peace, but I could kill it too (Watch, watch, and they—)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I could sell you peace, but I could kill it too"], "meaning": "The line “I could sell you peace” aligns with the overarching theme of the Yeat’s presented god-like persona. By asserting the ability to provide peace, Yeat positions himself as a deity or figure with the power to bring a sense of tranquility and order to others' lives. This role goes hand in hand with the repeated claims of being a god throughout the song.\n\nHowever, the subsequent line, “but I could kill it too,” introduces a layer of complexity to his divine portrayal. It implies that Yeat, despite his god-like attributes, holds the capability to disrupt the peace he offers. This paradoxical nature aligns with the duality often associated with divine figures – the ability to bring both blessings and chaos.\n\nIn the context of the song’s overall theme, these lines contribute to a narrative of the Yeat’s self-perceived importance and influence. He presents a character who not only revels in his god-like status but also acknowledges the potential for both benevolent and destructive actions, adding depth to the portrayal of power and control.", "annotation_id": "30933153", "url": "https://genius.com/30933153", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Psychocainë", "line": "And they watch", "vault_lines": ["And I know they load it up before they do it on the spot (Yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "People watch as Yeat rises to fame, stretches his influence and continues to earn more money while they don’t have and will never have the success that Yeat has. These people could include Haters, competition in the industry, and friends that Yeat has cut off.(due to known and unknown reasons.)", "annotation_id": "30930219", "url": "https://genius.com/30930219", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Psychocainë", "line": "Tell me that you fuckin’ God, I tell ya’ “lies” I’m the only one of them, that’s no despise", "vault_lines": ["Tell me that you fuckin' God, I tell ya' \"lies\""], "meaning": "Yeat is one of a kind. There are fakes out there but none of them are like him. He states “Tell me that you fuckin' God, I tell ya' lies” due to his god-like persona. And follows it up with “I’m the only one of them, that’s no despise” because they say that they are a god. (They compare themselves to him)", "annotation_id": "30926213", "url": "https://genius.com/30926213", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Psychocainë", "line": "Yeah, I look between the lines (Yeah, yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I look between the lines (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat is creative with his music. He has many unique sounds ranging from music like “Nun I’d Change” to songs like “Swërved it” and “3G\" (Ft Lil Uzi Vert). He try’s to be unique. He “Looks between the lines” or in other words “thinks outside the box”.\n\n(He looks between the lines while others look at the lines)", "annotation_id": "30926192", "url": "https://genius.com/30926192", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
