{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Provë sum", "line": "I boot off the X ’cause it give me abilities", "vault_lines": ["I boot off the X 'cause it give me abilities"], "meaning": "The “X,” otherwise known as ecstasy, makes Yeat go so insane that it gives him superpowers. Similar to Superman being able to fly, Yeat has the ability to murder any beat when he’s on said drug.", "annotation_id": "39647708", "url": "https://genius.com/39647708", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Provë sum", "line": "My diamonds wet, they crying", "vault_lines": ["My diamonds wet, they crying"], "meaning": "Here, SeptembersRich is referring to his diamond jewelry. When he says the diamonds are “crying” he means they’re so clean and shiny that light reflects off them like droplets of water, making them look as if they’re dripping or shedding tears. It also suggests that the diamonds are sparkling so intensely that they resemble water running down them, reinforcing the flex about his wealth and high-end jewelry", "annotation_id": "38955086", "url": "https://genius.com/38955086", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Provë sum", "line": "Them diamonds S.I, they not hitting for shit, nobody seeing them shine", "vault_lines": ["Them diamonds S.I, they not hitting for shit, nobody seeing them shine"], "meaning": "S.I is an undesirable quality of diamond and yeat is saying people with S.I quality diamonds cant flex them.", "annotation_id": "36934000", "url": "https://genius.com/36934000", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Provë sum", "line": "When I wake up, I’ma take a Perc’ before I brush my teeth", "vault_lines": ["When I wake up, I'ma take a Perc' before I brush my teeth"], "meaning": "– “Perc’” is short for Percocet, a prescription painkiller that contains oxycodone (an opioid). It’s often misused recreationally for its euphoric effects.\n– Taking it right away suggests dependency or addiction.", "annotation_id": "36346880", "url": "https://genius.com/36346880", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
