{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Provë sum", "line": "Bergdorf", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, bitch, your birds gon' tweak, I'm hittin' Bergdorf"], "meaning": "NY clothing store", "annotation_id": "31818801", "url": "https://genius.com/31818801", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Provë sum", "line": "Yeah, I fell in love with the bean, I got the best and it’s no in between", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I fell in love with the bean, I got the best and it's no in between"], "meaning": "Yeat is known for taking drugs and he is most likely talking about a Percocet since that is the most common drug he talks about in his songs.\n\nWhen he says the 2nd part of the bar, he’s is talking about that his plug gave him the best possible drug on the market, making him, according to Yeat in most of his songs, “leave the earth”, which is terminology for getting extremely high to the point where you leave the earth.\n\nBack to the first half of the bar, he is stating that he has an addiction to Percocet’s/drugs to the point where he “fell in love” with drugs.", "annotation_id": "28629919", "url": "https://genius.com/28629919", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Provë sum", "line": "When that bitch pull up, it’s WWE, finna beat down, yeah No Steve Austin, not no OT, ho, Draco hit him, OVO", "vault_lines": ["When that bitch pull up, it's WWE, finna beat down, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat uses many metaphors in these two bars. Firstly, WWE, a famous wrestling company, airs beat downs of their wrestlers. Yeat explains how he will beat down anyone who pulls up on him. Then, Yeat references famous WWE wrestler Steve Austin, to add onto his previous bar. Finally, Yeat explains that a “Draco hit him, OVO.” This bar is a beautiful double entendre. A Draco is the firearm of choice for many rappers in the scene, and OVO,or October’s Very Own, is a company started by famous rapper Drake. Yeat is relating his tool to a famous rapper in the final lyrics of this bar.", "annotation_id": "25631947", "url": "https://genius.com/25631947", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Provë sum", "line": "No S.I, flawless in", "vault_lines": ["We on the side where we win, no S.I, flawless in"], "meaning": "correct bar is “no SIs, flawless in”\nYeat is speaking about the clarity of his diamonds. SI means small inclusion, which are flaws that are noticeable at 10x magnification. Flawless diamonds are more expensive than SI diamonds, so Yeat is clarifying that he only wears flawless diamonds.", "annotation_id": "25039451", "url": "https://genius.com/25039451", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Provë sum", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-prove-sum-lyrics", "genius_title": "Provë sum", "genius_id": 6879156, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Probably!", "line": "Back in the day, we was sellin’ the work and the Percs out the motherfuckin’ back of apartments", "vault_lines": ["Back in the day, we was sellin' the work and the Percs out the motherfuckin' back of apartments"], "meaning": "This lyric describes a past experience where the speaker and others were involved in selling drugs, specifically mentioning “work” (likely referring to illegal substances) and “Percs” (short for Percocet, a prescription pain medication often abused recreationally). The phrase “out the back of apartments” suggests that this illegal activity took place discreetly, away from public view, likely indicating a clandestine operation to avoid detection by authorities. Overall, the lyric portrays a gritty, street-oriented narrative of past illegal activities.", "annotation_id": "31092023", "url": "https://genius.com/31092023", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Probably!", "line": "Lil’ ho, baguettes on my body, VS on my body, it hang from my neck like a motherfuckin’", "vault_lines": ["I told that bitch, \"You can fuck who you want, you just can't fuck a nigga who really ain't hard as me\""], "meaning": "This lyric describes someone wearing baguette-cut diamonds, a type of diamond cut popular for its elongated rectangular shape resembling a baguette bread. The line “VS on my body” likely refers to Very Slightly Included diamonds, a high clarity grade in the diamond grading scale, indicating very minor inclusions that are difficult to see under 10x magnification. The lyric emphasizes the opulence and luxury of the jewelry, with the diamonds hanging from the person’s neck as a symbol of their wealth and status.", "annotation_id": "31092011", "url": "https://genius.com/31092011", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Probably!", "line": "Nextel called me up, said they wan’ come sign, sign me, with two ex-bitches, they both Siamese", "vault_lines": ["Nextel called me up, said they wan' come sign, sign me, with two ex-bitches, they both Siamese"], "meaning": "Nextel is Yeat’s manager", "annotation_id": "26608710", "url": "https://genius.com/26608710", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
