{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Poppin", "line": "We get like this, you wish, lil’ bitch, we poppin’ (We poppin’)", "vault_lines": ["We get like this, you wish, lil' bitch, we poppin' (We poppin')"], "meaning": "Yeat refers to his fast lifestyle full of spending and indulgence. He flexes claiming we “wish” to live like him and that his lifestyle is so care free that they can be poppin. Poppin, in this case is consuming the substance “Percs”", "annotation_id": "25792057", "url": "https://genius.com/25792057", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Poppin", "line": "Percs’", "vault_lines": ["It ain't been a day that I ain't been high, bitch, Percs', I pop 'em"], "meaning": "Percs is short for Percocet, a medication that is a combination of Oxycodone, an opioid pain medication, and Paracetamol/Acetaminophen – an over the counter pain medicine", "annotation_id": "25551068", "url": "https://genius.com/25551068", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Poppin", "line": "I don’t fuck with nobody, lil’ bitch, I show you nothin’ (Show you nothin’) I ain’t trustin’ nobody, lil’ bitch, I keep a gun", "vault_lines": ["I don't fuck with nobody, lil' bitch, I show you nothin' (Show you nothin')"], "meaning": "Noah Smith expresses his ability to be independent despite the societal pressure that we are given as humans to find a mate. Rather, he does not have time for people who do not give him any benefits, this is an interesting line, being that he has a girlfriend. We also allude to Mr. Smith’s more aggressive nature doubling down on his independence by implying he has a firearm at his disposal. Meaning If people may get too close to him or act as if they have a relationship when they may not, he will not hesitate to use that firearm (dangerous).", "annotation_id": "25494003", "url": "https://genius.com/25494003", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Poppin", "line": "I need my drugs, I need my love (We get high)", "vault_lines": ["I need my drugs, I need my love (We get high)"], "meaning": "Yeat expresses his need and desire for heavy narcotics. He also expresses a need for romantic love in his life.\n\nIn the literal sense, he expresses his desire for love from a woman, however, this may be a metaphor for his addiction to drugs.\n\nYeat rarely discusses his love life in his music, however, he addressed the topic on the track “Call më,” rapping:\n\nI ain’t never thought I’d fall in love, and your love surrounding me (Yeah)\nAny time I think about fucking, I feel you around me (Yeah)\nEvery time I see your texts, them words arousing me (Yeah)\n\nYeat also discusses his drug use in most of his songs. An example of this is on “Dub,” where he raps:\n\n(Hey, hey) Where the problem at?\n(Hey, hey) I’m spinning off these Percs like I’m a laundromat", "annotation_id": "25452427", "url": "https://genius.com/25452427", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Poppin", "line": "Slide in the coupes, we fucked the driveway up (Skrrt, skrrt) Hopped inside the mansion, fucked the drywall up Kickin’ holes in the wall and fuckin’ hoes in my drawers", "vault_lines": ["Slide in the coupes, we fucked the driveway up (Skrrt, skrrt)"], "meaning": "Yeat describes an unruly mansion party, exemplifying his rockstar lifestyle.\n\nYeat and his friends arrived in a fleet of exotic cars, leaving tire marks on the driveway with the large vehicles. After entering the house, the group kicked holes in the wall, subsequently ruining the drywall, a commonly used material in American homes used to finish walls. Following this destruction, he slept with some women, presumably groupies or prostitutes.", "annotation_id": "25398264", "url": "https://genius.com/25398264", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Poppin", "line": "Yeah, I told my bitch I need one, need a topper, a bopper", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I told my bitch I need one, need a topper, a bopper"], "meaning": "“Topper” is referring to the popular activity of giving “sloppy top.” The meaning of “bopper” is to this day unknown and we will perhaps never know the true meaning behind it.", "annotation_id": "25360122", "url": "https://genius.com/25360122", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
