{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Poppin", "line": "You might catch me in the Tesla ’cause it’s drivin’, I’m nodding off", "vault_lines": ["You might catch me in the Tesla 'cause it's drivin', I'm nodding off"], "meaning": "Yeat alludes to the self-driving feature present on all new Teslas that are released, stating that he is allowed to snooze whilst driving, something which is dangerous and illegal in almost every other realistic circumstance. However, since his car drives itself, he can allow himself to succumb to the sleep-inducing effect of the various drugs that he’s consumed. Thus, Yeat flips the standard of what is cool by making it a flex that he is dozing off in his car, something which is generally considered inconsiderate, threatening, and lazy.", "annotation_id": "25199771", "url": "https://genius.com/25199771", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
