{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Poppin", "line": "Yeah, roll him like a filter, yeah, then smoke him like a bong (Phew)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, roll him like a filter, yeah, then smoke him like a bong (Phew)"], "meaning": "I think here he actually says “Roll him like a phillie, and/then smoke him like a bone”. I just think this makes a lot more sense than the current lyric. Phillie is derived from a type of cigar that could be used to roll a blunt and bone would likely be referring to a joint or some other meaning of the phrase “smoking bones”.", "annotation_id": "25181483", "url": "https://genius.com/25181483", "state": "pending", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
