{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Plenty options", "line": "(Cover my body in Cha-ne-ne, in the world, you still wouldn’t see me)", "vault_lines": ["I said all my diamonds dancing (Woo-woo) (No way)"], "meaning": "Yeat describes his flexing subtly in a double entendre; he describes himself dressed in and accompanied with high-luxury items, the brand of Chanel.\n\nWith this, he proclaims that the listener or person he’s conversing wouldn’t want a view of him wearing such a brand that might rival their own clothes.\n\nThe brand’s logo (two C’s to represent Chanel) also represent the word “see” in the line, making for a fine brag.", "annotation_id": "32867875", "url": "https://genius.com/32867875", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
