{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Outsidë", "line": "I’m puttin’ on for the westside, so I’ma bust a nut on her chest", "vault_lines": ["I'm puttin' on for the westside, so I'ma bust a nut on her chest"], "meaning": "Yeat, from Irvine, California, claims he will ejaculate on his partner’s chest to represent the western region of the United States.", "annotation_id": "26546672", "url": "https://genius.com/26546672", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Outsidë", "line": "Pullin’ up in big old bodies with bands like it’s parade", "vault_lines": ["Pullin' up in big old bodies with bands like it's parade"], "meaning": "Yeat flaunts his luxurious lifestyle, bragging about the amounts of cash in his old-school muscle cars.  He uses a play on the word “bands” — slang for money — and compares it to parades, typically led by marching bands.", "annotation_id": "25358734", "url": "https://genius.com/25358734", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Outsidë", "line": "YSL, feel like cologne", "vault_lines": ["YSL, feel like cologne"], "meaning": "Yeat uses a double entendre of Yves Saint Laurent, a designer brand that sells clothing and various colognes, and Young Stoner Life, Young Thug’s record label.", "annotation_id": "25313921", "url": "https://genius.com/25313921", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Outsidë", "line": "Pullin’ up in Tonkas, bitch, we learned just how to finesse (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["Pullin' up in Tonkas, bitch, we learned just how to finesse (Uh)"], "meaning": "Yeat is referring to the popular die cast dump truck kids toy, Tonka Trucks.\n\nNo ones pulling up on Yeat in a bigger truck and he’s proud of that", "annotation_id": "25275003", "url": "https://genius.com/25275003", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Outsidë", "line": "Giuseppe Zanotti with snakes when I’m walkin’, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Giuseppe Zanotti with snakes when I'm walkin', yeah"], "meaning": "In December 2021, Young Thug collaborated with the luxury brand Giuseppe Zanotti to design his own sneakers, the Giuseppe Zanotti Cobras.\n\n\n\nYoung Thug and his Giuseppe Zanotti Cobras\n\n\nThe $1,190 shoes have a distinct design, featuring a snake wrapped around the sole. In other words, Thug is walking around in his own designed shoes.", "annotation_id": "25199473", "url": "https://genius.com/25199473", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Outsidë", "line": "No, no, you can’t be no Twizzy Rich ’cause you don’t know us", "vault_lines": ["No, no, you can't be no Twizzy Rich 'cause you don't know us"], "meaning": "Yeat expresses his disdain for fake friends and fans, reinstating that he won’t allow anyone to claim close ties with him or his TwizzyRich label if he doesn’t want to associate with them.", "annotation_id": "25170137", "url": "https://genius.com/25170137", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Outsidë", "line": "Oh, you rich? Yeah", "vault_lines": ["Oh, you rich? Yeah"], "meaning": "Before Thug’s verse was previewed, Yeat previewed a line from Thug’s verse on a Instagram story:\n\nI waz in the club n hit a opp wit a chair 🪑 😂😂😂😂😂😂😂 Thug say dat on outsude 😂😂oh u rich yea\n\nHe also showed the file that there was proof Thug was on the song.", "annotation_id": "25100099", "url": "https://genius.com/25100099", "state": "pending", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Outsidë", "line": "Rollie flooded (Flooded) Diamonds flawless (Flawless) Bad thotties Big bodies (Skrrt, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Turn this shit up, my theme song, I might run out of gas"], "meaning": "Although “Wavëy Krazy” marks this rhythm’s first appearance, this is more notably a reiteration of his January 2022 feature on Yung Kayo’s “YEET,” where he rapped similar lines:\n\nYeat, me, diamonds, flooded (On me)\nBad thotties, pull up, uh, on me\n\nHe also interpolates Young Nudy’s flow on his 2016 track, “Yeah Yeah,” where Nudy raps:\n\nGangster (Yeah)\nBlood (Yeah), shooter (Yeah)\nKiller (Yeah), robber (Yeah)\nYeah (Yeah), finesser (Yeah)\nJugger (Yeah), I do it (Yeah)\nSticks (Yeah), get to it (Yeah)", "annotation_id": "25001736", "url": "https://genius.com/25001736", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
