{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Out thë way", "line": "You can try pullin’ up on us lil’ bitch (Ooh), you get hit with a muhfuckin’ AR (Oh)", "vault_lines": ["You can try pullin' up on us lil' bitch (Ooh), you get hit with a muhfuckin' AR (Oh)"], "meaning": "An AR (commonly misunderstood as an Assault Rifle) is an ArmaLite Rifle. ArmaLite is an American arms company that specializes in rifle production. The A.R. that is most likely being talked about in this line is the AR-15 or ArmaLite Rifle-15. The AR-15 is a rifle that can be used in 3 modes, semi-automatic, fully-automatic, and burst fire. Yeat says that if his gang is ambushed by oppositions, they will shoot back with AR’s.", "annotation_id": "28754883", "url": "https://genius.com/28754883", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Out thë way", "line": "(I-I’m working on dying)", "vault_lines": ["I think I'm Osama, lil' bitch, yeah, the way that I blew up and left on the Earth (Bang)"], "meaning": "The producer tag “I’m working on dying” comes from a producer-based collective in Philadelphia called “Working On Dying” Including the members: F1lthy, Oogie Mane, Brandon Finessin, BNYX, Kimchi, FaxOnly, 100yrd, Swaggyono, The Loosie Man, Jarek, Westsdemane, StoopidXool & Synergic\n\n\n\nWorking On Dying", "annotation_id": "28095805", "url": "https://genius.com/28095805", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
