{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Out thë way", "line": "Yeah, I make money, my thot-thot-thot ’bout to fuck that money all up (BNYX, ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I make money, my thot-thot-thot 'bout to fuck that money all up (BNYX, ooh)"], "meaning": "Yeat’s use of “thot-thot-thot” is likely an allusion to one of Offset’s adlibs in the Migos song, “Bad and Boujie”\n\n“Thot” is a somewhat offensive colloquialism used in reference to women, formed from an acronym that stands for either “that ho over there” or “thirsty ho over there.”", "annotation_id": "26881738", "url": "https://genius.com/26881738", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Out thë way", "line": "Yeah, I bought me the Crowdless", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I bought me the Crowdless"], "meaning": "Crowdless is a fashion brand that sells Ski masks and other designer items like sunglasses and shoes, Yeat is most likely referring to the ski mask that they sell, a signature part of his look like the Turban.", "annotation_id": "26708829", "url": "https://genius.com/26708829", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Out thë way", "line": "Yeah, look at these muhfuckin’ diamonds, listen the way that they sound (Hey, hey)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, look at these muhfuckin' diamonds, listen the way that they sound (Hey, hey)"], "meaning": "Yeat recently just got his finished piece of the Iced out “Big Tonka” chain that is exactly $101k.", "annotation_id": "26696743", "url": "https://genius.com/26696743", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Out thë way", "line": "You can be stuck in the mix with a couple lil’ blicks, but it’s always a way out (Hey, hey, I-I’m—)", "vault_lines": ["You can be stuck in the mix with a couple lil' blicks, but it's always a way out (Hey, hey, I-I'm—)"], "meaning": "Yeat recognizes that a life filled with violence is negative. He believes there is a way for him to leave a life of crime behind and move forward with legal endeavours, such as music.\n\nYeat echoes a similar sentiment on his track “Can’t stop it,” rapping:\n\nOn the phone with my demon, we build it up and then retire", "annotation_id": "26679585", "url": "https://genius.com/26679585", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Out thë way", "line": "Yeah, peeled off on the jakes, peeled off on the cops, peeled off on the swerve (Ooh, oh)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, peeled off on the jakes, peeled off on the cops, peeled off on the swerve (Ooh, oh)"], "meaning": "“Jakes” is a slang term that has had several meanings over the years. Historically, it was a slang word for lavatories, however, these days it is mostly used to refer to police.\n\n“Swervin'” means being under the influence of large amounts of alcohol or drugs, or, more specifically, driving while under the influence.\n\nThus, whilst under the influence of drugs, Yeat evaded the police.", "annotation_id": "26679563", "url": "https://genius.com/26679563", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Out thë way", "line": "I ran up my money the most, I’m richer than all of the nerds (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I ran up my money the most, I’m richer than all of the nerds (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Through pursuing music, Yeat has acquired immense wealth at the young age of 22, whereas many of his academically-inclined “nerd” peers that are undertaking tertiary education are likely still struggling financially due to the USA’s crippling student debt crisis.", "annotation_id": "26679502", "url": "https://genius.com/26679502", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Out thë way", "line": "I bought a Urus today, uh-huh Paint it all yellow, look like a bird (I-I’m—)", "vault_lines": ["I bought a Urus today, uh-huh"], "meaning": "Yeat’s newfound success has enabled him to buy a yellow Lamborghini Urus, a luxury SUV with a starting price of $230,000.\n\n\nThe car in question: A yellow Lamborghini Urus.\n\nHe compares the color of the car to Big Bird from Sesame Street.", "annotation_id": "26679448", "url": "https://genius.com/26679448", "state": "pending", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Out thë way", "line": "I think I’m Osama, lil’ bitch, yeah, the way that I blew up and left on the Earth (Bang)", "vault_lines": ["I think I'm Osama, lil' bitch, yeah, the way that I blew up and left on the Earth (Bang)"], "meaning": "Yeat compares his meteoric rise to stardom to Osama bin Laden, the legendary terrorist who bombs things. Yeat rapped a similar line on his track “Poppin”:\n\nFeel like Osama to us ‘cause we blow up like a bomb", "annotation_id": "26679107", "url": "https://genius.com/26679107", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Out thë way", "line": "Yeah, I ain’t even fuckin’ with nobody, bitch, got a crib in the ’burbs (Ooh, oh)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I ain't even fuckin’ with nobody, bitch, got a crib in the 'burbs (Ooh, oh)"], "meaning": "Since acquiring wealth as a rapper, Yeat has invested in residential real estate, purchasing a house in a quiet neighborhood in order to keep away from people he doesn’t like.\n\nYeat’s cadance mimics that of his hit song “Big tonka” with Lil Uzi Vert, on which he raps:\n\nI ain’t fucking with nobody, bitch, I'ma geek up\nGet high, get high as I like (Bih', bih', bih', bih')", "annotation_id": "26678974", "url": "https://genius.com/26678974", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Out thë way", "line": "Yeah, free YSL out the chain gang, big fuck 12, they birds (Brr)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, free YSL out the chain gang, big fuck 12, they birds (Brr)"], "meaning": "On May 9, 2022, twenty-eight members of Young Stoner Life records, including their label-head Young Thug, were arrested on charges of participation in street gang activity alongside a 56-count Racketeer Influenced and Corrupt Organizations Act (RICO) indictment. Gunna, Thug’s protégé, who was also indicted, turned himself in two days following their arrests.\n\nYeat screams for their freedom, dissing the police department by exclaiming “fuck 12” — a phrase simply meaning “fuck the police.”\n\nYeat has a strong bond with YSL signee Yung Kayo—one of the few members who slipped by the RICO case—as the duo has released four songs together, and supposedly has a collab mixtape in the works. He also seems to be acquainted with Gunna, who he’s collaborated with on “Rackz got më” and met in Paris, and very well bonded with Young Thug, who he’s collaborated with on “Outsidë.” He’s even name-dropped Thug on Lyfë, rapping this bar on “Up off X”:\n\nYeah, just got word from Thug, ‘bout to crank that bitch (What?)", "annotation_id": "26669513", "url": "https://genius.com/26669513", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
