{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "One Thing I Fear (Interlude)", "line": "How you know it’s real? How you know I’m real?", "vault_lines": ["How you know it's real? How you know I'm real?"], "meaning": "How do we know that anything is real? Is everything made-up?", "annotation_id": "38862637", "url": "https://genius.com/38862637", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "One Thing I Fear (Interlude)", "line": "(I just keep it real)", "vault_lines": ["I just sealed a deal, I just keep it real (Real)"], "meaning": "Yeat ignores his fantasies.", "annotation_id": "38861733", "url": "https://genius.com/38861733", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "One Thing I Fear (Interlude)", "line": "Just know it don’t get easier from here (From here) Just know that it’s nothin’ that a man won’t fear (A man won’t fear)", "vault_lines": ["Just know it don't get easier from here (From here)"], "meaning": "It doesn’t get easier if we keep fearing life. It can only get easier if we stop fearing the inevitable.", "annotation_id": "38861731", "url": "https://genius.com/38861731", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "One Thing I Fear (Interlude)", "line": "Yeah, every secret sealed Yeah, how you know it’s real?", "vault_lines": ["You don't know what's real"], "meaning": "Yeat is asking us how anything in this world is real. Are secrets real? We should not fear anything for this reason – nothing is permanent.", "annotation_id": "38861707", "url": "https://genius.com/38861707", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "One Thing I Fear (Interlude)", "line": "Gotta keep my chin up, gotta keep my fantasies aside", "vault_lines": ["Gotta keep my chin up, gotta keep my fantasies aside"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that it is important to remain positive in life, and keep pushing toward success – ‘fantasies’ do not help to achieve literal success.", "annotation_id": "38861694", "url": "https://genius.com/38861694", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "One Thing I Fear (Interlude)", "line": "And just know for your sake that I’ll never fear Just know for your own sake that it’s nothin’ you should fear", "vault_lines": ["Just know that it's nothin' that a man won't fear (A man won't fear)"], "meaning": "Even though bad things happen, we should not fear the future. Yeat is urging us to live in the present and fear nothing that is ahead of us.", "annotation_id": "38861687", "url": "https://genius.com/38861687", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "One Thing I Fear (Interlude)", "line": "You know I feel this way about a couple things, a couple certain things that make me feel good", "vault_lines": ["You know I feel this way about a couple things, a couple certain things that make me feel good"], "meaning": "Yeat is likely referring to drugs. Some months after this song, Yeat became sober, so the ‘way’ he felt about them started to shift. They, naturally, made him feel good but he knew it was wrong.", "annotation_id": "38861683", "url": "https://genius.com/38861683", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "One Thing I Fear (Interlude)", "line": "Know I don’t keep it pushin’ for no reason, I’ma do it for me, I’ma do it for us Know I don’t give a fuck about nobody bitch, all I care about is my family, my us, uh", "vault_lines": ["Know I do it for me, know I do it for us, yeah (Fear)"], "meaning": "Everything Yeat does is for his family. He keeps pushing and trying to be better for himself and for his family.", "annotation_id": "38861680", "url": "https://genius.com/38861680", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "One Thing I Fear (Interlude)", "line": "He don’t have a spine", "vault_lines": ["The devil say it's mine, he don't have a spine"], "meaning": "Yeat infers here that the devil is weak and only a voice in his head with no ‘spine’.", "annotation_id": "38861676", "url": "https://genius.com/38861676", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
