{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "On tha linë", "line": "Can’t even rock with you, you not a boss (Yeah, yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Can't even rock with you, you not a boss (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat implies that due to your low social status, he will not associate or ‘rock with you’ (hang around with you) or commit any crimes involving you. A boss is commonly a person of high status in a company or organization, sometimes the top of the food chain. Due to the fact that you have not attained this rank, he will not be associated with you in any way. Yeat is likely directing this bar at the opposition, or any people in his social group which he considers, unpopular or lame.", "annotation_id": "27803844", "url": "https://genius.com/27803844", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "On tha linë", "line": "They ask how the hell I make money, I couldn’t even tell ’em ’cause I don’t know how (Ah)", "vault_lines": ["They ask how the hell I make money, I couldn't even tell 'em 'cause I don't know how (Ah)"], "meaning": "Yeat is claiming people ask him how he makes his money, but he rebuts by saying he’s unable to because he doesn’t know.\n\nHe is likely referring to the fact that he makes so much money it is impossible to keep track of consistently.", "annotation_id": "26226544", "url": "https://genius.com/26226544", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
