{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "On tha linë", "line": "Back of a shotgun barrel kick back like buckets", "vault_lines": ["Back of a shotgun barrel kick back like buckets"], "meaning": "Yeat uses wordplay to tie the kickback or recoil of a shotgun to the English idiom “kick the bucket,” which means to die. His shotgun, which has plenty of kick, will kill you.", "annotation_id": "25535769", "url": "https://genius.com/25535769", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
