{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Oh eX whY", "line": "Trissy (And Wock’)", "vault_lines": ["Drank bad for my kidney but I'm still sipping Trissy (And Wock')"], "meaning": "This is a good example of yeat saying two words at once in one word. It’s easier to hear if you listen to the song. but he does not say “wock” and “walked” he says wock. The lyric is “…I’m still sipping Trissy and WOCKed in with fifty thousand bitch…”\n\nessentially he says wok as in lean but also says walk as in walk with your feet in the SAME word. this is proof yeat is a lyrical genius as he literally says two words at once.\n\nlisten to the song n ull hear it", "annotation_id": "37683046", "url": "https://genius.com/37683046", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Oh eX whY", "line": "Racks way too fat, watch ’em stack, they as tall as me", "vault_lines": ["Racks way too fat, watch 'em stack, they as tall me"], "meaning": "“Racks way to fat, watch ‘em stack, they as tall as me.” This bar encapsulates the monumental concept of money being a certain height, particular the height of the rapper or artist. Derived from the creator of the money-height bar, Lil Uzi Vert. Yeat says his money, being racks are getting way to fat, meaning to tall or large, and eventually obtain the height of Noah Smith, Yeat. Yeat has never publicly came out about his height, but we can assume he is between the height range of 5'7 to 5'9, this means he would need to obtain a big increment of money to match my kings height.", "annotation_id": "29851868", "url": "https://genius.com/29851868", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Oh eX whY", "line": "Call my twin my twizzy, call my bitch my bizzy Might just smoke this stizzy, and this Oxy’ got me dizzy", "vault_lines": ["Call my twin my twizzy, call my bitch my bizzy"], "meaning": "Avid listeners of Yeat are familiar with his signature lingo, with songs like 2021’s “Twizzy Rich” featuring these unusual terms:\n\nThey tryna be my twizzy, you already know ain’t no deal\n\nIn a July 2021 interview with Our Generation Music, Yeat explained the meaning behind “twizzy” and the other original words he’s concocted:\n\nIt’s another word for like, twin […] I was like in New York, I was with like this dude, uh, Fendi, I was like, “bro, I’m finna make up a new word,” he was like, “What?” And I was like, “twizzy,” he was like, “That shit stupid.” I just do that shit randomly, like I just be making up words like all the time.", "annotation_id": "29066864", "url": "https://genius.com/29066864", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Oh eX whY", "line": "You can’t check up on the things I did, I swear I got no history", "vault_lines": ["You can't check up on the things I did, I swear I got no history"], "meaning": "Yeat originally started rapping under the name “Lil Yeat” in 2016. He mentions having “no history,” alluding to the fact that a lot of the songs under his former moniker have been removed from the internet.\n\nIn an interview with Our Generation Music from July 2021, Yeat admitted that he had too much confidence in his older music:\n\nIt’s crazy ‘cause I thought I was good the whole time. […] I thought I was good like then […] and when I look back I’m like, “that shit was so bad,” like I thought I was good.\n\n\n\nYeat in 2018", "annotation_id": "29060787", "url": "https://genius.com/29060787", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Oh eX whY", "line": "Yeah, couldn’t call up my label a year ago, shit was so silent Now they calling me back like, “Yeat, we wanna sign you” (Fuck ’em)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, couldn't call up my label a year ago, shit was so silent"], "meaning": "Yeat was talking about how they didn’t want to sign him when he ws just growing but now that he up like a real nigga, now they want to sign em.", "annotation_id": "27045871", "url": "https://genius.com/27045871", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
