{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Oh My Pockëts", "line": "I don’t know how you live, I don’t know I don’t know where you go, I don’t know I don’t know and I don’t think I wanna know I don’t know if you can push along this road", "vault_lines": ["I don't know how you live, I don't know"], "meaning": "“I'on know how you live, I'on know”\n   -  Yeat is expressing uncertainty about someone else’s lyfestyle.\n\n“I'on know where you go, I'on know”\n   - Yeat is unaware of the someone else’s whereabouts or activities.\n\n“I'on know and I don’t think I wanna know”:\n   - Yeat is expressing a disinterest in finding out more about the other person’s life.\n\n“I'on know you can push a long this road”:\n   - Yeat is acknowledging that the other person is on their own path, and he prefers to keep his distance.", "annotation_id": "33222660", "url": "https://genius.com/33222660", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
