{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ORCHESTRATË", "line": "You say that I’m bad for no reason?", "vault_lines": ["You say that I'm bad for no reason?"], "meaning": "A lot of people (who usually don’t even listen to Yeat) hate him because of his repetitive sound, his flow. These haters say that every Yeat song is the same (which is clearly a lie). We can assume that next line “Bitch, I’m back up on ‘em (…)” refers to his relapse. His previous studio album “2093” tells the story of yeat’s struggle with drug addiction and withdrawal, about recovery and sobriety. Most fans who liked the old sound more hated this album and wanted “old Yeat” back – So, he was “forced” to go back to taking drugs, because that’s how he made his old music (in group chat with fans Yeat stated that he made Afterlyfe on Percs (aka Percocet/Oxycodone) and Up2me on “X” (aka Ecstasy/E)", "annotation_id": "33417106", "url": "https://genius.com/33417106", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ORCHESTRATË", "line": "You say that I’m bad for no reason?", "vault_lines": ["You say that I'm bad for no reason?"], "meaning": "A lot of people (who usually don’t even listen to Yeat) hate him because of his repetitive sound, his flow. These haters say that every Yeat song is the same (which is clearly a lie). We can assume that next line “Bitch, I’m back up on ‘em (…)” refers to his relapse. His previous studio album “2093” tells the story of yeat’s struggle with drug addiction and withdrawal, about recovery and sobriety. Most fans who liked the old sound more hated this album and wanted “old Yeat” back – So, he was “forced” to go back to taking drugs, because that’s how he made his old music (in group chat with fans Yeat stated that he made Afterlyfe on Percs (aka Percocet/Oxycodone) and Up2me on “X” (aka Ecstasy/E)", "annotation_id": "33415960", "url": "https://genius.com/33415960", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ORCHESTRATË", "line": "Bitch, I’m back up on ’em, on ’em, on ’em", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm back up on 'em, on 'em, on 'em"], "meaning": "Reference to Yeat‘s 13th song on his album Up 2 Me, called Bak on em, where Yeat says ‘Back on the Percs, i don’t when i’ll stop, I really wish I ain’t tried them’", "annotation_id": "33372393", "url": "https://genius.com/33372393", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ORCHESTRATË", "line": "Bentley, that bitch got the frogs", "vault_lines": ["And I got the Bentley, that bitch got the frogs"], "meaning": "Multiple times across his career, Yeat has named Bentley’s uniquely designed headlights and tail lights as frog-like, as the round lights look like a frog’s eyes.", "annotation_id": "33358467", "url": "https://genius.com/33358467", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ORCHESTRATË", "line": "Yeah, turn up at my show? At least just do it right Yeah, yeah, we go all night", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, turn up at my show? At least just do it right"], "meaning": "Yeat could be referring to his single before LYFESTYLE, “TURNMEUP”, released on SoundCloud in September.", "annotation_id": "33327316", "url": "https://genius.com/33327316", "state": "pending", "votes": -6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
