{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ON 1", "line": "Maybach", "vault_lines": ["Maybach golf course, driver, on me (Surf)"], "meaning": "Backpack. Keep a gun in his backpack. He got it on him", "annotation_id": "40762509", "url": "https://genius.com/40762509", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ON 1", "line": "Golf course, driver, on me (Surf)", "vault_lines": ["golf course, driver, on me (Surf)"], "meaning": "Yeat makes a clever double entendre, connecting both golf and guns.\n\nA “golf course driver” is the longest, lowest-loft, and largest-headed club in a golf bag, designed for maximum distance on tee shots. Primarily used on par-4 and par-5 holes, it helps reach the green faster, though it is often considered the hardest club to master.\nYeat’s wordplay comes into play here, since another name for a “golf course driver” is a 1 wood, or, less commonly, a “big stick.” So, by stating this, Yeat basically means that he has a “big stick” on him, or a large gun, using the golf wordplay to get it across.\nWell done, Noah.", "annotation_id": "39582050", "url": "https://genius.com/39582050", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ON 1", "line": "Yeah, yeah, we on one", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, yeah, we on one"], "meaning": "“We on one” is a slang phrase often used to mean being extremely high or intoxicated.  Yeat is emphasizing the chaotic drug-fueled energy of the moment", "annotation_id": "38955228", "url": "https://genius.com/38955228", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ON 1", "line": "It’s surfs on the side on the beach, all again (Surf)", "vault_lines": ["It's surfs on the side on the beach, all again (Surf)"], "meaning": "This reminds me of the beach vibe of Yeat’s song Heliman, which was released for the roll-out leading up to LYFESTYLE.", "annotation_id": "34787456", "url": "https://genius.com/34787456", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ON 1", "line": "No, we don’t stay at no Double Tree", "vault_lines": ["No, we don't stay at no Double Tree"], "meaning": "DoubleTree by Hilton is a fast-growing, upscale hotel brand popular among business and leisure travelers around the world. For more than 55 years, DoubleTree by Hilton has maintained its philosophy of making guests feel welcome while traveling, prioritizing the spaces and human moments that make travelers feel good.", "annotation_id": "33812068", "url": "https://genius.com/33812068", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ON 1", "line": "Yeah, I’m tryna cover my face, I’on want you to see my eyes (No)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I'm tryna cover my face, I'on want you to see my eyes (No)"], "meaning": "Yeat is known for wearing accessories like balaclavas and turbans which he uses to cover his face. He’s trying to hide his identity or just doesn’t want people to see his facial expressions. The accessories serve as a physical barrier highlighting his preference for maintaining a certain level of anonymity and mystery.", "annotation_id": "33345514", "url": "https://genius.com/33345514", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ON 1", "line": "On the Barbie’ (Burnt)", "vault_lines": ["on the Barbie' (Burnt)"], "meaning": "This bar is a reference to a 1984 Australian tourism advertisement. The ad was broadcast in the USA and UK from 1984 to 1990.\n\nIn the ad Australian actor Paul Hogan says “I’ll slip an extra shrimp on the barbie for you”. Meaning he’ll put another shrimp on the barbecue.\n\nIn this bar Yeat is saying that if he catches his enemies, he will metaphorically burn them like a shrimp on a barbecue.", "annotation_id": "33332879", "url": "https://genius.com/33332879", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ON 1", "line": "Yeah, and we get you burnt, shrimp on the Barbie’ (Burnt)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, and we get you burnt, shrimp on the Barbie' (Burnt)"], "meaning": "This bar is a reference to a 1984 Australian tourism advertisement. The ad was broadcast in the USA and UK from 1984 to 1990.\n\nIn the ad Australian actor Paul Hogan says “I’ll slip an extra shrimp on the barbie for you”. Meaning he’ll put another shrimp on the barbecue.\n\nIn this bar Yeat is saying that if he catches his enemies, he will metaphorically burn them like a shrimp on a barbecue.", "annotation_id": "33332799", "url": "https://genius.com/33332799", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ON 1", "line": "We leave you out of shape, crinkle cut fries", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we leave you out of shape, crinkle cut fries"], "meaning": "Crinkle cut fries are known to be often misshapen. Yeat threatens that one will cop significant losses if they confront him.", "annotation_id": "33319510", "url": "https://genius.com/33319510", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ON 1", "line": "Yeah, and we get you tracked like an iPhone", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, and we get you tracked like an iPhone"], "meaning": "Yeat conveys a sense of control, surveillance, and inescapability through this line by refering to the “Find My iPhone” app. This app has the capability of tracking other devices the user owns, suggesting that Yeat can monitor or find someone with ease. It has an undertone of power and threat, fitting the aggressive and confident tone of this album.", "annotation_id": "33319484", "url": "https://genius.com/33319484", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
