{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Nvr again", "line": "Pulled up and I chopped the helicopter, got the Scat", "vault_lines": ["Pulled up and I chopped the helicopter, got the Scat"], "meaning": "Yeat explains how he finessed a police helicopter with a ‘scat’. A ‘Scat’ is slang for a Dodge Charger Scat Pack. Although Scat Pack refers to Dodge’s old lineup of muscle cars (the R/T models) it is highly certain Yeat is referencing the newer Charger model. This model boasts a 6.4L V8 engine capable of 485hp (362kW) at 6000rpm. It serves as Dodge’s mid-range option, faster than the base SXT, but slower than the HELLCAT models.\n\nWith this in mind, it is plausible that Yeat was able to evade police helicopters in his high-performance Charger.\n\n\n\nPictured: 2020 Dodge Charger Scat Pack", "annotation_id": "29776374", "url": "https://genius.com/29776374", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Nvr again", "line": "Pull up outside, luh crank, yeah, and I pulled out the Benz, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Pull up outside, luh crank, yeah, and I pulled out the Benz, yeah"], "meaning": "This refers to Mercedes-Benz, a German luxury and commercial vehicle automotive brand.\n\nThis can also refer to the Mercedes-Benz GLE, mentioned previously in the song and other songs.", "annotation_id": "29232448", "url": "https://genius.com/29232448", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
