{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Nutrition in switzerland", "line": "I’ve been taking whippets, yeah, at 2 AM, yeah (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["I've been taking whippets, yeah, at 2 AM, yeah (Woo)"], "meaning": "Whippets, or nitrous oxide, are popular party inhalant drugs. You may also hear them referred to as “whippits” or “whip-its.” The drug gets its name from whipped-cream aerosol canisters that people open to misuse the gas inside. This is NOT to be confused with the British dog breed. Yeat is NOT a dog breeder.", "annotation_id": "31125331", "url": "https://genius.com/31125331", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
