{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Nun id change", "line": "I just have been stayin’ to myself, I don’t fuck with nobody, at all", "vault_lines": ["I just have been stayin' to myself, I don't fuck with nobody, at all"], "meaning": "He’s expressing a desire for solitude and isolation. He’s suggesting that he prefers to keep to himself and avoid interactions or connections with others. This could stem from a variety of reasons, such as a need for personal space, a desire to avoid drama or conflict, or perhaps feelings of mistrust or disillusionment with people around him. Yeat may be indicating that he finds solace and peace in being alone, choosing to focus on his own thoughts, emotions, and pursuits rather than engaging with others.", "annotation_id": "31021890", "url": "https://genius.com/31021890", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
