{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Nun id change", "line": "Pushin’ two-hundred, unwindin’, I’ma call a bitch up", "vault_lines": ["Pushin' two-hundred, unwindin', I'ma call a bitch up"], "meaning": "“Pushin' two-hundred and i’m whining”\n\nYeat most definitely has a supercharger in his car and when hitting top speeds they make a whine noise.", "annotation_id": "29169721", "url": "https://genius.com/29169721", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Nun id change", "line": "I don’t fuck with nobody, at all", "vault_lines": ["I don't fuck with nobody, at all"], "meaning": "YEAT uses hyperbole to illustrate that he keeps his circle of friends small.\n\nHe does fuck with some people including, his significant other, symone, and his bestie (former), September’s Rich.", "annotation_id": "28079959", "url": "https://genius.com/28079959", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Nun id change", "line": "I been fly (Fly), fly (Fly), fly (Fly), gettin’ high to the moon, man", "vault_lines": ["I been fly (Fly), fly (Fly), fly (Fly), gettin' high to the moon, man"], "meaning": "This line is often incorrectly interpreted as a metaphor, but Yeat is actually the latest person to set foot on the lunar surface. Thanks to his manned expedition, NASA scientists were able to determine that the water thought to exist on the Moon is, in fact, alien lean. The implications of this discovery may alter the course of human history.", "annotation_id": "27954027", "url": "https://genius.com/27954027", "state": "pending", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Nun id change", "line": "Gettin’ hit by a train, motherfuckin’ flame", "vault_lines": ["Gettin' hit by a train, motherfuckin' flame"], "meaning": "Truth : Yeat has done so many drugs he feels like he just got hit by a train.\n\nLie : Noah sadly got hit by a train, this caused him to almost die, he referenced this on his track “Died B4” when he says “I told ‘em I died before, they wouldn’t believe it (I did)”", "annotation_id": "27891517", "url": "https://genius.com/27891517", "state": "pending", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
