{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Now", "line": "I-I-I’m working on dying, BNYX", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, before I had these bands (I-I-I'm working on dying, BNYX"], "meaning": "“Working on Dying” is a Philadelphia-based hip-hop production collective and record label founded in 2012 by producers F1lthy and Oogie Mane . Known for their dark, heavy trap sound, they have collaborated with artists like Lil Uzi Vert, Future, and Bladee, and are prominent in the underground scene.\n\nI-I-I-I’m working on dying\nBNYX®\n\nBenjamin Saint Fort (born April 23, 1995), professionally known as BNYX® (pronounced Benny X), is an American record producer (and rapper, occasionally) from Philadelphia, Pennsylvania", "annotation_id": "39008116", "url": "https://genius.com/39008116", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Now", "line": "Really finna take ’em and pull up, la-la-la-la-la-la-la-la-la-la-la, bang ’em", "vault_lines": ["Really finna take 'em and pull up, la-la-la-la-la-la-la-la-la-la-la, bang 'em"], "meaning": "Yeat demonstrates his immense singing abilities, really putting emphasis on his dynamic and ever-changing vocal styles. Truly inspirational.", "annotation_id": "36807670", "url": "https://genius.com/36807670", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
