{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "No commënt", "line": "And the drum got a fucking stick on it", "vault_lines": ["And the drum got a fucking stick on it"], "meaning": "The drum-style magazine on Noah’s weapon is so large that it should be referred to as a “drum with a stick” as opposed to a “stick with a drum.” Yeat shifts the emphasis from the gun itself to the magazine to express its large capacity.", "annotation_id": "25485484", "url": "https://genius.com/25485484", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "No commënt", "line": "How you faking that you got a song with all of these rappers? (What?) How you faking that you got that money but you just a capper?", "vault_lines": ["How you faking that you got a song with all of these rappers? (What?)"], "meaning": "Here, Yeat sends a shot to Wick, also known as Autumn!, who was involved in a beef with Yeat himself and KanKan. The beef began after Autumn! exposed KanKan for abusing his ex-girlfriend Kandyxkat; due to the incident, Autumn! distanced himself from KanKan; despite this, Yeat decided to show support and side with KanKan, despite working with Autumn!. Following the incident, Autumn! released Portrayal!, which was released in response to Yeat by mimicking his flow and sonic style.\n\nTo combat Wick’s diss, Yeat decided to expose to the internet that Wick faked a feature with Lil Uzi Vert, which was revealed by KanKan after doing a diss about the exposing. To respond to KanKan, Wick did a diss against KanKan, Yeat, and SeptembersRich about the incident of stealing sounds and flows.", "annotation_id": "25483166", "url": "https://genius.com/25483166", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
