{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Never quit", "line": "Heard you need somebody, don’t you ever call me", "vault_lines": ["Heard you need somebody, don't you ever call me"], "meaning": "This is a display of Yeat’s devil-may-care attitude. He also professes that he is a loner and doesn’t like to be around people. People know that he is antisocial and does not care about anyone or anything about money. He is warning the person this message is for not to call on him for help in case of trouble.\n\nKw1ky Meaning: I don’t think it’s a line showing he’s antisocial / evil but rather a reference to haters / people who may have doubted him and who now ask for help", "annotation_id": "33542585", "url": "https://genius.com/33542585", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Never quit", "line": "Why the fuck you think that you could trust me? (Why?)", "vault_lines": ["Why the fuck you think that you could trust me? (Why?)"], "meaning": "In the previous line, Yeat saying “smokin' cigs” sounds like “moccasins”, a genus of venomous pit vipers, therefore referring to a snake. In modern slang, snake can refer to a person who acts in a deceitful way, underhanded, or backstabbing way, ultimately being untrustworthy.", "annotation_id": "32426668", "url": "https://genius.com/32426668", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
