{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Narcoticz", "line": "Uh-uh, uh-uh (Ah), say it again, not your kid, not your cuddy", "vault_lines": ["Uh-uh, uh-uh (Ah), say it again, not your kid, not your cuddy"], "meaning": "Yeat references Cleveland rapper Kid Cudi.", "annotation_id": "25166931", "url": "https://genius.com/25166931", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Narcoticz", "line": "Uh-uh, uh-uh (Ah), say it again, not your kid, not your cuddy", "vault_lines": ["Uh-uh, uh-uh (Ah), say it again, not your kid, not your cuddy"], "meaning": "Yeat references Cleveland rapper Kid Cudi.\n\n\n\n“Cuddie” or “cuddy,” short for “cutthroat,” is a Bay Area slang term popularized by the late Vallejo rapper Mac Dre with a similar meaning to “homie.”\n\nHe also used this line on 4L so the “say it again” part is referencing that", "annotation_id": "25166504", "url": "https://genius.com/25166504", "state": "pending", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
