{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Naked", "line": "Yeah, I just like to see you take it", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I just like to see you take it"], "meaning": "He likes to see her get intercourse (assuming he is not a cuck, from himself)", "annotation_id": "39150832", "url": "https://genius.com/39150832", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Naked", "line": "And I’m back in the city, back in the city, back in, baby (Is it worth the risk? Ayy, ooh)", "vault_lines": ["And I'm back in the city, back in the city, back in, baby (Is it worth the risk? Ayy, ooh)"], "meaning": "Returning to the city suggests a cycle, where Yeat re-enters the same environment and repeats the same behaviors. It ties into the album’s recurring theme of being unable to break patterns.", "annotation_id": "39149395", "url": "https://genius.com/39149395", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Naked", "line": "And I’m back in the city, back in the city, back in, baby (Is it worth the risk? Ayy, ooh)", "vault_lines": ["And I'm back in the city, back in the city, back in, baby (Is it worth the risk? Ayy, ooh)"], "meaning": "Returning to the city suggests a cycle, where Yeat re-enters the same environment and repeats the same behaviors. It ties into the album’s recurring theme of being unable to break patterns.", "annotation_id": "39149393", "url": "https://genius.com/39149393", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Naked", "line": "A dangerous game I’m always playin’", "vault_lines": ["A dangerous game I'm always playin'"], "meaning": "Yeat acknowledges the risk in his behavior, suggesting that his lifestyle and relationships are part of an ongoing cycle of self-destructive choices. The word “game” implies he’s aware, but still continues.", "annotation_id": "39149390", "url": "https://genius.com/39149390", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Naked", "line": "Different girls in different cities", "vault_lines": ["Different girls in different cities"], "meaning": "This line highlights repetition and lack of attachment. Relationships are interchangeable and tied to location rather than emotion, emphasizing a lifestyle built on constant movement and detachment.", "annotation_id": "39149383", "url": "https://genius.com/39149383", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Naked", "line": "I don’t like the games you playin’", "vault_lines": ["I don't like the games you playin'"], "meaning": "Yeat rejects emotional complexity or “games,” preferring direct, physical interaction. This reflects his inability, or unwillingness, to engage with deeper feelings, reinforcing the theme of emotional avoidance.", "annotation_id": "39149375", "url": "https://genius.com/39149375", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Naked", "line": "I, I just like to see you naked I just like to see you naked", "vault_lines": ["I, I just like to see you naked"], "meaning": "Yeat reduces attraction to pure physicality, stripping away emotion and personality. By focusing only on appearance, he dehumanizes the relationship, showing that intimacy in his world is detached from any deeper connection.", "annotation_id": "39149372", "url": "https://genius.com/39149372", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
