{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "NIGHT COME", "line": "Yeah, just face it (Yeah)", "vault_lines": [", yeah, just face it (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat adds this part of the line to “Like a blunt” to make a clever play on words.\nHe’s so rich that you have to just face it, or accept the fact that his money is seemingly endless. But also, “just face it” is a reference to “Like a blunt,” because the term “to face a blunt” is used to refer to smoking marijuana.", "annotation_id": "39467310", "url": "https://genius.com/39467310", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
