{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "NEW KRANKy", "line": "All these pussies wanna kick it I told them, “Taekwondo”", "vault_lines": ["All these pussies wanna kick it"], "meaning": "To “kick it” is understood as a colloquial way of saying to hang out or relax with someone. Yeat is saying that many female partners want to spend time with him. He then responds by saying, “Taekwondo.” Taekwondo is a martial art with a strong emphasis on kicking techniques. The word “Tae” in Taekwondo literally means “foot” or “to strike with the feet”. So Yeat is giving a clever or humourous response to the request to “kick it.”", "annotation_id": "37202608", "url": "https://genius.com/37202608", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
