{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Mysëlf", "line": "Dreams, talk ’bout lies, yeah, dreams, talk ’bout lies, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Dreams, talk 'bout lies, yeah, dreams, talk 'bout lies, yeah"], "meaning": "In the song “Myself” by rapper Yeat, the lyrics “Dreams, talk ‘bout lies, yeah, dreams, talk 'bout lies, yeah” suggest a juxtaposition between aspirations and falsehoods. This contrast can be interpreted in several ways:\n\n\nAspirations vs. Deceptions: The lyrics may highlight the tension between one’s dreams or goals and the lies one might tell themselves or others to achieve or justify those dreams.\nReality vs. Illusion: It could reflect the struggle between what one desires (dreams) and the misleading or untrue narratives (lies) that often surround or distort the path to achieving those desires.\nInner Conflict: These lines might indicate an internal conflict where dreams and lies coexist, suggesting that the pursuit of one’s dreams can sometimes involve self-deception or dealing with the falsehoods of others.\n\n\n\nOverall, the lyrics encapsulate a reflective moment where the artist contemplates the complex relationship between ambition and dishonesty.", "annotation_id": "32555004", "url": "https://genius.com/32555004", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Mysëlf", "line": "Talkin’ life, talkin’ life (Dreams), huh Talkin’ life, talkin’ life (Dreams), huh Talkin’ life, talkin’ life (Dreams)", "vault_lines": ["Talkin' 'bout life, from the love, uh, dreams from above"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that he is referring to his Life, and his Dreams. Probably trying to give the song a more heartfelt and “Real” tone.", "annotation_id": "32521112", "url": "https://genius.com/32521112", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
