{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Mysëlf", "line": "I don’t give a fuck ’bout nothin’, not even myself", "vault_lines": ["I don't give a fuck 'bout nothin', not even myself"], "meaning": "Yeat may signify his acknowledgment of his neglectful behavior towards their own well-being, potentially influenced by drug use. It suggests a profound disregard for both external concerns and personal health, highlighting a prioritization of immediate gratification over long-term consequences. This interpretation underscores the destructive nature of substance abuse and the toll it takes on physical and mental health. The repetition of the phrase emphasizes the depth of the speaker’s apathy and the extent to which he is disconnected from their own self-care. Overall, the line conveys a sense of self-destructive behavior and the struggles associated with addiction, capturing yeat disregard for both external responsibilities and their own bodily health in the pursuit of temporary relief or escape through drugs.", "annotation_id": "31021736", "url": "https://genius.com/31021736", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Mysëlf", "line": "Uh, I was yellin’ out, “Help,” yeah", "vault_lines": ["Uh, I was yellin' out, \"Help,\" yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat talks about drugs frequently in his lyrics, with some of the lyrics focusing on the bad part of having a drug problem but the track having an overall positive sound.\n\nIn this lyric, he calls attention to the lyrics he would say in those other songs, and confirming that he wasent bragging about his relationship to drugs, but crying for help, but his cries for help in his lyrics were shadowed by the hype sound of the beats he rapped over.", "annotation_id": "29514888", "url": "https://genius.com/29514888", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Mysëlf", "line": "I don’t give a fuck ’bout nothin’, not even myself", "vault_lines": ["I don't give a fuck 'bout nothin', not even myself"], "meaning": "This line could be seen as Yeat’s stark and nihilistic worldview. It becomes evident that his perspective is deeply influenced by this nihilistic thinking, which, in turn, has profound implications for his mental and emotional well-being. Yeat’s declaration that he doesn’t care about anything, not even himself, suggests a profound detachment from the world around him.\n\n“Not even myself” underscores how Yeat’s nihilistic outlook has affected his self-esteem and self-worth. It implies that he is experiencing self-destructive tendencies, such as substance abuse, as he has lost the motivation to prioritize his physical and mental health.", "annotation_id": "29454583", "url": "https://genius.com/29454583", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
