{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Mysëlf", "line": "And they wanted to diss, I didn’t I just sit back and, listen", "vault_lines": ["I just sit back and, listen"], "meaning": "YEAT and his son (autumn) have been in an ongoing quarrel online. The two have traded disses through social media posts, as well as in their musical tracks. Autumn has dissed YEAT several times throughout this scuffle, while YEAT rarely responds. The patterns of online interaction between the former comrades illustrate that YEAT does not care about autumn’s disses towards him. YEAT’s silence throughout shows he is above the childish behavior in which autumn continues to participate.\n\nBro deadass just sits back and listen.\n\nIn conclusion, YEAT > autumn", "annotation_id": "28079877", "url": "https://genius.com/28079877", "state": "pending", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Mysëlf", "line": "I don’t give a fuck ‘bout nothin’, I don’t give a fuck ’bout nothin’", "vault_lines": ["I don't give a fuck 'bout nothin', I don't give a fuck 'bout nothin'"], "meaning": "Myself starts off with very boastful lyrics about how Yeat doesn’t care about anything, before revealing how this uncaring and “I don’t give a fuck” attitude has negatively effected his health and left him empty and alone.", "annotation_id": "27983463", "url": "https://genius.com/27983463", "state": "pending", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Mysëlf", "line": "They can’t even fuck with the kid (Yeah) They can’t even fuck with the world I didn’t even knew that existed", "vault_lines": ["They can't even fuck with the god"], "meaning": "Yeat is likely referring to his innocence as a child or the early stages of his drug use & his unawareness of the effects, going on to say “I’m talkin’ ’bout these damages, from the drugs”. If you interpret the verse allegorically, “they\" might represent drugs. It seems to suggest that Yeat is reflecting on the impact of his drug use and the loss of his innocence, possibly implying a sense of regret or remorse for his actions.", "annotation_id": "27951372", "url": "https://genius.com/27951372", "state": "pending", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
