{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Moshpit fukit", "line": "Blah-blah, blah-blah, blah-blah, blah-blah, blah-blah, blah-blah, shut up, bitch (Yeah) Blah-blah, blah-blah, blah-blah, blah-blah, blah-blah, I get belligerent, I can’t even speak (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, turn up, turn up, turn up"], "meaning": "With this bar, Yeat is saying that everything his girl says to him just sounds like nonsense.", "annotation_id": "28466190", "url": "https://genius.com/28466190", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Moshpit fukit", "line": "(Tose’) Bitch, I’m sippin’ on mud, mud, mud (Tose’) Bitch, I’m sippin’ on mud, mud, mud (Tose’) Bitch, I’m sippin’ on mud, mud, mud (Tose’)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm sippin' on mud, mud, mud (Tose’)"], "meaning": "If it isn’t apparent enough, Yeat refers to lean as mud.", "annotation_id": "28165073", "url": "https://genius.com/28165073", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Moshpit fukit", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-moshpit-fukit-lyrics", "genius_title": "Moshpit fukit", "genius_id": 7807461, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Morë", "line": "I could lose control, uh, I’m a CEO, uh You can’t lose control, shit, ’cause you don’t have self control", "vault_lines": ["I could lose control, uh, I'm a CEO, uh"], "meaning": "Yeat’s persona on this track, as stated at the beginning of the verse, is that of Psycho CEO. As described in the album’s first track, Psycho CEO is a man with incredible power and terrifying wealth who is always in control of himself and his circumstances. Paradoxically, however, Psycho CEO also loves losing control, giving into his baser desires. By contrast, you have no self control, so how can you lose something you don’t have?", "annotation_id": "31735899", "url": "https://genius.com/31735899", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Morë", "line": "Makin’ trillion dollar money in this fuckin’ Forbes I’m a selfish fuck, yeah, I need more", "vault_lines": ["Makin' trillion dollar monеy in this fuckin' Forbes"], "meaning": "Forbes is famously known for documenting entrepreneur’s wealth, such as their Real Time Billionaire’s List or their 30 Under 30 list. They span and track success across all industries, including music. Currently, the richest rapper is JAY-Z with an estimated $2.5 Billion net worth, as of 2024, compared to Yeat’s estimated $5 Million. This shows how unrealistic that accomplishment of making “trillion dollar money” would be and how narcissistic Yeat is trying to display himself with the line, “I’m a selfish fuck, yeah, I need more.”\n\nYeat could also be talking about this from a perspective of a CEO (he characterizes himself as one in this album) whom are commonly considered the richest people in the world, and are the most closely monitored and documented by net worth websites like Forbes and Celebrity Net Worth. He could be displaying their greed and their lust for money, which never ends, which is why he also addresses himself as a “psycho CEO” like the intro track to 2093.\n\nThis is further reached with “Put a condo on the moon so they can’t talk to us,” as SpaceX and Tesla CEO Elon Musk had taken a $2.7 Billion dollar contract from NASA to go to the moon under the Artemis mission.", "annotation_id": "30937086", "url": "https://genius.com/30937086", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Morë", "line": "You can’t look back at your life and tell me one thing", "vault_lines": ["You can't look back at your life and tell me one thing"], "meaning": "Yeat can be referring to Generation Z, the generation known for being on screens the most and having a significantly short attention span. Some cases are so severe they become isolated out of social settings, and fall behind with learning skill, unable to possess common sense or life skills required to survive.\n\nAnother meaning could be his haters who are chronically online and  have nothing going on in their life  and if they were to have a conversation with Yeat they wouldn’t be able to tell him because of embarrassment.", "annotation_id": "30927473", "url": "https://genius.com/30927473", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Morë", "line": "No, you can’t get in with us, you a stupid fuck", "vault_lines": ["No, you can't get in with us, you a stupid fuck"], "meaning": "Yeat is on a whole other level. And doesn’t just rock with anyone. He doesn’t rock with what he calls “Lames”.", "annotation_id": "30926227", "url": "https://genius.com/30926227", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Morë", "line": "You always on the screen (Huh, huh)", "vault_lines": ["You always on the screen (Huh, huh)"], "meaning": "All of yeats haters sit behind a screen and talk bad about him. But they could never say the things they say to yeat if they were ever face to face.", "annotation_id": "30926076", "url": "https://genius.com/30926076", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Morë", "line": "And every time you thought you wanted somethin’, you needed more And then it come right back at you, throw you overboard", "vault_lines": ["And every time you thought you wanted somethin', you needed more"], "meaning": "These 2 lines refrence the middle stages of addiction, where you begin to take more drugs to have the same effect that they had in the beginning. The last line represents how addiction will end up controlling your life and “[throwing] you overboard”", "annotation_id": "30925375", "url": "https://genius.com/30925375", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Morë", "line": "I got tired of this shit, I had to let you go You remind me of something that I think I know, uh It remind me of myself when I lose control, uh", "vault_lines": ["It remind me of myself when I lose control, uh"], "meaning": "This set of lines refrences Yeats drug addiction. In an instagram story in october, he said he was 15 days sober and locking in on this album. The first line refrences the drugs themselves, saying he needs to let them go. While the second and third line refer to himself when he was on the drugs and losing control to them.", "annotation_id": "30925293", "url": "https://genius.com/30925293", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Morë", "line": "Yeah, comin’ out the woods at your yellow Ford", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, comin' out the woods at your yellow Ford"], "meaning": "In this line yeat warns his enemies that he is armed and dangerous.\n\n“fore” is a warning term shouted to alert others on the course when a golf ball is heading in their direction to prevent accidents or injuries.\n\nThis line is also a double entendre with the phrase “comin out the woods” being a reference to legendary golf player tiger woods and Yeat’s own forest property where producer Bnyx posted photos of himself and yeat shooting guns", "annotation_id": "30898599", "url": "https://genius.com/30898599", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Morë", "line": "Playin’ with they minds, remote control", "vault_lines": ["Playin' with they minds, remote control"], "meaning": "The lyric “Playin’ with they minds, remote control” by Yeat suggests the idea of exerting control or influence over others as if operating a remote control. It conveys the notion of manipulating or directing someone’s thoughts or actions to one’s advantage.", "annotation_id": "30898507", "url": "https://genius.com/30898507", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Morë", "line": "Put a condo on the moon so they can’t talk to us (Huh, huh)", "vault_lines": ["Put a condo on the moon so they can't talk to us (Huh, huh)"], "meaning": "This lyric suggests a desire to achieve a level of isolation or privacy that is so extreme that Yeat wants to place a condominium on the moon, a location far removed from Earth, to ensure that he cannot be reached or bothered by others.", "annotation_id": "30898489", "url": "https://genius.com/30898489", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
