{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Monëy so big", "line": "I ride that big body right out the lot, it’s a GLE, came with a tint", "vault_lines": ["I ride that big body right out the lot, it's a GLE, came with a tint"], "meaning": "The Mercedes-Benz AMG GLE is a luxury SUV.\n\nYeat even flexed in front of his GLE in the official music video to “Still Countin.”\n\n\n\n Yeat and his GLE", "annotation_id": "36771672", "url": "https://genius.com/36771672", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Monëy so big", "line": "Yeah, I pulled up in a Tonka and a helicopter, I’m goin’ nuts", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I pulled up in a Tonka and a helicopter, I'm goin' nuts"], "meaning": "Although the word “Tonka” stems from Tonka toy trucks, it refers to luxury high-powered SUVs, such as the Lamborghini Urus, which he owns and also frequently mentions in his music.\n\n\n\n Yeat and his Urus \n\nYeat even has a custom Tonka chain, created by Icebox in 2022.\n\n\n\nYeat also released several tracks named after it, including “Big tonka,” “Tonka,” and “Tonka 2.”", "annotation_id": "36771493", "url": "https://genius.com/36771493", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Monëy so big", "line": "Bitch ’bout to ride me like she on a RipStik", "vault_lines": ["Bitch 'bout to ride me like she on a RipStik"], "meaning": "RipStik is a brand of two-wheeled caster boards manufactured by Razor.", "annotation_id": "36771474", "url": "https://genius.com/36771474", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Monëy so big", "line": "Can’t even count the songs I made in a month, that’s a hundred and sixty hits (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Can't even count the songs I made in a month, that's a hundred and sixty hits (Yeah)"], "meaning": "In an Instagram Live on June 7, 2021, 2 days before recording Monëy so big, Yeat shows fans his song files on his computer for the last 30 days, showing that he made 175 songs in just the past 30 days alone (granted, some of them were just duplicates and instrumentals, but still impressive).", "annotation_id": "35277462", "url": "https://genius.com/35277462", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Monëy so big", "line": "Yeah, my money big body, my money Tonka", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, my money big body, my money Tonka"], "meaning": "Yeat exclaims that his money is as big as a Tonka Truck, meaning he has large amounts of money.", "annotation_id": "29362882", "url": "https://genius.com/29362882", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Monëy so big", "line": "I ride that big body right out the lot, it’s a GLE, came with a tint", "vault_lines": ["I ride that big body right out the lot, it's a GLE, came with a tint"], "meaning": "Yeat often carries his lingo throughout different songs, establishing his own recognisable dialect – allowing Yeat fans to feel a sense of connection to the artist. ‘Big body’ is a term that Yeat uses commonly describing the size of his car… or ‘Tonka’.\n\nHe also confirms the car which he’s talking about here is a ‘GLE’ (which is Yeat’s Matte Black Mercedes-Benz GLE 43 AMG).", "annotation_id": "28300950", "url": "https://genius.com/28300950", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
