{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk 2", "line": "I notice how they copy swag, I got 60 kids (Yeah, yeah) I was the first one to switch it up, I ain’t new to this (No I ain’t)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, ran it up, ran it up (Up)"], "meaning": "Yeat lets his copy-cats know he is onto them and sees them mimicking his style.\n\nIn terms of music, Yeat is undeniably one of the most notable in the Cloud Rap and Hyperpop genres that are very popular today. With this, it seems he is calling out people for riding his wave and trying to recreate his unique sound.", "annotation_id": "27183712", "url": "https://genius.com/27183712", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk 2", "line": "I done crashed the Cayenne, the left side is scuffed (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["I done crashed the Cayenne, the left side is scuffed (Woo)"], "meaning": "With this line, Yeat is referencing the Porsche Cayenne, manufactured by Porsche.\n\n\n\nYeat informs us that he has, unfortunately, crashed the luxury vehicle, most likely due to an indulgence in substances beforehand.", "annotation_id": "27183684", "url": "https://genius.com/27183684", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk 2", "line": "Yeah, I take this X so much, I thought I was flyin’ or some’ Yeah (Brr), Every mornin’, we takin’ flight or some’ (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I take this X so much, I thought I was flyin’ or some'"], "meaning": "X is short for ecstasy, a drug used for it’s effects, including: altered sensations, increased energy, empathy, and pleasure.\n\nYeat is saying that whenever he takes ecstasy, the effects of it makes him feel so high he imagines he is actually flying.", "annotation_id": "27183678", "url": "https://genius.com/27183678", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk 2", "line": "I don’t really (Nah), need this deal, bitch, I’m up", "vault_lines": ["I don't really (Nah), need this deal, bitch, I'm up"], "meaning": "Another line expressing Yeat’s great newfound income.\n\nUsually, when an artist signs a contract with a label, the label offers the artist money in order to pay for the artist’s services working for them.\n\nWith this line however, Yeat is stating that he is making enough money on his own and doesn’t need to sign a deal for profit.", "annotation_id": "27183641", "url": "https://genius.com/27183641", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk 2", "line": "Yeah, ran it up, ran it up (Up) All my pockets, uh, way too swollen, bitch, they buff", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, ran it up, ran it up (Up)"], "meaning": "Yeat saying that with his newfound success in rapping, his income rate is exceptionally high, making it so when he puts his money into his pockets, the large amount of cash makes them look swollen or as if they work out, making them appear buff.\n\nA “swollen” pocket of money", "annotation_id": "27183607", "url": "https://genius.com/27183607", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk 2", "line": "I went copped the Range, they gave me an umbrella", "vault_lines": ["I went copped the Range, they gave me an umbrella"], "meaning": "In this line Yeat is referring to the manufacturing brand, Land Rover’s car, the Range Rover.\n\nMost likely, Yeat is referring to the 2019, Range Rover Evoque Convertible model when he says, “…they gave me an umbrella.”\n\n\n\nThe Evoque Convertible is a Range that features a drop-top style upper so the “umbrella” Yeat is referring to is probably the cover that is able to be attached.", "annotation_id": "27183511", "url": "https://genius.com/27183511", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk 2", "line": "Yeah, I went copped the ’Pane, took it back to L.A.", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I went copped the 'Pane, took it back to L.A."], "meaning": "Stilpane is a brand of cough syrup that is abused and shipped to places like the US for cheap as normal lean prices are taxing.", "annotation_id": "25241791", "url": "https://genius.com/25241791", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
