{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "Take the bitch to Margiela, she go (Go)", "vault_lines": ["Take the bitch to Margiela, she go (Go)"], "meaning": "Maison Margiela, formerly Maison Martin Margiela, is a French luxury fashion house founded by Belgian designer Martin Margiela and Jenny Meirens in 1988 and headquartered in Paris.", "annotation_id": "28347297", "url": "https://genius.com/28347297", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "No AM to PM in 7-Eleven", "vault_lines": ["No AM to PM in 7-Eleven"], "meaning": "7-Eleven is a multinational convivence store chain, famously known for being open 24 hours a day. In this line, Yeat is referencing this fact, by saying that since the store is open in both the AM and PM hours of the day, there is no AM to PM in 7-11.", "annotation_id": "27401021", "url": "https://genius.com/27401021", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "Yeah, you rock Marc Jacobs, you smelly", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you rock Marc Jacobs, you smelly"], "meaning": "Apparently yeat isn’t a fan of the gay fashion designer Marc Jacobs. Possible homophobia. The negative votes on this annotation confirm.", "annotation_id": "27045187", "url": "https://genius.com/27045187", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "Fuck off the wave, you can’t ride in my boat (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["Fuck off the wave, you can't ride in my boat (Skrrt)"], "meaning": "A ‘boat’ is slang for a car with an extremely long front-end (typically built by an American manufacturer). Companies who have routinely designed cars of this style include Buick, Cadillac, and Chrysler. One of the few American “land boats” still in-production as of 2021 is the Dodge Challenger Hellcat, which Yeat has referenced in previous songs. Yeat’s adlibs also allude to him driving recklessly, by drifting and stepping on the gas in a quick fashion.", "annotation_id": "26679035", "url": "https://genius.com/26679035", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "Please don’t make me go, shh, like Melly", "vault_lines": ["Please don't make me go, shh, like Melly"], "meaning": "Florida rapper YNW Melly is being accused of shooting 2 of his friends, however it’s not confirmed.\n\nYeat is threatening that he would do something similar if someone would cross him.", "annotation_id": "25422799", "url": "https://genius.com/25422799", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "Second I pour up some Wock’ so I feel some (Go)", "vault_lines": ["Second I pour up some Wock' so I feel some (Go)"], "meaning": "Wock also known as Lean is a Promethazine and Codeine cough syrup mixed with sugary soda such as Faygo and Sprite It gets its name from the producer of the cough syrup, Wockhardt. Wockhardt cough syrup is a highly controlled substance for its sedative effects.", "annotation_id": "25397429", "url": "https://genius.com/25397429", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "Back to back, switch it to the Cayenne on the black top", "vault_lines": ["Back to back, switch it to the Cayenne on the black top"], "meaning": "Yeat flexes his massive SUV portfolio to listeners, and suggests on top of his custom GLE73 AMG and SRT Trackhawk, he also has a Porsche Cayenne that he is not afraid to daily drive.", "annotation_id": "25349367", "url": "https://genius.com/25349367", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "My twizzy gon’ lose it, pull out the lil’ Uzi", "vault_lines": ["My twizzy gon' lose it, pull out the lil' Uzi"], "meaning": "Twizzy is another word for twin or brother and they are going to lose it or go crazy and pull out a uzi a machine pistol known for its high rate of fire", "annotation_id": "25168704", "url": "https://genius.com/25168704", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "How I make two hundred bands off a laptop? (Two hundred)", "vault_lines": ["How I make two hundred bands off a laptop? (Two hundred)"], "meaning": "Yeat looks back on the days before he had the resources he now has. From a simple view, rappers going down his lane are opening up a source of income that seems almost unfair or unreal if you don’t take into account the work ethic they put in. They make the small investment of a $400-$2,000 laptop or desktop computer and flip that investment to $200,000 in streaming revenue, backend payouts and other forms that lead them to have little worries financially contrary to their state before rapping.", "annotation_id": "24473506", "url": "https://genius.com/24473506", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "Eliantte diamonds on me, I’m flooded (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Eliantte diamonds on me, I'm flooded (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Eliantte—primarily known for their chains, bracelets, and watches—is one of few jewelers who bring in frequent celebrity clients, especially rappers. Now being wealthy enough to afford, Yeat chooses to indulge in the high-end brand.", "annotation_id": "24473480", "url": "https://genius.com/24473480", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "I don’t wish for shit in this life, fuck a genie, yeah (Uh, uh)", "vault_lines": ["I don't wish for shit in this life, fuck a genie, yeah (Uh, uh)"], "meaning": "In Arabic culture a genie is a magical being that lives inside a lamp until they are summoned after which they grant the summoner three wishes.\n\n\n\nYeat likens his lack of need for the things people wish for to that of not needing a genie.", "annotation_id": "24473459", "url": "https://genius.com/24473459", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "Her coochie balder than bald, that bitch Caillou", "vault_lines": ["Her coochie balder than bald, that bitch Caillou"], "meaning": "Caillou is a successful Canadian television show made for kids. The protagonist, Caillou is known for his bald appearance which raised many different opinions on why the character was bald past babyhood. Some believe it was due to cancer, the illness that requires patients to take medications that kill excess cells including hair cells. Some believe Caillou would be unrecognizable being that he started off bald in the show.\n\nYeat makes a reference to the renowned baldness of Caillou in comparison to the subject’s vaginal areas lacking hair.", "annotation_id": "24473427", "url": "https://genius.com/24473427", "state": "pending", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "Make hits, slidin’ like Toosie, we rich like Lil’ Boosie", "vault_lines": ["Make hits, slidin' like Toosie, we rich like Lil' Boosie"], "meaning": "“Toosie Slide” is a song by Canadian rapper Drake from his commercial mixtape Dark Lane Demo Tapes (2020). It was released as the lead single on April 3, 2020, through Republic and OVO. The song is titled after social media influencer Toosie, who had previously helped the song go viral.\n\nHe also mentions Lil Boosie, which simply is just a shoutout.", "annotation_id": "24364330", "url": "https://genius.com/24364330", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "Canary yellow diamonds on piss, R Kelly (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Canary yellow diamonds on piss, R Kelly (Yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "This is in reference to when Robert Sylvester Kelly urinated on an underage woman. YEAT would not do this. But, commonly, canary yellow diamonds are referred to as piss or pee colored.", "annotation_id": "24360677", "url": "https://genius.com/24360677", "state": "pending", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "Got hundreds on me every day, yeah, blueys (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Got hundreds on me every day, yeah, blueys (Yeah)"], "meaning": "$100 bills, since October 8, 2013, have had a noticeable blue tint in comparison to bills of lower value. They also have a blue stripe down the center, to distinguish between real and fake bills.\n\nFlaunting his wealth, Yeat frequently carries hundred dollar bills, leaving no worries of being too short on cash—meaning his money is blue, not green.", "annotation_id": "23925684", "url": "https://genius.com/23925684", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "First I’ma pour up the Tris for the real ones", "vault_lines": ["First I'ma pour up the Tris for the real ones"], "meaning": "This lyric could have one of two meanings.\n\nIf you look at the lyrics the way they’re posted, Yeat is pouring a cup of lean for his “real ones” being those close to him. This could be looked at as Yeat pouring their cup before his as to be a “real one” himself\n\n“First, I’ma pour OUT the Tris for the real ones” is the way the lyric sounds in the song, and given he says “the” instead of “some” like he does in the line that follows this one, it seems likely this is the case.\n\nThe act of pouring out a drink (usually alcoholic) is a sign of remembrance for a friend or family member passing away. Yeat being a frequent sipper has decided instead of alcohol he’s going to pour out the much more expensive Tris (a brand of promethazine-codeine syrup) in remembrance of his “real ones” or dead homies.", "annotation_id": "23925573", "url": "https://genius.com/23925573", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "I might mix with an X, I might go leave the Earth", "vault_lines": ["I might mix with an X, I might go leave the Earth"], "meaning": "MDMA, commonly referred to as ecstasy, E, molly, or X, is a drug mostly used recreationally. The drug makes one feel euphoric and have their senses heightened.\n\n\n\nIn the previous lines, Yeat established that he’s been drinking lean and using Percocets. Here he claims he’s going to use ecstasy, along with the two, leading to a dangerous combination—resulting in many side effects, including the feeling of floating, or “leaving Earth.”", "annotation_id": "23923477", "url": "https://genius.com/23923477", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "I got two phones, one to scam, one the burner (Brrt)", "vault_lines": ["I got two phones, one to scam, one the burner (Brrt)"], "meaning": "A “burner phone” is a cheap and disposable phone that users can easily destroy or get rid of easily. As cybercrime becomes more traceable, criminals often use burner phones or numbers to avoid being caught. Similar tactics, such as VoIP services, VPNs, and temporary mail services, are also used to stay as anonymous as possible online.", "annotation_id": "23906245", "url": "https://genius.com/23906245", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "Go double cup Wock’ and then mix with a Perc’ (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Go double cup Wock' and then mix with a Perc' (Yeah)"], "meaning": "“Wockhardt” a.k.a. “Wock” is a pharmaceutical brand offering codeine, which is used in the creation of lean. Percocets (Percs) are a type of highly addictive drug.\n\nLean is usually served in double cups\n\nYeat has previously admitted to frequently using both drugs, in both songs and interviews", "annotation_id": "23854644", "url": "https://genius.com/23854644", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "My twizzy gon’ lose it, pull out the lil’ Uzi (Bah) Make hits, slidin’ like Toosie,", "vault_lines": ["My twizzy gon' lose it, pull out the lil' Uzi"], "meaning": "“Twizzy” is a term used notably by Yeat and other members of SlayWorld to mean “twin”\n\nUzis are popular compact sub machine guns used frequently in criminal activity. Lil Uzi Vert is an artist Yeat has referenced previously in songs such as “X ta C”\n\nI feel like Lil Uzi, you heard what I said lil' bitch\n\n“Sliding” means pulling up to an enemy to confront them, usually to hurt/kill them\n\n“Toosie slide” is a viral song created by drake, which also came with a dance. “Make hits” can be double entendre as it can refer to murder but also to making popular songs, which both toosie slide and money twërk are\n\nYeat is essentially saying that his twin is about to lose his temper and let his weapon dance on his enemies", "annotation_id": "23854565", "url": "https://genius.com/23854565", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Twërk", "line": "These kids gon’ cap a lot, call it fushigi (Fushigi)", "vault_lines": ["These kids gon' cap a lot, call it fushigi (Fushigi)"], "meaning": "In this line, Yeat is referring to the popular “as seen on tv” product from the late 2000’s, the “Fushigi Magic Gravity Ball.” The Fushigi ball received criticism from the public upon release due to it not following its commercial’s claims stating it could be used to “defy gravity and appear to float in mid-air.” Yeat is comparing this false advertisement from the Fushigi brand to how these kids are capping.", "annotation_id": "23750344", "url": "https://genius.com/23750344", "state": "pending", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
