{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "Bitch, I’m 20, but I’ma clap her when we lit, every day", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm 20, but I'ma clap her when we lit, every day"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying here that even though he is 20, he still drinks alcohol and gets drunk while having sex despite not being 21.", "annotation_id": "39515056", "url": "https://genius.com/39515056", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "Uh, no they not even higher, ’cause I see they not even showing up Why she hit my phone so much? I swear that she gon’ blow it up I do what I want every day ’cause I know enough This money shit is great, but, fuck it all, ‘cause I’m gon’ throw it up (spend it) Yeah, you could have made it, but you didn’t ’cause you fucked it up Now I got this Rollie looking different ’cause I bust it up (yeah) And I got a Fanta with some Tris, I’m ’bout to pour it up I thank God that I’m rich, ’cause back then, yeah, I was so poor enough (let’s go)", "vault_lines": ["Uh, no they not even higher, 'cause I see they not even showing up"], "meaning": "He flowed hard right here", "annotation_id": "39449558", "url": "https://genius.com/39449558", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "Money in the escrow, bought a new estate, just to raise my power", "vault_lines": ["Money in the escrow, bought a new estate, just to raise my power"], "meaning": "Escrow is basically a financial arrangement where a neutral third party holds funds or assets on behalf of two parties involved in a transaction until specific conditions are met. So, basically, people pay his estate for him.\n   Yeat claims this will bring him power and rank in society.", "annotation_id": "36876494", "url": "https://genius.com/36876494", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "Got some fresh rolled Backwood, window shake, we just smoking louder", "vault_lines": ["Got some fresh rolled Backwood, window shake, we just smoking louder"], "meaning": "Here Yeat is saying he smoking, assumably weed, from a brand of best-selling filled cigar called Backwoods.\n\n\n\n   Commonly in 420 culture, weed is referred to as “loud”- because of its distinct and powerful odor. Yeat plays on the term by implying he is smoking so loud, the windows in a building could shake- as though it were from literal sound shock waves.", "annotation_id": "36876439", "url": "https://genius.com/36876439", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "Okay, let’s go, if you wanna bake, we can hit the towers (Let’s go)", "vault_lines": ["Okay, let's go, if you wanna bake, we can hit the towers (Let's go)"], "meaning": "I personally believe that Yeat is refering to a building of club space, however, that cannot rule out the more in-your-face assumption taht yeat is somehow aligning “baking” (either getting high or making drugs), to the September 11th, 2001 terrorist attacks on the world trade center. He is perhaps comparing putting a flame to a joint/blunt to the the flames that came from the initial impact of the planes.\n\n  \n\n   As a self-indulgent input, I’d like to recall W. B. Yeats' poem ‘The Tower’ that portrays the absurdity of growing old.", "annotation_id": "36828274", "url": "https://genius.com/36828274", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "No, no, we don’t do no date, I don’t buy no flowers", "vault_lines": ["No, no, we don't do no date, I don't buy no flowers"], "meaning": "Yeat is claiming that he doesn’t partake in literal, traditional dates and buying girls flowers. This can be confirmed in his reoccuring use of describing the women he’s with as “bitches” or “hoes”, saying that these terms are either all he wants of them OR they are the specific types of women he gets with.", "annotation_id": "36828249", "url": "https://genius.com/36828249", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "I just got my mojo from my dojo like I’m Austin Powers", "vault_lines": ["I just got my mojo from my dojo like I'm Austin Powers"], "meaning": "In this line,Yeat makes a reference to the Austin Power series of comedic action films. According to the Fandom Wiki, Mojo is a viscous liquid essence of Austin Powers' sex drive that provides his prowess.\n   And accoriding to Urban Dictionary, Mojo Dojo is a figure of speech used in reference to a man or woman experiencing something that increases their ability to attract and satisfy sexual partners, to Yeat is saying he has.", "annotation_id": "36828190", "url": "https://genius.com/36828190", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "I just spend three thousand on a belt, I count this shit for hours", "vault_lines": ["I just spend three thousand on a belt, I count this shit for hours"], "meaning": "$3,000 USD is a lot of cash to spend on only a belt, which is most likely exactly Yeat says this- to flex the money that he has. His next line refers to his counting of said money, since no matter how big the bill, hand counting 3K would be time consuming.\n\n   As added on research, the belt he speaks of being about 3K USD makes it impossible that it is of either of the brands he mentioned in the previous line, but rather maybe a Chrome Hearts, another Yeat favorite, or perhaps Stefano Ricci.", "annotation_id": "36828025", "url": "https://genius.com/36828025", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "Just got back from Barney’s, just got back from Zara’s", "vault_lines": ["Just got back from Barney's, just got back from Zara's"], "meaning": "Barney’s is a Luxury pop-up shop that used to sell home decor and clothes in New York before going out of business later after the release of this song.\n\n\n\nHe then also, mentions Zara, a semi-luxurious Spanish fashion retailer that sells accesories, clothes, and beauty products.", "annotation_id": "36827897", "url": "https://genius.com/36827897", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "Yeah, and my brother, he could slide if you would like (boom, boom), he got a lethal weapon, trigger is the button he is pressing", "vault_lines": ["(Let's go) Uh, we on Venice, on the beach, just smoking lettuce"], "meaning": "Here Yeat threatens a supposed opposer, saying that his brother (most likely a close friend, shooter, or Twizzy*)\nwill “slide\"on you (to find and attack/shoot one) if you make that your decision.\n\n   He then says that said brother already has his finger on the trigger of a firearm, hinting at the fact that the sliding is evident and could happen anytime.", "annotation_id": "36827851", "url": "https://genius.com/36827851", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "I got hundreds fetish, money come and go, but let’s go spend it (let’s go spend it)", "vault_lines": ["I got hundreds fetish, money come and go, but let's go spend it (let's go spend it)"], "meaning": "Here, Yeat creatively flips his previous line:\n\n“I got money fetish, bitches come and go, but let’s go get it (okay, okay)”\n\nHowever, this time, rather than easy women and supposed “bitches”, he refers to money, that he also has come and go, just as easy as the hoes do. He again ends on the more upligting note of “Let’s go spend it”", "annotation_id": "36827696", "url": "https://genius.com/36827696", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "Playing tennis with my bitch, a lot of rackets", "vault_lines": ["Playing tennis with my bitch, a lot of rackets"], "meaning": "It’s plausible that Yeat in this line could be referencing tennis bracelet, a simple kind of classic diamond bracelet, saying that he is going to adorn said bitch in the jewelry. It could be also be that he is making a double entendre of the word “racket” and is implying he and said bitch are going to be “making a racket” while having sex.\n\n   Neither of these assumptions rule out that Yeat could’ve meant that he was genuinely playing the sport tennis with his bitch.", "annotation_id": "36827633", "url": "https://genius.com/36827633", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "I got money fetish, bitches come and go, but let’s go get it (okay, okay)", "vault_lines": ["I got money fetish, bitches come and go, but let's go get it (okay, okay)"], "meaning": "In this line, Yeat compares his innate attraction to wealth as that of a fetish, a strange and particular/specific sexual desire and attraction. What he means is that he loves getting the bag so much, that it practically seems as though it bring him sexual gratification or kink-like pleasure.\n\nHe then also says “bitches come an go”, meaning that the relationships and endeavours in his life move fast and are to be lost, but, follows up the depressive statement with a more positive message- “Let’s go it”, as in go get said women, in spirit of the fast lyfestyle.", "annotation_id": "36827558", "url": "https://genius.com/36827558", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "Money longer, big old bank, I feel like I’m Uzi", "vault_lines": ["Now my money longer, big old bank, I feel like I'm Uzi"], "meaning": "A reference to the famous trap track by Lil Uzi Vert “Money Longer” which skyrocketed his career for the better and exclaimed his gaining of money and fame for cars and a luxurious lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "36109952", "url": "https://genius.com/36109952", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "I could rap or I could sing like Carrie Underwood", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I could rap or I could sing like Carrie Underwood"], "meaning": "Yeat states that he can rap but similarly if he would like to he could rap like Carrie Underwood. A female American country artist who is an eight time grammy winner and also featured as a host and judge of American Idol.", "annotation_id": "36109935", "url": "https://genius.com/36109935", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "And new baguetties on my wrist, and it’s so precious, stacking, Tetris, all your shit is fake and mine is real, go test it (Yeah, go test it)", "vault_lines": ["(Let's go) Uh, we on Venice, on the beach, just smoking lettuce"], "meaning": "YEAT uses his lyrical masterpeice to diesribe the baguettie dimonds on his wrist. He says they stack like Tetris a popular video game where you stack blocks. He says “Test It” that also is part of the bar as it ryhmes with tetris.", "annotation_id": "34797204", "url": "https://genius.com/34797204", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "(Let’s go) Uh, we on Venice, on the beach, just smoking lettuce", "vault_lines": ["(Let's go) Uh, we on Venice, on the beach, just smoking lettuce"], "meaning": "While Yeat is in Los Angeles, he makes sure to visit and spend time at Venice Beach, a famous tourist destination.\n\nWhile at this location, Yeat makes sure to smoke on his favorite herb-lettuce, slang for marijuana.\n\n\n\nVenice Beach, California", "annotation_id": "26305914", "url": "https://genius.com/26305914", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "Diamonds on my neck, yeah, they different colors", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds on my neck, yeah, they different colors"], "meaning": "Weiland makes a reference to one of his top singles, 2018’s “Colors.” The rapper claims that his necklace jewelry contains a variety of coloration.\n\nhttps://genius.com/Weiland-colors-lyrics", "annotation_id": "26305910", "url": "https://genius.com/26305910", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "Ran off with his money, set him up, that bitch was decoy I made fifty off these Navies, had a big bag", "vault_lines": ["Ran off with his money, set him up, that bitch was decoy"], "meaning": "Yeat explains how he set up a Head, by promising to give them a cut of the money (usually 50/50) if they went into a navy federal and used they personal info to open a bank account to load fraudulent funds on using him as a decoy so he’d get arrested and not Yeat. He then goes to flex the fact that he made 50K from using the Navy Federals\n\nNavy federal is a Credit Union which is a bank that recently got hit with a huge amount of fraud specifically check fraud as they were pretty much letting everyone deposit any check with any amount on a freshly made account.\n\n\n\nThis could be connected to Weiland as around the time this song came out Weiland and Yeat were close friends they are both in the cover art, and Weiland is known for being involved in Fraud as Weiland was seen posting on his story asking for people to be heads for Navy Federal.", "annotation_id": "25461983", "url": "https://genius.com/25461983", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "I’m in beast mode, and we on TV, I call it Chowder", "vault_lines": ["I'm in beast mode, and we on TV, I call it Chowder"], "meaning": "Yeat is talking about the Cartoon Network show “Chowder”", "annotation_id": "25262353", "url": "https://genius.com/25262353", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Money Fetish", "line": "“Wassup in that pot with crack?” Baby, that’s the Arm & Hammer", "vault_lines": ["\"Wassup in that pot with crack?\" Baby, that's the Arm & Hammer"], "meaning": "Arm & Hammer is a company known for making baking soda among other things. Crack cocaine appears to be a white powder similar to baking soda, so the two are compared metaphorically in this line.", "annotation_id": "24810464", "url": "https://genius.com/24810464", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
