{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Million Dollar Minion", "line": "Filet mignon", "vault_lines": ["Ooh, cut it up with my millions (Ayy), filet mignon"], "meaning": "Filet mignon is an expensive cut of beef often associated with luxury and wealth.\n\nThe lyric may also reference “FILET MINION”, a nickname used by Yeat during the song’s rollout before the official title “Million Dollar Minion” was revealed.", "annotation_id": "40266854", "url": "https://genius.com/40266854", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Million Dollar Minion", "line": "You not a rich Minion, yeah, you a dork (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["You not a rich Minion, yeah, you a dork (Ooh)"], "meaning": "This is likely a play on Yeat’s 2022 promotional single “Rich Minion.” By contrasting a “rich Minion” with a “dork,” “Yeat uses the Minions theme to continue the money-focused themes that appear throughout much of his music.”", "annotation_id": "40266808", "url": "https://genius.com/40266808", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Million Dollar Minion", "line": "You not a rich Minion, yeah, you a dork (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["You not a rich Minion, yeah, you a dork (Ooh)"], "meaning": "Obvious reference to Yeat’s “Rich Minion”, commissioned for the Lyrical Lemonade trailer of the previous Minions movie, Minions: The Rise of Gru.", "annotation_id": "40257847", "url": "https://genius.com/40257847", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Million Dollar Minion", "line": "I’m with the Minions, callin’ up Dort (Ooh, haha) Call up the Minions, callin’ up Dort (Ooh) Call up the Minions, callin’ up Dort (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Call up my Minions, I'm callin' up Dort (Slide)"], "meaning": "Dort is an intergalactic robot character first seen in Minions and Monsters, voiced by actor, playwright, and filmmaker Jesse Eisenberg. Dort plays a central role in the film, helping save the minions from an alien invasion.\n\nYeat includes an alien motif in much of his music, often claiming to be an alien, have seen aliens, or live on extraterrestrial planets. Similarly, Dort is from interplanetary alien origins.\n\n\n\nDort seen with Dick the minion", "annotation_id": "40203795", "url": "https://genius.com/40203795", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
