{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Mad bout that", "line": "I call my bizzy Balenci ’cause B", "vault_lines": ["I call my bizzy Balenci 'cause B"], "meaning": "Both “bizzy” (yeat’s significant other) and “Balenci” (balenciaga) start with B, meaning that yeat views his bizzy as that of high luxury status", "annotation_id": "25857508", "url": "https://genius.com/25857508", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Mad bout that", "line": "Yeah, my bitch like a old, old bitch, she put on the chompers (Eat it up, eat it up)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, my bitch like a old, old bitch, she put on thе chompers (Eat it up, eat it up)"], "meaning": "“chompers” is a slang word for the dentures worn by elderly people whose natural teeth have fallen out or been removed, they are cosmetic but also serve the purpose of chewing food when eating.\nYeat says his bitch is “old” and puts on “chompers” as a metaphor for preparing to suck his dick.", "annotation_id": "25729864", "url": "https://genius.com/25729864", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Mad bout that", "line": "If he shit talkin’, light him up like he’s a lantern", "vault_lines": ["If he shit talkin', light him up like he's a lantern"], "meaning": "A lantern is a device that can be held and illuminate the area in which it is held. Noah “Yeat” Smith has crafted clever wordplay with the phrase “light up” which can also mean to shoot a gun at.", "annotation_id": "25523517", "url": "https://genius.com/25523517", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
