{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "MARGIELA ROOF", "line": "And you know I’m ballin’, pull up in that 2 door coupe", "vault_lines": ["And you know I’m ballin', pull up in that 2 door coupe"], "meaning": "This bar refers to luxury 2-door vehicles, likely an Aston-Martin or a high-end BMW coupe. These cars are telltale signs of wealth, referred to as “ballin'”.", "annotation_id": "41610868", "url": "https://genius.com/41610868", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "MARGIELA ROOF", "line": "And I’m with my gang I’m booted", "vault_lines": ["And I'm with my gang I’m booted"], "meaning": "Yeat is referring to being with a group of his friends or acquaintances. In this usage, “booted” refers to being intoxicated heavily, usually with prescription drugs such as Percocet or opioids.", "annotation_id": "41610850", "url": "https://genius.com/41610850", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "MARGIELA ROOF", "line": "I been in this cut man", "vault_lines": ["I been in this cut man"], "meaning": "Being “in a cut” usually means to be laying low in a secluded area, typically a part of a neighborhood. This bar insinuates that Yeat is laying low after an illegal activity, which is strengthened by the frequent mentions of robbing.", "annotation_id": "41610831", "url": "https://genius.com/41610831", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "MARGIELA ROOF", "line": "It’s Lil Yeat in this shit", "vault_lines": ["It's Lil Yeat in this shit"], "meaning": "From when Yeat started making music in 2016 until April 12th, 2018, he went under the alias “Lil Yeat”. This alias was replaced with just “Yeat” on his release of his single, “Brink!” on April 13th, 2018.", "annotation_id": "41610826", "url": "https://genius.com/41610826", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "MARGIELA ROOF", "line": "Baby on a 5th", "vault_lines": ["Baby on a 5th"], "meaning": "“A fifth” refers to a fifth of alcohol. A fifth of alcohol contains approximately 17.2 standard drinks, which is a very large and unsafe amount of alcohol to be consuming in a single sitting. The recommended maximum amount of standard drinks in a day is 4 for men, and 3 for women.\nBased on Yeat’s use of the word “baby”, it is assumed that the inebriated person is a woman, likely a romantic partner of his.", "annotation_id": "41610792", "url": "https://genius.com/41610792", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "MARGIELA ROOF", "line": "I’mma stack up all these bands and get that shit for you", "vault_lines": ["I'mma stack up all these bands and get that shit for you"], "meaning": "This bar could be directed towards a romantic partner that Yeat is pursuing, his family, or his friends. He states in this bar that his goal is to make money to give to his people, or to buy them what they desire.", "annotation_id": "41610754", "url": "https://genius.com/41610754", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "MARGIELA ROOF", "line": "I been grindin’ for that shit Grinding for that limelight", "vault_lines": ["I been grindin' for that shit"], "meaning": "Being “in the limelight” refers to being at the center of public attention, interest, or fame. This bar is Yeat announcing that his goals are to become famous in the future.", "annotation_id": "41610730", "url": "https://genius.com/41610730", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "MARGIELA ROOF", "line": "My whole left side ain’t movin’", "vault_lines": ["My whole left side ain't movin'"], "meaning": "This bar describes the feeling of being weighed down, or being unable to move. This is most commonly associated with the intoxication caused from Codeine, commonly referred to as lean.", "annotation_id": "41610610", "url": "https://genius.com/41610610", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "MARGIELA ROOF", "line": "Watch me grab that shit Then watch me fucking jugg", "vault_lines": ["Watch me grab that shit"], "meaning": "Jugging (sometimes spelt “jugg”) is a common slang term that means to rob or steal, and make money out of it.", "annotation_id": "41610604", "url": "https://genius.com/41610604", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "MARGIELA ROOF", "line": "Yeah we on the block Watch me stick n’ move it Lemme get these racks Post it up and now I’m boolin’ Bitch I’m coolin’", "vault_lines": ["Yeah we on the block"], "meaning": "In this instance, Yeat is likely referring to robbing someone and leaving the area quickly, before hanging out and calming down in a separate location.\n\n“Stick and move” is a slang term meaning to perform an action quickly, then leave the area or change direction shortly afterwards.\n\nBoth “post it up” and “boolin'” can have similar meanings, both being to hang out in an area. However, “boolin'” originates from “coolin'”, due to a retaliatory action commonly seen from members of a Los Angeles gang known as the Bloods. Due to a feud between a rival gang known as the Crips, some members of the Bloods would change the Letter C in writing and speech to a B, resulting in words such as “boolin'” for “coolin'”.\n\nIt is possible that Yeat was using “post it up” as a way to infer that he was flexing his money on social media, although there isn’t much evidence proving or disproving such.\n\n“Boolin” definition, via dictionary.com", "annotation_id": "41610573", "url": "https://genius.com/41610573", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "MARGIELA ROOF", "line": "Bitch I’m fuckin’ zooted", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I'm fuckin' zooted"], "meaning": "Zooted is a slang word that means highly inebriated, from sources such as marijuana, alcohol, or other drugs, usually to a point of feeling “out of it”, or extremely relaxed.", "annotation_id": "41610469", "url": "https://genius.com/41610469", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "MARGIELA ROOF", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-margiela-roof-lyrics", "genius_title": "MARGIELA ROOF", "genius_id": 9719457, "source": "api"}
