{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "M.F.U.", "line": "Percs on the side, I’ma crush, I’ma hit from the side (From the side)", "vault_lines": ["Percs on the side, I'ma crush, I'ma hit from the side (From the side)"], "meaning": "Yeat makes a metaphor for having sex with a girl.\n\n“Percs on the side” is a setup for the next part of the line, where he mentions “crushing,” as in crushing percs into small peices. He compares the impact to having sex with a girl from the side.", "annotation_id": "36880052", "url": "https://genius.com/36880052", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "M.F.U.", "line": "(Uh) So much fun, so many bitches, got so much guns (Fun) So much mon’, so much money, got so much mon’ (So much) Uh, so much fun, so much funny, have so much fun (Fun)", "vault_lines": ["So much mon', so much money, got so much mon' (So much)"], "meaning": "These lines are a subtle throwback to Yeat’s unreleased first-version “LYFESTYLE” era track “real trendsetter”, first performed at his Wireless 2023 set.\n\n(Real trendsetter, all they do is copy trendsetter)\nWe had so much fun (Yeah-uh-yeah, Dream, this shit go dummy)\nYeah (All they do is copy trendsetter), we got so much guns\n(Real trendsetter, all they do is copy trendsetter) Yeah, we got so much money (Yeah-uh-yeah)\nYeah (All they do is copy trendsetter), I have so much fun (More, yeah)\n\n– Yeat, 2023", "annotation_id": "36702076", "url": "https://genius.com/36702076", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "M.F.U.", "line": "Ain’t never had picked up a spatula (Squidward)", "vault_lines": ["So much mon', so much money, got so much mon' (So much)"], "meaning": "this is a reference to the hit show SpongeBob where the main character SpongeBob SquarePants uses a spatula to flip burgers and he also references one of the main character’s Squidward in the adlib.", "annotation_id": "36507167", "url": "https://genius.com/36507167", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "M.F.U.", "line": "I’m allergic to broke hoes, a nigga be sneezing, put diamonds all up in my nostril (Sheesh)", "vault_lines": ["I'm allergic to broke hoes, a nigga be sneezing, put diamonds all up in my nostril (Sheesh)"], "meaning": "SahBabii references his allergy to women who seem’s to be broke, he also give a subtle nod to how he stop’s his sneezing with diamonds up his nose.", "annotation_id": "36507054", "url": "https://genius.com/36507054", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "M.F.U.", "line": "Bitch from Philly, I call her a nut (Nut)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch from Philly, I call her a nut (Nut)"], "meaning": "In the context of Philly’s slang, a nut is a person who is considered not the norm, crazy, or a downright fool.", "annotation_id": "36469482", "url": "https://genius.com/36469482", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
