{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lët ya know", "line": "Yeah, you’s a “pick me” on the low, I know your stuff", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you's a \"pick me\" on the low, I know your stuff"], "meaning": "Yeat says that he knows that you’re a “pick me” which is a word used in pop culture referencing a girl who always wants to be picked or chooses for attention.", "annotation_id": "28520544", "url": "https://genius.com/28520544", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lët ya know", "line": "I just take the Perc’ and then I float", "vault_lines": ["I just take the Perc' and then I float"], "meaning": "In this sentence, rapper Yeat states; upon consuming the yerky (percocet – more familiarly known as perc 30) he transcends human physicality granting him the ability of levitation. This could infer that Yeat is greater/higher than everyone after he takes narcotics.", "annotation_id": "25686551", "url": "https://genius.com/25686551", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lët ya know", "line": "These bitches jumpin’ on me like some rope", "vault_lines": ["These bitches jumpin' on me like some rope"], "meaning": "Yeat is making a tongue-in-cheek metaphor on the state of the working class, as he takes on the role of a member of the ruling class, with the jumprope being representative of middle and working class people.", "annotation_id": "25327115", "url": "https://genius.com/25327115", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lët ya know", "line": "It feel like I’m dying on that X, ho Yeah, I be taking Percs just for my head, ho", "vault_lines": ["It feel like I'm dying on that X, ho"], "meaning": "Yeat is referencing his on going pill addiction coming off his last line saying this “This could be my last song, ho” stating he could OD at any given moment due to the mixing of lean and pills on a daily basis", "annotation_id": "25155887", "url": "https://genius.com/25155887", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lët ya know", "line": "This could be my last song, ho", "vault_lines": ["This could be my last song, ho"], "meaning": "😢Nooooo Yeat Noooooooo 😣😣😣😣", "annotation_id": "25076574", "url": "https://genius.com/25076574", "state": "pending", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lët ya know", "line": "Couldn’t decide on the Perc’ or the X, I took ’em both", "vault_lines": ["Couldn't decide on thе Perc' or the X, I took 'em both"], "meaning": "Yeat emotionally explores a conundrum that he faces regularly, that being whether to ingest a Percocet or an Ecstacy. It is a mental battle, and Yeat is unfortunately losing on both fronts. In the end, he decides to pop them both in order to experience a doubled high effect. This could be a primary reason for why Yeat states in the chorus of this very track that “This could be my last song, ho”(Yeat, Line 1).", "annotation_id": "24473804", "url": "https://genius.com/24473804", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lët ya know", "line": "I make the best songs when I’m dyin’, I thought you knew", "vault_lines": ["I make the best songs when I'm dyin', I thought you knew"], "meaning": "This is a callback to the chorus where Yeat says “It feel like I’m dying on the X, ho”. Saying he makes the best songs when he’s under the influence of Ecstasy", "annotation_id": "23950765", "url": "https://genius.com/23950765", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lët ya know", "line": "Yeah, you not my twizz, you not my twin, you not my bro, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you not my twizz, you not my twin, you not my bro, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat uses twizz (twizzy) to refer to someone that he considers a close friend. It is also the name of his label, TwizzyRich Ent. which his close friend and collaborator SeptembersRich, who is featured on this album, is signed to. He explains the meaning in this interview with OGM\n\nhttps://youtu.be/b1Fu_nvUhXQ", "annotation_id": "23928056", "url": "https://genius.com/23928056", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
