{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "I got slimes in the mud", "vault_lines": ["High as hell, took that carat, I got slimes in the mud"], "meaning": "“Slime” is Young Thug / YSL slang for close homies. “In the mud” = coming from nothing or being in gritty environments. Yeat adopting slime culture links him to ATL trap influence.", "annotation_id": "36849586", "url": "https://genius.com/36849586", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "Linked with the devil, told him I just need a signature, need his autograph I ain’t never sold my soul but I just donated it to you", "vault_lines": ["Linked with the devil, told him I just need a signature, need his autograph"], "meaning": "Symbolic exaggeration — people accuse rappers of “selling their soul” for fame. Yeat flips this by saying he didn’t sell his soul but still inked success.", "annotation_id": "36849565", "url": "https://genius.com/36849565", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "You must’ve thought I was done (Haha) You must’ve thought I was done (That’s not how I’ma end it) You must’ve thought I was done (I put my whole shit in it)", "vault_lines": ["You must've thought I was done (Haha)"], "meaning": "This part introduces Yeat’s first ever beat switch. The lyrics come in after the beat and melody seem to come to an end, only to switch up and start again. Yeat is sure that the listener thought the song was about to end but he has more for us to listen to.", "annotation_id": "35567778", "url": "https://genius.com/35567778", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "I be high as fuck, I don’t need to catch a flight (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["I be high as fuck, I don't need to catch a flight (Woo)"], "meaning": "Yeat in this “bar” is rapping about how he takes drugs,  gets “high” (under the influence) and takes so much that he doesn’t need to catch a flight.", "annotation_id": "35442412", "url": "https://genius.com/35442412", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "You could say that shit again but do you live by it? (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["You could say that shit again but do you live by it?"], "meaning": "In this line, Mr. Smith is questioning the authenticity of whether someone is staying true to how they claim to be living/acting.\n\nHe is critiquing people who’s actions don’t line up with their words, highlighting a disconnect between their reputation (or what they do in front of others) and their integrity (or what they do when no one’s watching).", "annotation_id": "33250591", "url": "https://genius.com/33250591", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "[Bridge]", "vault_lines": ["We just walkin' 'round, bitch, we outside"], "meaning": "In the bridge, there are reversed vocals that, when played backward again, reveal the following lyrics:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=quYu8ym2Eig\n\nSaid to my guys “I can’t leave these drugs”\nWhat will I do when the devil come?\nHe said “I’m watching you” ah ha\nSpent all my money I’m too up\nMan, I’m done with these hoes, ahh\nI can’t do it no more, ah\nI signed ‘bout 4 months ago, worst decision I’ve chose\nAnd it’s just the truth", "annotation_id": "33230733", "url": "https://genius.com/33230733", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "You couldn’t handle that shit, I know your ass was slumped, fall over", "vault_lines": ["You couldn't handle that shit, I know your ass was slumped, fall over"], "meaning": "Yeat warns against being overconfident or getting ahead of oneself, suggesting that the listener was caught off guard and fell down or slumped.", "annotation_id": "33223822", "url": "https://genius.com/33223822", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "Ride around town with a whole lot of guap, we just havin’ some fun", "vault_lines": ["Ride around town with a whole lot of guap, we just havin' some fun"], "meaning": "Yeat describes himself riding through town with alot of money.", "annotation_id": "33165756", "url": "https://genius.com/33165756", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "Brought the Cayenne outside, bought the big body", "vault_lines": ["Brought the Cayenne outside, bought the big body"], "meaning": "The Porsche Cayenne is a luxury SUV that Yeat commonly talks about as well as the Lamborghini Urus. Yeat refers to said cars as “Big Bodies” This is because of their large size, and Yeat likes referring to them as such", "annotation_id": "32549532", "url": "https://genius.com/32549532", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "Bitch, I made a couple M’s, not off rapping, yeah, but who knew?", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I made a couple M's, not off rapping, yeah, but who knew?"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that he made a couple million, however, not off of his rapping career. This can be attributed to his scamming and drug dealing he did earlier in his life with his accomplice and teacher SeptembersRich.", "annotation_id": "32549525", "url": "https://genius.com/32549525", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "All my diamonds flawless, none SI (SI)", "vault_lines": ["All my diamonds flawless, none SI (SI)"], "meaning": "Yeat is referring the the clarity of his diamonds, those of which are graded on a scale from I3 -> FL. Yeat is saying that his diamonds fall under the flawless category and that he has only the highest quality diamonds", "annotation_id": "32549507", "url": "https://genius.com/32549507", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "Now I’m livin’ life just how I dreamed about it", "vault_lines": ["Now I'm livin' life just how I dreamed about it"], "meaning": "Now that Yeat has made it in the mainstream industry he is living life just how he dreamed about it probably referring to the newfound money, connections, fame, and other perks of being a famous rapper", "annotation_id": "32549473", "url": "https://genius.com/32549473", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
