{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "You could say that shit again but do you live by it?", "vault_lines": ["You could say that shit again but do you live by it?"], "meaning": "You can talk about a lifestyle but do you actually live it?", "annotation_id": "31187216", "url": "https://genius.com/31187216", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "I don’t gotta flex, huh, back to the lab, yeah (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I don't gotta flex, huh, back to the lab, yeah (Yeah)"], "meaning": "What Yeat was referring to here was that he doesn’t need to show to anyone but himself who he is as a person. The arrogance in his lyrics shows the egotistical person he has made of himself.\n\nHe supports his egotistical behavior by continuously spending his time in the lab, which may refer to the area in which he progresses himself mentally.\n\nA lab can be inferred as a place for personal research and improvements, such as a music recording studio in his case.", "annotation_id": "30444060", "url": "https://genius.com/30444060", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "Did this by myself so no, I don’t need no advice (Ha, ha), yeah", "vault_lines": ["Did this by myself so no, I don't need no advice (Ha, ha), yeah"], "meaning": "In a July 2021 interview with Our Generation Music, Yeat remarks figuring out how to record himself without the help of a recording engineer and finding his sound with Weiland’s assistance:\n\nLike when I was in New York, I didn’t really know how to record myself but like it was because my presets [were] ass. It sounded so bad, I didn’t want to do it. […] I remember Weiland came up to my crib and gave me his stuff he had on his […] presets, and then from there on, I just like hooked it up […] and it made everything just way easier.", "annotation_id": "29083471", "url": "https://genius.com/29083471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "Every time I took a step back, I got closer Every time I was on the edge, I jumped over", "vault_lines": ["Every time I took a step back, I got closer"], "meaning": "Every time Yeat had a setback in life he used it to get closer to his goal. Every time he had a choice or opportunity in front of him, he didn’t hesitate.", "annotation_id": "28094276", "url": "https://genius.com/28094276", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "Yeah, you must’ve thought I was done", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you must've thought I was done"], "meaning": "This is referring to the fact that the song sounded like it was ending, due to the fact that before the bridge the beat was reversing, which is a common way to signify that the song is ending.\n\nSo, In short, you must of thought he was done.", "annotation_id": "28071137", "url": "https://genius.com/28071137", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "I just be taking these Percs, hunnid milligrams, I feel like Walking Dead zombie", "vault_lines": ["I just be taking these Percs, hunnid milligrams, I feel like Walking Dead zombie"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that the amount of percs (Percocet) he is taking is making him sick and feel like a zombie", "annotation_id": "28014761", "url": "https://genius.com/28014761", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "All of my money insane, I don’t even know how to bluff (Can’t lie)", "vault_lines": ["All of my money insane, I don't even know how to bluff (Can't lie)"], "meaning": "Noah implies that he has so many honeybunzz that even if he were to try to hyperbolize his money he couldn’t.", "annotation_id": "27965158", "url": "https://genius.com/27965158", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "I just went into Chanel with twenty bands, I don’t got nothing left on me", "vault_lines": ["I just went into Chanel with twenty bands, I don't got nothing left on me"], "meaning": "Yeat has never shied away from rapping about his eagerness of spending money on luxurious items. In this line, Yeat exclaims how he spent $20,000 in the Chanel store and left with no money as he spent everything he had.", "annotation_id": "27925529", "url": "https://genius.com/27925529", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "One of my twins called, he say he proud of the guy", "vault_lines": ["One of my twins called, he say he proud of the guy"], "meaning": "May be a reference to Izaya Tiji, who later said “I told bro he would go up and then he met Drizzy, I’m so proud of Yeat” on his song Still Lit.", "annotation_id": "26529062", "url": "https://genius.com/26529062", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "I just tatted all that shit on me, then it happened, bitch, it’s too true", "vault_lines": ["I just tatted all that shit on me, then it happened, bitch, it's too true"], "meaning": "Yeat has a sigil of his stage name on his right arm, a symbol used in magic. Presumably charged as a wealth or success sigil associated with the name. He credits his success to the spell put on the tattoo.", "annotation_id": "26364135", "url": "https://genius.com/26364135", "state": "pending", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "I might just pull out the X, I’m taking Perkies for fun", "vault_lines": ["I might just pull out the X, I'm taking Perkies for fun"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Yeat only being able to make music at his best when he is under the influence of opioids. This can also be perceived as yeat becoming so used to nice things, that the only way he can have fun is by taking a risk on his life.", "annotation_id": "25845279", "url": "https://genius.com/25845279", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "Why can’t you just be yourself? If you’re not a lame, don’t you got nothin’ to hide?", "vault_lines": ["Why can't you just be yourself? If you're not a lame, don't you got nothin' to hide?"], "meaning": "Yeat advocates a philosophy of radical self-acceptance. Free from his fetters of insecurity, Yeat criticizes those who have failed to accept themselves- the only personal quality one should be ashamed of is being a “lame.”", "annotation_id": "25836980", "url": "https://genius.com/25836980", "state": "pending", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "Yeah, I see the light I seen the light flash in the corner of my eye (Yeah, yeah) I already told you this but I had to tell you twice (Twice) This a dangerous lifestyle, everyday I roll the dice (It’s what?)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I see the light"], "meaning": "Yeat may be referring to “lights” seen in an overdose-induced hallucination.\nUnderstandably, this situation causes stress to Yeat’s hypothetical partner, to whom he must explain that he is aware of the risks of a drug-fueled lifestyle and accepts them fully. He embraces the inherent unknowability of the absurd.\n\nThis is also a reference to the chorus of Livë Hi, in which Yeat also says he saw the light flash in the corner of his eye. This is clearly not a new occurrence.\n\nAlso, Yeat mentions in this lyric: “This a dangerous lifestyle, everyday I roll the dice.” Since he’s making his album ADL ( A Dangerous Lyfe), this shows his knowledge that this life and its danger are constant elements of his career.", "annotation_id": "25836969", "url": "https://genius.com/25836969", "state": "pending", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lying 4 fun", "line": "Yeah, these kids are corny like kettle, yeah, all they do is bite", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, these kids are corny like kettle, yeah, all they do is bite"], "meaning": "To bite in this sense would be to rip off another person’s style, especially with respect to music or fashion. From early hip-hop culture and graffiti.", "annotation_id": "25431191", "url": "https://genius.com/25431191", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
