{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lyfestylë", "line": "All that molly why your jaw so tight", "vault_lines": ["All that molly why your jaw so tight"], "meaning": "The whole chorus is Yeat under the influence of drugs asking his sober self if he could do the things that the high yeat does. High yeat was able to make 170 songs per month (work around the clock) and make sucessful albums (work the job) and this line signifies how the drugs stopped him from speaking out agaisnt them by keeping his jaw tight (not talking/complaining)", "annotation_id": "30925582", "url": "https://genius.com/30925582", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
