{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lyfestylë", "line": "This not Breaking Bad, I bring my motherfuckin’ pipe", "vault_lines": ["This not Breaking Bad, I bring my motherfuckin' pipe"], "meaning": "Yeat cleverly intertwines a cultural reference with a bold declaration. Invoking “Breaking Bad,” a series synonymous with meth production, sets up an expectation around drug culture. Yet, Yeat twists this with “I bring my motherfuckin' pipe,” which could double as a nod to drug use and a metaphor for his music delivery—his “hits.” Unlike the destructive paths in “Breaking Bad,” Yeat suggests his craft is about producing impactful music. This line showcases Yeat’s skill in blending references and personal expression, hinting at his ability to deliver music that’s as addictive as the substances depicted in the show, but in a creative, life-affirming way.\n\n_1-35_screenshot.jpg)", "annotation_id": "30902387", "url": "https://genius.com/30902387", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lyfestylë", "line": "This not Breaking Bad, I bring my motherfuckin’ pipe", "vault_lines": ["This not Breaking Bad, I bring my motherfuckin' pipe"], "meaning": "Yeat cleverly intertwines a cultural reference with a bold declaration. Invoking “Breaking Bad,” a series synonymous with meth production, sets up an expectation around drug culture. Yet, Yeat twists this with “I bring my motherfuckin' pipe,” which could double as a nod to drug use and a metaphor for his music delivery—his “hits.” Unlike the destructive paths in “Breaking Bad,” Yeat suggests his craft is about producing impactful music. This line showcases Yeat’s skill in blending references and personal expression, hinting at his ability to deliver music that’s as addictive as the substances depicted in the show, but in a creative, life-affirming way.\n\n_1-35_screenshot.jpg)", "annotation_id": "30902365", "url": "https://genius.com/30902365", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lyfestylë", "line": "Could you do what I did and do it twice?", "vault_lines": ["Could you do what I did and do it twice?"], "meaning": "Yeat is emphasizing the uniqueness of his journey and the hard work behind his success. This line serves as a rhetorical question that underscores his self-confidence and the notion that his achievements are not easily duplicated. It’s a common theme in rap to measure success not just by material wealth but by the ability to sustain and multiply success over time, making this line both a declaration of Yeat’s current status and a challenge to peers and critics alike.", "annotation_id": "30902347", "url": "https://genius.com/30902347", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lyfestylë", "line": "Could you do what I did and do it twice?", "vault_lines": ["Could you do what I did and do it twice?"], "meaning": "Yeat is emphasizing the uniqueness of his journey and the hard work behind his success. This line serves as a rhetorical question that underscores his self-confidence and the notion that his achievements are not easily duplicated. It’s a common theme in rap to measure success not just by material wealth but by the ability to sustain and multiply success over time, making this line both a declaration of Yeat’s current status and a challenge to peers and critics alike.", "annotation_id": "30902338", "url": "https://genius.com/30902338", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lyfestylë", "line": "Pull up with the Martians and they know I’m ’bout to fly (Fly)", "vault_lines": ["Pull up with the Martians and they know I'm 'bout to fly (Fly)"], "meaning": "Noah exposes his collaboration with Martians. Based on a multi-level analysis and transdimensional projections of the Mars Galactic Timeline, he most likely refers to factions of Orion Humans and Zeta hybrids (the Greys). These were dimensional blending projects with Alien technologies that allowed time travel to the future (2093 and far beyond).\n\nMost of the collaborations between humans and aliens were of a negative nature, genetic experiments, developing Mind Control programs and perfecting psychotronic warfare.", "annotation_id": "30900585", "url": "https://genius.com/30900585", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lyfestylë", "line": "Judge always tryna give me time, give me fed time and that’s plenty time And I ain’t got time like the end of time, I’ll kill a nigga like I’m killin’ time", "vault_lines": ["Judge always tryna give me time, give me fed time and that's plenty time"], "meaning": "Here, Wayne plays around with the different uses of the word “time”, interpolating another guest verse of his own, from JID’s 2022 track “Just In Time”, on which Wayne raps:\n\nNo problem to kill ‘em, that’s killin’ time\nI done did my time\nBut you know they still be tryna give me time ‘til the end of time\nSince the beginnin’ of time I put in the time\nAnd that’s all the time, that’s in time", "annotation_id": "30898715", "url": "https://genius.com/30898715", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lyfestylë", "line": "I ain’t playin’ with they bitch asses, Lil Tunechi, I spit acid", "vault_lines": ["I ain't playin' with they bitch asses, Lil Tunechi, I spit acid"], "meaning": "In the lyric “I ain’t playin' with they bitch asses, Lil Tunechi, I spit acid,” Lil Wayne is using wordplay to assert his dominance and prowess as a rapper. “Lil Tunechi” is one of Lil Wayne’s nicknames, and by referencing himself in the third person, he’s emphasizing his own persona and reputation. The phrase “I spit acid” is a metaphorical way of saying that his rap verses are potent, powerful, and potentially corrosive to his competitors. Essentially, he’s asserting that he doesn’t take lightly any challengers to his status in the rap game and that his lyrical abilities are formidable.", "annotation_id": "30898520", "url": "https://genius.com/30898520", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Lyfestylë", "status": "done", "targets": 25, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-and-lil-wayne-lyfestyle-lyrics", "genius_title": "Lyfestylë", "genius_id": 10060932, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luv monëy", "line": "Yeah, ride in a Maybach on shrooms, yeah, I do this (Yeah, I do)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, ride in a Maybach on shrooms, yeah, I do this (Yeah, I do)"], "meaning": "Maybach is a luxury sub-brand of Mercedes-Benz, offering the most exclusive versions of Mercedes SUVs and sedans. These models are focused on comfort, perfection, craftsmanship, and high-end materials, competing with Rolls-Royce and Bentley. He is under the influence of “Shrooms”, an illegal substance. He states, “Ride in a Maybach,” Possibly meaning he has a chauffeur driving for him.\n\nMercedes Maybach:", "annotation_id": "37900295", "url": "https://genius.com/37900295", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luv monëy", "line": "I got flawless diamonds on me", "vault_lines": ["I got flawless diamonds on me"], "meaning": "A flawless diamond (FL) is the highest clarity grade, meaning it has no internal inclusions or external blemishes visible under 10x magnification by a skilled grader, making it exceptionally rare, valuable, and pristine from both an internal and external perspective.", "annotation_id": "37878800", "url": "https://genius.com/37878800", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
