{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luv monëy", "line": "Got a bad ting in Mumbai cooking Pilau", "vault_lines": ["Got a bad ting in Mumbai cooking Pilau"], "meaning": "Pilau is a type of seasoned rice common in Indian culture. Foux references Mumbai––India’s largest city––as where his “ting,” or fling, is located.\n\nIn describing a past relationship (or hookup) in a global context, Foux highlights his expansive resources and accessibility to parts of the world ––put simply, it’s another flex.", "annotation_id": "28903112", "url": "https://genius.com/28903112", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luv monëy", "line": "Perc’ got me in my mental (Huh, huh)", "vault_lines": ["Perc' got me in my mental (Huh, huh)"], "meaning": "Yeat refers to a percocet––a medical-grade opioid used to treat pain––that he takes recreationally. Opioids are known to slow down one’s breathing and heart rate, ultimately resulting in a more relaxing experience for the user. This high-like state can result in a lucid, or mental state.", "annotation_id": "28903007", "url": "https://genius.com/28903007", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luv monëy", "line": "Yeah, I just went and bought the doves time to bring the birds out (Brr)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I just went and bought the doves time to bring the birds out (Brr)"], "meaning": "“Dove” is slang for Cocaine. Yeat states that he bought cocaine and uses birds flying as a metaphor for being high on the mind altering inhibitor.", "annotation_id": "26008950", "url": "https://genius.com/26008950", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luv monëy", "line": "Fuck the underground shit, I feel too big (I feel too)", "vault_lines": ["Fuck the underground shit, I feel too big (I feel too)"], "meaning": "Lancey Foux is often called or given the title of being an underground rapper, which can be presumably annoying or frustrating to someone who is on the rise to fame, but is labelled with such terms in the process. Lancey implies that he doesn’t believe he’s an “underground rapper” or a “SoundCloud rapper.”\n\nOther people in his lane who may possibly suffer similar frustration can include artists in the Rage/Trap/Cloud-Rap genre such as Autumn!, Ken Car$on, and SSGKobe.", "annotation_id": "25563011", "url": "https://genius.com/25563011", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luv monëy", "line": "Pop out, smoke, rest in peace to Woo (Chyeah)", "vault_lines": ["Pop out, smoke, rest in peace to Woo (Chyeah)"], "meaning": "Lancey pays his respects to drill rapper Pop Smoke, who sadly passed away from a fatal gunshot wound following a home invasion on February 19, 2020. Woo is a well-known nickname for the rapper, who was best known for hit singles such as “Dior” and “Welcome To The Party”.", "annotation_id": "25483291", "url": "https://genius.com/25483291", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
