{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luh gëek", "line": "You don’t get no fuckin’ money (Uh), you don’t get no fuckin’ fame (Uh) I don’t give a fuck about it (Ah), all this shit could really change (Deep) I ain’t use to have nothin’ (Nothin’), now I pulled up in a plane", "vault_lines": ["You don't get no fuckin' money (Uh), you don't get no fuckin' fame (Uh)"], "meaning": "This lyric can be interpreted as Yeat reflecting on his rise to fame how people were quick to doubt him as he was blowing up. He proves them wrong by stating that he’s now flying on private planes.", "annotation_id": "34497269", "url": "https://genius.com/34497269", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
