{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luh gëek", "line": "Yeah, diamonds all over my teeth, bitch, I don’t brush a tooth", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, diamonds all over my teeth, bitch, I don't brush a tooth"], "meaning": "Yeat doesn’t graze a single tooth when he brushes his teeth, as diamond grills cover up the outside layer of his teeth. Although Yeat has never been seen wearing grills, it wouldn’t be too shocking if he owned them due to his newfound peak in popularity.", "annotation_id": "26110914", "url": "https://genius.com/26110914", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luh gëek", "line": "All my demons talk to me, who else could I explain? (Luh geek) All my demons talk to me, how else could I explain? Yeah (Luh geek) All my demons talk to me, how else could I explain it? (What’s up?) They told me what they were gon’ do, yeah, and none of it happened (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["All my diamonds gon' talk to me, who else I got to blame? (Luh crank)"], "meaning": "Yeat describes an effect of drug-induced psychosis, hallucinating demonic creatures speaking to him whilst under the influence.\n\nYeat has rapped about how demons helped him gain success in the industry on several songs. For example, on “Monëy so big,” he states:\n\n‘Bout to tell you how I’m doin’ and shit\nI got the devil on my phone, he told me, keep doin' this shit\nYeah, devil taught me how to get rich\nYeah, how many bands? six-six\n\nReddit user Primateur has proposed a theory on how the devil was able to help Yeat gain industry success.", "annotation_id": "25760125", "url": "https://genius.com/25760125", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luh gëek", "line": "Big boy Lamb’, I’m in the big boy truck (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["Big boy Lamb', I'm in the big boy truck (Skrrt)"], "meaning": "Yeat is in a Lamborghini Urus, a luxury SUV that costs upwards of $218,000.", "annotation_id": "25760021", "url": "https://genius.com/25760021", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luh gëek", "line": "All my pockets lift weights (They fat) All my pockets in the gym every day", "vault_lines": ["All my pockets lift weights (They fat)"], "meaning": "Yeat frequently describes his copious amounts of money in unique, eccentric ways. Here, Yeat uses a play on words calling his pockets athletic or swole — indicating heaps of money are inside them.\n\nYeat referred to his money in a similar way on his September 2021 track “Trëndy way”:\n\nFirst my money twerk, now it’s lifting weights\nMoney in the gym, now it’s heavyweight", "annotation_id": "25201664", "url": "https://genius.com/25201664", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Luh gëek", "line": "How the fuck my brothers switch up on me? Yeah, why you cappin’? Boy, you fucked up ’cause I’m rich now, I don’t give a fuck what happened (Fuck ’em)", "vault_lines": ["How the fuck my brothers switch up on me? Yeah, why you cappin'?"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that if any of his big affiliated partners switch up on him or tells lies to him, he wouldn’t care about it cause he knows hes rich and has other more things to do instead of staying with them. Yeat also refferences about switching up on him on songs like “Forëally / 4LY” that if you switch up on him. You would die. This could be a possible shot at Autumn! since their ongoing beef.", "annotation_id": "25118404", "url": "https://genius.com/25118404", "state": "pending", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
