{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Liv Likë Dis", "line": "Huh-huh, what’s up with you? You’re lurkin’, girl, what’s up with you? Yeah, I earned it, yeah, what’s up with you? I love it, ho, what’s up with you? I need it, ho, what’s up with you? I", "vault_lines": ["Huh-huh, what's up with you?"], "meaning": "In these lines, Yeat confronts a partner who has turned transactional and greedy. Right after paying attention to her constant demands, he states his own hard work against her greed. By stating “Yeah, I earned it,” Yeat draws a line between the wealth he built and her undeserving expectations. Her “lurkin'” shows she is a danger, who is trying to secretly be with him for the money.\n\nRather than expressing his own sexual desire, Yeat uses mocking dialogue to throw her exact words back at her. The lines “I love it, ho” and “I need it, ho” label her as an “I-need-it” type of person who only speaks up to request expensive items. The constant repetition of “what’s up with you?” shows him questioning this behavior from her. So this shows how his success turns his relationships to be dangerous to his lyfe.", "annotation_id": "41151152", "url": "https://genius.com/41151152", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Liv Likë Dis", "line": "How do you live like this? How do you live like this? Huh? How do you live like this? Huh? How do you live like— how do you live like this?", "vault_lines": ["How do you live like this?"], "meaning": "In the outro of the song it can interpreted as Yeat talking to his old self saying “How do you live like this?”, asking his old self how he could live a lifestyle filled with drug and alcohol abuse after now experiencing sobriety.", "annotation_id": "40467002", "url": "https://genius.com/40467002", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Liv Likë Dis", "line": "She said, “Tonka, you live with the birds”", "vault_lines": ["She said, \"Tonka, you live with the birds\""], "meaning": "ho’s=birds. he’s chilling with the ho’s", "annotation_id": "39924571", "url": "https://genius.com/39924571", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Liv Likë Dis", "line": "Hundred bands in Balenci’, this is not Tom Ford (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Hundred bands in Balenci', this is not Tom Ford (Huh)"], "meaning": "Yeat spent $100,000 (1 band = $1000) in Balenciaga, which is a well known luxury brand. Tom Ford is also a luxury brand, but Yeat doesn’t shop there since their not expensive enough for him to flex.", "annotation_id": "39224913", "url": "https://genius.com/39224913", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Liv Likë Dis", "line": "I went 2x2, my boy got a Tonka", "vault_lines": ["I went 2x2, my boy got a Tonka"], "meaning": "Reference to Yeat’s song “2x2”\n\nTonka is a big-body luxury truck/SUV.", "annotation_id": "39224872", "url": "https://genius.com/39224872", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Liv Likë Dis", "line": "I was the first ones covered with turbans", "vault_lines": ["I was the first ones covered with turbans"], "meaning": "A unique article of clothing often wore by Yeat earlier on in his career. Made him stand out even more.", "annotation_id": "39171009", "url": "https://genius.com/39171009", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Liv Likë Dis", "line": "I was the first ones covered with turbans", "vault_lines": ["I was the first ones covered with turbans"], "meaning": "Yeat is stating that he was the first artist to start off in an anonymous way, covering his face with a turban. This shows how influential Yeat really is, with artists like EsDee Kid imitating his style.", "annotation_id": "39162113", "url": "https://genius.com/39162113", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Liv Likë Dis", "line": "Way back when (Huh) I ain’t have nobody to trust but you (Oh)", "vault_lines": ["Way back when (Huh)"], "meaning": "Yeat reflects on a time before fame, when trust was limited but genuine. This contrast emphasizes how success has complicated his relationships, making it harder to distinguish authenticity from opportunism.", "annotation_id": "39149230", "url": "https://genius.com/39149230", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Liv Likë Dis", "line": "You said that you was all love, but you was all lies, baby (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["You said that you was all love, but you was all lies, baby (Huh)"], "meaning": "This line introduces betrayal into the narrative, marking a shift from superficial relationships to emotional consequences. It suggests that what was perceived as love was ultimately dishonest, reinforcing the idea that relationships in Yeat’s world are unstable and transactional.", "annotation_id": "39149229", "url": "https://genius.com/39149229", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Liv Likë Dis", "line": "Rolls-Royce tank (Woo, woo) Got hundreds in my Rolls-Royce tank", "vault_lines": ["Rolls-Royce tank (Woo, woo)"], "meaning": "When rappers or car enthusiasts call a Rolls-Royce a “tank,” they’re usually referring to the Rolls-Royce Cullinan, a massive luxury SUV with a commanding, almost unstoppable presence. Sometimes the Phantom gets the nickname too, especially older models with a long, heavy body, but most of the time, “tank” points to the Cullinan.", "annotation_id": "39146429", "url": "https://genius.com/39146429", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Liv Likë Dis", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-liv-like-dis-lyrics", "genius_title": "Liv Likë Dis", "genius_id": 13296377, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LiteWork", "line": "Slayworld soldier", "vault_lines": ["I ain't mean to brag, its a hundred on the stash"], "meaning": "Slayworld was founded in 2016. It was an underground collective with numerous rappers, producers, and affiliates. This group works together and makes music called “pluggnb,” which has been a buzz in the underground music scene for some time now and is starting to gain mainstream acceptance. The roster seems to change regularly, but some current and past members are Izaya Tiji, Endoh, Autumn!, Summrs, KanKan, Yeat, and more.", "annotation_id": "31043001", "url": "https://genius.com/31043001", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LiteWork", "line": "KanKan on the beat", "vault_lines": ["KanKan on the beat"], "meaning": "Before Kankan made music, he was a producer. He produced songs for\nThouxanbanFauni, Ron$oCold, Lil Pump, Duwap Kaine, BoofBoiIcy, Smokepurpp, Famous Dex, Yung Bans, Warhol.ss, Summrs, and Autumn.\n\nKankan first started producing when he was a teenager, producing earlier tracks such as, “Trust Issues” by Duwap Kaine, “Caillou” by Lil Boom, and “Dicks Out For Harambe” by Lil Boom. Kankan then later produced popular tracks making a name for him, such as “Fuck a Swisher” by Smokepurpp & Xavier Wulf, and “Talkin Shit” by Famous Dex & Lil Pump in late 2016 and 2017.", "annotation_id": "31042998", "url": "https://genius.com/31042998", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LiteWork", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-litework-lyrics", "genius_title": "LiteWork", "genius_id": 6452129, "source": "api"}
