{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LYFE PARTY", "line": "Yeah, uh, we outside, shawty (Uh-huh)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, uh, we outside, shawty (Uh-huh)"], "meaning": "Yeat is mentioning how he is ‘outside’, which is the polar opposite of inside and also the word ‘shawty’, a popular way in hip-hop and urban culture to describe a young, attractive woman, though its use can also be interpreted as a catcall.", "annotation_id": "36807058", "url": "https://genius.com/36807058", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LYFE PARTY", "line": "Yeah, we don’t fuck with them, and they don’t fuck with us, ain’t no shit has changed, huh", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we don't fuck with them, and they don't fuck with us, ain't no shit has changed, huh"], "meaning": "Not 100% sure but i think this might be a sneak diss to 0pium", "annotation_id": "34916187", "url": "https://genius.com/34916187", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LYFE PARTY", "line": "Weep down on your knees, if you tell the God, “Please” Yeah, tell me when you mean it, yeah, don’t lie to me", "vault_lines": ["Weep down on your knees, if you tell the God, \"Please\""], "meaning": "These two verses show a lot about Yeat’s personality. The first line shows his superiority complex and narcissistic personality(he also calls himself a psychopath on multiple songs on 2093). He professes himself as a God and wants you to get on your knees and beg him(Probably for forgiveness). The next line is a line dripping of contempt where he doesn’t like when people lie to him. This is due to past friends like SeptembersRich or Opium trying to destroy him or make fun of him or degrade him. These past events cause trust issues which caused him to hate liars.", "annotation_id": "34788507", "url": "https://genius.com/34788507", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LYFE PARTY", "line": "All these muh’fuckin’ fake-ass bitches, buyin’ stream mode", "vault_lines": ["All these muh'fuckin' fake-ass bitches, buyin' stream mode"], "meaning": "These could be Yeat making fun of people who pay money to buy stream views or likes and views for their music.", "annotation_id": "34788496", "url": "https://genius.com/34788496", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LYFE PARTY", "line": "All of us on bright mode, all my diamonds shine, ho", "vault_lines": ["All of us on bright mode, all my diamonds shine, ho"], "meaning": "Yeat uses his impressive wordplay here with the analogy of “bright mode.” he is saying his diamonds are like bright mode on his phone because just like bright mode on his phone his diamonds shine extremely bright", "annotation_id": "34788488", "url": "https://genius.com/34788488", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LYFE PARTY", "line": "Everythin’ we touch so hot, it’s fifty thousand degrees", "vault_lines": ["Everythin' we touch so hot, it's fifty thousand degrees"], "meaning": "While this line seems self-explanatory, it has a much deeper meaning. Yeat points out that everything he does, from wearing certain clothing items to making up new words, becomes popular, and everyone “hops on” or joins the trend, making it new and “hot.” The line 50,000 degrees is just an exaggeration to show how influential Yeat is today.", "annotation_id": "33371183", "url": "https://genius.com/33371183", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LYFE PARTY", "line": "Huh, I’m in the Maybach, ‘clinin’ the seat, and this bih’ hydraulic", "vault_lines": ["Huh, I'm in the Maybach, 'clinin' the seat, and this bih' hydraulic"], "meaning": "Maybach is a luxury car brand that is owned by Mercedes and is considered to be Mercedes’s most luxurious vehicles available. Yeat is saying that there are reclining seats and hydraulics on the vehicle, which are features that are only present on vehicles with high-end technology, which is expensive.", "annotation_id": "33333457", "url": "https://genius.com/33333457", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LYFE PARTY", "line": "In Tonka, uh-huh, big body", "vault_lines": ["In Tonka, uh-huh, big body"], "meaning": "‘Tonka’, Yeats term for a Luxury SUV. Yeat could be referring to many different vehicles, but it is likely it is a Mercedes GLE/G-Wagon, Lamborghini Urus, or Bentley Bentayga.", "annotation_id": "33333453", "url": "https://genius.com/33333453", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LYFE PARTY", "line": "Yeah, all my cars bought, no renewal, heh-huh", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, all my cars bought, no renewal, heh-huh"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying here that all of the cars that he owns, he bought outright and no payment plans such as renewals. With many rappers and people faking their riches by renting high-priced cars, Yeat is saying that his riches are real.", "annotation_id": "33333443", "url": "https://genius.com/33333443", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LYFE PARTY", "line": "We outside with Bentley truck, huh", "vault_lines": ["We outside with Bentley truck, huh"], "meaning": "Yeat is more than likely referring to the Bentley Bentayga, a British Luxury SUV. Yeat is both seen in and references luxury SUV’s in his songs, such as the Lamborghini Urus, Mercedes GLE, and Mercedes G-Wagon.", "annotation_id": "33333434", "url": "https://genius.com/33333434", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
