{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LOCO", "line": "Once they see this life, they jump on it like it’s a pogo", "vault_lines": ["Once they see this life, they jump on it like it's a pogo"], "meaning": "People quickly gravitate toward his lifestyle once they see the luxury. The pogo stick simile suggests bouncing onto whatever seems exciting or profitable.", "annotation_id": "38798018", "url": "https://genius.com/38798018", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LOCO", "line": "Go ’head, go ’head (What?) Go ’head, go ’head Go ’head, go ’head Go ’head, go coco (Go loco) Money got me loco, uh, she on powder, coco", "vault_lines": ["Go 'head, go 'head (What?)"], "meaning": "“Coco” refers to cocaine. “Loco” (Spanish for crazy) suggests money has made him reckless or wild. The line connects wealth, drug culture, and instability.", "annotation_id": "38798007", "url": "https://genius.com/38798007", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
