{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LOCO", "line": "Double tied, switchin’ sides, no, you can’t feel me", "vault_lines": ["Double tied, switchin' sides, no, you can't feel me"], "meaning": "‘'double tied’‘ means his feelings, identity, and life are safely securely knotted together, making him impenetrable and emotionally detached from others.\n\n‘'switchin sides’‘ could be him talking about his lack of loyalty between relationships and switching friend groups and situations.", "annotation_id": "37004037", "url": "https://genius.com/37004037", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LOCO", "line": "I’m ‘bout to pull up at the crib that I built for myself (Huh, huh), you gon’ pull up at Marriott (Huh, huh)", "vault_lines": ["Go 'head, go 'head (What?)"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying he built this life for himself. The crib I built for myself is symbolic of his permanent stay in his success. in contrast to the other person’s life, which is temporary and dependent on someone else’s success", "annotation_id": "37004003", "url": "https://genius.com/37004003", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
