{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LOCO", "line": "I went and flooded my diamonds, yeah, ’cause I could", "vault_lines": ["I went and flooded my diamonds, yeah, 'cause I could"], "meaning": "“Flooded” refers to a piece of jewelry being completely covered by diamonds. He’s showing off his wealth and that he can spend money on extravagant items like so.", "annotation_id": "36486790", "url": "https://genius.com/36486790", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LOCO", "line": "I just pulled up in some Marmot", "vault_lines": ["I just pulled up in some Marmot"], "meaning": "Marmot is a brand of outdoor apparel, which Yeat would most likely where while on his property practicing his shooting.", "annotation_id": "36469603", "url": "https://genius.com/36469603", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LOCO", "line": "I fucked my money up and now it’s pregnant with some triplets", "vault_lines": ["I fucked my money up and now it's pregnant with some triplets"], "meaning": "Yeat’s consistent use of sexually charged metaphors to describe his wealth reveals a complex relationship with his financial success. The repeated imagery of “fucking up” his money, suggesting both reckless spending and intense pleasure\n\nThis kind of line is also seen on a number of different tracks on Yeat’s discography, released and unreleased:\n\nReleased tracks:\n\nRollin – 2 Alive :\n‘I just went doubled my money, then I fucked it up again, made it go thrice.’\n\nLuh m – 2 Alive :\n‘Fucked my money up so much, It told me that it’s cumming.’\n\nAlways Alivë – Alivë :\n‘I went and fucked my money up, I was horny.’\n\nFuk tha Clout – KanKan (feat. Yeat) :\n‘Yeah, I fuck my money up so much it told me that it came.’\n\nUnreleased tracks:\n\nReal is Rarë – (Scrapped from Up 2 Më) :\n‘I fucked my money up so much, I done ejaculated.’\n\nStill – Lil Yachty (feat. Yeat) :\n‘I fucked my money up so good, it told me that it came.’\n\nStarted Off – (Unknown era) :\n‘I fucked up my money, then gave it a kiss.’\n\nThis common sexualisation of his money is not merely boastful; it’s a performative act. It’s less about the literal act of spending and more about the feeling of control and abundance. The sexual language heightens the sense of power and dominance associated with his wealth. It is a key element of his unique style and thematic consistency.", "annotation_id": "36437836", "url": "https://genius.com/36437836", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "LOCO", "line": "Have you ever forgot something and you can’t remember it? All the time But it’s like how do your brain forget it forgot?", "vault_lines": ["Have you ever forgot something and you can't remember it?"], "meaning": "This sample is taken from a ZIAS & B. Lou stream where B. Lou questions the brain:\n\nLike, have you ever forgot something and you can’t remember it? But it’s like, how do your brain forget it forgot? Like, I forgot, but then I was like, “How did I forget that I forgot?”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/shorts/Kvz5DlyM-Yc\n\nThe duo also reacted to “The Bell” three months prior to this track being released.", "annotation_id": "36427667", "url": "https://genius.com/36427667", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
