{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Krazy 2 Më", "line": "My twizzy goin’ up, [?], I’m Twizzy Rich, so it’s us now", "vault_lines": ["My twizzy goin' up, [?], I'm Twizzy Rich, so it's us now"], "meaning": "“Twizzy Rich” Was yeats label that he made with his long time friends: SeptembersRich and Nextel. After they had a falling out, yeat created his new label “Lyfestyle Corporation” named after his upcoming studio album.", "annotation_id": "29538134", "url": "https://genius.com/29538134", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Krazy 2 Më", "line": "She said, “Do you love me?” I told that bitch, “Always” But I got a couple of them, so I told ’em all I’ll wait", "vault_lines": ["But I got a couple of them, so I told 'em all I'll wait"], "meaning": "Yeat has so many girls that are interested in him that he has a hard time telling them he doesn’t love them. In order to keep good ties with all of them, he tells them that he’ll wait to have a relationship because he isn’t ready. This allows him to continue the affair with all of them.", "annotation_id": "29538107", "url": "https://genius.com/29538107", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
