{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Kranky (Arriba)", "line": "Pockets big, got me looking Rikishi, that’s Scotty 2 Hotty, the worm (Worm)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I just pulled up in that vert' (Phew, ooh)"], "meaning": "“Pockets big” or “Pockets fat” is a common term used by Uzi as well as other trap artists. It’s a play on words to indicate that there is a lot of money in his pockets which is what makes them big.\n\nRikishi, a WWE wrestler, weighs in at 425 pounds and is being compared to Uzi’s pockets being big.\n\n\n\nRikishi inside of the ring\n\n\nScotty 2 Hotty, another wrestler, happens to be Rikishi’s WWE tag-team partner. He is famous for doing the worm as a finishing move after fights.", "annotation_id": "25861405", "url": "https://genius.com/25861405", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Kranky (Arriba)", "line": "Four pockets full, I’m on Lil Baby, so I had to wait on my turn (Turn)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I just pulled up in that vert' (Phew, ooh)"], "meaning": "On this line, Uzi makes a double entendre in reference to Atlanta recording artist Lil Baby and his February 2020 project My Turn. He also pays homage to Lil Baby’s crew, 4PF, an initialism for “4 Pockets Full” which is capitalized upon in the lyric by Uzi.\n\n\n\nLil Baby wearing his custom 4PF chain.", "annotation_id": "25787070", "url": "https://genius.com/25787070", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
