{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "King tonka", "line": "Yeah, we move on, we get—, we get richer than ya We all livin’ on these drugs", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we move on, we get—, we get richer than ya"], "meaning": "In these lines, Yeat is implying that he and his associates are progressing in life, becoming wealthier, and potentially more successful than others. The mention of “livin' on these drugs” suggests a lifestyle intertwined with substance use, which might contribute to their perceived success or lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "31810178", "url": "https://genius.com/31810178", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "King tonka", "line": "Uh, I don’t pay attention, I don’t need attention I just do the fuck, uh, what I want, when I want", "vault_lines": [", I don't pay attention, I don't need attention"], "meaning": "In this line, Yeat is asserting his independence and self-assurance. He’s saying that he doesn’t seek attention from others because he’s confident in himself. He does what he wants, when he wants, without concerning himself with the opinions or approval of others.", "annotation_id": "31810176", "url": "https://genius.com/31810176", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "King tonka", "line": "We send him to Heaven, get ’em gone, I said (Send him)", "vault_lines": ["We send him to Heaven, get 'em gone, I said (Send him)"], "meaning": "In this line, Yeat is suggesting that someone is being killed, euphemistically referring to their death as being “sent to Heaven.” It implies a cold attitude towards violence or retribution.", "annotation_id": "31810171", "url": "https://genius.com/31810171", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "King tonka", "line": "You could tell me shit, but you don’t tell me nothing I’m a number one rich ass junkie", "vault_lines": ["You could tell me shit, but you don't tell me nothing"], "meaning": "In these lines, Yeat seems to be expressing a sense of detachment or indifference towards the opinions or advice of others. When he says, “You could tell me shit, but you don’t tell me nothing,” he’s suggesting that people may attempt to offer him advice or guidance, but he doesn’t find it particularly useful or meaningful.\n\nThe second line, “I’m a number one rich ass junkie,” could be interpreted in a couple of ways. It could mean that Yeat is addicted to wealth and success, constantly striving to attain more riches and elevate his status. Alternatively, he might be using “junkie” metaphorically to describe his intense dedication or obsession with achieving financial success, likening it to an addiction.", "annotation_id": "31810166", "url": "https://genius.com/31810166", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "King tonka", "line": "Diamonds said, diamonds said, “We don’t give a fuck” Diamonds said, “Diamonds on you, never show up”", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds said, diamonds said, \"We don't give a fuck\""], "meaning": "In these lines, Yeat seems to be personifying diamonds as if they are speaking. When he says “Diamonds said, ‘We don’t give a fuck,’” he could be referring to the idea that material possessions like diamonds don’t care about external opinions or judgments. They remain unbothered and confident regardless of what others think.\n\nThe second line, “Diamonds said, ‘Diamonds on you, never show up,’” could be interpreted as a metaphor for the idea that one’s worth or value is often overlooked or underestimated by others. Despite having valuable possessions like diamonds, they may not always receive recognition or acknowledgment from those around them.", "annotation_id": "31810163", "url": "https://genius.com/31810163", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "King tonka", "line": "I’m a number one rich ass junkie", "vault_lines": ["I'm a number one rich ass junkie"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying he is the richest junkie (drug addict)", "annotation_id": "31787357", "url": "https://genius.com/31787357", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
