{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "King tonka", "line": "I be high, I’m geekin out my head, I’m on a heliplane", "vault_lines": ["I be high, I'm geekin out my head, I'm on a heliplane"], "meaning": "Double entendre here by Yeat:\n\n\n“I be high, I’m geekin out my head…” is self explanatory\n“…I’m on a heliplane” Yeat is saying he is so high that he is on a heliplane (he’s geeked so much he feels like he is in the sky) and also that he is on a heliplane which could be referring to “737, we get high and crash”", "annotation_id": "31622831", "url": "https://genius.com/31622831", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "King tonka", "line": "(No way)", "vault_lines": ["Boot up on the X, on the X game (No way)"], "meaning": "When this snippet was previewed, this simple adlib, barely noticable, was believed to be the beginning of a Lil Uzi Vert feature. But, as it turns out, it was not.", "annotation_id": "31524318", "url": "https://genius.com/31524318", "state": "pending", "votes": -6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "King tonka", "line": "It king Tonka (Err, err), it king Tonka (Err, err), it king T— (Ugh, ugh)", "vault_lines": ["It king Tonka (Err, err), it king Tonka (Err, err), it king T— (Ugh, ugh)"], "meaning": "Yeat refers to himself here as “King Tonka,” as he has previously done in 2093. This is also the title of this track meaning it’s potentially a sequel to [Tonka] (https://genius.com/Yeat-tonka-lyrics) and/or [Big tonka] (https://genius.com/Yeat-big-tonka-lyrics).", "annotation_id": "31426890", "url": "https://genius.com/31426890", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "King tonka", "line": "Yeah, we could fly around, like the Bentley-truck-ing (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we could fly around, like the Bentley-truck-ing (Woo)"], "meaning": "Yeat might be suggesting that he and someone else could travel luxuriously and freely, akin to driving around in a Bentley truck.\n\nThe Bentley could also be a metaphor for a private jet.", "annotation_id": "31422549", "url": "https://genius.com/31422549", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "King tonka", "line": "Pull up, and we geek all night (All night)", "vault_lines": ["Pull up, and we geek all night (All night)"], "meaning": "Yeat here portrays a scene of recreational drug use and staying awake for an extended period of time. Possibly as part of a social gathering or party atmosphere.", "annotation_id": "31412902", "url": "https://genius.com/31412902", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
