{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "King tonka", "line": "737, we get high and we crash (Phew)", "vault_lines": ["737, we get high and we crash (Phew)"], "meaning": "This line is a double entendre. Yeat is saying he and his friends get high at 7:37 in the morning and they then proceed to crash out as the effects of the drugs wear off.\n\nThis line however also refers to the Boeing 737 a common commercial aircraft line which obviously gets high whenever it takes off and is prone to crashing when doing so.", "annotation_id": "31401958", "url": "https://genius.com/31401958", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
