{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "Yeah, I made this shit up, but I’m back on them charts (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I made this shit up, but I'm back on them charts (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat is an artist who maintains an anonymous persona. Whenever he takes time off after releasing an album, he creates his own innovative sound and image, which still succeeds. He can push the boundaries of rap and alter it while still performing great numbers.\n\nThe point of this line is to talk about his uniqueness which he reflects a lot about on Lyfe.", "annotation_id": "34360090", "url": "https://genius.com/34360090", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "No, you can’t rock with the mob, can’t rock with the gang, lil’ bitch, we not feeling you (Uh) All this shit feeling familiar, uh Got the game in a lock and I’m killin’ ’em (Ooh) I touch a mill’ every first of the month, that’s why my pockets not big enough (Ooh) Ride ’round the city inside of the Tonka, yeah, but this shit still not big enough (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Got hunnid round, bitch, got hunnid round, bitch, got hunnid round, bitch, got hunnid round chops"], "meaning": "To the people Yeat addresses, you aren’t real enough to hang with his crew, who top everyone else’s clique because of their success. He’s so successful that he claims his wallets can’t contain the constant money he accumulates. Yet he still casually affirms that the boastful accomplishments aren’t enough; he wants more and implies he can do more.", "annotation_id": "34360034", "url": "https://genius.com/34360034", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "Yeah, I got some brothers, who movin’ that chicken", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I got some brothers, who movin' that chicken"], "meaning": "What he means by “moving chicken” it means that his bro is pushing out coke and making sum moneys out of it", "annotation_id": "32015107", "url": "https://genius.com/32015107", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "Hit the ceiling lil’ bitch, and I’m feelin’ ’em", "vault_lines": [", hit the ceiling lil' bitch, and I'm feelin' 'em"], "meaning": "When he says he hits the ceiling, he means when he starts to come up on the percocet high, he gets so high that he hits the ceiling.", "annotation_id": "32015104", "url": "https://genius.com/32015104", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "I’m takin’ the Perc’ with", "vault_lines": ["I'm takin' the Perc' with"], "meaning": "Yeat says he’s taking the Perc with Amoxicillin but don’t get it confused, he means Acetaminophen because that’s what Percocet contains in combination with Oxycodone. He merely says Amoxicillin to strategically keep the flow of the lyrics.", "annotation_id": "31260334", "url": "https://genius.com/31260334", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "Yeah, I pull up to London with shanks on me, bitch, I’m stabbin’ they ears (Luh shank)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I pull up to London with shanks on me, bitch, I'm stabbin' they ears (Luh shank)"], "meaning": "Yeat is british. Oi bruv mate bloody hell what is in the sky 🇬🇧🇬🇧🇬🇧☕️☕️☕️🔪🔪🔪", "annotation_id": "30693346", "url": "https://genius.com/30693346", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
