{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "(I-I’m working on dying)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I made this shit up, but I'm back on them charts (Yeah)"], "meaning": "In this lyric (or bar as the cool kids say). Yeat announces that he is in-fact, working on dying. This means Yeat also known as Noah Smith, is working on not being with us anymore. This begs the question; Should we be worried about Yeat? (I mean this line itself scares me as a fellow Yeat enjoyer) or should we carry on as this is just a line in a song? In my personal opinion, we cannot let this behaviour pass off as “just a bar” because this sounds like Yeat could be engaged in self harm! To raise awareness about this subject, please use #helpyeat on twitter! Anyways as I wrap up my annotation, I would like you fellow Yeat enjoyers to ask yourself a question. How can we allow this as a society?\nKind Regards, Woman Lover", "annotation_id": "26769861", "url": "https://genius.com/26769861", "state": "pending", "votes": -30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "I’m on the side with the gremlin, gremlin, pull up and fuck my system and the mayhem", "vault_lines": ["I'm on the side with the gremlin, gremlin, pull up and fuck my system and the mayhem"], "meaning": "Yeat describes his side chick as a “gremlin,” describing their sex as “mayhem.” This term refers to a short girl, usually under 5’2, who has unmatched sexual prowess. Due to their abilities in the bedroom, these women are ideal for side chicks. An example of a typical “gremlin” is Snooki from Jersey Shore.", "annotation_id": "26679335", "url": "https://genius.com/26679335", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "Yeah, I got some brothers, who movin’ that chicken, yeah (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I got some brothers, who movin' that chicken, yeah (Yeah)"], "meaning": "“Moving chicken” is slang for selling cocaine, which Yeat famously rapped about on his breakout track, “Get Busy”:\n\nYeah, how I was servin' chickens, huh, in the mail", "annotation_id": "26679322", "url": "https://genius.com/26679322", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "I’m drinkin’ that dirty, that muddy, that cup, that mud, that muhfuckin’ what? We come from that dirty, we drinkin’ that dirty, we come from that dirty stuff", "vault_lines": ["We come from that dirty, we drinkin' that dirty, we come from that dirty stuff"], "meaning": "As a result of growing up poor, Yeat and his crew now enjoy the finer things in life thanks to his newfound success. Notably, he’s sipping on dirty sprite, also known as lean, a beverage prepared by mixing prescription strength cough syrup containing codeine and promethazine with soda.", "annotation_id": "26679289", "url": "https://genius.com/26679289", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "Them drugs is killin’ ’em, killin ’em Drugs is killin ’em, drugs is killin ’em", "vault_lines": ["Them drugs is killin 'em, drugs is killin 'em"], "meaning": "Although Yeat frequently raps about taking drugs on Lyfë, he recognizes the harmful effect this has on him and those around him, be that friend or foe. Yeat’s statements are backed by facts, as, in 2021, over 100,000 people died from a drug overdose in the USA.", "annotation_id": "26679269", "url": "https://genius.com/26679269", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "Got hunnid round, bitch, got hunnid round, bitch, got hunnid round, bitch, got hunnid round chops Got hunnid round, bitch, got hunnid round, bitch, got hunnid round, bitch, got hunnid round chops", "vault_lines": ["Got hunnid round, bitch, got hunnid round, bitch, got hunnid round, bitch, got hunnid round chops"], "meaning": "Yeat and his crew keep firearms, namely with 100-round capacity magazines, which, in keeping with the song’s violent theme, they intend to use to kill their opps.", "annotation_id": "26679239", "url": "https://genius.com/26679239", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Killin ëm", "line": "Come every time back from my break, yeah, and I’m all on the charts (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Come every time back from my break, yeah, and I'm all on the charts (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Between each of his releases, Yeat has taken a break to record new material. As a result, he gets better with each release, soaring to new heights on the charts.\n\nYeat has been on multiple charts, such as Apple Music, Spotify, and Billboard, multiple times for hits such as “Talk,” “Rich Minion,” “Monëy so big,” and more.", "annotation_id": "26674686", "url": "https://genius.com/26674686", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
