{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Kant dië", "line": "I just been pullin’ up, shittin’ on them all day, I stink (Oh)", "vault_lines": ["I just been pullin' up, shittin' on them all day, I stink (Oh)"], "meaning": "Yeat establishes his dominance over his competition by using the popular phrase “shitting on them,” however, he takes it to the next level. To emphasize the magnitude of the shitting that he is doing, he uses adjectival language to describe himself. In this, he says “I stink”.\n\nYeat continues to amaze his listeners with his exquisite lingual choices with every new release, with the only exception being Afterlyfe.", "annotation_id": "28386064", "url": "https://genius.com/28386064", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
