{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Jus Wokëup", "line": "Woke up, I just woke up to a bag, I just woke up", "vault_lines": ["Woke up, I just woke up to a bag, I just woke up"], "meaning": "In this line, Yeat uses the term “bag” to refer to money, wealth, or a profitable opportunity. Suggests that financial success has become so common in his life that he can literally wake up and already have money waiting for him", "annotation_id": "38955071", "url": "https://genius.com/38955071", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
