{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Jump", "line": "Bitch I touched a milli, yeah, ridin’ ’round by myself now (Self) Pulled up on the fuckin’ scene, but it’s not a playground (Ah) I don’t give fuck ’bout what you sayin’, yeah, what you said now? You don’t make more money than me, you gotta sit down, yeah You tried to steal my swag from me, you gotta sit down", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I touched a milli, yeah, ridin' 'round by myself now (Self)"], "meaning": "This verse is a possible diss towards rapper Autumn!\n\n\n\nThe beef started off when Autumn! released a snippet on his Instagram (which is now released and is called Portrayal!).\n\n\n\nYeat believed that Autumn! was biting his style and called him out for it via an Instagram story (which was deleted very quickly) and they went back and forth via Instagram stories. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VWtbF6aXFI8&t=70s", "annotation_id": "25273931", "url": "https://genius.com/25273931", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
