{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "If We Being Rëal", "line": "I forget everything, I don’t even know where my tip is And I’ll change everything, I don’t know how l’Il top this", "vault_lines": ["I don't know how to feel"], "meaning": "Yeat is confronting his musical limit and potential, uncertain if and how he can surpass what he’s already accomplished throughout his career.", "annotation_id": "38614381", "url": "https://genius.com/38614381", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "If We Being Rëal", "line": "I take the money to another level I take the plane to another level I take the heights to a newer level I take gettin’ high to a newer level", "vault_lines": ["I take the money to another level"], "meaning": "Yeat wants to keep evolving and keep growing his fanbase, gaining riches while also expanding his horizons to different paths as seen with the diversity of this song and it’s album, 2093.", "annotation_id": "31449262", "url": "https://genius.com/31449262", "state": "pending", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "If We Being Rëal", "line": "I had to cut the pill off, yeah But if we bein’ real though, yeah Nah, I don’t never feel nothin’", "vault_lines": ["I had to let a little off, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat made this album completely sober, no longer using drugs. He expresses how he used to abuse pill medication to get high. He also tells us how he doesn’t feel anything when sober, and how beating his addiction is a struggle.", "annotation_id": "30939169", "url": "https://genius.com/30939169", "state": "pending", "votes": 86, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
