{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "IMMA BASTARD", "line": "(Yeah, I pull up Texas, big dawgs, yeah) (Longhorn, motherfucker, bitch, I get ya killed)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I pull up Texas, big dawgs, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat references the Texas Longhorns, the University of Texas athletic program, which includes major teams like football and basketball. The Longhorn symbol is widely associated with size, strength, and dominance, especially through its football culture. In the bar, Yeat uses this imagery alongside “big dawgs” to emphasize power, presence, and a larger-than-life identity, rather than referring to a specific sport.", "annotation_id": "39082864", "url": "https://genius.com/39082864", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
