{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "IMMA BASTARD", "line": "I might be a bastard, I might fuck them off the lot I might be a bastard, I might kick them out they spot, huh I might be a bastard, I might move them out they plot I might be a bastard, I might fuck them, all they thots I might be a bastard, I might move them out they blocks", "vault_lines": ["I might be a bastard, I might move them out they blocks"], "meaning": "The repetition builds a persona. Yeat leans into being reckless, unapologetic, and disruptive, framing himself as someone who doesn’t follow rules or care about consequences.", "annotation_id": "39082781", "url": "https://genius.com/39082781", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
