{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "Pendants I put ’round my neck, make a Cartier Cartier watch, it’s not even a starter pack", "vault_lines": ["Pendants I put 'round my neck, make a Cartier"], "meaning": "Cartier jewelry is a status symbol in hip-hop, but YoungBoy flexes that his level of wealth goes far beyond the “starter pack” of luxury watches and chains. For him, Cartier is just the beginning, not the pinnacle, of what he can afford.", "annotation_id": "36802319", "url": "https://genius.com/36802319", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I used to ride up to slimes in the Pontiac I got this shit in position, I’m quarterback", "vault_lines": ["I used to ride up to slimes in the Pontiac"], "meaning": "He references his old days driving a Pontiac, a modest car compared to his luxury vehicles today. The “quarterback” metaphor shows his leadership role — he’s the one in control, calling the plays and directing his team, both in life and in the music industry.", "annotation_id": "36802316", "url": "https://genius.com/36802316", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "They was talkin’ ’bout me ’cause my clothes was dingy Hand-me-downs, I used to wear from my cousin", "vault_lines": ["They was talkin' 'bout me 'cause my clothes was dingy"], "meaning": "YoungBoy recalls being ridiculed for wearing old, worn-out clothes passed down from family members. This detail highlights the poverty he grew up in and the struggles he faced before fame. It’s a moment of vulnerability that contrasts with his current wealth and success.", "annotation_id": "36802288", "url": "https://genius.com/36802288", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I had to grind and it take me a minute", "vault_lines": ["I had to grind and it take me a minute"], "meaning": "Here he reflects on his journey. Success didn’t come overnight — it took time, persistence, and hard work. The “grind” refers not only to his career in rap but also to surviving his difficult upbringing.", "annotation_id": "36802283", "url": "https://genius.com/36802283", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I got some twizzies, they crazy, they kill you, they get you like", "vault_lines": ["I got some twizzies, they crazy, they kill you, they get you like"], "meaning": "“Twizz” or “Twizzies” is a popular term used by Yeat and underground rappers. A twizz is someone who is someone who is very close to you ( friend , homie, brother ).", "annotation_id": "27217954", "url": "https://genius.com/27217954", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I mix the Oxy’ with X, bitch, I’m booted like", "vault_lines": ["I mix the Oxy' with X, bitch, I'm booted like"], "meaning": "Yeat is telling us here that he mixes drugs and becomes booted. The popular drugs are Oxycodone and Xanax. They are often mixed for pill consumption. Booted is a term used for being under the influence of pills", "annotation_id": "27217943", "url": "https://genius.com/27217943", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "DOP", "vault_lines": ["I upgraded my linen, huh, DOP"], "meaning": "*BOP (Big Ol’ Player)", "annotation_id": "27038227", "url": "https://genius.com/27038227", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I’m at the top of this shit like I’m Big Ole pimpin’", "vault_lines": ["I'm at the top of this shit like I'm Big Ole pimpin'"], "meaning": "The “Big ole” part can also be interpreted as “Big O”.\n\nBig O notation is a mathematical notation that describes the limiting behavior of a function when the argument tends towards a particular value or infinity.\n\nBy this, Yeat means that he will always be on top for eternity like the Big O.", "annotation_id": "27005180", "url": "https://genius.com/27005180", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I’m not your friend, your twizz’, your cousin, listen, no, I’m not friendly", "vault_lines": ["I'm not your friend, your twizz', your cousin, listen, no, I'm not friendly"], "meaning": "Yeat makes it clear, if you are not his friend, Twizz (word for “bro”), or  related, he is going to take you as a threat to him or his money.", "annotation_id": "26964775", "url": "https://genius.com/26964775", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "You broke, lil’ bitch, we in the big boy league, you still countin’ them pennies (Bitch)", "vault_lines": ["You broke, lil' bitch, we in the big boy league, you still countin' them pennies (Bitch)"], "meaning": "Yeat is comparing his vast amounts of wealth to him being in the “big leagues”, making a lot of money. Yeat then states his hater’s wealth is so minuscule they are still collecting Pennies to get by.", "annotation_id": "26964729", "url": "https://genius.com/26964729", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "I Don’t Text Back", "line": "I’ll fly with the birds", "vault_lines": ["I was just talkin' to God, I'll fly with the birds"], "meaning": "This is a nod to Summrs‘ “Bird Business” term he makes in songs like “Swing Ya Pole.”\n\nDon’t get your face took off, lil' pussy, you know I fly with the birds\n\nYeat has collaborated with Summrs numerous times on songs like “Countup,” “Already Said It,” and “Alien Language,” amongst many others.", "annotation_id": "26952630", "url": "https://genius.com/26952630", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
