{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hëlly (Hëllcat)", "line": "Yeah, I had a Fashion Week, I was in France with my slut and she ate it up", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I had a Fashion Week, I was in France with my slut and she ate it up"], "meaning": "yeat refers to another his unreleased song, called fashun week", "annotation_id": "36626945", "url": "https://genius.com/36626945", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hëlly (Hëllcat)", "line": "And the coupe a SRT, watch me peel this bitch top speed", "vault_lines": ["And the coupe a SRT, watch me peel this bitch top speed"], "meaning": "An SRT is a type of performance vehicle made by Dodge known for  having exceptional horsepower, making it faster than most cars.\n\n\n\nYeat expresses how when he drives his SRT, he often finds himself speeding, most-likely exceeding the speed limit.", "annotation_id": "27182699", "url": "https://genius.com/27182699", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hëlly (Hëllcat)", "line": "I used to be so down bad, ain’t even know what to do, ah Now I got all this money on me, my face is all blue", "vault_lines": ["I used to be so down bad, ain't even know what to do, ah"], "meaning": "Yeat speaks about how he used to be poor and in a less stable state in terms of wealth.\n\nWith his newfound success in rapping, he lets us know his income has become so high that he even has hundred dollar bills, a kind of American currency which, inferred by the name, is worth one hundred dollars.\n\n\n\nHundred dollar bills are often referred to as “blue bills” or “blue faces” because of the slightly-altered color along with the blue line down the middle of the bill that other types of printed bills lack.", "annotation_id": "27182647", "url": "https://genius.com/27182647", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hëlly (Hëllcat)", "line": "I like to take X everyday of the week, I’m a geek, I get fuckin’ nerdy", "vault_lines": ["I like to take X everyday of the week, I'm a geek, I get fuckin' nerdy"], "meaning": "X is short for ecstasy, a drug used for it’s effects, including: altered sensations, increased energy, empathy, and pleasure.\n\n\n\nEcstasy is a type of drug Yeat frequently references in his music as one of his go-to substances to indulge in.\n\nWhen under the influence of a drug, i.e, ecstasy it is also referred to as being “geeked” or geeking\" off of the substance.\n\nYeat compares himself being geeked off of ecstasy to being a nerd, often called a geek.", "annotation_id": "27182603", "url": "https://genius.com/27182603", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hëlly (Hëllcat)", "line": "Yeah, and I told you I’m a kid, still sip baby bottle juice", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, and I told you I'm a kid, still sip baby bottle juice"], "meaning": "Yeat is comparing himself to a small child, drinking out of baby bottles to consume his drink mixture.\n\nOften, Wockhardt, which is more commonly referred to as lean, is poured into toddler’s notable baby bottles for drinking in order to slow how much is consumed.\n\n\n\nLean, often called Purple Drank, is a mixture of drugs and sometimes soda, put into a separate container to drink from. It’s known to make the consumer feel calm and relaxed but there are many risks of drinking it, including possible death.", "annotation_id": "27182514", "url": "https://genius.com/27182514", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hëlly (Hëllcat)", "line": "Every time I fell in love with this slut, I bought a tool", "vault_lines": ["Every time I fell in love with this slut, I bought a tool"], "meaning": "Yeat let’s us know about his trust issues.\n\nWhenever Yeat feels himself becoming emotionally attached to a female, he buys himself a weapon in order to protect himself from them potentially backstabbing him.", "annotation_id": "27182390", "url": "https://genius.com/27182390", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hëlly (Hëllcat)", "line": "Woah, woah, these drugs don’t help me (None, none) Woah, woah, mm, no, I’m not healthy Woah, woah, I’m goin’ to Hell, twin", "vault_lines": ["Woah, woah, these drugs don't help me (None, none)"], "meaning": "Yeat expresses his problems dealing with drugs. He knows they don’t benefit him healthwise but it seems he’s too far  down the path of addiction to quit so easily.\n\nThe combination of frequently mentioning the devil as one of his associates and using frowned upon substances also leads himself to believe he is unfortunately going to Hell when he dies.", "annotation_id": "27182381", "url": "https://genius.com/27182381", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hëlly (Hëllcat)", "line": "Woah, woah, I heard a Hellcat Woah, woah, this bitch a Hellcat (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Woah, woah, this bitch a Hellcat (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat is in disbelief at the fact that he can now afford high-priced items, i.e, the Dodge Challenger Hellcat.", "annotation_id": "27178762", "url": "https://genius.com/27178762", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
