{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hëavyweight", "line": "Yeah, I’m gettin’ that top, I’m gettin’ that noggin", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I'm gettin' that top, I'm gettin' that noggin"], "meaning": "As Yeat has mentioned multiple times in this song, he is getting oral sex from a very attractive woman, likely the one referenced in the next bar.", "annotation_id": "28695289", "url": "https://genius.com/28695289", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hëavyweight", "line": "7.62 leave him— 7.62 leave him cut", "vault_lines": ["7.62 leave him— , 7.62 leave him cut"], "meaning": "The 7.62 mm caliber is a nominal caliber used for a number of different cartridges. Historically, this class of cartridge was commonly known as .30 caliber, the equivalent in Imperial and United States Customary measures. It is most commonly used in full-power military main battle rifle (MBR) cartridges. The measurement equals 0.30 inches or three decimal lines, written .3″ and read as three-line.", "annotation_id": "28282404", "url": "https://genius.com/28282404", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hëavyweight", "line": "I hold my weight", "vault_lines": ["I hold my weight"], "meaning": "To contribute your part to something. People who carry their own weight are contributing equally to a task assigned to them. They are carrying out the part assigned to them and not relying on other to pick up their slack.", "annotation_id": "27888370", "url": "https://genius.com/27888370", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hëavyweight", "line": "Yeah, I will plead the Fifth, uh (Shh, shh, shh)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I won't plead the fifth"], "meaning": "This refers to the fifth amendment in the US Constitution. When one pleads the fifth they refuse to talk or corporate with a case. If one does not plead the fifth they agree to talk.\n\nThis fact seems to contradict Yeats next lines about refusing to talk.", "annotation_id": "27888106", "url": "https://genius.com/27888106", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
