{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "How it go", "line": "We don’t take life slow, we go God speed", "vault_lines": ["We don't take life slow, we go God speed"], "meaning": "Godspeed is an expression meaning to wish good luck/prosperity to someone typically going on a long journey.\n\nYeat is inverting the meaning of this usual expression to actually mean to live life fast, or to go “God speed”", "annotation_id": "28226649", "url": "https://genius.com/28226649", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "How it go", "line": "Ask me “What’s at stake?”, I told ’em ”Flank”", "vault_lines": ["Ask me \"What's at stake?\", I told 'em \"Flank\""], "meaning": "In this exquisite line artist Noah Oliver “Yeat” Smith makes a delightful play on words with “stake” and “flank”. “Stake” is similar sounding to “steak”, and the flank is a part of flesh from a cow’s body.\nI would like to take this moment to share a personal story on how this song changed my life.\nI was afflicted with herpes and could not get females to touch me.", "annotation_id": "27884199", "url": "https://genius.com/27884199", "state": "pending", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "How it go", "line": "Yeah, I keep stackin’ bills like I’m Cosby (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I keep stackin' bills like I'm Cosby (Yeah)"], "meaning": "This line is a play on the name of Bill Cosby, a famous comedian and actor. He was charged on multiple counts of sexual misconduct and rape in the mid 1960s.", "annotation_id": "27879438", "url": "https://genius.com/27879438", "state": "pending", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "How it go", "line": "Riding in a Cayenne with the blick (Yeah), that how it pole (Woo) Vroom-vroom-vroom-room, vroom, that how it roar", "vault_lines": ["Riding in a Cayenne with the blick (Yeah), that how it pole (Woo)"], "meaning": "The Cayenne is a luxury SUV, or “Tonka,” produced by German automobile manufacturer Porsche. He’s driving in the car with a firearm, refered to as a “pole.”\n\nYeat previously rapped about the Cayenne on the 2021 track “Told Ya,” rapping:\n\nI went into the Porsche, bitch, I went and bought a Cayenne", "annotation_id": "26113372", "url": "https://genius.com/26113372", "state": "pending", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
