{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "HeliMAn", "line": "Bend after bend, I can’t sleep", "vault_lines": ["Bend after bend, I can't sleep (Bend after bend)"], "meaning": "bend after bend can translate to getting High after getting high which can lead to less sleep or little to no sleep if you go back to his afterlyfe  album he’s being using the term bend all the way to bad bend which is probably when he gets High and goes out to get violent. in the song bad bend it’s also named demon so yea sum connection demon/violent/bad bend", "annotation_id": "33707655", "url": "https://genius.com/33707655", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "HeliMAn", "line": "Bag after bag, on the week (Yeah) Bend after bend, I can’t sleep (Bend after bend)", "vault_lines": ["Bag after bag, on the week (Yeah)"], "meaning": "In these lines, Yeat is likely referring to his relentless hustle and work ethic. “Bag after bag, on the week” suggests that he’s consistently making money, possibly through various endeavors or business opportunities. “Bend after bend, I can’t sleep” could imply that he’s constantly on the move or engaged in activities related to his success, to the point where it affects his ability to rest or relax. Overall, these lines convey his dedication to grinding and staying active in pursuit of his goals.\n\nBend is a reference to his mentioning of “bad bends”, which are negative psychological effects caused by the intoxication of drugs such as ecstasy pills and promethazine (lean).", "annotation_id": "31810152", "url": "https://genius.com/31810152", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
