{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Heavy stunts", "line": "And I won’t talk ‘em, I’m goin’ bray’, I’m goin’ cray’", "vault_lines": ["And I won't talk 'em, I'm goin' bray', I'm goin' cray'"], "meaning": "Dispute over whether he says i’m going bray or brick.\n\nIf he is saying bray (brazy), the definition is obvious\n\nHowever, if you hear “I’m goin’ brick”, basically he’s saying he’s  going hard. A reference to the term “bricked up” and to the simple fact that a brick is hard. Yeat goin hard and he goin crazy.", "annotation_id": "31623516", "url": "https://genius.com/31623516", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
