{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Hatër", "line": "I’m a fire guy, walked inside the building with some grease, I’m serving Five Guys (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["I'm a fire guy, walked inside the building with some grease, I'm serving Five Guys (Woo)"], "meaning": "In this line, Yeat is admitting to giving someone a hard time.\n\n“Grease” is a slang term for being an annoyance; If someone is giving you grease, they are making things unpleasant and difficult for you.\n\nThe use of the word “grease” is also directly related to mentioning the American fast-food chain “Five Guys”. Five Guys sell burgers which are cooked in grease.", "annotation_id": "26570707", "url": "https://genius.com/26570707", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
