{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "HEARD OF MË", "line": "Wanna see you fall, yeah, I’m coming for your heart", "vault_lines": ["Wanna see you fall, yeah, I'm coming for your heart"], "meaning": "This verse is a callback to his 2093 album. In some shape or form, Yeat sneaks in the “I wanna see you fall” on his songs on the 2093 album.\n\nYeat specifically is saying this to the Psycho CEO\nA tiktoker by the name of “vrysad”\nposts videos on such things after realizing that Yeat will make his voice higher or deeper depending on the alter ego he uses. The deeper voice on the 2093 album was the Psycho CEO\n\n\n\nDm me if you want to know more about Yeat Lore", "annotation_id": "33542913", "url": "https://genius.com/33542913", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "HEARD OF MË", "line": "Geek up like a God", "vault_lines": ["Yeah (Woo), huh (No), geek up like a God"], "meaning": "“geeked up” means to be under the influence. Yeat is describing a state of intense euphoria or being extremely high, likening it to the elevated status of a god. This comparison emphasizes how untouchable and elevated he feels, showing a sense of confidence and invincibility.", "annotation_id": "33448996", "url": "https://genius.com/33448996", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "HEARD OF MË", "line": "Even though it’s the night, I can see in the dark (Woo-ooh-ooh) You like all these lights, you say diamonds an art", "vault_lines": ["Even though it's the night, I can see in the dark (Woo-ooh-ooh)"], "meaning": "This album has many mentions of diamonds and lights. Yeat is not only bragging about his lavish & flashy lifestyle, he wants to show that he is in control of it.\n\nYeat claims that the way he arranges his diamonds/jewelry can be seen as a form of art. His ability to “see in the dark,” is just a way to flex how shiny and perfect his diamonds are, creating light for him to see even at night time.", "annotation_id": "33436270", "url": "https://genius.com/33436270", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "HEARD OF MË", "line": "Yeah, that money, power, respect, it’s what I needed, eh", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, that money, power, respect, it's what I needed, eh"], "meaning": "Follow up to Future & Metro Boomin ft. Kendrick Lamar – Like that\n“D-O-T, the money, power, respect\nThe last one is better”\nhttps://youtu.be/N9bKBAA22Go?si=ESFdWnVKGjg8ZAvv", "annotation_id": "33351018", "url": "https://genius.com/33351018", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "HEARD OF MË", "line": "This got them scratchin’ they heads like I keyed it", "vault_lines": ["This got them scratchin' they heads like I keyed it"], "meaning": "Yeat compares the confusion he causes to the reaction someone would have if their car was keyed, leaving them puzzled and frustrated.", "annotation_id": "33323170", "url": "https://genius.com/33323170", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "HEARD OF MË", "line": "Bands on the call (Woo), Benz on the car (Woo-ooh-ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Bands on the call (Woo), Benz on the car (Woo-ooh-ooh)"], "meaning": "Mercedes Benz, a French Luxury Automotive brand. Yeat is saying here that he has a Mercedes, which he is likely referring to his Maybach and GLE, which he has mentioned previously in other songs.", "annotation_id": "33323164", "url": "https://genius.com/33323164", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "HEARD OF MË", "line": "Maybe I’m just too real for all this shit, you know I bleed it", "vault_lines": ["Maybe I'm just too real for all this shit, you know I bleed it"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that his authenticity might be too much for others to handle, emphasizing that he truly lives what he raps about.", "annotation_id": "33323163", "url": "https://genius.com/33323163", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "HEARD OF MË", "line": "Diamonds on my body, when I walk through the city, lights on me", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds on my body, when I walk through the city, lights on me"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying here that he has diamonds on his body (likely his wrists and his neck) and that when he walks through a city, ‘lights’ are on him, likely referring to smartphone flashlights (fans recording)", "annotation_id": "33323159", "url": "https://genius.com/33323159", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
