{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "H.A.B", "line": "Foo-ey", "vault_lines": ["High as a bitch, I'm high as a kite, oh (Skrrt)"], "meaning": "“foo-ey” is another example of Yeat’s unique lyrical lingo, and is among other words like “twizzy” and “luh chonka”.\n\nThe term “foo-ey” is used to state that his opp’s “drip” is counterfeit, and that the opps want to be like Yeat.", "annotation_id": "30952476", "url": "https://genius.com/30952476", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
