{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "In the club, this bitch ride on me, I’m a rail (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["In the club, this bitch ride on me, I'm a rail (Yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "In this line, Yeat compares himself to a rail, and explains that in the club, a woman rides on his penis.", "annotation_id": "28705469", "url": "https://genius.com/28705469", "state": "pending", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "I really just want a Percocet, I’m finna get pissy (Ooh, yeah, pissy)", "vault_lines": ["I really just want a Percocet, I'm finna get pissy"], "meaning": "Yeat explains how, without his percocets he will get angry. This is possibly due to his addiction withdrawals to percs.", "annotation_id": "28485193", "url": "https://genius.com/28485193", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "They can’t even tell the real from the fake, I wish ’em well (Say)", "vault_lines": ["They can't even tell the real from the fake, I wish 'em well (Say)"], "meaning": "If someone has terminal disease, or something else threatening their life, someone may “wish them well”. In drug dealing, many manufacturers mix their drugs with the lethal fentanyl to make the production process cheaper and make the drugs stronger. If someone cannot tell real drugs from the fake (fentanyl) Yeat will wish them well as fentanyl can be deadly.", "annotation_id": "27267155", "url": "https://genius.com/27267155", "state": "pending", "votes": -4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "Yeah, pull up now, we finna get busy, yeah, yeah (Ayy, ayy, ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, pull up now, we finna get busy, yeah, yeah (Ayy, ayy, ayy)"], "meaning": "Unfortunately, “Get Busy” is too ambiguous to discern precisely. It could mean he wants a woman to pull up and to inseminate. Alternatively, he could be beckoning his squadron to produce banger compositions such as this.\n\nIn the following lines, he speaks of a “bitch” who wants white inside her nose and drinking children, maybe evidencing the former interpretation.", "annotation_id": "26518801", "url": "https://genius.com/26518801", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "I really just want a Percocet, I’m finna get pissy", "vault_lines": ["I really just want a Percocet, I'm finna get pissy"], "meaning": "this is referring to opioid withdrawals, often causing someone to be pissed off", "annotation_id": "26160602", "url": "https://genius.com/26160602", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "Pull up, who that is? (Errt, errt)", "vault_lines": ["Pull up, who that is? (Errt, errt)"], "meaning": "People hear his loud vehicle when he pulls up to a function.", "annotation_id": "25295767", "url": "https://genius.com/25295767", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "I’m on this Perc’, it got me stupid, I’m a snail (Bitch, I’m stuck)", "vault_lines": ["I'm on this Perc', it got me stupid, I'm a snail (Bitch, I'm stuck)"], "meaning": "A snail moves at the approximate rate of 0.03 miles per hour. To give some scale for reference, a car usually travels at around 70 miles per hour when on a freeway. That is quite the discrepancy. In this specific line, Yeat mentions that being on a “Perc” has made him mentally incapacitated, or in other words unintelligent, and for this reason his brain is working at a slower rate than normal. On top of that, Percocets are also depressants, so Yeat would be physically much slower in his motor control due to the mentioned opioid. Quite a clever double entendre utilized by Noah Smith to implicate how the given Percocet has manipulated his mood.\n\nA picture of a (slow-moving) snail:\n\n\n\nA picture of Percocets:\n\n\n\nA picture of Noah Oliver Smith:\nhttps://images.complex.com/complex/images/c_crop,h_2701,w_3006,x_117,y_900/c_fill,dpr_auto,f_auto,q_auto,w_1400/fl_lossy,pg_1/ciigcrhunll6bwxqaptv/yeat-what-you-need-to-know?fimg-client-default", "annotation_id": "24922679", "url": "https://genius.com/24922679", "state": "pending", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "Yeah, brought a dub inside Chanel, I’m finna go crazy (Ooh, ooh, ooh, yeah, crazy)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, brought a dub inside Chanel, I'm finna go crazy (Ooh, ooh, ooh, yeah, crazy)"], "meaning": "A “dub” is $20,000.", "annotation_id": "24640114", "url": "https://genius.com/24640114", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "Bitch want white inside her nose, finna get Lizzy (Yeah, finna call Lizzy)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch want white inside her nose, finna get Lizzy (Yeah, finna call Lizzy)"], "meaning": "“White” refers to cocaine; “Lizzy” refers to Lizzie McGuire, a white girl. “White girl” is a slang term for cocaine.", "annotation_id": "24633168", "url": "https://genius.com/24633168", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "Got surround sound inside this tizzy (Whew)", "vault_lines": ["Got surround sound inside this tizzy (Whew)"], "meaning": "“Tizzy,” short for “Tonka,” refers to a vehicle.", "annotation_id": "24474631", "url": "https://genius.com/24474631", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "My bitch ’bout to pull up on me then drink my kids (Up, up)", "vault_lines": ["My bitch 'bout to pull up on me then drink my kids (Up, up)"], "meaning": "Yeat simplistically asserts that his “bitch,” a female sex partner, is going to perform oral sex on him until he climaxes, ejaculating in her mouth, causing her to swallow his “kids,” which is a slang term for semen.", "annotation_id": "23850558", "url": "https://genius.com/23850558", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "Yeah, how I was servin’ chickens, huh, in the mail", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, how I was servin' chickens, huh, in the mail"], "meaning": "Yeat asserts that, before achieving success as a rapper, he was shipping “chickens,” slang for cocaine, across the United States, using its postage system.", "annotation_id": "23847895", "url": "https://genius.com/23847895", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "I, I got Tose’ on the way, finna get dizzy (Tose’, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I, I got Tose' on the way, finna get dizzy (Tose', yeah)"], "meaning": "“Tose” is short for Toseína, a common cough syrup often used in making lean.", "annotation_id": "23847873", "url": "https://genius.com/23847873", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "We not books to read, we not Cat in the Hat, no ​Sam-I-Am (Told him, go) I cook that lil’ shit up, Green Eggs and Ham (Told him, go)", "vault_lines": ["We not books to read, we not Cat in the Hat, no ​Sam-I-Am (Told him, go)"], "meaning": "Yeat references the well-known children’s books The Cat in the Hat and Green Eggs and Ham by Dr. Seuss.\n\nYeat explains that, unlike a children’s book, he is not easily read, and his personality is very unpredictable. When he warns that he will “cook that lil' shit up, Green Eggs and Ham”, it’s a double entendre; “cook” metaphorically states that he will shoot anyone that messes with him, but also refers to the more common use as in “cooking” food, or making literal green eggs and ham.", "annotation_id": "23844313", "url": "https://genius.com/23844313", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "Yeah, how you want the double C but no Chanel? (Yeah, what the fuck?)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, how you want the double C but no Chanel? (Yeah, what the fuck?)"], "meaning": "“Double C” has three potential meanings:\n\n\nFrench luxury brand Chanel’s iconic logo, which comprises two interlocked Cs\n\nCocaine, a recreational drug spelt with two Cs\nA double cup filled with lean\n\n\n\n\nThus, Yeat questions why a girl wants drugs, such as cocaine or lean, instead of items from Chanel.\n\n\n\nChanel trainers featuring the brand’s iconic logo", "annotation_id": "23843383", "url": "https://genius.com/23843383", "state": "accepted", "votes": 78, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "I just poured an eight, I feel like Yams", "vault_lines": ["I just poured an eight, I feel like Yams"], "meaning": "A$AP Yams was the founder and leader of the A$AP Worldwide collective. One of the many things he was known for was his heavy lean consumption, which ultimately lead to his untimely death in January 2015.\n\nYeat is “pouring an eight”, or 8 oz. of promethazine with codeine, into his drink.", "annotation_id": "23841540", "url": "https://genius.com/23841540", "state": "accepted", "votes": 99, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gët Busy", "line": "Yeah, this song already was turnt, but here’s a bell (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, this song already was turnt, but here's a bell (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Many of Yeat’s recent viral songs, such as “Money Twërk” and “Mad bout that,” feature prominent bells in the instrumental. Yeat explained in an interview with Our Generation Music that he often adds the bells himself on top of instrumentals from other producers.\n\nThis line went viral before the song’s release, leading to “Gët Busy” becoming one of Yeat’s most popular songs before it was even released. This even ended up catching the attention of Drake, who quoted the line on his Instagram story.", "annotation_id": "23684503", "url": "https://genius.com/23684503", "state": "accepted", "votes": 295, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
