{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gëek high", "line": "7-Eleven", "vault_lines": ["I pour the 7-Eleven double cup of my drankie, yeah, drankie (I'm pourin' up this lean, uh)"], "meaning": "7-Eleven is the operator of the largest chain of small stores in 19 countries under Seven-Eleven Japan, operating primarily through franchising. It is the largest chain with 79,000 outlets, with major chains in Japan, the United States, Sweden, Mexico, Canada, the Philippines, Hong Kong, Taiwan, Malaysia and Thailand.\n\nInfo from Wiki", "annotation_id": "30590912", "url": "https://genius.com/30590912", "state": "pending", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gëek high", "line": "Put that pussy lil’ boy on a tee, turn him to a tattoo (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Put that pussy lil' boy on a tee, turn him to a tattoo (Yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "getting put on a t shirt or getting turned into a tattoo refers to how the dead is honored nowadays. ken is saying he’s going to be the reason you end up on a shirt, meaning he’s gonna kill you.", "annotation_id": "26617879", "url": "https://genius.com/26617879", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gëek high", "line": "First thing I did in the morning when I woke up, took a cranky, then I got to the junkie, yeah", "vault_lines": ["First thing I did in the morning when I woke up, took a cranky, then I got to the junkie, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat begins his day by taking a “cranky,” which is a slang term for a Percocet, a form of oxycodone medication used to treat pain.", "annotation_id": "26164996", "url": "https://genius.com/26164996", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gëek high", "line": "I just pulled up with a YFM hoodie and Issey Miyake the vest, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I just pulled up with a YFM hoodie and Issey Miyake the vest, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat strongly alludes to two pieces of designer clothing: a vintage Yohji Yamamoto “YFM” hoodie, and an Issey Miyake nylon tactical vest.\n\n\n\n\n\nYeat previously rapped about Issey Miyake on his August 2021 track “Fukit,” rapping:\n\nMix the Issey Miyake jeans with the Chrome Hearts, yeah\nI ain’t sad, just got a cold heart", "annotation_id": "25809185", "url": "https://genius.com/25809185", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gëek high", "line": "[Verse 2: Ken Carson]", "vault_lines": ["double cup of my drankie, yeah, drankie"], "meaning": "It is widely believed that Ken Carson’s verse was recorded using a Nintendo DS.\n\n\n\nPictured: Carson holding the Nintendo DS that he is believed to have used to record his verse for the song.", "annotation_id": "25809173", "url": "https://genius.com/25809173", "state": "pending", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Gëek high", "line": "I hit up Eliantte, I need diamond rings (Yeah, real geekers)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I hit up Eliantte, I need diamond rings (Yeah, real geekers)"], "meaning": "According to GQ Eliantte is “one of the go-to jewelers for rappers like Nicki Minaj, Migos, 21 Savage, Young Thug and many, many more.”", "annotation_id": "25761237", "url": "https://genius.com/25761237", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
