{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Griddlë", "line": "She move it, move it, move it (Move it, move it)", "vault_lines": ["She move it, move it, move it (Move it, move it)"], "meaning": "When Mr .Toliver says move it, move it, move it he is referring the the 2008 song by will. i. am “I like to move it” song", "annotation_id": "39153256", "url": "https://genius.com/39153256", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Griddlë", "line": "I’ma serve this shit out like this shit was a riddle", "vault_lines": ["They tryna 'stand what I'm sayin', lil' bitch, I'ma serve this shit out like this shit was a riddle"], "meaning": "Yeat compares his delivery to a riddle, implying that his lifestyle and lyrics aren’t meant to be immediately understood. This reflects his abstract style and also mirrors how chaotic experiences are often difficult to fully interpret.", "annotation_id": "39149180", "url": "https://genius.com/39149180", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Griddlë", "line": "I’m in love with the bitch, she a freak, geek show", "vault_lines": ["I'm in love with the bitch, she a freak, geek show"], "meaning": "Yeat redefines “love” as something purely physical and performative. By calling it a “geek show,” he reduces the relationship to spectacle and excess, suggesting that what he calls love is actually driven by drugs, lust, and entertainment rather than emotion.", "annotation_id": "39149160", "url": "https://genius.com/39149160", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
