{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Got rich", "line": "Got the blick on my side, keep it super tucked", "vault_lines": ["Got the blick on my side, keep it super tucked"], "meaning": "By ‘blick’ Yeat refers to a gun, most likely a pistol.", "annotation_id": "28482288", "url": "https://genius.com/28482288", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Got rich", "line": "I blew up like Osama, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I done got rich, yeah, bitch, I blew up like Osama, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat refers to an Arabic terrorist, Osama Bin Laden who is associated with the suicide bombings on the world trade center. Yeat also says he blew as in got popular.\n\n\nOsama", "annotation_id": "26461816", "url": "https://genius.com/26461816", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Got rich", "line": "I done got rich, yeah, the X got a whole lot stronger", "vault_lines": ["I done got rich, yeah, the X got a whole lot stronger"], "meaning": "X (Ecstacy) is a lot stronger if you have a lot of money", "annotation_id": "26457085", "url": "https://genius.com/26457085", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Got rich", "line": "I don’t like wasting time so much, my watches filled with ice", "vault_lines": ["I don't like wasting time so much, my watches filled with ice"], "meaning": "Yeat emphasizes that he does not like to waste his valuable time on mediocre things, implying that by becoming successful, you get to wear diamond-covered watches, but your time becomes more valuable than ever, therefore Yeat chooses to live a purposeful life instead.\n\n\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: He says, “I don’t like wasting time, so my watch is filled with ice,” meaning he values his time so much that he preserves it with “ice” – a slang reference to the diamonds in his watch.", "annotation_id": "25560642", "url": "https://genius.com/25560642", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Got rich", "line": "I would just ride around, GLE AMG 43, windows tinted", "vault_lines": ["I would just ride around, GLE AMG 43, windows tinted"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that he drives around in a Mercedes-Benz GLE 43 AMG, that also has the windows tinted. This is a very classy and luxurious car, costing upwards to $72,000.", "annotation_id": "24942208", "url": "https://genius.com/24942208", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Got rich", "line": "I just walk in YSL, yeah, and I bought me like five shoes", "vault_lines": ["I just walk in YSL, yeah, and I bought me like five shoes"], "meaning": "YSL, short for Yves Saint Laurent, is a French luxury fashion house. Yeat is claiming he walked into a YSL store and bought 5 different pairs of shoes. He’s essentially flexing his wealth.\n\nThe start of the album shows Yeat’s rise to fame and his humble beginnings. Although 5 shoes might not seem like much at first, for someone who only recently obtained wealth, it’s an important experience.", "annotation_id": "24942171", "url": "https://genius.com/24942171", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Got rich", "line": "I just pulled up in the Tonka", "vault_lines": ["I just pulled up in the Tonka"], "meaning": "Tonka is an American producer of toy trucks. The company is known for making steel toy models of construction-type trucks and machinery.\n\nHe’s saying he is pulling up while driving a wide-body vehicle.", "annotation_id": "24942153", "url": "https://genius.com/24942153", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Got rich", "line": "Not no quarantine, yeah, we outside, yeah, we outside", "vault_lines": ["Not no quarantine, yeah, we outside, yeah, we outside"], "meaning": "Refrencing the COVID-19 quarantine mandate, where the government suggested people to stay in their houses (not go outside) to lessen the spread of the disease. Basically, when he’s saying no quarantine, he means that he’s staying outside.", "annotation_id": "24487301", "url": "https://genius.com/24487301", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Got rich", "line": "I get cranky in the AM, need to Perky up", "vault_lines": ["I get cranky in the AM, need to Perky up"], "meaning": "Yeat is not a morning person. He takes the prescription painkiller, Percocet, to get rid of his grumpiness. Therefore he perks up, meaning to become cheerful, which sounds similar to the street name for Percocet, perc.", "annotation_id": "23950733", "url": "https://genius.com/23950733", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
