{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Good Day", "line": "I keep the shh on the bedside", "vault_lines": ["I keep the shh on the bedside"], "meaning": "Yeat says he keeps a “shh” on his bedside, which is a secluded way to say “gun”. He could also be saying this as a way to refer to his gun as having a silencer, hence it being quiet (shh). Yeat also says similar lines like this, like in his song “Diëd B4” when he says “Twizzy pull up with the shh shh, this shit ridiculous”.", "annotation_id": "39363199", "url": "https://genius.com/39363199", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
