{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Goin Back 2 Ella", "line": "Called up my wrists and told ’em I’m finna put a hundred thousand on ’em", "vault_lines": ["Called up my wrists and told 'em I'm finna put a hundred thousand on 'em"], "meaning": "He uses metaphor to explain that he will spend $100k+ on his wrists in either expensive watches or bracelets. Talking to inanimate objects, like his wrists, is a humorous way to say that and it shows more about his psyche, possibly because of his drug use.", "annotation_id": "40873839", "url": "https://genius.com/40873839", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Goin Back 2 Ella", "line": "I got a Rolls Royce umbrella", "vault_lines": ["I got a Rolls Royce umbrella"], "meaning": "All modern Rolls-Royce models come with a built-in courtesy umbrella. These umbrellas are cleverly concealed within a special compartment inside one of the vehicle’s front or rear doors; in this instance, Yeat is showing off an umbrella from this luxury brand following his acquisition of one", "annotation_id": "40407527", "url": "https://genius.com/40407527", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
