{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Goin Back 2 Ella", "line": "Bitch, I came out the beast like I’m in Belly", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I came out the beast like I'm in Belly"], "meaning": "This line is likely a reference to the 1998 movie “Belly,” which is a crime drama film directed by Hype Williams. The movie follows the lives of two friends, Tommy and Sincere, who are involved in various criminal activities, including drug dealing and violence.", "annotation_id": "29656453", "url": "https://genius.com/29656453", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Goin Back 2 Ella", "line": "Yeah, Maison Margiela that bitch, I went and put paint on her face", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, Maison Margiela that bitch, I went and put paint on her face"], "meaning": "Yeat is referencing Maison Margiela painted gats here, a popular sneaker. Maison Margiela also does paint splatter jeans/pants.", "annotation_id": "29292974", "url": "https://genius.com/29292974", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
