{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Give My Last", "line": "Yeah, Cactus Jack on my SBs, I feel like I was Faygo (SoFaygo)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, Cactus Jack on my SBs, I feel like I was Faygo (SoFaygo)"], "meaning": "Surf flexes his SB Dunk Lows, a promotional sneaker collaboration between Travis Scott and Nike Skateboarding released in February, 2021. Nike’s website describes the shoes:\n\nThe [sneaker’s] canvas tears away to reveal woodsy-style camo patterns that have been present in other Travis Scott Nike collabs. Rope-style laces run up to a thick tongue emblazoned with a label that nods to his burgeoning Cactus Jack label.\n\n\n\nCactus Jack is the record label established by Scott, whose branding can be found imprinted on his Nike collaborations.\n\nIn April, 2020, underground hip-hop artist SoFaygo became a signee to Cactus Jack Records after Travis had heard the rapper’s viral hits circulating online. Faygo—who like Surf, originates from Atlanta, Georgia—is known for his popular singles “Knock Knock” from 2020 and “Off the Map,” released the following year.", "annotation_id": "24007117", "url": "https://genius.com/24007117", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Give My Last", "line": "Fuck from the back, that’s a rack, that’s a rack", "vault_lines": ["Fuck from the back, that's a rack, that's a rack"], "meaning": "This line interpolates and directly quotes Lil Uzi Vert’s chorus on the April, 2019 single “That’s a Rack”:\n\nFuck from the back, hit her once, that’s a wrap (Let’s go)\nNo strings attached, that’s a rack, that’s a rack (Rack, rack)\nNo strings attached, that’s a rack, that’s a rack (Rack)\n\nThis callback to an earlier Uzi track is far from Surf’s first mention of the Philadelphia rapper in his music. In August, 2020, Surf name-dropped Uzi on the chorus to “Moody,” released as a part of Baddest Human (Deluxe).\n\nShe want to fuck one time, make a movie\nDiamonds gon' dance on me, Lil Uzi\nMy bitch bad, nah-nah, she a beauty\n\nIn late November, 2020, Surf released “LIKE UZI SAID,” arguably Surf’s most prominent nod to Uzi’s likeness. On the song, Surf raps:\n\nLike Uzi said, “Why you keep callin'?”\nI blew her back ‘cause a young nigga ballin’\nI’m at the top, ain’t no way that I’m fallin'\nI gave you all of myself ‘cause I’m all in\n\nThe quoted line referencing Vert’s “20 Min,” released late 2017.", "annotation_id": "23898576", "url": "https://genius.com/23898576", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Give My Last", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Surf-give-my-last-lyrics", "genius_title": "Give My Last", "genius_id": 7078322, "source": "api"}
