{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "Got a bad lil’ bitch, she got a hobby And I like that ’cause I don’t gotta take no time away from it", "vault_lines": ["Got a bad lil' bitch, she got a hobby"], "meaning": "Yeat says how he likes his girl’s attitude because she has her own stuff to deal with, and she’s not dependent on a man for most of her time.\n\nThis is also a pattern as Yeat says in a previous bar, “I don’t got time for mistakes or to be fuckin' up, so I’m sendin' you off in a different way”\n\nShowing that he dislikes girls that have nothing going on and are always annoying him, instead of serving a purpose.", "annotation_id": "37083763", "url": "https://genius.com/37083763", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "All of the money and fame put aside, man, my family gon’ stay the same, yeah, that’s gon’ never change", "vault_lines": ["It's no more coming down, yeah"], "meaning": "Money changes, people change.\n\nYeat is putting his real friends and his family first over everything, no matter what, all the way till death.", "annotation_id": "37083761", "url": "https://genius.com/37083761", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "All of the money and fame put aside, man, my family gon’ stay the same, yeah, that’s gon’ never change", "vault_lines": ["It's no more coming down, yeah"], "meaning": "Money changes, people change.\n\nYeat is putting his real friends and his family first over everything, no matter what, all the way till death.", "annotation_id": "37083751", "url": "https://genius.com/37083751", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "I don’t got time for mistakes or to be fuckin’ up, so I’m sendin’ you off in a different way", "vault_lines": ["It's no more coming down, yeah"], "meaning": "Having a significant other can lead to failures within the relationship, and distractions outside it. Here, Yeat says that he has to let go of a woman because he can’t be making simple mistakes like that, due to another person’s imperfection.", "annotation_id": "37083728", "url": "https://genius.com/37083728", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "24/7/11 poppin’ Perkies, baby, I know it", "vault_lines": ["24/7/11 poppin' Perkies, baby, I know it"], "meaning": "24/7 – all day, every day\n7/11 – the store\n\nPerkies: percocet", "annotation_id": "36627066", "url": "https://genius.com/36627066", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "I told my twizzy let’s go hit Ferrari", "vault_lines": ["I told my twizzy let's go hit Ferrari"], "meaning": "“Twizzy” is slang for “close friend”. Yeat is saying that he told his friend to go to the Ferrari dealership with him.", "annotation_id": "36627060", "url": "https://genius.com/36627060", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "I’m on this plane every day, so it’s showin’ you, baby, I’m higher than you in a different way", "vault_lines": ["It's no more coming down, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat packs two doubles in one bar. “Plane” is both the literal aircraft he’s on daily while on tour and a higher plane of existence. “Higher” works the same way — he’s above everyone in status and mindset, with the obvious nod to being high. Basically, he’s high in every way.", "annotation_id": "36583758", "url": "https://genius.com/36583758", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "I’m on this plane every day, so it’s showin’ you, baby, I’m higher than you in a different way", "vault_lines": ["It's no more coming down, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat is bragging about flying on a private jet every day while also making a wordplay reference to being high on drugs.", "annotation_id": "36581955", "url": "https://genius.com/36581955", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "King Tonka, King Tonka (What?) Tell me like King Tonka, King Tonka Can you please, King Tonka, King Tonka? (What you want?) Can you please, King Tonka, King Tonka? Can you? No", "vault_lines": ["King Tonka, King Tonka (What?)"], "meaning": "Here, Yeat expresses burnout from constant demands and expectations placed on him by fans, the industry or people around him repeatedly calling on him to perform, provide or deliver.\n\n“King Tonka” represents one of Yeat’s high-life personas, and the repetition mimics the overwhelming noise and pressure tied to that identity. By ending with “Can you? No,” Yeat subtly rejects the expectations attached to the persona.\n\nThis moment reinforces the song’s larger narrative about personal growth and moving on, whether from past personas, relationships or even the sound that defined his earlier career.", "annotation_id": "36469067", "url": "https://genius.com/36469067", "state": "pending", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "[Intro]", "vault_lines": ["It's no more coming down, yeah"], "meaning": "Possible Inspiration from “DAISIES” by Justin Bieber", "annotation_id": "36458025", "url": "https://genius.com/36458025", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "Yeah, it’s called growing pains Yeah, it’s called growing pains Once you outgrow them all We call that shit growing pains", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, it's called growing pains"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that evolving beyond limitations or leaving behind what no longer serves you, including relationships, can feel bittersweet, regretful, or painful as you move forward and leave things behind.", "annotation_id": "36441934", "url": "https://genius.com/36441934", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "Yeah, it’s called growing pains Yeah, it’s called growing pains Once you outgrow them all We call that shit growing pains", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, it's called growing pains"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that evolving beyond limitations or leaving behind what no longer serves you, including relationships, can feel bittersweet, regretful, or painful as you move forward and leave things behind.", "annotation_id": "36441924", "url": "https://genius.com/36441924", "state": "pending", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "I was the kid, now I’m the man", "vault_lines": ["I was the kid, now I'm the man"], "meaning": "In previous songs, Yeat has referenced in lyrics how ‘they doubted the kid’ or ‘didn’t believe in the kid’. Here, ‘the kid’ represents his younger self who was underestimated, constantly doubted and not taken as seriously. Yeat recognises his transformation, acknowledging his growth and evolution as an artist. Now undoubtedly a respected and established member in the rap music industry.", "annotation_id": "36441204", "url": "https://genius.com/36441204", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GROWING PAINS", "line": "It’s no more coming down, yeah It’s so much falling down", "vault_lines": ["It's no more coming down, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat knows he is not gonna fall off, planning to only go higher than he is in the rap scene at this moment.\nComing down may also depict the unpleasant worn out effect after using drugs, stating that he will be in a constant state of high\nThis could also mean that he believes that his next album, “A DANGEROUS LYFE”, which’s name he’s got tatted on his back, will be his best project he’s gonna release.", "annotation_id": "36438197", "url": "https://genius.com/36438197", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
