{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GONË", "line": "Yeah, uh, call you “Thin slice” ’cause your bread thin", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, uh, call you \"Thin slice\" 'cause your bread thin"], "meaning": "Correct Lyrics say “Call me thin slice is your bread thin?”\n\n“Thin bread” is a saying meaning a low amount of money as the slang term “bread” is used to refer to money. What he means by “call me thin slice” is someone is saying Yeat has “thin bread” as bread is sliced and a thin slice of bread would mean a low amount of money.", "annotation_id": "32270626", "url": "https://genius.com/32270626", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
