{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GONE 4 A MIN", "line": "I don’t meet in the middle, don’t do no borderline (Ah)", "vault_lines": ["I don't meet in the middle, don't do no borderline (Ah)"], "meaning": "This is a throwback to Yeat’s old and debut songs that came before the Alive album. One of the songs was RolEy DÆ 2 in which he says,“Talk to my demon no its no more switching sides.” Yeat is saying their is no more middle ground for him", "annotation_id": "33692141", "url": "https://genius.com/33692141", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GONE 4 A MIN", "line": "And they gon’ get swept under the rug every time (Ooh, woo)", "vault_lines": ["And they gon' get swept under the rug every time (Ooh, woo)"], "meaning": "This refers likley to his haters, or any other type of person he may be talking about, falling up short in life when compared to him.", "annotation_id": "33531326", "url": "https://genius.com/33531326", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GONE 4 A MIN", "line": "Let’s slow down for a minute (What’s the rush?) Get real for a minute with me Maybe I’m bad for myself (Ooh, ooh) Maybe I’m bad for myself (Yeah) Every time we take a picture (Ooh, ooh) Gettin’ high and drunk, the perfect mixture", "vault_lines": ["Let's slow down for a minute (What's the rush?)"], "meaning": "YEAT is saying he needs to take some time to think realistically and acknowledge the fact that his habit of doing drugs is harming him.", "annotation_id": "33442109", "url": "https://genius.com/33442109", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GONE 4 A MIN", "line": "We crushin’ they dreams like a we gon’ snort a line", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we crushin' they dreams like a we gon' snort a line"], "meaning": "Yeat crushes dreams to the extent that they can snorted, like cocaine.\n\nThis could also refrence the anticipation of an album with the same sound as 2093 with Yeat crushing that hope with LYFESTYLE, which is a return to his pre sobriety style of music, along with being the latest entry to his “LYFE” series of albums.\n\nIn powder form, cocaine needs to have very small particles, so it can be snorted easily. This involves “crushing” or grinding any lumps in the powder to get a smoother texture.\n\nyeat is back on drugs 😔😞", "annotation_id": "33418834", "url": "https://genius.com/33418834", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GONE 4 A MIN", "line": "Fuck it, throw me another cup (Woo, ooh) ‘Cause it ain’t gon’ get colder when it’s over", "vault_lines": ["Fuck it, throw me another cup (Woo, ooh)"], "meaning": "Yeat is so addicted to drugs it no longer matters for him if he takes them or not. “‘Cause it ain’t gon’ get colder when it’s over” is a metaphor in which he says that when he dies – he can’t feel worse than state he is right now. It is propably about the irreversible effects of long-term drug abuse", "annotation_id": "33416270", "url": "https://genius.com/33416270", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GONE 4 A MIN", "line": "I’m on that heli-time", "vault_lines": ["Always flyin' so you know I'm on that heli-time"], "meaning": "This might be a small reference to SoundCloud exclusive track Heliman", "annotation_id": "33410651", "url": "https://genius.com/33410651", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GONE 4 A MIN", "line": "Way too rich", "vault_lines": ["They done fucked up, they done got me way too rich"], "meaning": "Cut lyfestyle song called “way2rich” reference\n\nhttps://youtu.be/xaFctQSCsus?si=tC54V52jqXiwLK9z", "annotation_id": "33349328", "url": "https://genius.com/33349328", "state": "pending", "votes": -11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GONE 4 A MIN", "line": "Yeah, high all the time Why she like, “Why you always high all the time?” Uh, damn it I be out my mind in this shit, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Yеah, high all the time"], "meaning": "Yeat is known to have a long relationship with drugs, and after his newfound sobriety from 2093, he seems to be back on (at least some) drugs; and it’s clearly a conflict he has.", "annotation_id": "33327494", "url": "https://genius.com/33327494", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GONE 4 A MIN", "line": "I’m a geekster, baby, I do this all the time (Ooh) Yeah, we gon’ do it all the time, all the time (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["I'm a geekster, baby, I do this all the time (Ooh)"], "meaning": "Yeat is using “geekster” to refer to getting high, indicating that it’s a regular part of his lyfestyle. By saying he does this all the time, he’s showing how frequently he engages in this activity. This repetition focuses on his commitment to this lyfestyle and how it’s a consistent part of his daily routine.", "annotation_id": "33325059", "url": "https://genius.com/33325059", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GONE 4 A MIN", "line": "Why you rushin’? Why you rushin’? (Ru-ru-ru-shi-shi-shin’) [Break] Ah, ooh, ooh, ooh Been away for a minute now Know you felt that (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Why you rushin'? Why you rushin'? (Ru-ru-ru-shi-shi-shin')"], "meaning": "The first lines of the verse allude to Yeat and a partner who is expressing sexual impatience, made most apparent where Yeat says he “knows” she “felt” how he’s “been away for a minue”. The lines about drug use, breathing/heart rate, and taking it slow hint at a dynamic in which Yeat is trying to enjoy his time after time away from his partner.", "annotation_id": "33324755", "url": "https://genius.com/33324755", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
