{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GODAMNIT", "line": "You say ”It’s a problem”, where your MAC then?", "vault_lines": ["You say \"It's a problem\", where your MAC then?"], "meaning": "In this scenario, the “problem” in question refers to a street fight, or possible beef. Yeat asks where the person’s “MAC” is at, referencing a MAC-10, or MAC-11, a weapon of high machinery and strong artillery.   It also plays on the Apple Mac (MacBook or iMac). Given that many modern rappers record and “mix” their own problems (or tracks) on computers, he is mocking the opponent for being more of a “studio gangster” than a real threat.", "annotation_id": "39467092", "url": "https://genius.com/39467092", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
