{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GOD TALKIN SHHH", "line": "No, we not no quarterbacks at all, but we gon’ punt through (Awoo)", "vault_lines": ["No, we not no quarterbacks at all, but we gon' punt through (Awoo)"], "meaning": "After falling to move the ball up the field three times consecutively, Quarterbacks will  occasionally punt the football down field. This is done to hopefully maximize the distance for the opposing team to prevent them from scoring.", "annotation_id": "34477105", "url": "https://genius.com/34477105", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GOD TALKIN SHHH", "line": "They see I know ’bout turbans, 737 don’t ban me", "vault_lines": ["They see I know 'bout turbans, 737 don't ban me"], "meaning": "Yeat frequently refers to turbans in his songs and has been seen wearing various designer scarves, sometimes in the style of how keffiyehs are worn. (Keffiyehs are also used to be wrapped into a turban.)\n\nYeat says “…737 don’t ban me” because the wearing of turbans and keffiyehs is sometimes associated with Middle-Eastern terrorist groups like Al-Qaeda, who are responsible for the 9/11 attacks where they used planes similar to the Boeing 737 Yeat mentions.", "annotation_id": "34423942", "url": "https://genius.com/34423942", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GOD TALKIN SHHH", "line": "(Huh, yeah, yeah, hol’ up) Hold your thought, shut the fuck up while I’m thinking", "vault_lines": ["(Huh, yeah, yeah, hol' up) Hold your thought, shut the fuck up while I'm thinking"], "meaning": "Yeat doesn’t want you to express your opinion while he is thinking", "annotation_id": "34072999", "url": "https://genius.com/34072999", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GOD TALKIN SHHH", "line": "Taliban my head like a shaman, like a monk, yeah (Awoo)", "vault_lines": ["Taliban my head like a shaman, like a monk, yeah (Awoo)"], "meaning": "Yeat shows he is still attached to his old self as he used to always rock a turban on his head that he also made two songs about “Taliban” in the album “2 Alivë” and “Turban” in the album “Up 2 Më”.", "annotation_id": "34072982", "url": "https://genius.com/34072982", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GOD TALKIN SHHH", "line": "A lot of brothers ain’t have my back I’on feel a way, I cut them off easy Yeah, I take that slice, I take that shit cheesy", "vault_lines": ["A lot of brothers ain't have my back"], "meaning": "In these three lines Yeat almost clearly speaks about how he cut off Septembersrich after he betrayed Yeat behind his back.", "annotation_id": "34072974", "url": "https://genius.com/34072974", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
