{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "Swerve, swerve, I take the Lamb’ out of here", "vault_lines": ["Swerve, swerve, I take the Lamb' out of here"], "meaning": "“taking the Lamb' out of here” refers to driving away in his Lamborghini Urus. (Which he mentions in many songs.) This showcases his flashy lyfestyle.", "annotation_id": "33450650", "url": "https://genius.com/33450650", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "Toot up the Maybach truck, this bitch got hydraulics", "vault_lines": ["Toot up the Maybach truck, this bitch got hydraulics"], "meaning": "Maybach is a subdivision of Mercedes-Benz, a luxury car company. The Maybach ofter refers to sedans, SUVs, and 4-runners.\n\nHydraulics are on typically every car, but some are better than others. A good hydraulics system makes a car ride much smoother over rough terrain and roads, so Summrs is alluding to his car riding smoothly no matter what, befitting someone of his wealth.", "annotation_id": "33442191", "url": "https://genius.com/33442191", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "I still rock Alyx with the buckle, take off my belt and whoop ’em (Hahaha)", "vault_lines": ["I still rock Alyx with the buckle, take off my belt and whoop 'em (Hahaha)"], "meaning": "Summrs is referring to 1017 ALYX 9SM a high end designer clothing brand which is famously known for their rollercoaster belt buckles & hardware which are made with various metals.\n( It’s going to hurt when you get hit by his belt. )", "annotation_id": "33424132", "url": "https://genius.com/33424132", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "Stand over you then I bust you", "vault_lines": ["Stand over you then I bust you"], "meaning": "Summrs is saying how he will stand on top of his opposition and bust him. Meaning he will shoot the enemy.", "annotation_id": "33389388", "url": "https://genius.com/33389388", "state": "accepted", "votes": -6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "Beat her cat from the back, I’m loving this bitch arch, yeah, huh", "vault_lines": ["Beat her cat from the back, I'm loving this bitch arch, yeah, huh"], "meaning": "The term “cat” is a clean term for “pussy”. And arching is caused when a female and male are having anal intercourse, in this line, Summrs is saying how when he’s indulging in anal sex with his girlfriend, he likes the way she arches her back as she’s taking in the load.", "annotation_id": "33389367", "url": "https://genius.com/33389367", "state": "accepted", "votes": -9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "Go ’head, bust your diamonds, you can get like me Go ’head, bust your style, go ’head, steal my jeans", "vault_lines": ["Go 'head, bust your head, diamond, diamond"], "meaning": "This is a play on the word “genes”. “Jeans” represent his literal style being stolen while “genes” represents his personality being replicated and imitated.", "annotation_id": "33366135", "url": "https://genius.com/33366135", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "Tryna catch his ass at the show, okay, we booked ’em (Okay, uh)", "vault_lines": ["Tryna catch his ass at the show, okay, we booked 'em (Okay, uh)"], "meaning": "This is likely a reference to Opium’s Homixide Gang whom Summrs fought on stage during their tour. Yeat also took Summrs’s side after the release of Lyfestyle on Instagram posting with the caption “IstyleUstyleWestyle”. This is mocking HXG’s last album “I5U5WE5” and marks as Yeat’s first public response to the long brewing rumored Opium beef.", "annotation_id": "33366064", "url": "https://genius.com/33366064", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "Told ’em to pack like a Russian (Woah, woah, woah, woah)", "vault_lines": ["Told 'em to pack like a Russian (Woah, woah, woah, woah)"], "meaning": "People thought that this line may refer to Russo-Ukrainian war. Summrs could say that he pack the bodies of Ukrainians in the bags, like he is Russian, or – he puts the bodies of Russians. The meaning of the line depends on which side he supports in the conflict, which we don’t know.\n\nBut on of the Russian fans asked Summrs about meaning of this line, and he said that he mean flavor of Backwoods “Russian Cream”", "annotation_id": "33332471", "url": "https://genius.com/33332471", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "Guns hot like the Suns (Woah), D. Book ’em (Woah, woah, woah)", "vault_lines": ["Guns hot like the Suns (Woah), D. Book 'em (Woah, woah, woah)"], "meaning": "Summrs is referring to infamous basketball Devin Booker in this line who is known to have played for the Phoenix Suns all throughout his basketball career.\n\n\n\nSummrs makes a bar out of the team’s name being the Suns referring to his guns being as hot as the heat of the sun.", "annotation_id": "33328154", "url": "https://genius.com/33328154", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "Robin", "vault_lines": ["Go 'head, bust your head, diamond, diamond"], "meaning": "This tag belongs to Canadian producer and A&R, Yung Robin. He’s known for his production work with iayze and glaive.\n\nThis marks Yung Robin’s first appearance with Yeat and collaborator, Summrs.", "annotation_id": "33327165", "url": "https://genius.com/33327165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "In the night, when we demons, yeah, we lurk (Woo-ooh)", "vault_lines": ["In the night, when we demons, yeah, we lurk (Woo-ooh)"], "meaning": "Yeat is using the imagery of “demons” to give a sense of danger and mystery, suggesting that he and his crew are possibly engaging in risky or rebellious behavior during the night while being stealthy and on lookout.", "annotation_id": "33324663", "url": "https://genius.com/33324663", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "Yeah, go ‘head, be a meme, they gon’ forget about you, yeah I’m the real King Yeat, wan’ speak? Go get a voucher", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, go 'hеad, be a meme, thеy gon' forget about you, yeah"], "meaning": "On May 31st Ian released his debut album “Valedictorian,” the album cover being based off a meme. Ian is also known for taking the own style of Playboi Carti & Yeat and applying it to his music. Here Yeat is basically just saying that he’s the real King Yeat since online they call Ian a Yeat clone for ripping his style and flows. So this could be interpreted as a jab at Ian.", "annotation_id": "33321636", "url": "https://genius.com/33321636", "state": "pending", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GO2WORK", "line": "Replace her heart, I bought this lil’ bitch Chrome Heart", "vault_lines": ["Replace her heart, I bought this lil' bitch Chrome Heart"], "meaning": "“Chrome Hearts” is a fashion company, known for its iconic embroidering and is distinguished as a brand worn by individuals intending to show off their wealth and status.\n\n\n\nSummrs refers to both stealing his partner’s heart and replacing it with chrome and to providing his partner with luxurious garments such as Chrome Hearts.", "annotation_id": "33320460", "url": "https://genius.com/33320460", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
