{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": ", open wide, bitch (Uh)", "vault_lines": [", open wide, bitch (Uh)"], "meaning": "Y-Yessir!~~", "annotation_id": "38458599", "url": "https://genius.com/38458599", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "You get bread, or what? Worst off, yeah, we wanna see you worst off (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["You get bread, or what?"], "meaning": "“You get bread, or what?”\n“Get bread” is slang for making money. This line questions whether the other person actually earns money or is just pretending to be rich or successful.\n\n“Worst off, yeah, we wanna see you worst off (Yeah)”\nThis is a bold and aggressive line. It doesn’t just mean “we’re better than you.” It means “we actively want to see you doing badly.” It shows a desire not just to win, but to see others lose — a sign of hostility or dominance.\n\n“Are you mad? (Yes) Are you glad? (Yes)”\nThese questions seem sarcastic or rhetorical. The speaker is mocking the other person, suggesting they’re emotionally unstable, confused, or reacting strongly — possibly angry, jealous, or bitter. It’s a taunt, playing with their emotional reaction.", "annotation_id": "36159993", "url": "https://genius.com/36159993", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "I don’t hit the five, I hit the ten (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["I don't hit the five, I hit the ten (Woo)"], "meaning": "The homixide gang and opium are commonly knows as the “fives”. When yeat says this he means that he’s not only going for them, hes going for everyone associated with them.", "annotation_id": "35695846", "url": "https://genius.com/35695846", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "You hand us scissors, we cut you thin", "vault_lines": ["You hand us scissors, we cut you thin"], "meaning": "A menacing metaphor suggesting betrayal leads to punishment.", "annotation_id": "33961311", "url": "https://genius.com/33961311", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "Moon, compromise, I ain’t makin’ room (Eh)", "vault_lines": ["Moon, compromise, I ain't makin' room (Eh)"], "meaning": "For Yeat, this line symbolizes his refusal to compromise or share his success, likening his ambition to staking a solitary claim to the unattainable heights of the moon.", "annotation_id": "33961309", "url": "https://genius.com/33961309", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "How I fly high? ’Cause I’m ballin’, bitch (Ball)", "vault_lines": ["How I stand tall? 'Cause I'm ballin', bitch"], "meaning": "success and luxury are portrayed as the reasons for his elevated status.", "annotation_id": "33961302", "url": "https://genius.com/33961302", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "Why the fuck you fall? Hit ya arteries (Woo, woo)", "vault_lines": ["Why the fuck you fall? Hit ya arteries (Woo, woo)"], "meaning": "For Yeat, this line conveys his unflinching readiness to confront threats head-on, using violent imagery to assert his dominance and the high stakes of living in his world.", "annotation_id": "33961300", "url": "https://genius.com/33961300", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "Who you gon’ call? (Ha) Who you gon’ call? Police, huh? (Yeah, how the—)", "vault_lines": ["Who you gon' call? (Ha) Who you gon' call? Police, huh? (Yeah, how the—)"], "meaning": "Yeat mocks his enemies, insinuating that their only recourse is to involve authorities—a sign of weakness in his worldview.", "annotation_id": "33961296", "url": "https://genius.com/33961296", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "Trunk full of hunnids (Woo-woo) and some drugs, need some coke soon (Yeah, yeah-yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Trunk full of hunnids (Woo-woo) and some drugs, need some coke soon (Yeah, yeah-yeah)"], "meaning": "For Yeat, this line reflects the duality of his life, where immense wealth and success coexist with the chaos and dangers of fame’s indulgences.", "annotation_id": "33961294", "url": "https://genius.com/33961294", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "Worst off, yeah, we wanna see you worst off (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Worst off, yeah, we wanna see you worst off (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat displays an unapologetic edge, openly admitting that he thrives on seeing others fail—a nod to competitive aggression in his world.", "annotation_id": "33961286", "url": "https://genius.com/33961286", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "You get bread, or what?", "vault_lines": ["You get bread, or what?"], "meaning": "A direct challenge to others, asking if they’re truly making money. This speaks to Yeat’s obsession with material success and wealth.", "annotation_id": "33961281", "url": "https://genius.com/33961281", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "You ain’t compared to us (Not with us)", "vault_lines": ["You ain't compared to us (Not with us)"], "meaning": "Yeat establishes dominance, signaling that others are not on his level.", "annotation_id": "33961278", "url": "https://genius.com/33961278", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "Seen, seen ya’ flyin’ off so far", "vault_lines": ["Seen, seen ya' flyin' off so far"], "meaning": "This line could mean he’s seen someone he used to be close to moving on or distancing themselves. “Flyin' off so far” might suggest that the person is going in their own direction, possibly achieving things without him, or simply drifting apart.", "annotation_id": "33437643", "url": "https://genius.com/33437643", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
