{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "Purse’s name Chanel", "vault_lines": ["You ain't compared to us (Not with us)"], "meaning": "Chanel, a French luxury brand is mentioned here to imply that Yeat only buys luxury/rich clothing. He could be referring to buying the bag for Symone Ryley, his current girlfriend, and this is not the first time he has mentioned Chanel as previously mentioned in other songs such as Get Busy.", "annotation_id": "33322875", "url": "https://genius.com/33322875", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "It’s back to back geek mode, on time again", "vault_lines": ["It's back to back geek mode, on time again"], "meaning": "Yeat’s saying he’s constantly in “geek mode” which means he’s high. So, Yeat is saying he’s getting high back-to-back, and he’s doing it regularly.", "annotation_id": "33322652", "url": "https://genius.com/33322652", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "I don’t hit the five, I hit the ten (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["I don't hit the five, I hit the ten (Woo)"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying he’s aiming higher or achieving more than just the average “five”. It suggests striving for excellence or going beyond expectations.", "annotation_id": "33322600", "url": "https://genius.com/33322600", "state": "pending", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "We stay out Four Seasons, fuck the Wynn", "vault_lines": ["We stay out Four Seasons, fuck the Wynn"], "meaning": "Here, Yeat expresses his dislike for The Wynn, a hotel based in Las Vegas and his preference for the Four Seasons, hotel a more premium luxurious resort than The Wynn", "annotation_id": "33317587", "url": "https://genius.com/33317587", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "Three little piggies, we comin’ in, uh", "vault_lines": ["Three little piggies, we comin' in, uh"], "meaning": "Yeat is likening himself to the “Big Bad Wolf”, who in the story “Three Little Pigs”, destroys and enters the houses of two of the pigs.", "annotation_id": "33317550", "url": "https://genius.com/33317550", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "I see dead people in my head (Dead)", "vault_lines": ["I see dead people in my head (Dead)"], "meaning": "This line could be interpreted as Yeat experiencing hallucinations or visions of deceased individuals. It might suggest a mental struggle or trauma that causes these visions.", "annotation_id": "33242949", "url": "https://genius.com/33242949", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
