{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "Frog eye, bitch (Wha’?)", "vault_lines": ["Frog eye, bitch (Wha'?)"], "meaning": "“Frog eye” headlights are a specific style of car headlights where circular beams sit near the hood of the car, giving the vehicle the appearance of a frog with beady eyes\n\nYeat has also mentioned the term many times in his songs\n\nIn a frog-eyed Bentley, pull off on the feds, hol' up (Skrrt)", "annotation_id": "32559704", "url": "https://genius.com/32559704", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "Yeah (Woo), we could call the priest (Chop)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah (Woo), we could call the priest (Chop)"], "meaning": "Yeat could be saying that his inner circle could call the priest because of the actions happening like heavy use of drugs or some other unmentioned shenanigans.", "annotation_id": "32253627", "url": "https://genius.com/32253627", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "GEEK TIMË", "line": "You ain’t inside, we get ya trucked (Loo-ha-ha-ha) You ain’t on our side, we get you flocked, uh", "vault_lines": ["You ain't inside, we get ya trucked (Loo-ha-ha-ha)"], "meaning": "Noah Oliver Smith is asserting dominance and loyalty within his group. He warns that if someone is not part of his inner circle (“ain’t inside”), they will be forcefully excluded (“get ya chucked”). Additionally, if someone is merely on the side (“on side”), meaning they are not fully trusted or part of the inner group, they will face aggression or attack (“get you flocked”).", "annotation_id": "32253625", "url": "https://genius.com/32253625", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
