{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Fuck the cops", "line": "I guess that I’m the one with problems, I can’t keep a friend", "vault_lines": ["I guess that I'm the one with problems, I can't keep a friend"], "meaning": "Yeat is probably talking about his old friend septembersrich who used to be Yeat’s bro but apparently he switched up.", "annotation_id": "31392479", "url": "https://genius.com/31392479", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Fuck the cops", "line": "Go ahead and hang yourself, just like an ornament", "vault_lines": ["Go ahead and hang yourself, just like an ornament"], "meaning": "Ornaments are traditionally and decoratively held on Christmas trees around the time of December.\n\nWhen one wants to make another person that whom they are in conversation to have the urge to give in to suicidal tendencies, they may blurt out a harsh and abrupt insult as to ask for them to hang themselves, preferably by a noose.\n\nYeat, in this case, is asking for the listener or person that he is directing this insult forwards to kill themselves by hanging. Along with this, he tells them that he doesn’t give a fuck what the listener/intended person does and that they’ll cut off ties with them after such spoken insult for the greater good of his reputation and or career.\n\nAlong with seasonal depression, gloomy skies, and climate change lowering snow quantities, one might take into consideration Yeat’s unexpected words of hate due to emotional distress around the months of winter.\n\nThus, Yeat has no care or positive rebuttal in the matter as he has consistently spoken to the listener through his music to reevaluate their lives because of their financial status and inferiority, or end up “going out sad” alike many others who have lived on Earth;\n\nYour life a joke, you better grab you some rope (Huh)\n\nLyrics from the verse of Rav3 p4rty.\n\n\nNow you turned your back on me, don’t look at me like, “What’s the move?”\n‘Cause if you ask me, I’d tell you to put that gun to your mouth and press shoot (Bah, bah, bah)\nAnd at the end of the day I never been pressed about you (Bah, bah, bah)\n\nLyrics from the verse of Swërved it (4L).", "annotation_id": "30445410", "url": "https://genius.com/30445410", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
