{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Forëally / 4Ly", "line": "Glass, not no S.I., had to tell ’em that we is not friendly", "vault_lines": ["Glass, not no S.I., had to tell 'em that we is not friendly"], "meaning": "In this line, Yeat is showing his dislike for S.I diamonds once again as previously mentioned on other songs.\n\n\n\nThis time he calls them glass, no matter if they were actual diamond or not, showing he and his friends have no tolerance for the cheap option of diamonds, and they must be rated flawless.", "annotation_id": "34138937", "url": "https://genius.com/34138937", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
