{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flip", "line": "All my money blue, you would’ve thought it was Crip", "vault_lines": ["All my money blue, you would've thought it was Crip"], "meaning": "Yeat makes a clever reference to flex how much money he has. The Crips are an LA gang of which members commonly wear/represent the color blue, whether it be a bandana, clothes, or shoes. Yeat compares this color to his money, which happens to be blue because they are all $100 bills, which in America have a blue strip running vertically down the center.", "annotation_id": "24473507", "url": "https://genius.com/24473507", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
