{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flawlëss", "line": "Marry my bitch and I treat her like Marge", "vault_lines": ["Marry my bitch and I treat her like Marge"], "meaning": "Uzi’s girlfriend as of the song’s release is Florida artist JT, one half of the popular rap duo, City Girls.  Uzi plans to treat her the way Homer Simpson treats his wife, Marge, in the long running animated sitcom, The Simpsons. Notably, Homer’s limited intelligence causes him to act irrationally, often putting his family and himself in uncomfortable and occasionally dangerous circumstances, however, he is ultimately loving towards his family.", "annotation_id": "26673399", "url": "https://genius.com/26673399", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flawlëss", "line": "I was that fresh young nigga rockin’ Marni", "vault_lines": ["I was that fresh young nigga rockin' Marni"], "meaning": "Always ahead of the curve, Uzi has been wearing garments from Italian luxury brand Marni. He famously has a song titled “Marni on Me” from his 2020 collaborative project with Future, Pluto x Baby Pluto.", "annotation_id": "26673076", "url": "https://genius.com/26673076", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flawlëss", "line": "When I play golf, only time for a par", "vault_lines": ["When I play golf, only time for a par"], "meaning": "A par is a predetermined score an expert golf player is expected to make in a given hole. Uzi compares their ability in the rap game or in general to golf, boasting how they themself only operate on an expert level at all times.", "annotation_id": "26671859", "url": "https://genius.com/26671859", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flawlëss", "line": "Niggas, they rats, they like mice, they like Minnie and Mickey", "vault_lines": ["Niggas, they rats, they like mice, they like Minnie and Mickey"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert uses a play on words on a “rat”—a slang term for an untrustworthy person or a snitch—comparing the “rat” or “mouse” in question to Minnie and Mickey Mouse.\n\n\n\nMinnie Mouse (left) and Mickey Mouse (Right)\n\n\nThe same analogy is heard in Uzi’s March 2020 track “Baby Pluto,” with Uzi rapping:\n\nMan, I heard that nigga Mickey, that’s too risky", "annotation_id": "26671641", "url": "https://genius.com/26671641", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flawlëss", "line": "Money swollen like cyst, huh", "vault_lines": ["Money swollen like cyst, huh"], "meaning": "A cyst is a fluid-filled lump that appears underneath the human skin, which can become swollen, and tender once inflamed.\n\nYeat uses the term swollen to describe his large amounts of money, as when something becomes swollen, it typically grows larger.", "annotation_id": "26669935", "url": "https://genius.com/26669935", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flawlëss", "line": "Young nigga, yeah, I’m raw like Maaly (Ha, ha, Maaly)", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga, yeah, I'm raw like Maaly (Ha, ha, Maaly)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert employs word play on their right-hand producer and fellow Philidelphia native Maaly Raw’s name. Uzi and Maaly Raw have an extensive list of collaborations, the most notable being Uzi’s 2016 smash hit “Money Longer.”", "annotation_id": "26669746", "url": "https://genius.com/26669746", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flawlëss", "line": "Rock Balenciaga on Dickie", "vault_lines": ["Rock Balenciaga on Dickie"], "meaning": "Uzi has recently nicknamed themself Mr. B, due to how much time they spend in the Balenciaga store, going so far as to sleep and record songs there.", "annotation_id": "26669711", "url": "https://genius.com/26669711", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flawlëss", "line": "When life give you lemons, then crush that, it’s Simply", "vault_lines": ["When life give you lemons, then crush that, it's Simply"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert takes a spin on one of the most well-known inspirational quotes, “When life gives you lemons, make lemonade,” while employing wordplay, referencing the lemonade brand Simply Lemonade. Notably, Yeat played off the brand’s name alongside Uzi, as in April 2022, he sold custom lemonade bottles at a pop-up shop which were named “Simply Twizzy.”\n\n\n\nSimply Twizzy, Twizzlërs, and tour merch", "annotation_id": "26669695", "url": "https://genius.com/26669695", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flawlëss", "line": "They done put faith in the kid, huh", "vault_lines": ["They done put faith in the kid, huh"], "meaning": "“They” refers to the backers and executives that have believed in and invested in Yeat, or, as he refers to himself here, the “kid.”\n\nThe “kid” can refer to a gangsta, hustler, fighter, or artist that is the best at what they do.\n\nSince people have started having faith in Yeat, he has achieved a lot of success.", "annotation_id": "26667666", "url": "https://genius.com/26667666", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flawlëss", "line": "Yeah Out here thuggin’, my boy How many money chains you made, jit? Shit, sixty-five, you heard me? Hold on, what your money on your shoes for? That mean I walk to the money Damn You know what I’m sayin’? Money on my watch, that mean time is money Money on my phone, that mean I talk to the money (Yeah) Money on my chain, that mean the money hang with me (Oh, really?) Money on my hat, that mean money on my mind Money on my Kool-Aid, that mean my money sweet Oh, yeah, G, what the-what is on your, uh, shades for? Shades, that mean I see the money, you heard me? Out here thuggin’, you feel me? Just chillin’ Sixty-five money chains on my neck, oh, yeah Out here thuggin’, you know what I’m saying? Chillin’ ​Sharedatbitchlikeapizza, you heard me?", "vault_lines": ["Out here thuggin', my boy"], "meaning": "“Flawlëss” intro samples a viral 2018 YouTube video of the internet comedian Sharedatbitchlikeapizza wearing dollar bills on a chain alongside all his other accessories.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LBqFU5Fkf-8\n\nYeat and his affiliates spoke about the chance of possibly being sued over using this excerpt due to copyright. That didn’t turn out to be the case, however, as Sharedatbitchlikepizza would show his appreciation for Yeat sampling the clip in an Instagram post, further describing how it “changed his life.”\n\nShoutout to my nigga [Yeat] for putting my sample on his album I had a dream last night he change me and my nigga [Nolovejroc] life and made show we got rich 🤑 appreciation that check [Interscope Records] ❤️\n\n\n\nThe image attached to Sharedatbitchlikeapizza’s Instagram post.", "annotation_id": "26666583", "url": "https://genius.com/26666583", "state": "accepted", "votes": 187, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flawlëss", "line": "Buffy the Vampire Slayer with these Cartiers (Cartier)", "vault_lines": ["Buffy the Vampire Slayer with these Cartiers (Cartier)"], "meaning": "Buffy the Vampire Slayer is an American supernatural drama television series created by writer and director Joss Whedon and based on the eponymous 1992 film. In the show, Buffy Summers—played by Sarah Michelle Gellar—is the most recent to be put in a group of young women named “Vampire Slayers,” who are destined by fate to fight vampires alongside other dark entities.\n\nLil Uzi Vert employs a play on words between Buffy’s name and the high-end Cartier Buffs—Cartier’s luxury eyewear, known for its high quality and noble look.\nhttps://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRwPjKpswdygNpVuqnnZDl3j9rUrsY77_GBbw&usqp=CAU\n\nUzi wearing Cartier Buffs\n\n\nIt is also important to note that Buffy Summers was popularly known for wearing a plethora of glasses in the TV show, which Uzi could also be referring to.", "annotation_id": "26666474", "url": "https://genius.com/26666474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Flawlëss", "line": "Take a Perc’ in the Tonka, that’s it", "vault_lines": ["Take a Perc' in the Tonka, that's it"], "meaning": "Yeat is under the influence of a Percocet while inside of the “tonka\"—a term used to describe a large size of a high-powered luxury SUV, such as the Mercedes-Benz GLE or the Lamborghini Urus.\n\nHe’s used the phrase countless times and has even titled songs after it, such as “Big tonka,” “Tonka,” “Tonka 2,” and “King Tonka.”", "annotation_id": "26666070", "url": "https://genius.com/26666070", "state": "accepted", "votes": 145, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
