{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Finally #FRËË", "line": "When I die, gon’ play this shit, but don’t get mad, that’s what it used to be", "vault_lines": ["When I die, gon' play this shit, but don't gеt mad, that's what it used to be"], "meaning": "On March 26 2026, beloved rapper and songwriter Noah Olivier Smith (stage name “Yeat”) dropped his sixth studio album “A Dangerous Lyfe”, which many argue is the downfall—or essentially— the death of Yeat. This line could be seen as a foreshadowing of his future, as Yeat clearly states that when he dies, play this song to show how his lyfe and music was, and when he says “don’t get mad”, this could be interpreted as the audience being mad about how incredible his music was, but he basically says “dont cry because its gone, smile because it happened”.", "annotation_id": "39421235", "url": "https://genius.com/39421235", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
