{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Feel sum", "line": "No, I couldn’t tell you what’s real, couldn’t tell you what I see (Can’t tell you what I see)", "vault_lines": ["No, I couldn't tell you what's real, couldn't tell you what I see (Can't tell you what I see)"], "meaning": "In this line Yeat expresses how his drug use distorts his perception of reality. He says he “couldn’t tell you what’s real” and “can’t tell you what I see,” which suggests that his mind is so altered that he can’t distinguish between reality and hallucinations. The repetition emphasizes his confusion and shows how drugs have disconnected him from the normal way people experience the world", "annotation_id": "38955156", "url": "https://genius.com/38955156", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
