{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Feel more", "line": "Yeah, wake up, yeah, wake up, yeah, wake up, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, wake up, yeah, wake up, yeah, wake up, yeah"], "meaning": "He’s telling the aforementioned nappy person/people to wake up on him as he should not be slept on any longer. This song proves such a claim.", "annotation_id": "27169477", "url": "https://genius.com/27169477", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Feel more", "line": "Nappy, they was sleeping on me but not no more", "vault_lines": ["Nappy, they was sleeping on me but not no more"], "meaning": "A continuation of the previous lines' rhyme scheme. Yeat has remained under the radar until now, as the world is finally waking up to his sound.", "annotation_id": "25783816", "url": "https://genius.com/25783816", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Feel more", "line": "She said, “Yeat, yeah, I wanna feel more” Told that bitch to take some X to feel more Happy, not no Gilmore", "vault_lines": ["She said, \"Yeat, yeah, I wanna feel more\""], "meaning": "Presumably, Yeat is revealing an anecdote in which a girl he’s sleeping with told him she wants to feel more of him sexually. Alternatively, she merely wants to feel more intoxicated.\nYeat suggests she take ecstasy, nicknamed ‘X,’ to increase her sensations and mood, as MDMA is known to make users temporarily feel happier.\nHe then uses wordplay to link the euphoric feeling of ecstasy to movie character Happy Gilmore played by Adam Sandler in the popular 1996 comedy. His rhyme scheme allows the end of the previous line to flow into the next, rhyming ‘feel more’ with ‘Gilmore’\n“take some X to feel more happy.”", "annotation_id": "25783812", "url": "https://genius.com/25783812", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Feel more", "line": "Pinstripe the Palm Angels hoodie like a zoo, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Pinstripe the Palm Angels hoodie like a zoo, yeah"], "meaning": "Palm Angels is a California-based luxury designer with notably expensive sweatshirts. Yeat compares his Palm Angels hoodie to a zoo animal, like a zebra because of its pinstripes.\n\nIn saying ‘zoo,’ Yeat could also be referring to New York designer brand ‘Zoo York’ which often incorporates pinstripes into their clothing, using the New York Yankees' jerseys as inspiration.\n\nPalm Angels hoodie:\n\n\n\nZoo York hoodie:", "annotation_id": "25783688", "url": "https://genius.com/25783688", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Feel more", "line": "Nappy, they was sleeping on me but not no more", "vault_lines": ["Nappy, they was sleeping on me but not no more"], "meaning": "A continuation of the previous lines' rhyme scheme. Yeat has remained under the radar until now, as the world is finally waking up to his sound.", "annotation_id": "25783591", "url": "https://genius.com/25783591", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Feel more", "line": "She said, “Yeat, yeah, I wanna feel more” Told that bitch to take some X to feel more Happy, not no Gilmore", "vault_lines": ["She said, \"Yeat, yeah, I wanna feel more\""], "meaning": "Yeat reveals an anecdote in which a girl he’s sleeping with told him she wants to “feel more” [Of him? Could be sexual].\nYeat suggests she take ecstasy, ‘X’, to elevate her mood and sensations, as MDMA is known to be quite euphoric.\nNoah follows the anecdote with wordplay linking the euphoric feeling of ecstasy to movie character Happy Gilmore played by Adam Sandler in the hit 1996 namesake comedy. Noah’s rhyme scheme allows the end of the previous line to flow into the next, rhyming 'feel more’ with ‘Gilmore.’", "annotation_id": "25783469", "url": "https://genius.com/25783469", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
