{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Familia", "line": "Million for million, building for building Billion for billion, la familia ain’t feeling ya’ Million for million, building for building Billion for billion, la familia ain’t feeling ya’", "vault_lines": ["Million for million, building for building"], "meaning": "This hook is a nod to the song “Home Sweet Home” by the group Mansion Makers, where they sing, “Billion for billion, we’re building a mansion.”", "annotation_id": "30937983", "url": "https://genius.com/30937983", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Familia", "line": "Million for million, building for building Billion for billion, la familia ain’t feeling ya’ Million for million, building for building Billion for billion, la familia ain’t feeling ya’", "vault_lines": ["Million for million, building for building"], "meaning": "This hook is a nod to the song “Home Sweet Home” by the group Mansion Makers, where they sing, “Billion for billion, we’re building a mansion.”", "annotation_id": "30937980", "url": "https://genius.com/30937980", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Familia", "line": "Had to mix it up, I double back and then I swirl", "vault_lines": ["Had to mix it up, I double back and then I swirl"], "meaning": "Yeat was constantly told that all his songs sounded the same. In order to prove everyone wrong he had to switch up (mix it up) his sound. Which he did in the album afterlyfë and especially this album, 2093.", "annotation_id": "30926289", "url": "https://genius.com/30926289", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
