{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Familia", "line": "I’m pissin’ on this beat, it’s like a bathroom stall", "vault_lines": ["I'm pissin' on this beat, it's like a bathroom stall"], "meaning": "Yeat is implying that he is asserting his twizzy dominance by urinated on the instrumental he is currently nutting on. While simultaneously playing with Drake’s snake.", "annotation_id": "30924502", "url": "https://genius.com/30924502", "state": "pending", "votes": -8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Familia", "line": "Number one worldwide, so we keep it perfect", "vault_lines": ["Number one worldwide, so we keep it perfect"], "meaning": "Yeat has literally already gone number 1 globally in his song with Drake “IDGAF”, which reached the top spot on the Billboard Global 200 charts, a list of the 200 most popular songs of the week globally.", "annotation_id": "30910992", "url": "https://genius.com/30910992", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Familia", "line": "I go tit for tat, I go blick for gat", "vault_lines": ["I go tit for tat, I go blick for gat"], "meaning": "In this lyric, Yeat is expressing a readiness to retaliate or respond in kind to any actions taken against him. “Tit for tat” is a phrase that means responding to an action with a similar action. Similarly, “blick for gat” suggests retaliating with force or violence (“blick” being slang for shooting or attacking). Together, these phrases convey a sense of assertiveness and a willingness to defend oneself or take action when provoked.", "annotation_id": "30908570", "url": "https://genius.com/30908570", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Familia", "line": "Still not say a word", "vault_lines": ["still not say a word"], "meaning": "possible reference to yeat using “not-actual-words” like twizzy and tonka.", "annotation_id": "30902096", "url": "https://genius.com/30902096", "state": "pending", "votes": -17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Familia", "line": "When you get the money, yeah, this shit gon’ run the world", "vault_lines": ["When you get the money, yeah, this shit gon' run the world"], "meaning": "In this lyric, Yeat suggests that with wealth comes influence and power. He implies that once someone acquires a significant amount of money, they will have the ability to impact the world around them in a significant way. The phrase “this shit gon' run the world” indicates that money can be a driving force behind decision-making, control, and influence on a global scale. It reflects the idea that financial success can lead to greater authority and impact in various aspects of life and society.", "annotation_id": "30898635", "url": "https://genius.com/30898635", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Familia", "line": "When you get the money, yeah, this shit gon’ run the world", "vault_lines": ["When you get the money, yeah, this shit gon' run the world"], "meaning": "In this lyric, Yeat suggests that with wealth comes influence and power. He implies that once someone acquires a significant amount of money, they will have the ability to impact the world around them in a significant way. The phrase “this shit gon' run the world” indicates that money can be a driving force behind decision-making, control, and influence on a global scale. It reflects the idea that financial success can lead to greater authority and impact in various aspects of life and society.", "annotation_id": "30898632", "url": "https://genius.com/30898632", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Familia", "line": "Bought a brand new crib, this shit gon’ sit out way in Europe", "vault_lines": ["Bought a brand new crib, this shit gon’ sit out way in Europe"], "meaning": "In this lyric, Yeat describes purchasing a new home, emphasizing its location in Europe. The phrase “this shit gon' sit out way in Europe” suggests that the house is situated in a distant or prestigious location, possibly indicating Yeat’s success and ability to afford luxury properties in international settings. It conveys a sense of wealth and status, as well as a willingness to invest in lavish assets.", "annotation_id": "30898552", "url": "https://genius.com/30898552", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Familia", "line": "You a fat ass rat, you go chit for chat", "vault_lines": ["You a fat ass rat, you go chit for chat"], "meaning": "Yeat implies that people are rats and all they do is go “chit for chat” a spin on the common adage “band for band” in which people will compete in pulling out large sums of money in order to one up the other person. This song uses this as an overarching theme in which he takes many spins on the “blank for blank” template", "annotation_id": "30898538", "url": "https://genius.com/30898538", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Familia", "line": "Keep that shit like Drizzy, it’s all a blur That shit for all the dogs on the Earth", "vault_lines": ["Keep that shit like Drizzy, it’s all a blur"], "meaning": "It’s All a Blur' is the name of Drake’s tour that ran from Wed, Jul 5, 2023 – Tue, Apr 16, 2024. Yeat is saying that he takes so many drugs that everything is a blur.\n\nA bitch is a female dog. Yeat is saying that a female whom he has come into contact with is rather promiscuous and has been with ‘all the dogs on earth’, which also alludes to Drakes album ‘For All the Dogs’ where Yeat was featured in “IDGAF”", "annotation_id": "30898161", "url": "https://genius.com/30898161", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
