{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Fake Luv Freestyle", "line": "Yeah, we on demon time", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we on demon time"], "meaning": "You wanna get fyed, you fye", "annotation_id": "38609124", "url": "https://genius.com/38609124", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Fake Luv Freestyle", "line": "(Had to change my life to all the times I do what I never did) (Woah) (Had to change my life for all the things they said I never did) (Had to quit them drugs, had to quit that love, had to quit the trap, had to quit the drugs) (Had to quit them Percs’, had to quit them drugs, had to quit that, had to quit that, had to quit that)", "vault_lines": ["My demon can't see, all my demons can't see (Woah, woah)"], "meaning": "Again, Yeat refers to his addiction to drugs, but this time thinks he has to quit them, instead of living normally with them.\nHe also says he’s indebted, for things he hasn’t done.", "annotation_id": "27548287", "url": "https://genius.com/27548287", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Fake Luv Freestyle", "line": "You ain’t seen demon in there (Woah) Yeah, that’s a demon in there (Woah) Yeah, he gon’ fuck wit’ yo’ head (Fuck wit’ yo’ head)", "vault_lines": ["You ain't seen demon in there (Woah)"], "meaning": "At the start of the song, Yeat says his demon couldn’t see him, but now they have arrived. Fuck what you had could mean that the demons will give you a new life, for better or for worse.", "annotation_id": "27548285", "url": "https://genius.com/27548285", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Fake Luv Freestyle", "line": "I’m gon’ get it live, you hallucinatin’ on them drugs (Drugs) Can’t tell what’s real from the fake no more, everybody switchin’ up (Up) So let’s go through them hunnids inside of the club, ’til we wake up the sun (Woah) I just called up my brother, we codeine dreamin’, it’s too easy to run (Woah) I just called up my guys, and we told ’em we did it, he told ’em it’s done (Woah) I just called up my mama, I told her we did it, I told her it’s done (Woah) No, I can’t change for the homie, I take me a Perc’ and I slump (Woah) Had to fold on temptation ’cause I made a million, yeah, in a month (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we on demon time"], "meaning": "Yeat first raps about people hallucinating off the drugs, but then speaks on the fact that he’s dreaming off codeine, and how he slumps off percs. This is his temptation he refers to at the end.\n\nThe difference for Yeat is he is able to keep up with his mom and his guys, even off the drugs.", "annotation_id": "27548280", "url": "https://genius.com/27548280", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Fake Luv Freestyle", "line": "We forever stuck inside a elevator, where we only goin’ up (Up)", "vault_lines": ["We forever stuck inside a elevator, where we only goin' up (Up)"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying his trajectory is headed upwards, basically meaning he won’t ever fail now, and that he will be successful.", "annotation_id": "27548277", "url": "https://genius.com/27548277", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Fake Luv Freestyle", "line": "And know we fyed up, they wan’ have my Feng Shui (Woah) They know I’m fyed up, they wan’ see what the one say (Fye)", "vault_lines": ["And know we fyed up, they wan' have my Feng Shui (Woah)"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying now that he’s up, people finally want to listen to what he has to say, and want to copy his style.", "annotation_id": "27548273", "url": "https://genius.com/27548273", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Fake Luv Freestyle", "line": "I sold a thirty k, ain’t ever switchin’ up", "vault_lines": ["I sold a thirty k, ain't ever switchin' up"], "meaning": "Could be referring to Yeat selling 35k first week with 2Alive, very good numbers for a debut album.", "annotation_id": "27548267", "url": "https://genius.com/27548267", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Fake Luv Freestyle", "line": "I look to my left, bitch, yeah, it’s all envy that I see Only fake bullshit, yeah, on my timeline all I see All that jim-jim (Yeah), all that Twit’ talk (Yeah), all that bitch shit, all that bitch talk (Yeah) All that, alla-alla, alla-alla, alla-alla, alla-alla, alla-alla (Yeah), all that bitch talk", "vault_lines": ["I look to my left, bitch, yeah, it's all envy that I see"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying all he sees is envy and bullshit, especially on social media. This could also be referring to old friends that ditched him trying to rekindle their friendship, also known as fake friends, or fake love like the song name.", "annotation_id": "27548259", "url": "https://genius.com/27548259", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
