{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FOR LYFE", "line": "Get away from us, we don’t like losin’ dollars (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Get away from us, we don't like losin' dollars (Yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat does not want any more outsiders joining the group that he’s formed as he feels their desire to join is not in the group’s best interest. New people could create problems as they were not with Yeat by his side while he became famous. They did not believe in him and they would only cause Yeat and his associates to lose money.", "annotation_id": "33388910", "url": "https://genius.com/33388910", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
