{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FOR LYFE", "line": "(Yeah, yeah, for life) Could you do this shit for life? (Yeah, for— yeah, for life) Would you do this shit for life?", "vault_lines": ["(Phew) Yeah, for life"], "meaning": "Yeat is questioning if other musicians are as dedicated as he is. He goes on to ask the rhetorical question to other musicians “Could you do this shit for life?”. In Yeats mind, he knows that nobody else is as dedicated as he is to making music. Rather than doing it for money, Yeat makes music because he loves to do so.", "annotation_id": "33388781", "url": "https://genius.com/33388781", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
