{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FLYTROOP", "line": "I could barely stand, I could barely sit", "vault_lines": ["Uh (Bih'), I could barely stand, I could barely sit"], "meaning": "In the context of hip-hop and Yeat’s frequent references to substances, it most-likely describes the effects of being under the influence—feeling disconnected from one’s body, heavy, or unable to function normally.", "annotation_id": "33733946", "url": "https://genius.com/33733946", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FLYTROOP", "line": "Holdin’ up the weight on your shoulder, you can’t carry (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Holdin' up the weight on your shoulder, you can't carry (Woo)"], "meaning": "This is another one of Yeat’s double-meaning verses. In one sense we can say he is talking about people carrying a burden and weight on their shoulders from anything that they don’t like in their life and they’re trying to carry that burden but they can’t carry it\n\nYeat also could be talking about carrying heavy weapons due to the Flytroop music video.", "annotation_id": "33692075", "url": "https://genius.com/33692075", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FLYTROOP", "line": "I could tell you normal life ain’t comin’, ’cause shit get dangerou-ous", "vault_lines": ["I could tell you normal life ain't comin', 'cause shit get dangerou-ous"], "meaning": "This verse is a hint towards Yeat’s next studio album ADL(A Dangerous Lyfe) that is rumored to drop on Christmas 2024\n\n\nEdit*\nYeat confirmed that ADL is dropping in 2025 and not on 2024 Christmas", "annotation_id": "33321694", "url": "https://genius.com/33321694", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FLYTROOP", "line": "I could smell your bullshit over here,", "vault_lines": ["I could smell your bullshit over here,"], "meaning": "A double entendre of “bullshit” is used here. Taken literally, it suggests a strong smell, as if someone is close enough to detect an unpleasant smell. Figuratively however, “bullshit” refers to lies or nonsense, and to “smell” it implies detecting dishonesty or deception from a distance. This is used to show that Yeat knows that the subject is lying.", "annotation_id": "33319533", "url": "https://genius.com/33319533", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FLYTROOP", "line": "We on X too (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Huh, I'm a fly soldier, I'm a fly troop"], "meaning": "X is a derived term for Ecstacy, a commonly used drug with many rappers such as Yeat and Ken Carson. Yeat being on X is a very common appearance with Yeat, as he has mentioned this many times previously in his songs, Such as Up off X.", "annotation_id": "33241083", "url": "https://genius.com/33241083", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
