{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FLYTROOP", "line": "Yeah, we call you six feet, ’cause we get you buried (Woo-ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we call you six feet, 'cause we get you buried (Woo-ooh)"], "meaning": "yeat is stating he can kill people and have their body cremated/buried underground.\n\nit’s worth noting he may be incorporating wordplay with the term “six feet under,” which according to google means “Buried six feet underground; not alive; dead.”", "annotation_id": "31660890", "url": "https://genius.com/31660890", "state": "pending", "votes": -7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FLYTROOP", "line": "When you clear up old lies (Phew, it’s said), don’t it get scary?", "vault_lines": ["When you clear up old lies (Phew, it's said), don't it get scary?"], "meaning": "yeat states that people may fear telling the truth about old lies, as admitting you lied is usually quite hard and can come with criticism.", "annotation_id": "31660874", "url": "https://genius.com/31660874", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FLYTROOP", "line": "Every time I fuck up somethin’ else, I make the lane switch", "vault_lines": ["Every time I fuck up somethin' else, I make the lane switch"], "meaning": "Yeat is talking about the mixed reviews on his latest project “2093”.\n\nThe album was released in mid-February of 2024, and has since been subjected to mixed reviews from critics and fans.\n\nYeat is implying that whenever he drops something that is remotely viewed as less good, he switches it up and gets back on track", "annotation_id": "31463179", "url": "https://genius.com/31463179", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
