{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "But the ship ain’t hit my house and it had told me what to—", "vault_lines": ["But the ship ain't hit my house and it had told me what to—"], "meaning": "Yeat is referring to the real aliens that he saw as a kid with this line. He mentions these aliens in some interviews.", "annotation_id": "36404778", "url": "https://genius.com/36404778", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "Look into my eyes, you’ll see a thousand things You’ll see a thousand things, you’ll see a thousand things", "vault_lines": ["I seen a thousand things, I seen a thousand things"], "meaning": "What Yeat means by “you see a thousand things” is he’s been through ups and downs in either his personal or professional life and he’s seen it all during his career.", "annotation_id": "35442473", "url": "https://genius.com/35442473", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "H-h-hey, s-s-s—", "vault_lines": ["When I was young (Ah-woo), I seen a alien in my life (I seen a thousand things)"], "meaning": "This tag belongs to producer 730hahah, a producer from Russia. 730hahah a signee of Lyfestyle Corporation label and also best known for his work with Yeat, Kai Angel and others.", "annotation_id": "34225288", "url": "https://genius.com/34225288", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "Just keep drivin’, I keep drivin’ life (I seen a thousand things)", "vault_lines": ["Just keep drivin', I keep drivin' life (I seen a thousand things)"], "meaning": "He snaps from the depressing tone of the previous line and tells the listeners to pay the notion of fate no mind, to keep their hope, and keep pushing forwards through life no matter what. Probably because he believes that since it is predestined, it shouldn’t be worried over.", "annotation_id": "33561564", "url": "https://genius.com/33561564", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "But make no mistake (Ah-woo), ah, you can’t choose your fate, ah (I seen a thousand things) You can’t choose your fate, ah, you can’t choose your fate, huh", "vault_lines": ["I seen time stop, I seen a thousand things"], "meaning": "Even though he knows that he gives others hope, he himself is hopeless, and believes that people are destined to end up a certain way, that people don’t change. This repetition provides more emphasis; the repetition of this line specifically sounds extremely hollow and almost bitter at the coldness of fate.", "annotation_id": "33561563", "url": "https://genius.com/33561563", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "Ridin’ in this bitch (Ah-woo), ’round town on this bitch (I seen a thousand things, I seen a thousand things) I was sellin’ hope, yeah, I was sellin’ faith, ah (I seen a thousand things)", "vault_lines": ["When I was young (Ah-woo), I seen a alien in my life (I seen a thousand things)"], "meaning": "He gives people hope with his music, that they change their lives for the better. The repetition of the ‘I seen a thousand things’ adlib is akin to his thoughts while opening this song, wanting to explain what all he’s been through, but not knowing how at the beginning. Also the stutter at, ‘windo- windows,’ is representative of his anxiety from telling his story in this song, and is later brought back.", "annotation_id": "33561557", "url": "https://genius.com/33561557", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "(I seen a thousand things)", "vault_lines": ["I seen a thousand things"], "meaning": "Yeat is likely referring to his long history of drug abuse. As he goes on to mention later in the song, he had a bad drug overdose in 2020 in which doctors had to resuscitate him.", "annotation_id": "33452869", "url": "https://genius.com/33452869", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "I can’t handle shit (Yeah, oh-oh), I can’t handle shit, yeah (Yeah, yeah) I had to feel (I’ma lay off the tweak)", "vault_lines": ["I can't handle shit (Yeah, oh-oh), I can't handle shit, yeah (Yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "YEAT acknowledges his flaws and his inability to handle matters. His use of past tense in “I done had feelings” imply that this is not the case anymore, suggesting he is emotionally numb. The final ad lib is him saying he is going to lay off the tweak, or stop doing drugs. This indicates that he may be motivated to fix his problems and become a better person for himself.", "annotation_id": "33442309", "url": "https://genius.com/33442309", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "I’ma end this off on a good note (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I'ma end this off on a good note (Yeah)"], "meaning": "This part of the song has a different beat that is more uplifting and calm. On the normal version of the album, this is the last song, making the second part of this song function as an outro to the album. This more peaceful instrumental is what he is talking about when he says he wants to end this off on a good note.", "annotation_id": "33442271", "url": "https://genius.com/33442271", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "Maybe I’m really not from this Earth", "vault_lines": ["Maybe I'm really not from this Earth"], "meaning": "yeat has seen visions (he said in an interview) and they were from different planets and shi", "annotation_id": "33366192", "url": "https://genius.com/33366192", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "I’m a drug addict, I can’t stay asleep", "vault_lines": ["I'm a drug addict, I can't stay asleep"], "meaning": "Yeat is known to be a drug addict, taking many different substances such as Ecstacy, MDMA, Weed, and many others. 2093 was his first sober album, and Yeat is saying in this line that he cannot sleep due to the psychoactive effects of all the drugs.", "annotation_id": "33333504", "url": "https://genius.com/33333504", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "I got what I deserve, I put in all that work", "vault_lines": ["I got what I dеserve, I put in all that work"], "meaning": "yeat is referencing his fame and money and what he had to do to get it “i put in all that work” he made 15 songs a day for over 5 years showing his dedication to music", "annotation_id": "33320073", "url": "https://genius.com/33320073", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "I hope you ready for A DANGEROUS LYFE", "vault_lines": ["I hope you ready for A DANGEROUS LYFE"], "meaning": "Teasing his next album A Dangerous Lyfestyle potentially releasing in 2025\n\nhttps://genius.com/amp/albums/Yeat/A-dangerous-lyfe", "annotation_id": "33317604", "url": "https://genius.com/33317604", "state": "pending", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "When I was young (Ah-woo), I seen a alien in my life (I seen a thousand things) And it told me what to do, yeah, they came late at night", "vault_lines": ["When I was young (Ah-woo), I seen a alien in my life (I seen a thousand things)"], "meaning": "In an interview with 032c, Yeat recounts an alien encounter at the age of eleven:\n\nThat was deadass. It was real. I won’t go into too much detail because I’m not sure if they want me to talk about this right now. The aliens, I mean, I will say one thing though, they are really tall—and looked almost human. I remember everything on the night that it transpired, second for second. I can tell the difference between a dream and reality, and I know I was awake. That’s also my first memory. Everything before that feels fake. Sometimes I think I might not be even from here, because I have dreams about other planets.\n\nHe also mentions this encounter throughout his discography, even going as far as revolving his 2024 album, 2093, about his experience, claiming he’s from a different universe and referencing the aforementioned encounter as evidence.", "annotation_id": "30547476", "url": "https://genius.com/30547476", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "FATË", "line": "Seen the way I died, then I watched it on rewind", "vault_lines": ["Seen the way I died, then I watched it on rewind"], "meaning": "Yeat went to the hospital in 2020 from a drug overdose. Most likely, this line is a reference to this case, and Yeat mentions this not for the first time in his songs.", "annotation_id": "28902960", "url": "https://genius.com/28902960", "state": "pending", "votes": 62, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
