{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Extraaa", "line": "I don’t discriminate none of my bread, I’m not cheeseist", "vault_lines": ["I don't discriminate none of my bread, I'm not cheeseist"], "meaning": "Yeat claims he doesn’t get picky about where his money comes from with a clever play on words. He invents the word “cheeseist” to describe someone that discriminates against types of cheese (slang for money), similar to how the word “racist” means someone who expresses prejudice against certain races. In this way, Yeat claims that he doesn’t discern his sources of income with picky preferences, showing that he’s not afraid to get his hands dirty when necessary.", "annotation_id": "38041614", "url": "https://genius.com/38041614", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
