{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Evolvëd", "line": "They already know that I’m up, yeah, I don’t gotta wait in no line", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, they already know that I'm up, yeah, I don't gotta wait in no line"], "meaning": "Here, Yeat uses “I’m up” to suggest that he is moving fast and not waiting for anything, implying confidence and momentum. It could also be a double meaning, hinting that he is “high” on drugs, which fits with common slang.", "annotation_id": "38942103", "url": "https://genius.com/38942103", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Evolvëd", "line": "I been talked to my devil, he told me let’s get it, let’s do it, it’s time to go, go up", "vault_lines": ["I been talked to my devil, he told me let's get it, let's do it, it's time to go, go up"], "meaning": "In this line, the “devil” likely symbolizes temptation or negative influences in the artist’s life, such as drugs. It suggests that these influences are pushing him to continue doing his thing, even if it may be harmful.", "annotation_id": "38942068", "url": "https://genius.com/38942068", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Evolvëd", "line": "The way they see me blow up", "vault_lines": [", the way they see me blow up"], "meaning": "he line references Osama bin Laden who is often mentioned in rap as a metaphor for something that “blows up.” In this context, “blow up” can refer both to explosions and to gaining massive popularity. Yeat is likely comparing the explosive impact of Osama-related imagery to how his music or career is rapidly “blowing up” and becoming widely known", "annotation_id": "38942012", "url": "https://genius.com/38942012", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
