{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Earnëd it", "line": "No, I don’t fuck with you, you a bug-ass lame, you a motherfuckin’ fly Nobody fuck with you, you a operator, you a motherfuckin’ spy", "vault_lines": ["I love my- (yeah) everyone of my bitches yeah"], "meaning": "Call back and interpolation of his track “Doublë”:\n\nHow you know all that shit? You a spy\nHeard you snitchin', you a bug, you a fly", "annotation_id": "41583748", "url": "https://genius.com/41583748", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Earnëd it", "line": "Every time you talk to me, it sounded dumb as fuck, I (No) can’t understand you", "vault_lines": ["I love my- (yeah) everyone of my bitches yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that because he views himself as being on a completely different level, what the other person says sounds unintelligent or irrelevant to him. Which the reason why he said “got a lot of money, i can’t relate to you.”.", "annotation_id": "41558686", "url": "https://genius.com/41558686", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Earnëd it", "line": "Uh, let it burn, baby, burn, burn, baby, like a candle (Ooh, heh, heh-heh)", "vault_lines": ["I love my- (yeah) everyone of my bitches yeah"], "meaning": "This may connect with the idea of the conflict between Travis Scott when Yeat released ON NOTHING where it was stated\n\nI don’t fuck with Flame, not a lot to say, if I saw a candle, I’d shush it\n\nWhich can highly indicate that Yeat is not done with this conflict until he says so.", "annotation_id": "41552391", "url": "https://genius.com/41552391", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Earnëd it", "line": "I was outside in the turban, scammin’ and makin’ money and just do what I did", "vault_lines": ["I love my- (yeah) everyone of my bitches yeah"], "meaning": "During Yeat’s rise to fame from 2021 to 2022, he was known for his prominent use of wearing turbans, even mentioning this habit on the track “Turban”:\n\nPerfect, rockin' a turban (Oh yeah, oh yeah)\n\n\n\nWhile finding success, stealing from people was a common tactic to get money, as scamming and fraud were common within the underground scene during his come-up. His former friend and then-frequent collaborator SeptembersRich discussed this type of scamming at the time on “Trëndy way:”\n\nI just made thirty thousand jugging kids on the ‘Gram", "annotation_id": "41543772", "url": "https://genius.com/41543772", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Earnëd it", "line": "If you can’t understand me, l hand your ass a manual (Birdie)", "vault_lines": ["I love my- (yeah) everyone of my bitches yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat is known for using his own slang and unusual vocabulary throughout his music, including terms such as “twizzy,” “Tonka,” “luh,” “geeked,” and “shmunk.” He also frequently stretches, slurs, or changes the pronunciation of words as part of his delivery.\n\nHere, Yeat jokes that anyone who can’t understand his lingo needs a manual, as if his way of speaking requires its own instruction guide.", "annotation_id": "41118728", "url": "https://genius.com/41118728", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Earnëd it", "line": "Ayy, uh, really be living like kings do, bitch, I’m Tut (I’m Tut)", "vault_lines": ["I love my- (yeah) everyone of my bitches yeah"], "meaning": "Yeat compares his lavish wealth and high status to Tutankhamun, or King Tut, who was an ancient Egyptian pharaoh whose tomb became famous for the large amount of gold, jewelry, and other valuables inside.", "annotation_id": "41118681", "url": "https://genius.com/41118681", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Earnëd it", "line": "Birkin", "vault_lines": ["I love my- (yeah) everyone of my bitches yeah"], "meaning": "Birkin bags are luxury handbags made by Hermès and are known for their high prices and limited availability. Yeat says he bought one for his partner as a reward because “she earned it,” using the purchase as another display of his wealth.", "annotation_id": "41118671", "url": "https://genius.com/41118671", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
