{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "ELIMINATË", "line": "Squeeze that money, lemonade", "vault_lines": ["Squeeze that money, lemonade"], "meaning": "This is potentially a shot at up-and-coming artist, Ian, who not only has been accused of stealing Yeat’s flow on multiple occasions, he also released his album on the same day as LYFESTYLE. This lyric could be interpreted as Yeat calling out not only Ian, but Lyrical Lemonade as well who gave Ian his big break with his music video for “FIGURE IT OUT”. “Squeeze that money, lemonade” is a double entendre; one must squeeze lemons to make lemonade and sell it; just as Ian allegedly squeezed (Metaphorically) Yeat’s sound and style to market it for profit.", "annotation_id": "33325716", "url": "https://genius.com/33325716", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
