{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Dëserve it", "line": "(Wake up, F1lthy, let’s go, let’s go)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, yeah, I deserve it (Deserve it)"], "meaning": "This is the producer tag for American record-producer, F1lthy.\nF1lthy is known for his production with artists within the Trap-genre such as Playboi Carti, Lil Uzi Vert, Bladee, and LUCKI.\n\nF1lthy has collaborated with Yeat previously on other records such as “Got rich” and “Smooktobër,” from his second major-label studio album 2 Alivë.", "annotation_id": "25537125", "url": "https://genius.com/25537125", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Dëserve it", "line": "Everything easy, a layup", "vault_lines": ["Big body, got me the Lamb', yeah, everything easy, a layup"], "meaning": "In this line, Yeat explains how everything he’s been doing is easy like a basketball layup which is considered to be an easy way to make a two point shot in basketball.", "annotation_id": "25322168", "url": "https://genius.com/25322168", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
