{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Dëmon tied", "line": "(I-I’m—) (I-I’m—) (I-I’m working on dying) (BNYX)", "vault_lines": ["Woo-hoo, hmm, woo (Hmm)"], "meaning": "“Working on Dying” is a Philadelphia-based hip-hop production collective and record label founded in 2012 by producers F1lthy and Oogie Mane . Known for their dark, heavy trap sound, they have collaborated with artists like Lil Uzi Vert, Future, and Bladee, and are prominent in the underground scene.\n\nI-I-I-I’m working on dying\nBNYX®\n\nBenjamin Saint Fort (born April 23, 1995), professionally known as BNYX® (pronounced Benny X), is an American record producer (and rapper, occasionally) from Philadelphia, Pennsylvania", "annotation_id": "38983030", "url": "https://genius.com/38983030", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
