{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Dëmon 2", "line": "Yeah, every mornin’ take a Tesla, bitch, I live in outer space", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, every mornin' take a Tesla, bitch, I live in outer space"], "meaning": "There is a double meaning here: “Tesla” refers to MDMA pills shaped like the logo of the popular car brand.\n\nThe Tesla car brand is also known for having sent a “Roadster” model into space.\n\nWhen Yeat says, “Every morning I take a Tesla, bitch, I live in outer space,” he is referencing both points mentioned above.", "annotation_id": "40446639", "url": "https://genius.com/40446639", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Dëmon 2", "line": "Yeah, I told ’em that I died, but they didn’t believe it, ah (What?)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I told 'em that I died, but they didn't believe it, ah (What?)"], "meaning": "Trying to figure out how many times yeat has died is tricky as in songs he claims to have “died” anywhere from 3-8 times. This a reference to a drug overdose in which he only has 1 confirm OD under his belt. They didn’t believe he died ig", "annotation_id": "37104570", "url": "https://genius.com/37104570", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
