{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Doublë", "line": "I ain’t never pull a goddamn loan out", "vault_lines": ["I ain't never pull a goddamn loan out"], "meaning": "In this line, Yeat references his financial wisdom and his wealth by stating that he will not be using loans, which often cause financial harm due to their interest rates, and also states that he does not need to borrow money as he has more than enough.", "annotation_id": "29769402", "url": "https://genius.com/29769402", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
