{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Doublë", "line": "Say it again for the kids that just doubted", "vault_lines": ["Say it again for the kids that just doubted"], "meaning": "Yeat references his early doubters and flaunts how he is famous now where as most of his early haters are still broke.", "annotation_id": "29769390", "url": "https://genius.com/29769390", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Doublë", "line": "Getting rich just like this is a hobby (Ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Getting rich just like this is a hobby (Ayy)"], "meaning": "It is well known that getting richer only gets easier after accumulating wealth, as wealth builds upon it self in a free market capitalist economy. Yeat alludes to this phenomenon in this, flaunting his lavish wealth and ease of increasing it.", "annotation_id": "29769371", "url": "https://genius.com/29769371", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
