{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Doublë", "line": "Off the Perc’, I can’t walk at all, paraplegic", "vault_lines": ["Off thе Perc', I can't walk at all, paraplegic"], "meaning": "One of the major side effects of overconsumption of opioids is complete paralysis from the waist down\n\nThankfully this paralysis is temporary and full mobility of the legs is restored when the drug wears off", "annotation_id": "27491443", "url": "https://genius.com/27491443", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Doublë", "line": "You ain’t geekin’ boy, your life is a lie", "vault_lines": ["You ain't geekin' boy, your life is a lie"], "meaning": "“Geekin” it means to be high off of any type of pill: Xanax, Percocet, Ecstasy, Molly.\n\nAnd in this line, Yeat refers that the dude is lying about taking pills.", "annotation_id": "26998697", "url": "https://genius.com/26998697", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Doublë", "line": "Big body, big body, big body, big body, big body", "vault_lines": ["Pull off in a Tonka, yeah, this a big body, big body, big body, big body, big body"], "meaning": "“Big Body” Either refers to a large SUV championed by BMW’s Alpina Division or Mercedes AMG. Most likely he is yet again referring to his GLE 73.", "annotation_id": "25267851", "url": "https://genius.com/25267851", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Doublë", "line": "I be geeked, I take a Tes’ in the Tesla", "vault_lines": ["I be geeked, I take a Tes' in the Tesla"], "meaning": "Yeat makes a reference to the Tesla pill, a form of ecstasy that’s in the shape of the Tesla Motors' logo. He exclaims that he takes the drug while in one of Tesla’s high-end luxury vehicles.\n\n\n\nHe used this analogy later on in this album, on “Gëek high”:\n\nI pop a Tesla, it’s helping the climate", "annotation_id": "25209758", "url": "https://genius.com/25209758", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Doublë", "line": "666, 777, drink it", "vault_lines": ["Big body GLE-ski, I went bought it (Oh, na-na-na)"], "meaning": "777 (or triple seven) is typically considered God’s number, hence the reference to heaven in the following line.\n\nHowever, triple deuces can be interpreted as three multiplied by two, which gives us 6. 666 is often considered the Number of the Beast, and is often used to invoke Satan. Taking drugs is considered by Christians to be a wrongful act, as it’s damaging the temple that is your body, hence the reference to ‘pouring this bitch up’ (likely with lean) following the 666 bar.\n\nThis isn’t the first time Yeat has referenced religion. He references 777 and 666 in the first part of the verse of this very song:\n\n666, 777, drink it\n\nLater in the same verse:\n\nBut the devil told me everything fine\n\nAnd again on Monëy so big:\n\nI got the devil on my phone, he told me, keep doin' this shit\nYeah, devil taught me how to get rich\nYeah, how many bands? six-six", "annotation_id": "25195015", "url": "https://genius.com/25195015", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Doublë", "line": "My diamonds real pissy, they potty (Hey, hey)", "vault_lines": ["My diamonds real pissy, they potty (Hey, hey)"], "meaning": "His diamonds are yellow resembling piss from a potty or toilet.", "annotation_id": "25168545", "url": "https://genius.com/25168545", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Doublë", "line": "Go ’head, chop ’em up like Paul Bunyan", "vault_lines": ["Go 'head, chop 'em up like Paul Bunyan"], "meaning": "Paul Bunyan is a giant lumberjack and folk hero in American and Canadian folklore, known for having superhuman abilities. Yeat tells his affiliates to “chop ‘em up,” or attack their opponents in the same way Paul Bunyan would chop a tree.", "annotation_id": "25164536", "url": "https://genius.com/25164536", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
