{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Don’t tëll", "line": "Y’all been going out sad, had to jump in (Ahh-ahh-ahh)", "vault_lines": ["Y'all been going out sad, had to jump in (Ahh-ahh-ahh)"], "meaning": "yeat had to step in for people thats down bad", "annotation_id": "36762424", "url": "https://genius.com/36762424", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Don’t tëll", "line": "Them racks don’t lie, them racks don’t tell (Ah) (Ooh-ooh-ooh) Them racks don’t lie, them racks don’t fail (Tell, ah) (Ahh-ahh-ahh) Them racks don’t cry, them racks don’t tell (Oh-ah) (Ooh-ooh-ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Them racks don't lie, them racks don't tell (Ah) (Ooh-ooh-ooh)"], "meaning": "Yeat often uses “racks” as slang for stacks of money thousands of dollars. In these lyrics, he’s emphasizing that money is reliable it doesn’t lie, snitch, or betray him like people might. The repetition reinforces the idea that wealth provides stability, unlike relationships, which can be unpredictable or untrustworthy. Essentially, he’s saying that his money is a constant in his life; it won’t deceive him, fail him, or show emotions.", "annotation_id": "34554570", "url": "https://genius.com/34554570", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Don’t tëll", "line": "(Dream, this shit go dummy)", "vault_lines": ["Made a lot of racks just from puttin' bells (Dream, this shit go dummy, bells on this bih) (Ahh-ahh-ahh)"], "meaning": "This is the tag for one of the song’s producers, Dream Awake.", "annotation_id": "31007237", "url": "https://genius.com/31007237", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Don’t tëll", "line": "Made a lot of racks just from puttin’ bells (Dream, this shit go dummy, bells on this bih) (Ahh-ahh-ahh)", "vault_lines": ["Made a lot of racks just from puttin' bells (Dream, this shit go dummy, bells on this bih) (Ahh-ahh-ahh)"], "meaning": "Yeat has indeed made a lot of monetary value along with developing a positive reputation for himself from the process of creating enjoyable music with the addition of the tubular bell, catching listeners off guard before keeping them interested with flow changes and synthetic beats.\n\nAccording to “No commënt” by Yeat, he implies he made a 13-million dollar deal, allegedly referring to the joint deal between Yeat, Interscope Records, and Geffen Records:\n\nGot thirteen mill' from the deal, pockets so real (Ha, yeah)", "annotation_id": "30301694", "url": "https://genius.com/30301694", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
