{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Dangerous House", "line": "[Verse]", "vault_lines": ["All I think about, she all I think about (Everywhere)"], "meaning": "The whole verse is talking about a relationship that is purely physical, and implied to be harmful for both people involved, but despite that ,they come back to eachother due to some twisted attraction.\n\nThemes of this twisted relationship are especially apparent in the second half of the verse where Yeat says:\n\n“You know what’s coming ahead\nYeah, you know you feel it again\nYeah, that’s why you turn around and come back again\nYeah, you come inside a dangerous house again”", "annotation_id": "39204455", "url": "https://genius.com/39204455", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Dangerous House", "line": "It’s a dangerous house, dangerous house here Dangerous house, dangerous (Come in) A dangerous house, dangerous house here (Come in) Dangerous house, dangerous house (Here)", "vault_lines": ["It's a dangerous house, dangerous house here"], "meaning": "Yeat is talking about a relationship which is dangerous for both people involved, not only emotionally but maybe even physically ,since in the refrain he says:\n\n“Yeah, all she ever hear is sirens (Woo-woo-woo)”\n\nThe same themes of a crumbling and nonfunctional relationship are also explored in the 15th track of the album “Went Wrong”", "annotation_id": "39174075", "url": "https://genius.com/39174075", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Dangerous House", "line": "It’s a dangerous house, dangerous house here Dangerous house, dangerous (Come in) A dangerous house, dangerous house here (Come in) Dangerous house, dangerous house (Here)", "vault_lines": ["It's a dangerous house, dangerous house here"], "meaning": "Yeat is talking about a relationship which is dangerous for both people involved, not only emotionally but maybe even physically ,since in the refrain he says:\n\n“Yeah, all she ever hear is sirens (Woo-woo-woo)”\n\nThe same themes of a crumbling and nonfunctional relationship are also explored in the 15th track of the album “Went Wrong”", "annotation_id": "39174053", "url": "https://genius.com/39174053", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Dangerous House", "line": "[Intro] All I think about, she all I think about (Everywhere) She all I think about, she all I think about (Put me out of the game) She all I think about, she all I think about (Everywhere) She all I think about, she— (Put me out of the game) It’s a shock, who are you? How come it’s so easy? How come it’s so easy?", "vault_lines": ["All I think about, she all I think about (Everywhere)"], "meaning": "Sampled from “loyal & marie” by Dijon\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HMQQJteBwdk", "annotation_id": "39157824", "url": "https://genius.com/39157824", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
