{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "DISEASE", "line": "You got your hand out so much, we chop your hand then", "vault_lines": ["You got your hand out so much, we chop your hand then"], "meaning": "When Yeat says “You got your hand out so much, we chop your hand then”, he’s using exaggerated, violent imagery to talk about cutting off freeloaders. “Hand out” refers to people constantly asking for money, favors, or clout without contributing anything. “Chop your hand” isn’t literal, but a metaphor for shutting them out completely, cutting access, or removing them from his circle. The line reinforces Yeat’s theme of self-reliance and intolerance for leeches once success is achieved.", "annotation_id": "38716906", "url": "https://genius.com/38716906", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "DISEASE", "line": "And you want to get head like me But you never seen what I’ve seen", "vault_lines": ["And you want to get head like me"], "meaning": "Yeat draws a line between desire and experience. Others want his status but haven’t endured the pressure, chaos, or transformation that came with it.", "annotation_id": "38603297", "url": "https://genius.com/38603297", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "DISEASE", "line": "And you want to get head like me But you never seen what I’ve seen", "vault_lines": ["And you want to get head like me"], "meaning": "Yeat draws a line between desire and experience. Others want his status but haven’t endured the pressure, chaos, or transformation that came with it.", "annotation_id": "38603294", "url": "https://genius.com/38603294", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "DISEASE", "line": "Yeah, ’cause I got so much of this cheese", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, 'cause I got so much of this cheese"], "meaning": "“Cheese” is slang for money. Yeat emphasizes abundance to the point it feels overwhelming, reinforcing wealth as a core theme.", "annotation_id": "38603285", "url": "https://genius.com/38603285", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "DISEASE", "line": "And I got so much of this bread, it’s like it’s creepin’ on me, a disease", "vault_lines": ["And I got so much of this bread, it's like it's creepin' on me, a disease"], "meaning": "He personifies money as something uncontrollable and consuming, suggesting excess wealth has become unavoidable and almost burdensome.", "annotation_id": "38603281", "url": "https://genius.com/38603281", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "DISEASE", "line": "Yeah, ’cause I got so much of this cheese", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, 'cause I got so much of this cheese"], "meaning": "“Cheese” is slang for money. Yeat emphasizes abundance to the point it feels overwhelming, reinforcing wealth as a core theme.", "annotation_id": "38603274", "url": "https://genius.com/38603274", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "DISEASE", "line": "And I got so much of this bread, it’s like it’s creepin’ on me, a disease", "vault_lines": ["And I got so much of this bread, it's like it's creepin' on me, a disease"], "meaning": "He personifies money as something uncontrollable and consuming, suggesting excess wealth has become unavoidable and almost burdensome.", "annotation_id": "38603270", "url": "https://genius.com/38603270", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "DISEASE", "line": "Yeah, it won’t ever be the same, you don’t understand it", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, it won't ever be the same, you don't understand it"], "meaning": "This reflects the permanent shift success brings. Yeat emphasizes that once he reached this level, his mindset and life became fundamentally different from those who stayed behind.", "annotation_id": "38603268", "url": "https://genius.com/38603268", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
