{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "D I E", "line": "He finna die, D-I-E (Die) He finna die (Yeah), D-I-E (Die) He finna die (Yeah), D-I-E (Die) He finna die (Yeah), D-I-E (Die), yeah (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["He finna die, D-I-E (Die)"], "meaning": "The amount of drugs consumed and digested by Yeat that he would take daily makes him certain that another person would die with his level of intoxication.\n\nContrarily, Yeat’s main intent in this song is to seek out a foe of his who has been talking recklessly, arriving to their location and then camping outside (preferably in his Tonka) with high-end firearm weapons.", "annotation_id": "31181705", "url": "https://genius.com/31181705", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
