{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Crashëd dat bitch", "line": "That’s taxiderm’", "vault_lines": ["Killed my opp and put him in my living room, that's taxiderm'"], "meaning": "“that’s taxidermy”\n\nTaxidermy is the art of preserving an animal’s body, people usually do this with wildlife but Uzi is insinuating he is ruthless and will do this to the opposition.", "annotation_id": "28225083", "url": "https://genius.com/28225083", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Crashëd dat bitch", "line": "(Damn, Trgc made that?)", "vault_lines": ["Riding in that Tonka, you can't see me, windows black, ha (Damn, Trgc made that?)"], "meaning": "Trgc is an American record producer and frequent collaborator of Yeat. He is known for his production with Yeat, Lil Yachty, SoFaygo, and Yung Mal.\n\nThe duo have collaborated together on previous tracks; most notably on tracks such as “Monëy so big,” “Sorry Bout That,” and “Money Twërk” which also appear to be some of Yeat’s biggest-hits to date.\n\nTrgc is the most frequent producing collaborator of Yeat’s two studio albums, 2 Alivë and Up 2 Më, developing such a chemistry with the artist allowing a musical-adroitness from the duo.", "annotation_id": "25791606", "url": "https://genius.com/25791606", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
