{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Can’t stop it", "line": "Yerc after Perc’, after Yerc, I can’t stop", "vault_lines": ["Yerc after Perc', after Yerc, I can't stop"], "meaning": "Yeat is addicted to drugs but a drug he constantly talks about are “percs” more commonly known as “Percocets” In this line he talks about he constantly does drugs and cant stop.", "annotation_id": "30928953", "url": "https://genius.com/30928953", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Can’t stop it", "line": "I bought a crib in the sky (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I bought a crib in the sky (Yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat here indicates that he has “bought a crib in the sky” this can imply two things : Yeat has bought a house in the hills, referring to it as a “crib in the sky” due to the fact it is high up. However it could also mean that Yeat has bought a (penthouse) apartment, apartments are most of the time the time high up with penthouses being on the top. Therefore Yeat calls this a “crib in the sky”", "annotation_id": "27656218", "url": "https://genius.com/27656218", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Can’t stop it", "line": "R.I.P. to the dumbass kid, gon’ try geeked up on syrup", "vault_lines": ["R.I.P. to the dumbass kid, gon' try geeked up on syrup"], "meaning": "YEAT mentions codeine (syrup) quite often in his music, and the pleasures of getting intoxicated (geeked.) The lyric acknowledges his influence on the youth. YEAT, while he glamorizes the drug, he warns his audience of the dangers of substance abuse and how codeine can actually cause harm. YEAT preemptively sends his condolences to the kids that didn’t listen to his advice.", "annotation_id": "26729438", "url": "https://genius.com/26729438", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Can’t stop it", "line": "Don’t know why I did this shit, just heard it and I do it", "vault_lines": ["Don't know why I did this shit, just heard it and I do it"], "meaning": "Yeat has an infamous backstory to his rap career, some think he doesnt actually like his career due to the amount of times he has said something similar to this stanza", "annotation_id": "26699523", "url": "https://genius.com/26699523", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Can’t stop it", "line": "Takin’ the yanky, more janky, more banky", "vault_lines": ["Takin' the yanky, more janky, more banky"], "meaning": "With each drug, or “yanky,” that Yeat takes, the more unstable, or “janky,” he becomes. However, as he continues to take drugs to enhance his creative process, he sees more success in the music industry, rising to new heights with each release. Thus, he’s willing to sacrifice his mental and physical health to generate a fortune, or “banky.”", "annotation_id": "26679206", "url": "https://genius.com/26679206", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Can’t stop it", "line": "You gon’ get whacked, you gon’ get whacked like a spanking (Mm-hm)", "vault_lines": ["You gon' get whacked, you gon' get whacked like a spanking (Mm-hm)"], "meaning": "To have someone “whacked” is Italian-American slang meaning to have someone killed, which Yeat compares to a spanking, which is often done by parents to discipline a misbehaving child. Thus, in keeping with the song’s violent tones, Yeat threatens to have his opps killed.", "annotation_id": "26679198", "url": "https://genius.com/26679198", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Can’t stop it", "line": "I been swervin’ off the Earth", "vault_lines": ["I been swervin' off the Earth"], "meaning": "“Swervin'” can mean being under the influence of large amounts of alcohol or drugs, or, more specifically, driving while under the influence. Thus, Yeat is so high that he could (metaphorically) leave the Earth’s surface.", "annotation_id": "26679181", "url": "https://genius.com/26679181", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Can’t stop it", "line": "Yeah, I learned my lesson, for these jakes, I say they shworms Thought they was gon get eat up like a fish, get eat by worm", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I learned my lesson, for these jakes, I say they shworms"], "meaning": "Yeat recounts a learning experience\n\n“Jakes” is a slang term that has had several meanings over the years. Historically, it was a slang word for lavatories, however, these days it is mostly used to refer to police.\n\nThus, Yeat views the police as “fish,” “worms,” or “shworms,” meaning that they insignificant low-life creatures that will be “eaten up” or killed if they mess with him and his crew.", "annotation_id": "26679167", "url": "https://genius.com/26679167", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Can’t stop it", "line": "I got the big ol’ whip, got a big ol’ Glock, got the big ol’ stick with a binkie (What? Shh)", "vault_lines": ["I got the big ol' whip, got a big ol' Glock, got the big ol' stick with a binkie (What? Shh)"], "meaning": "Yeat lists several of his possessions, including an SUV, which is presumably a reference to his Mercedes-Benz AMG GLE Coupé, a Glock-brand pistol, and a large firearm with a silencer, or “binkie” as it is referred to here.", "annotation_id": "26679150", "url": "https://genius.com/26679150", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Can’t stop it", "line": "Yeah, they gon’ copy my trend, they gon’ copy my sound, they gon’ copy the guy", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, they gon' copy my trend, they gon' copy my sound, they gon' copy the guy"], "meaning": "In his relatively short time in the hip-hop game, he has already started many trends and popularized his own lingo. He previously discussed his influence on the track “Trënds & Topics.”", "annotation_id": "26679136", "url": "https://genius.com/26679136", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Can’t stop it", "line": "On the phone with my demon, we build it up and then retire", "vault_lines": ["On the phone with my demon, we build it up and then retire"], "meaning": "Yeat indicates that he knows his actions to be immoral, yet he does what he must to build his fortune.\n\nThe term “demon” refers to a savage individual who is willing to harm or kill anyone who gets in their way.\n\nAt this point in his life, Yeat is prepared to conduct heinous actions, such as (presumably) selling drugs and hitting licks, in the pursuit of wealth before denouncing a life of crime.", "annotation_id": "26679120", "url": "https://genius.com/26679120", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Can’t stop it", "line": "Diamonds in my pinkie, yeah, the diamonds on my hair", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds in my pinkie, yeah, the diamonds on my hair"], "meaning": "Yeat is saying that he’s go so much jewelry that they’re basically on every part of his body. Including his own hair and pinkie. Yeat has been known to acquire expensive jewelry. Even talking about it in his songs, and exclusive interviews.", "annotation_id": "26673085", "url": "https://genius.com/26673085", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
