{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Cant trust me", "line": "I’m in 2093, I’m drinkin’ alien, ballin’", "vault_lines": ["I'm in 2093, I'm drinkin' alien, ballin'"], "meaning": "This line is a direct callback to Yeat’s interview with Andrew Callaghan on Channel 5 in July 2022. When asked what he would do if he had a time machine, Yeat responded:\n\n“I’ll go to the future, like six million years, see what’s going on. They’d probably be in like spaceships drinking like alien lean.”\n\nAlien lean in 2022 was a high idea of his. In his 2093 world building he is living this hypothetical and manifesting his own lore.", "annotation_id": "38437893", "url": "https://genius.com/38437893", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
