{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "COMË N GO", "line": "I’m, I’m, I’m in her pink walls, I’ma call her asbestos", "vault_lines": ["I'm, I'm, I'm in her pink walls, I'ma call her asbestos"], "meaning": "“Pink walls” is slang for the inside of a vagina. Yeat flips it into a construction joke by calling her “asbestos,” which is something found inside building walls. It’s a mix of sexual imagery and wordplay, with the asbestos part also hinting she might be risky or “dangerous” to mess with.", "annotation_id": "36517771", "url": "https://genius.com/36517771", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
