{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bëttr 0ff", "line": "When you count that bread, this shit get dough", "vault_lines": ["When you count that bread, this shit get dough"], "meaning": "This lyric uses a play on words to convey a message about financial success. “Counting bread” is a slang term for counting money, specifically referring to counting stacks of bills. The phrase “this shit get dough” suggests that when you count money or accumulate wealth (dough being a slang term for money), it increases or grows, indicating that financial success leads to even more prosperity. Essentially, the lyric implies that when you focus on accumulating wealth, your financial situation improves and grows.", "annotation_id": "31092077", "url": "https://genius.com/31092077", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
