{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bought The Earth", "line": "Don’t tell me twice, put it on the—, fuck that", "vault_lines": ["Don't tell me twice, put it on the—, fuck that"], "meaning": "Yeat was about to say “put it on the Bible” but instead says on the person’s life", "annotation_id": "32617288", "url": "https://genius.com/32617288", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bought The Earth", "line": "I bought the Earth, I sold it too I’d sell ya’ whole life if I could too", "vault_lines": ["I bought the Earth, I sold it too"], "meaning": "The repetition of “I bought the earth, I sold it too” highlights his control and the transitory nature of his possessions.", "annotation_id": "31342483", "url": "https://genius.com/31342483", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bought The Earth", "line": "When it comes night, always on the loose When it comes night, what you gon’ do? I don’t need the light, I see right through I see your reflection in my rearview Damn, what a good view Damn, what we could do? Damn, I’m paranoid and rude Damn, more disrespectful than you thought you knew", "vault_lines": ["I don't hear a word when you talk"], "meaning": "The outro suggests a sense of resignation and acceptance of the consequences, questioning whether their pain brings freedom to others.", "annotation_id": "31342450", "url": "https://genius.com/31342450", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bought The Earth", "line": "And I know why you confused, I got a way with words Is it money? Is it power? Which one first?", "vault_lines": ["And I know why you confused, I got a way with words"], "meaning": "In that case, the lines suggest that Yeat is reflecting on his own ability to use persuasive language to influence others. He questions whether the person he’s addressing is driven more by money or power, indicating his awareness of the power dynamics at play and his ability to navigate them to his advantage.", "annotation_id": "31342437", "url": "https://genius.com/31342437", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bought The Earth", "line": "Yeah, I know it’s not all great, but I love feelin’ this way", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I know it's not all great, but I love feelin' this way"], "meaning": "This line expresses a paradoxical sentiment where yeat acknowledges that not everything is perfect, yet they still enjoy the feeling they are experiencing. It reflects a complex emotional state where despite recognizing the imperfections, they find value and pleasure in the overall experience.", "annotation_id": "31342419", "url": "https://genius.com/31342419", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bought The Earth", "line": "Am I wrong for bein’ selfish? Am I wrong for puttin’ me first?", "vault_lines": ["Am I wrong for bein' selfish?"], "meaning": "A rhetorical question, nodding to events such as:\n\n-Changing his sound\n-Being off the drugs\n-His abandonment from the label “Twizzy Rich” after he got into a drama with his closest partner ‘Septembers Rich’\n\nWhatever it may be, these events could (and have) changed him for the better.", "annotation_id": "30942762", "url": "https://genius.com/30942762", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bought The Earth", "line": "(All day) I like a mixture (All day) Off the drugs, but I miss ’em (All day) I tried to warn you ’bout this shit, but you ain’t listen anyway (All day) I’m in 2093 all day", "vault_lines": ["(All day) I'm in 2093 all day"], "meaning": "He’s sober however he misses the drugs.\n“i tried to warn you ‘bout this shit..” could be a nod to songs like “Killin ëm” where he talked about drugs and their effect.\n\nHe has taken so much drugs throughout his life, that he feels as if he’s in the future, he’s in the year 2093.", "annotation_id": "30942737", "url": "https://genius.com/30942737", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bought The Earth", "line": "Paint a picture with some blood all day", "vault_lines": ["Paint a picture with some blood all day"], "meaning": "He feels like he needed to sacrifice his relationships in order to get what he wanted\nor to get what wants.\nHence the metaphor “Paint a picture with some blood”", "annotation_id": "30942726", "url": "https://genius.com/30942726", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bought The Earth", "line": "I’ll never look back on the bridge I burned", "vault_lines": ["I'll never look back on the bridge I burned"], "meaning": "He’ll never look back at the things he left.\n\nThis could refer to the different sounds he’s been through, or perhaps the label “twizzy rich” he made and left due to behind the scenes drama including his falling out with his closest partner “Septembers Rich”", "annotation_id": "30919879", "url": "https://genius.com/30919879", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
