{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Ball On Em 2", "line": "Yeah, I seen ’em fall off, it turn fall on ’em (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I seen 'em fall off, it turn fall on 'em (Yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Yeat references his oppositions in the rap game that he has witnessed rise and lose traction in popularity. He makes a comparison of their fall from grace to the falling off of leaves when the fall season comes in.\n\nThis is likely a diss on Autumn! (Twinuzis), a rapper who has been in repeated tensions with Yeat over the last year. Autumn!’s stage name is the secondary title of the season commonly known as Fall, and over the course of the two underground giants' beef, fans have been claiming that Autumn! is/has been falling off.", "annotation_id": "26641300", "url": "https://genius.com/26641300", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
