{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bak on ëm", "line": "How the hell you sip fake drop?", "vault_lines": ["How the hell you sip fake drop?"], "meaning": "“Drop” in this context could refer to “wock” or “Lean”, a drink containing promethazine, activis, or codeine in conjunction with Sprite and candy. Noah Oliver Smith questions the people he’s speaking to asking them how they are consuming fake “lean”.", "annotation_id": "25914887", "url": "https://genius.com/25914887", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bak on ëm", "line": "With the Percs, there ain’t never a drought", "vault_lines": ["With the Percs, there ain't never a drought"], "meaning": "Yeat (Noah Oliver Smith) claims that with the percs (Percocet 30) there is never a drought. When the presence of water is vast and plentiful there could never be a drought. Smith makes this connection by claiming the percs are as bountiful as water.", "annotation_id": "25418305", "url": "https://genius.com/25418305", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bak on ëm", "line": "Yeah, I been doing that shit for a while", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I been doing that shit for a while"], "meaning": "Yeat here can be talking about different things here, but most likely he means\n\n-Rapping; his first tracks go back to 2017-2018, notably with his 3-track project “Deep Blue Strips”\n\n\n\n-Drugs; he has admitted to taking many drugs since he was a teenager in different interviews and songs", "annotation_id": "23936909", "url": "https://genius.com/23936909", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
