{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Bak in town", "line": "I’m back in town (Doo-doo-doo-doo, yeah, phew, woo)", "vault_lines": ["I'm back in town"], "meaning": "Yeat expresses that he is back in Los Angeles or preferably the town known as Palm Springs, which is located in central Riverside County in California.\n\nYeat has stated that he has visited Palm Spring before, such as on the song ‘How culd I change’\n“Got a crib in East LA and Palm Springs”\n\nWhich connects to his lyricism here as there is an airport connected right across from the town.", "annotation_id": "36850255", "url": "https://genius.com/36850255", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
