{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "BRIGHTS ON", "line": "We know you dying you dead you fried", "vault_lines": [", huh (Yeah) we know you dying you dead you fried"], "meaning": "The lyric tells us a message about someone who is struggling with their mental and emotional well-being, possibly due to external pressures or internal conflicts. It reflects themes of vulnerability and the challenges of maintaining composure in a demanding environment.", "annotation_id": "35403528", "url": "https://genius.com/35403528", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "BRIGHTS ON", "line": "Rap by the freeway and then hit the 10 (Fire)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, and that made me fire, rap by the freeway and then hit the 10 (Fire)"], "meaning": "This lyric tells us a message about Yeat’s ability to create outstanding music in any setting, achieving top-tier success and recognition. It reflects his confidence and the high quality of his work, suggesting that he can produce “fire” tracks even in unconventional circumstances.", "annotation_id": "35403454", "url": "https://genius.com/35403454", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "BRIGHTS ON", "line": "Put you in the sky you don’t know where you at or where you been", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, put you in the sky you don't know where you at or where you been"], "meaning": "Together, the lyric conveys a message about the disorienting effects of sudden elevation or success. It reflects on how being thrust into a new, high-status environment can lead to confusion and a loss of self-awareness. This theme aligns with Yeat’s exploration of the complexities and challenges that come with fame and success.", "annotation_id": "35403438", "url": "https://genius.com/35403438", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "BRIGHTS ON", "line": "We put you outside call you “Ceiling Fan”", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you blowing like the wind, we put you outside call you \"Ceiling Fan\""], "meaning": "The lyric conveys a message of rejecting or mocking someone who is overly eager or obsessed, labeling them as a “Silly Fan” and pushing them out of the inner circle. This reflects themes of exclusivity and the dynamics of social groups, where individuals who don’t fit in or act inappropriately are cast aside.", "annotation_id": "35403424", "url": "https://genius.com/35403424", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "BRIGHTS ON", "line": "But she done at the ten", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, put you in the sky you don't know where you at or where you been"], "meaning": "The lyric suggests that the woman has completed her actions or is finished with something by a specific time or point. In the context of Yeat’s music, which often explores themes of relationships and lifestyle, this could imply a transient or casual interaction, where the woman’s involvement is limited to a certain time or situation.", "annotation_id": "35403410", "url": "https://genius.com/35403410", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "BRIGHTS ON", "line": "We trapping like perks again", "vault_lines": ["We trapping like perks again"], "meaning": "Together, the lyric conveys a sense of being under constant surveillance and scrutiny, likening it to the obsessive tracking associated with addictive substances. It reflects the pressures and challenges that come with fame, where personal actions are closely watched and analyzed by others.", "annotation_id": "35403404", "url": "https://genius.com/35403404", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "BRIGHTS ON", "line": "You hold it up when you dead", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, put you in the sky you don't know where you at or where you been"], "meaning": "In the context of Yeat’s music, which often explores themes of resilience, status, and the pressures of fame, this line suggests that even in challenging or low moments—metaphorically referred to as being “dead\"—one continues to maintain their image, reputation, or lifestyle. It’s about perseverance and the determination to uphold one’s identity and success, regardless of circumstances.", "annotation_id": "35403361", "url": "https://genius.com/35403361", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
