{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Always Alivë", "line": "I’m feeling blessed like I just sneezed", "vault_lines": ["I'm feeling blessed like I just sneezed"], "meaning": "This line is a pun that draws a connection between two meanings of the word “blessed.” When someone sneezes, people say “Bless you” as a way to show respect. Yeat turns this common phrase into a lyrical bar to show fortune and success — simply implying he feels “blessed” in life like a sneeze.", "annotation_id": "34088879", "url": "https://genius.com/34088879", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
