{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Already Said It", "line": "I need the face, need the Helmut Lang", "vault_lines": ["We go insane, yeah, I need the face, need the Helmut Lang"], "meaning": "Yeat uses “Helmut Lang” as a double entendre. On the surface, he is referencing the luxury fashion brand, but “Helmut” sounds like “helmet,” something worn to protect the head. Paired with “I need the face,” the line becomes a sexual play on words, with “head” being implied through the helmet reference.", "annotation_id": "40646302", "url": "https://genius.com/40646302", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Already Said It", "line": "Dinner with a rich bitch, I told that bitch, “You could pay”", "vault_lines": ["Dinner with a rich bitch, I told that bitch, \"You could pay\""], "meaning": "In this bar Yeat flexes that his girls are rich too, as he is able to ask them to pay if he wants.\nUnlike some dudes who only date baddie broke girls who want their money, Yeat can date bad bitches who dnt even gotta be going w him. he flexing that bitches arent js w him for his bread", "annotation_id": "37634436", "url": "https://genius.com/37634436", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
