{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Already Rich", "line": "Woah, I just left the earth (Brr), still not as high as Yeat (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Woah, I just left the earth (Brr), still not as high as Yeat (Ooh)"], "meaning": "Yeat metaphorically states that, if one were to leave the Earth’s atmosphere, they’d still not reach his current level of intoxication. Yeat also speaks in third person when referring to himself, which indicates that he is more intoxicated than one could possibly imagine.", "annotation_id": "26678943", "url": "https://genius.com/26678943", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Already Rich", "line": "This bitch, she just ask me if I got a Tonka for really, I told her, “I got a X6” (Woo, woo)", "vault_lines": ["This bitch, she just ask me if I got a Tonka for really, I told her, \"I got a X6\" (Woo, woo)"], "meaning": "Yeat brags about his BMW X6, a car which is large enough to be classified as a ‘Tonka’, to one of his female companions", "annotation_id": "26678926", "url": "https://genius.com/26678926", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Already Rich", "line": "Bringin’ the whip out the back wit’ the tinted windows, bitch, I feel like the president (President)", "vault_lines": ["Bringin' the whip out the back wit' the tinted windows, bitch, I feel like the president (President)"], "meaning": "In most “The Batman” interpretations bruce Wayne commonly has a “batmobile” which is an all-black motor vehicle with an illegal amount of tint to make the windows darker. Often times in luxury vehicles rappers and celebrities will tint their windows to maintain their privacy.\n\nThe President Of The United States(POTUS) is transported from location to location with a lot of military backup and completely tinted bulletproof windows for his protection. Yeat states that with his tinted windows he feels like the president as they both use very tinted windows in their motor vehicles.", "annotation_id": "25914799", "url": "https://genius.com/25914799", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Already Rich", "line": "And I just be callin’ up Eliantte for new diamonds, I told ’em to turn on the sink (Shine)", "vault_lines": ["And I just be callin' up Eliantte for new diamonds, I told 'em to turn on the sink (Shine)"], "meaning": "Elliante, Elliante & Co, is a jewelry brand commonly referenced by yeat(see big stonëz). Elliante produces chains and jewelry for the rap and hip-hop community.\n\nWhen yeat says “turn on the sink(shine)” he’s asking Elliante to turn on the “sink” so his new diamonds are “wet”. Wet diamonds refer to “drip” which is a slang word for jewelry or good-looking clothes.", "annotation_id": "25914768", "url": "https://genius.com/25914768", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
