{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "All typëz", "line": "I just poured up a deuce, but it’s not a Sprite", "vault_lines": ["I just poured up a deuce, but it's not a Sprite (Not a sprite)"], "meaning": "A “deuce” is slang for two fluid ounces, and in this context Yeat is referring to two ounces of codeine/promethazine cough syrup, commonly associated with lean.\n\nLean is commonly mixed with a soft drink, especially Sprite. By saying “but it’s not a Sprite,” Yeat implies that although he poured a deuce of syrup, he mixed it into a different drink rather than the stereotypical Sprite mixture.", "annotation_id": "41612913", "url": "https://genius.com/41612913", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
