{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "All Different", "line": "At the end of the day I’m still alive I can’t take back what I did, there’s no point in trying You can see the drug damage in my eyes", "vault_lines": ["At the end of the day I'm still alive"], "meaning": "Yeat’s drug habits are no secret; he boasts about how many Percs and X he takes in nearly every song of his. But in the outro to All Different, he’s much more sensitive to their effects on his body. However it’s too late for Yeat to quit: the damage has already been done to his body, and he’s still alive, so why would he try to stop now?", "annotation_id": "29555113", "url": "https://genius.com/29555113", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
