{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "All Different", "line": "My pockets filled with caskets (Hold up), and presidents", "vault_lines": ["My pockets filled with caskets (Hold up), and presidents"], "meaning": "A casket serves as a burial container for the deceased, mainly used during funerals.\n\nThe $50 bill and $100 bill both have the face of dead ex-Presidents. The $100 bill being Benjamin Franklin, who passed away April 17, 1790.\n\nYeat creates a play on words to indicate that his pockets are filled with a large amount of money, hence why the reference to past presidents was added onto the line.", "annotation_id": "25991290", "url": "https://genius.com/25991290", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
