{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Aint Us", "line": "I’m cuttin’ ties with all them broke boys, I brought the scissors", "vault_lines": ["I'm cuttin' ties with all them broke boys, I brought the scissors"], "meaning": "Yeat says he is cutting off the “broke boys” he came up with, suggesting he is switching up on some of his day-one friends now that he has become successful. “I brought the scissors” extends the phrase “cutting ties” into a literal image, emphasizing that the separation is intentional and final.", "annotation_id": "40646657", "url": "https://genius.com/40646657", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
