{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Aint Us", "line": "I wake up, take a X, then take a Perc’, then lay awake", "vault_lines": ["I wake up, take a X, then take a Perc', then lay awake"], "meaning": "These lyrics are incorrect.\nThe real lyrics are: “I wake up, take a X, then take a Perc', to land with”\n\nthis makes a lot more sense as a X is a upper and a perc is a downer. So he wakes up, takes a X pill and “flies high as fuck” , but because he needs to come down and and chill out he takes and perc to “land with”.\n\nListen to the song n u will hear land with ive never heard “lay awake”. though yeat does have themes of being awake for extended peroids of time, he also feqently refereces “flying high with the gods” and being a “plane” and “flying everyday” so it also makes sense he would need a downer to land.", "annotation_id": "37655571", "url": "https://genius.com/37655571", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
