{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "Aint Try (Tried Once)", "line": "They say, “How many times you died?” I only died once", "vault_lines": ["They say, \"How many times you died?\" I only died once"], "meaning": "In slang terms, “dying” refers to a rapper / artists losing popularity overtime. However, this line refers to when Yeat actually died from overdose in 2020, where he had to be shocked back to life.\n\n\n\nYeat saying he “only died once” refers to him saying that he still hasn’t lost fame, saying his only death was his overdose.", "annotation_id": "30782819", "url": "https://genius.com/30782819", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
