{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "5 2 Üh 60", "line": "They wondering, how much did I make? Fuck it, fifty figures", "vault_lines": ["They wondering, how much did I make? Fuck it, fifty figures"], "meaning": "SeptembersRich claims to be so rich he makes 50 figures. Which would be 10 quindecillion or $10,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000. This is 10 decillion times more than the all the money in the world. SeptembersRich is literally fucking god.", "annotation_id": "25993897", "url": "https://genius.com/25993897", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "5 2 Üh 60", "line": "My twizzy way too crazy smokin’ fronto leaf", "vault_lines": ["My twizzy way too crazy smokin' fronto leaf"], "meaning": "Fronto leaf, also known as Grabba leaf, is an alternative to traditional rolling papers. It’s a tobacco leaf that’s air-cured to develop a rich taste and aroma and is known for being darker than other cigar and blunt leaves, due to the curing process and lack of further artificial processing.\n\nYeat puts us in the know by revealing his twizzy may be insane due to his preference for smoking leaf over papers.", "annotation_id": "24963453", "url": "https://genius.com/24963453", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "5 2 Üh 60", "line": "Y’all be cappin’ ’bout the fashion, y’all some Helmut lames", "vault_lines": ["Y'all be cappin' 'bout the fashion, y'all some Helmut lames"], "meaning": "Yeat refers to the Austrian fashion designer and brand Helmut Lang as a play on words. Helmut Lang is famous for minimalist designs and deconstructed pieces, regaining popularity in recent years despite conflicting opinions on the brand.\n\nSwitching “Lang” for “lame”, Yeat shames those who aren’t up to his standards style and brand wise.", "annotation_id": "24875023", "url": "https://genius.com/24875023", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "5 2 Üh 60", "line": "They said I’m new wave from my sound to my lettering", "vault_lines": ["They said I'm new wave from my sound to my lettering"], "meaning": "Yeat is attributing his success to his marketing technique. Reasonably so, he’s right. The artist popularized a new sound and his own take on rage music, of which the artist has been the undisputed face of in 2021. Since his 3-peat album tear, artists such as Swae Lee, Coi Leray & Kid Buu have all copied his sound, and artists such as UnoTheActivist, Lil Yachty, Drake & Lil Uzi Vert have either worked with the artist or showed interest in collaborating with him.\n\nIn addition to Yeat’s sound, his lettering style has also been a key factor in marketing himself to becoming a household name in the current soundcloud scene. The artist has made himself stand out by typing in manners as follows:\n\n“Lüh Crankem”, “Shmunky” & “All Daë”\n\nThis unorthodox way of typography has made tracks such as Gët Busy, Monëy so Big, Monëy Twerk & Not Tha Samë bring the artist millions of streams individually. This is the reference the artist uses for why people call him new wave.", "annotation_id": "24825004", "url": "https://genius.com/24825004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
