{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3G", "line": "Stackin’ them rackies up, stand like three feet (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Stackin' them rackies up, stand like three feet (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Here Lil Uzi Vert describes the action of placing currency (U.S. Dollars) On top of one another, symbolizing his great abundance in the rather thin currency (.0043 inches), explaining that the height of the bills will reach 3 feet once stacked.", "annotation_id": "27809168", "url": "https://genius.com/27809168", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3G", "line": "I just woke up, take a X for the boot up", "vault_lines": ["I just woke up, take a X for the boot up"], "meaning": "Yeat is talking about X (molly), and putting it into the form of a liquid to “boot up” or inject it.", "annotation_id": "25753251", "url": "https://genius.com/25753251", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3G", "line": "I just called up my lil’ demon, he told me to take every Perc’ ’til it’s gone (Boot)", "vault_lines": ["I just called up my lil' demon, he told me to take every Perc' 'til it's gone (Boot)"], "meaning": "Yeat commonly talks about his demons and selling his soul.\n\nIn Yeat’s song “Lying 4 Fun”, Yeat says, “Linked with the devil, told him I just need a signature, need his autograph\nI ain’t never sold my soul but I just donated it to you”\n\n\n\nA Perc is the nickname for the painkiller known as Percocets, that contains a combination of Oxycodone (a semi-Synthetic Opiate).\n\nYeat is referring to his drug usage", "annotation_id": "25708312", "url": "https://genius.com/25708312", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3G", "line": "Takin’ the molly, the better batch", "vault_lines": ["Takin' the molly, the better batch"], "meaning": "3,4-Methyl​enedioxy​methamphetamine, commonly known as ecstasy or molly, is a psychoactive drug primarily used for recreational purposes.\n\nLil Uzi Vert is referring to his usage of molly.", "annotation_id": "25708281", "url": "https://genius.com/25708281", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3G", "line": "I done pulled up with a whole lot of guap", "vault_lines": ["I done pulled up with a whole lot of guap"], "meaning": "Guap is a large sum of money. Uzi has referenced the word guap in many songs, most notably on the Young Thug assisted “Got The Guap” from his album, LUV vs The World 2.\n\nYou know Mr. Lil Uzi got the guap\nI swear, Mr. Lil Uzi got the guap", "annotation_id": "25673404", "url": "https://genius.com/25673404", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3G", "line": "Out my mind, bitch, I’m feeling like Buddha (Out my mind)", "vault_lines": ["Out my mind, bitch, I'm feeling like Buddha (Out my mind)"], "meaning": "Gautama Buddha, simply known as Buddha, was a leader and teacher of the renowned world religion Buddhism. The name Buddha translates to “awakened one” or “to know.”\n\nYeat states that he’s out of his mind from drugs, unlike Buddha who achieves his out-of-mind state by meditation practices and peacefulness.", "annotation_id": "25579496", "url": "https://genius.com/25579496", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3G", "line": "Yeah, Mike Jackson, hee-hee (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, Mike Jackson, hee-hee (What?)"], "meaning": "He is making the noise Michael Jackson made.", "annotation_id": "25544442", "url": "https://genius.com/25544442", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3G", "line": "I’ve been countin’ racks ever since 3G (Racks)", "vault_lines": ["I've been countin' racks ever since 3G (Racks)"], "meaning": "3G is the third generation of wireless mobile telecommunications technology. It was the upgrade over 2G, 2.5G, GPRS and 2.75G EDGE networks, offering faster data transfer, and better voice quality. This network was superseded by 4G, and later on 5G.\n\nSo by means, Lil Uzi Vert in this verse claims he’s been getting money ever since 3G was introduced (2002).", "annotation_id": "25500931", "url": "https://genius.com/25500931", "state": "pending", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3G", "line": "Where am I? (Woah) Yeah, yeah, outer space (Oh, my God) Yeah (What?), outer space (What? Yeah) Yeah (Huh?), outer space (Oh, my God), yeah (What?) [Chorus: Lil Uzi Vert] Outer space, outer space (What? Oh, my God) Outer space, outer space (Where am I?) Outer space, outer space (Huh? Oh, my God) Outer space, outer space (Woah) Outer space, outer space (Huh? Oh, my God) Outer space, outer space (Yeah) Outer space, outer space (What?) Outer space, outer space (Yeah, ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, yeah, outer space (Oh, my God)"], "meaning": "Uzi is frequently known for calling himself a celestial being who isn’t from Earth and is from outer space; an example of this would be on “Venetia”:\n\nAnd I’m not from earth, I’m from outer space (Woah, let’s go)\nAnd I’m different (Uh), I’m wavy", "annotation_id": "25487346", "url": "https://genius.com/25487346", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3G", "line": "Fuckin’ that bitch and her aunt, yeah (Huh?)", "vault_lines": ["Fuckin' that bitch and her aunt, yeah (Huh?)"], "meaning": "UZI has mentioned this bar before in his popular song from Eternal Atake “Myron” where he mentions: “Cause I could fuck your bitch and fuck your mom and auntie”", "annotation_id": "25487341", "url": "https://genius.com/25487341", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3G", "line": "I’ve been up inside that Tonk’, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I've been up inside that Tonk', yeah"], "meaning": "A “Tonk'” (Shortened version of Tonka) is a car which was popularized by Yeat himself, the Tonka trend first started after Yeat made a song called “Tonka” off his album Alivë, which blew up on TikTok and other social medias. On his track “Still Countin” he also talks about he was the first one on the music to do a trend about the car.\n\nRacks came in, I was still in the Tonka, ha (Ooh-ooh)\nRacks came in, they can’t fit in this Tonka, ha (Ooh)\nRacks came in, but I’m still in this Tonka, yeah (Ooh-ooh)\nSeven mill' on the table and I’m still sayin' Tonka, yeah (Ooh-ooh)", "annotation_id": "25483425", "url": "https://genius.com/25483425", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3G", "status": "done", "targets": 13, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-3g-lyrics", "genius_title": "3G", "genius_id": 7695024, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3AM", "line": "Double C, Double C, Double C, Double C, Double C, Double C", "vault_lines": ["Double C, Double C, Double C, Double C, Double C, Double C"], "meaning": "“Double C” refers to Chanel, a prestigious French fashion brand founded by Coco Chanel. The interlocking C’s in its logo represent timeless elegance and luxury. In this case, “yeat” is referring to Chanel, highlighting its exclusivity due to high costs. People gravitate towards Chanel products to showcase opulence and sophistication, making it a symbol of status and refined fashion taste.", "annotation_id": "29414372", "url": "https://genius.com/29414372", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3AM", "line": "Moncleezy", "vault_lines": ["I see you in that same Moncleezy"], "meaning": "Moncleezy refers to Moncler, a luxury fashion brand known for its high-end winter clothing and accessories. In this case, “yeat” is discussing a Moncleezy jacket, which combines style and warmth for colder seasons. People choose Moncler products for their fashionable yet functional designs, particularly their iconic down jackets and coats.", "annotation_id": "29414346", "url": "https://genius.com/29414346", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3AM", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-3am-lyrics", "genius_title": "3AM", "genius_id": 8546872, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3093* / Big body*", "line": "Guns in the trunk of the bed (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Guns in the trunk of the bed (Woo)"], "meaning": "“Guns in the trunk of the bed” likely refers to firearms being stored in the trunk of a car or in the bed of a pickup truck. The “trunk” is the enclosed cargo area in the rear of most cars, while the “bed” refers to the open cargo area of a pickup truck.", "annotation_id": "32230609", "url": "https://genius.com/32230609", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3093* / Big body*", "line": "Benz, big, body (Body)", "vault_lines": ["Benz, big, body (Body)"], "meaning": "“Benz big body” is a slang term used to refer to a large and luxurious Mercedes-Benz vehicle, typically one of their high-end models with a spacious and impressive body style. The term “big body” emphasizes the size and luxury of the car, highlighting its status and presence on the road.", "annotation_id": "32230600", "url": "https://genius.com/32230600", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "3093* / Big body*", "line": "Yeah, we leave everybody on read (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we leave everybody on read (Huh)"], "meaning": "“Leaving someone on read” refers to the situation where someone reads a message sent via a text messaging or social media app but does not respond to it, yeat is saying he doesnt gaf about anyone and leaves them on read", "annotation_id": "32230596", "url": "https://genius.com/32230596", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
