{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2TONE", "line": "My Victoria Just let this be a secret, your panties, girl, I’ll keep it, huh", "vault_lines": ["Just let this be a secret, your panties, girl, I'll keep it, huh"], "meaning": "“My Victoria / Just let this be a secret, your panties, girl, I’ll keep it, huh”\n\nDon Toliver makes a reference to the lingerie brand Victoria’s Secret. By saying “My Victoria” and “Just let this be a secret,” he alludes to both the brand’s name and a private intimate relationship.", "annotation_id": "36499651", "url": "https://genius.com/36499651", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2TONE", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-and-don-toliver-2tone-lyrics", "genius_title": "2TONE", "genius_id": 12042654, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2Planës", "line": "Money on the bed, money on the jet Money on the yacht, money on the top I got all this guap, I got all this bread I can’t feel the same, y’all can talk to feds Y’all the fuckin’ lames, y’all the fuckin’ snitches Y’all the fuckin’ brains, I got everything I got all this guap, I got all these bitches I got all the money, I get everything You don’t understand, I got all this shit Everything I want, everything I need Flexin’ when I want, doin’ what I want Talkin’ when I want, doin’ what I want Pull up to a show, do I wanna do it? I don’t fuckin’ know, I don’t fuckin’ care Every time I wanna fuckin’ do it I’ma build up in that buildin’ and I’ll do it there", "vault_lines": ["I got this guap, this shit gon' shake my fuckin' hand"], "meaning": "These lyrics are sampled from Yeat’s 2023 track, Wanna Be Me, which he previewed through his Instagram.\n\nThe vocals are directly sampled from the original song, which can be identified by the producer tag of the original track leaking through.\nThe producer tag belonged to Bred, whom worked with Yeat in the past. His producer tag says the following:\n\nI don’t give a fuck, bruh, I'ma always be me\n\nUltimately, this is not the first time Yeat has went into his archives to rework on it for ADL. Track 5, “What I Want“, is a primary example of Yeat reworking his vault with fellow collaborator BNYX®.", "annotation_id": "39143151", "url": "https://genius.com/39143151", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2Planës", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Yeat-2planes-lyrics", "genius_title": "2Planës", "genius_id": 13303529, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2Nite", "line": "Turn another page in the book, burn", "vault_lines": ["Turn another page in the book, burn"], "meaning": "This line most likely relates to Yeat’s constant focus on evolution and progression, constantly asking “Whats next?” And not concerning himself with the past. He doesnt care what happened before, only what he can do next.\n\nYeat has been on record numerous times respecting his past and the lessons and stories/art that come from it, but he doesnt let it slow him down from constantly improving and evolving.", "annotation_id": "39185994", "url": "https://genius.com/39185994", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2Nite", "line": "And I know they don’t speak your language", "vault_lines": ["And I know they don't speak your language (Ooh)"], "meaning": "This line is most likely a metaphor for living life different than most people, and having opinions/choices most people wouldnt align with or even understand. The “language” is only something Yeat and the “you” mentioned understand, while “they” can’t understand what they mean.\n\nThis is further solidified in the next line, where he dismisses their importance due to this.", "annotation_id": "39160336", "url": "https://genius.com/39160336", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2Nite", "line": "But tonight, it’s fuck ’em all", "vault_lines": ["But tonight, it's fuck 'em all (Ooh)"], "meaning": "This line likely alludes to Yeat’s unconcern for outsider’s opinions and input for his life and how he lives it.", "annotation_id": "39160322", "url": "https://genius.com/39160322", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2Nite", "line": "I’m a ball hog, baby, know you know that (Oh)", "vault_lines": ["I'm a ball hog, baby, know you know that (Oh)"], "meaning": "“Ball hog” comes from a common saying in many different sports. It usually describes a player who rarely passes and keeps control of the ball. Yeat uses the saying metaphorically to describe his personality and dominance over the industry.\n\n“Ball hoggers” are typically confident, passionate and selfish suggesting that Yeat believes he’s the one in control of his success and isn’t relying on anyone else.", "annotation_id": "39158096", "url": "https://genius.com/39158096", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2Nite", "line": "And we get you cut like some coke and watch you bleed (I-I-I—)", "vault_lines": ["And we get you cut like some coke and watch you bleed (I-I-I—)"], "meaning": "This line plays on drug imagery and violence at the same time. “Cut like some coke” refers to how cocaine is often cut  to increase volume and profit. Yeat flips this saying into a threat.\n\n“Watch you bleed\" reinforces that violent image, but it is also referencing a real side effect of coke: frequent nosebleeds caused by damage to the nasal passages.\n\nOverall, the bar blends street imagery (drug culture) with aggression, a common theme in Yeat’s music where flexing power and intimidation go hand in hand.", "annotation_id": "39158056", "url": "https://genius.com/39158056", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2Nite", "line": "Uh, only big bank, uh, we got bad bitches, uh, Richard Mil’ plain", "vault_lines": ["Uh, only big bank, uh, we got bad bitches, uh, Richard Mil' plain"], "meaning": "Possible reference to Gunna’s “Richard Millie Plain”\nhttps://genius.com/16679390", "annotation_id": "39150803", "url": "https://genius.com/39150803", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2Nite", "line": "But tonight, it’s fuck ’em all (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["But tonight, it's fuck 'em all (Ooh)"], "meaning": "This line highlights impulsivity, choosing temporary escape over meaningful connection. It shows how quickly emotional vulnerability is replaced by reckless behavior.", "annotation_id": "39149354", "url": "https://genius.com/39149354", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2Nite", "line": "Turn another page in the book, burn", "vault_lines": ["Turn another page in the book, burn"], "meaning": "Burning a page again reflects his habit of erasing the past instead of learning from it. This repetition from earlier in the album shows that his approach hasn’t changed, even as the themes shift toward love.", "annotation_id": "39149349", "url": "https://genius.com/39149349", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2Nite", "line": "Yeah, I been waitin’ on your call (I-I-I—)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I been waitin' on your call (I-I-I—)"], "meaning": "This line introduces vulnerability, showing Yeat in a rare position of waiting on someone else. It contrasts with his usual dominance, suggesting emotional dependence beneath his confident exterior.", "annotation_id": "39149344", "url": "https://genius.com/39149344", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2Nite", "line": "I been waitin’ at the fire (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I been waitin' at the fire (Yeah)"], "meaning": "The “fire” can symbolize both passion and danger. Waiting at the fire suggests anticipation for connection, but also hints that whatever he’s waiting for may burn him. This dual meaning reflects the album’s idea that love and danger are inseparable.", "annotation_id": "39149341", "url": "https://genius.com/39149341", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
