{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2093", "line": "Get your things mixed up when you— (Hoo) Yeah, your things mixed up", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, your days mixed up"], "meaning": "He’s talking about diffusion right here if you analyse carefully you can see ‘you get your things mixed up’ this shows that he is getting his wock mixed with a perc in his cup which proves that yeat is a generational rapper", "annotation_id": "30909819", "url": "https://genius.com/30909819", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Yeat", "song": "2093", "line": "(I live in) 2093 (I live in) 2093 (I live in) 2093 I live 2090-free (I live in) 2090, free (I live in) Twenty friends by the— (I live in) Racks by the beach (I live in) 2093, free", "vault_lines": ["(I live in) 2090, free"], "meaning": "Yeat has been open about his self-centered lifestyle and his futuristic way of thinking. In an interview with Channel 5, Yeat sarcastically speaks upon his futuristic fantasies if he were given a time machine:\n\nUh… I don’t know. I would, uh… I would go to the future.\n\nYeat has also expressed his narcissistic behavior in his songs, such as 2021’s “Told Ya”:\n\nI’m the latest and the greatest, that’s the craziest part about it\nAnd I told ‘em that they never gon’ make it, that’s the part they doubted\n\nConveying that he’s living in 2093, Yeat claims he is more intelligent than the average individual and believes he lives in the future because of his self-proclaimed wits.", "annotation_id": "29999716", "url": "https://genius.com/29999716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
